#. ja: バラクーダ埠頭
#. de: Barrakuda-Pier
#. fr: Quais du barracuda
#. column 14: "Under the azure, I gazed down upon warships three, their billowing sails of crimson leaving no doubt as to who truly rules the seas." Such were the merchant's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: These docks provide safe mooring for the Thalassocratic Navy's principal squadrons, also known as the Crimson Fleet. To prevent sabotage, admittance to the area is forbidden to the general citizenry; however, on clear days, one may catch a glimpse of the armada flagship, the <i>Triumph</i>, from atop one of Limsa Lominsa's myriad spans.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162688:0:13"
msgid "Barracuda Piers"
msgstr "Причалы Барракуды"

#. ja: ――ある商人が見た景色。\n眼下を見やれば、そこには赤き帆の軍艦が三隻。海都「リムサ・ロミンサ」の底力を感じた。
#. de: Zu Füßen dieses Händlers liegen drei Kriegsschiffe. Mit ihren leuchtend roten Segeln verkörpern sie die geballte Kampfkraft der Meeresmetropole.
#. fr: Avant de déjeuner, les gourmets limséens savent d'où regarder les trois navires de guerre aux voiles écarlates qui sont le fleuron de la marine du Maelstrom.
#. column 13: Barracuda Piers
#. column 15: These docks provide safe mooring for the Thalassocratic Navy's principal squadrons, also known as the Crimson Fleet. To prevent sabotage, admittance to the area is forbidden to the general citizenry; however, on clear days, one may catch a glimpse of the armada flagship, the <i>Triumph</i>, from atop one of Limsa Lominsa's myriad spans.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162688:0:14"
msgid "\"Under the azure, I gazed down upon warships three, their billowing sails of crimson leaving no doubt as to who truly rules the seas.\" Such were the merchant's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Под лазурным небом я взглянул вниз: три военных корабля, алые паруса вздуваются на ветру — сразу видно, кто здесь истинный властелин морей». Так говорил торговец. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: リムサ・ロミンサが誇る旗艦艦隊「黒渦艦隊」の軍艦が投錨する軍用埠頭。一般市民の立ち入りは制限されているが、見晴らしのいい場所からなら、総旗艦「トライアンフ号」をはじめとする軍艦の姿を見ることができる
#. de: So stolze Schiffe wie die <i>Triumph</i>, Flaggschiff der Kriegsflotte des Mahlstroms und Stolz von Limsa Lominsa, liegen hier vor Anker. Nicht für jedermann zugänglich, aber umso malerischer.
#. fr: Ce lieu est celui où sont amarrés les navires de guerre du Maelstrom. Son accès est interdit au public pour des raisons de sécurité, mais les curieux savent d'où admirer la puissante armada, notamment son célèbre vaisseau étendard, le Triomphe.
#. column 13: Barracuda Piers
#. column 14: "Under the azure, I gazed down upon warships three, their billowing sails of crimson leaving no doubt as to who truly rules the seas." Such were the merchant's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162688:0:15"
msgid "These docks provide safe mooring for the Thalassocratic Navy's principal squadrons, also known as the Crimson Fleet. To prevent sabotage, admittance to the area is forbidden to the general citizenry; however, on clear days, one may catch a glimpse of the armada flagship, the <i>Triumph</i>, from atop one of Limsa Lominsa's myriad spans."
msgstr "На этих причалах стоят главные эскадры Владычицы морей — их ещё называют Алым флотом. Чтобы предотвратить диверсии, простым горожанам вход сюда запрещён. Но в ясный день с одного из многочисленных мостов Лимсы-Ломинсы можно увидеть флагман флота, <i>«Триумф»</i>."

#. ja: 海賊船「アスタリシア号」
#. de: Die <i>Astalicia</i>
#. fr: Astalicia
#. column 14: "A flagon or two o' grog havin' filled me 'ead with big ideas, I eyed that 'ive o' villainy from the pier, feelin' as if I could cut down Hyllfyr 'imself. Woke the next mornin' strung up by me ankles. Aye, was lucky to escape with me life." Such were the buccaneer's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Registered as a trade vessel hailing from foreign waters, this battle-scarred warship captained by the lord of the region's underworld, Hyllfyr, serves as a gathering place for brigands, cutthroats, and the purveyors of sundry other breeds of villainy. It is here that the city<hyphen>state's many pirate crews find new recruits to join their ranks.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162689:0:13"
msgid "The <i>Astalicia</i>"
msgstr "<i>«Асталисия»</i>"

#. ja: ――ある海賊が見た景色。\n酒を飲めば気分は大物。ヤバい奴らの縄張りで、大物気取りで港を一望。翌日、目が覚めたら吊されていた。
#. de: Frei wie ein Freibeuter! Mit einem kräftigen Schluck gestärkt ist auch der ungebärdigste Kontrahent auf See nur ein kleines Blättchen im Ozean - doch Hochmut kommt vor dem Fall. Vielleicht schon am nächsten Morgen.
#. fr: Le soir, les pirates éméchés aiment se tenir au bout d'un espar pour admirer le port sous un ciel étoilé... avant d'attraper un badaud pour s'amuser à le pendre.
#. column 13: The <i>Astalicia</i>
#. column 15: Registered as a trade vessel hailing from foreign waters, this battle-scarred warship captained by the lord of the region's underworld, Hyllfyr, serves as a gathering place for brigands, cutthroats, and the purveyors of sundry other breeds of villainy. It is here that the city<hyphen>state's many pirate crews find new recruits to join their ranks.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162689:0:14"
msgid "\"A flagon or two o' grog havin' filled me 'ead with big ideas, I eyed that 'ive o' villainy from the pier, feelin' as if I could cut down Hyllfyr 'imself. Woke the next mornin' strung up by me ankles. Aye, was lucky to escape with me life.\" Such were the buccaneer's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«От кружки-другой эля у меня голова пошла кругом. С пирса я глядел на это осиное гнездо и думал, что и самого Хильфира одолею. А наутро проснулся подвешенным за ноги. Да, ещё повезло унести ноги живым». Так говорил пират. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 三大海賊の筆頭格である海賊団「断罪党」が保有するガレオン船。表向きは外国籍の商船とされているが、それが大海賊「ヒルフィル」の持ち船であることは公然の秘密。船内は、海賊諸派の社交場となっている
#. de: Die Galeone der berüchtigten „Henkershorde“. Obgleich als Handelsschiff von Übersee getarnt, ist es ein offenes Geheimnis, dass dies Hyllfyrs Hauptquartier und Treffpunkt von Piraten aller Lager ist.
#. fr: Cet imposant galion appartient à l'équipage pirate des Bourreaux. Bien qu'il soit enregistré comme navire marchand étranger, tout Limsa Lominsa sait qu'il est la propriété de l'illustre Hyllfyr et sert de repaire aux corsaires et autres coupe-jarrets.
#. column 13: The <i>Astalicia</i>
#. column 14: "A flagon or two o' grog havin' filled me 'ead with big ideas, I eyed that 'ive o' villainy from the pier, feelin' as if I could cut down Hyllfyr 'imself. Woke the next mornin' strung up by me ankles. Aye, was lucky to escape with me life." Such were the buccaneer's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. macro: <hyphen> — a hyphen that does not break the line (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162689:0:15"
msgid "Registered as a trade vessel hailing from foreign waters, this battle-scarred warship captained by the lord of the region's underworld, Hyllfyr, serves as a gathering place for brigands, cutthroats, and the purveyors of sundry other breeds of villainy. It is here that the city<hyphen>state's many pirate crews find new recruits to join their ranks."
msgstr "Зарегистрированный как торговое судно из чужих вод, этот видавший виды боевой корабль под командованием Хильфира, владыки здешнего преступного мира, служит сборищем для разбойников, головорезов и прочих отъявленных мерзавцев. Здесь пиратские команды Лимсы-Ломинсы пополняют свои ряды новыми людьми."

#. ja: シーソング石窟の慰霊碑
#. de: Monument in der Klagegrotte
#. fr: Stèle du chant marin
#. column 14: "In a dank cavern that's never known the sun, the patter of the rain me only companion, I dropped to one knee and said me farewells to me ill-fated mates. They sing no songs for fishermen, but the sea swallows us all the same." Such were the old mariner's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: “I am the waves that bear, I am the winds that guide.<br>I am the evening stars, I am the morning sky.<br>I am born of the sea, and there shall I die.”<br><br>Nestled within a shallow cavern situated to the south of Summerford Farms sits an ancient monolith upon which is carved this, the Sailors' Requiem.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162690:0:13"
msgid "Seasong Grotto"
msgstr "Грот Морской Песни"

#. ja: ――ある船乗りが見た景色。\n出漁前の俺だけの儀式。朝日届かぬ薄暗い洞穴で、逝った仲間に黙祷する。静かな雨音を、鎮魂歌に代えて。
#. de: Das tägliche Ritual des Fischers vor der ersten Ausfahrt im kühlen Dämmerlicht der Höhle - ein stilles Gedenken an die verunglückten Kameraden, die begleitet vom Widerhall der Wassertropfen in das Requiem der Seeleute einzustimmen scheinen.
#. fr: Les pêcheurs superstitieux ne manquent jamais d'aller prier à l'entrée d'une grotte pour leurs camarades disparus avant de partir en mer, lorsque la pluie joue un requiem pour leurs âmes.
#. column 13: Seasong Grotto
#. column 15: “I am the waves that bear, I am the winds that guide.<br>I am the evening stars, I am the morning sky.<br>I am born of the sea, and there shall I die.”<br><br>Nestled within a shallow cavern situated to the south of Summerford Farms sits an ancient monolith upon which is carved this, the Sailors' Requiem.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162690:0:14"
msgid "\"In a dank cavern that's never known the sun, the patter of the rain me only companion, I dropped to one knee and said me farewells to me ill-fated mates. They sing no songs for fishermen, but the sea swallows us all the same.\" Such were the old mariner's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«В сырой пещере, где солнце не показывалось отродясь, под стук дождевых капель я опустился на колено и простился с товарищами, которых сгубило море. О рыбаках песен не поют, да только море всех нас поглотит». Так говорил старый моряк. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 船乗りたちの慰霊碑。魂を運ぶとされるウミネコの姿と共に、「私は支える波であり、私は導く風である。私は夜の星であり、私は朝の空である。私は海で生を受け、そして、海で死に向かう」との鎮魂歌が刻まれている
#. de: Ich bin die Welle, die mich auf dem Rücken trägt, ich bin der Wind, der Gischt auf alle Wellen schlägt. Ich bin die tausend Sterne hoch am Firmament, das Morgenrot, dem Meer geboren, bis es mich im Tod umfängt.
#. fr: Érigée à la mémoire des marins disparus, cette stèle porte l'inscription “Je suis la vague qui porte, je suis le vent qui guide. Je suis l'étoile qui brille dans la nuit, je suis le calme blanc du matin. Je suis né dans la mer, et c'est en elle que je mourrai...”
#. column 13: Seasong Grotto
#. column 14: "In a dank cavern that's never known the sun, the patter of the rain me only companion, I dropped to one knee and said me farewells to me ill-fated mates. They sing no songs for fishermen, but the sea swallows us all the same." Such were the old mariner's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162690:0:15"
msgid "“I am the waves that bear, I am the winds that guide.<br>I am the evening stars, I am the morning sky.<br>I am born of the sea, and there shall I die.”<br><br>Nestled within a shallow cavern situated to the south of Summerford Farms sits an ancient monolith upon which is carved this, the Sailors' Requiem."
msgstr "«Я — волны, что несут, я — ветра, что ведут.<br>Я — вечерние звёзды, я — утреннее небо.<br>Я рождён морем и в нём же умру».<br><br>В неглубокой пещере к югу от ферм Саммерфорда стоит древний каменный столб. На нём высечена эта «Заупокойная песнь моряков»."

#. ja: スカイリフト
#. de: Himmelszug
#. fr: Ascenciel
#. column 14: "Backbreakin', arse-bustin' work, it is. But seein' me vessels ridin' the winds, soarin' off to far lands where me legs will never carry me─well, at least me sweat and blood ain't been for naught, eh?" Such were the laborer's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Once an endless expanse of flat, rocky meadows, middle La Noscea is now severed atwain by a sheer cliff known as the Descent. To maintain overland trade routes from the easterly outposts of Aleport and Bronze Lake, Lominsan engineers created the Skylift─a tower of wooden scaffolding outfitted with pulleys, winches, and lighter-than-air balloons.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162691:0:13"
msgid "The Skylift"
msgstr "Небесный подъёмник"

#. ja: ――ある荷運び人が見た景色。\n辛い力仕事の合間、休憩中に見る景色が好きだ。青空に浮かぶ気球の美しさよ。
#. de: Das Verladen der Waren ist Knochenarbeit. In einer kleinen Pause lässt der Arbeiter gerne die Gedanken schweifen - in die Ferne, vorbei an den Lastenballons im blauen Himmel, bis an den Horizont und weiter, immer weiter.
#. fr: Lorsqu'ils prennent une pause l'après-midi, les convoyeurs noscéens aiment admirer les ballons qui transportent les marchandises au-dessus de la mer.
#. column 13: The Skylift
#. column 15: Once an endless expanse of flat, rocky meadows, middle La Noscea is now severed atwain by a sheer cliff known as the Descent. To maintain overland trade routes from the easterly outposts of Aleport and Bronze Lake, Lominsan engineers created the Skylift─a tower of wooden scaffolding outfitted with pulleys, winches, and lighter-than-air balloons.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162691:0:14"
msgid "\"Backbreakin', arse-bustin' work, it is. But seein' me vessels ridin' the winds, soarin' off to far lands where me legs will never carry me─well, at least me sweat and blood ain't been for naught, eh?\" Such were the laborer's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Тяжёлая работёнка, спину ломит, сил нет! Зато глянешь, как мои суда парят на ветру и уносятся в дальние края, куда мне и ногами не добраться, — и понимаешь: кровь и пот пролиты не зря, а?» Так говорил грузчик. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 第七霊災時の地殻変動によって生じた「デセント断崖」を乗り越えるために、リムサ・ロミンサの荷運び人たちが共同で建設、運営している昇降機。通常の昇降機のほか、気球を使った物資の上げ下ろしも行っている
#. de: Der durch die Siebte Katastrophe aufgebrochene „Abstieg“ teilt La Noscea quer von Norden nach Süden. Ohne den Lastenheber des Himmelszugs wäre die gigantische Felswand für schwere Lasten kaum zu überwinden.
#. fr: Cette installation gérée par les convoyeurs limséens permet de transporter les mar<shy>chan<shy>di<shy>ses à l'aide de palans et de ballons le long de La Descente, un précipice apparu lors du septième fléau au beau milieu de la plaine de la Noscea centrale.
#. column 13: The Skylift
#. column 14: "Backbreakin', arse-bustin' work, it is. But seein' me vessels ridin' the winds, soarin' off to far lands where me legs will never carry me─well, at least me sweat and blood ain't been for naught, eh?" Such were the laborer's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162691:0:15"
msgid "Once an endless expanse of flat, rocky meadows, middle La Noscea is now severed atwain by a sheer cliff known as the Descent. To maintain overland trade routes from the easterly outposts of Aleport and Bronze Lake, Lominsan engineers created the Skylift─a tower of wooden scaffolding outfitted with pulleys, winches, and lighter-than-air balloons."
msgstr "Когда-то средняя Ла-Носкея была бескрайней равниной с ровными каменистыми лугами. Теперь её разделяет отвесный обрыв — Спуск. Чтобы сохранить сухопутное сообщение с восточными поселениями Алепортом и Бронзовым озером, инженеры Лимсы-Ломинсы построили Небесный подъёмник — деревянную башню с блоками, лебёдками и воздушными шарами."

#. ja: ラザグラン街道
#. de: La Thagran-Landstraße
#. fr: Route orientale de la Thagran
#. column 14: "When the skies turn grey and spirits sag, I climb high and look upon roads blazed long ago. I turn my thoughts to the hardships of my forebears till mine own worries drift away, and I find strength to carry on." Such were the sentry's words, and I would see as she saw.
#. column 15: When the <i>Galadion</i> fell victim to the Navigator's fury and ran aground on the southern shores of Vylbrand seven hundred years ago, it was her two helmsmen, Jean De Nevelle and Guy La Thagran, who were tasked with exploring the newfound island─the former heading east, the latter, west. To this day, their routes still serve as La Noscea's two main thoroughfares.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162692:0:13"
msgid "La Thagran Eastroad"
msgstr "Восточный тракт Ла-Таграна"

#. ja: ――ある警備兵が見た景色。\n灰色の空のように気分が晴れないときは、高所に登る。先人が拓いた街道を見て、開拓の苦労に思いを馳せる。
#. de: Ein Wachsoldat in einem kurzen Moment der Muße. Gerade wenn der graue Himmel aufs Gemüt drückt, soll man sich hohe Ziele für den Tag stecken. Der Blick auf die alte Straße ruft die enorme Leistung der Pioniere in Erinnerung, die diese Route einst erschlossen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'ils se sentent d'humeur grisâtre, les casaques jaunes n'hésitent pas à monter sur une palissade pour admirer la Noscea avant le milieu de la journée.
#. column 13: La Thagran Eastroad
#. column 15: When the <i>Galadion</i> fell victim to the Navigator's fury and ran aground on the southern shores of Vylbrand seven hundred years ago, it was her two helmsmen, Jean De Nevelle and Guy La Thagran, who were tasked with exploring the newfound island─the former heading east, the latter, west. To this day, their routes still serve as La Noscea's two main thoroughfares.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162692:0:14"
msgid "\"When the skies turn grey and spirits sag, I climb high and look upon roads blazed long ago. I turn my thoughts to the hardships of my forebears till mine own worries drift away, and I find strength to carry on.\" Such were the sentry's words, and I would see as she saw."
msgstr "«Когда небо сереет и на душе тоскливо, забираюсь повыше и смотрю на дороги, проложенные давным-давно. Вспоминаю, как тяжело пришлось нашим предкам, — и мои заботы отходят на второй план. Снова появляются силы идти дальше». Так говорила часовая. Я решил взглянуть на всё её глазами."

#. ja: 中央から低地を抜け、東ラノシアへと通じる街道。入植初期に、建国船「ガラディオン号」の航海士「デネベール」と共に、島を探検して地形把握に務めたエレゼン族冒険家「ラザグラン」の名にちなみ、そう呼ばれている
#. de: Diese Fernstraße vom zentralen ins östliche La Noscea ist nach dem früheren Seefahrer Guy La Thagran benannt, der in der Siedlerzeit gemeinsam mit seinem Kameraden Jean De Nevelle Vylbrand erforschte und vermaß.
#. fr: Cet axe de circulation, qui relie la Noscea centrale à la Noscea orientale, a reçu le nom de Guy la Thagran, un navigateur élézen qui s'est illustré en explorant l'île de Vylbrand en compagnie de son camarade Jean de Nevelle lorsque le Galadion s'y est échoué.
#. column 13: La Thagran Eastroad
#. column 14: "When the skies turn grey and spirits sag, I climb high and look upon roads blazed long ago. I turn my thoughts to the hardships of my forebears till mine own worries drift away, and I find strength to carry on." Such were the sentry's words, and I would see as she saw.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162692:0:15"
msgid "When the <i>Galadion</i> fell victim to the Navigator's fury and ran aground on the southern shores of Vylbrand seven hundred years ago, it was her two helmsmen, Jean De Nevelle and Guy La Thagran, who were tasked with exploring the newfound island─the former heading east, the latter, west. To this day, their routes still serve as La Noscea's two main thoroughfares."
msgstr "Семьсот лет назад <i>Галадион</i> пал жертвой ярости Навигатора и сел на мель у южных берегов Вилбрандта. Исследовать новый остров поручили двум его рулевым — Жану де Невелю и Гаю Ла-Таграну: первый отправился на восток, второй — на запад. И по сей день их маршруты остаются двумя главными трактами Ла-Носкеи."

#. ja: ソルトストランド
#. de: Salzstrand
#. fr: Atolls de sel
#. column 14: "Under the watchful gaze of the Wanderer, I cast a line to waters far below. Looking upon those pillars, grotesque and beautiful, my thoughts drift to that fateful day five years ago." Such were the fisher's words, and I would see as she saw.
#. column 15: When struck by a fallen shard from Dalamud's outer shell, a massive amount of concentrated aether was released from just below the surface of the Rhotano Sea, immediately fusing with and crystallizing the towering fount of saltwater which was expelled during the impact. City<hyphen>state-funded exploratory forays into the inner crater have all yet to return...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162693:0:13"
msgid "The Salt Strand"
msgstr "Соляной берег"

#. ja: ――ある漁師が見た景色。\n放浪の神に見守られ、釣り糸を垂らす。眼下に見える塩の柱を目に、5年前の惨劇を思う。
#. de: Ein Fischer hat unter dem Schutz Oschons, des Wanderers, noch immer seine Leine ausgeworfen. Zu seinen Füßen erstreckt sich die bizarre Salzwüste, die an die große Tragödie vor fünf Jahren gemahnt.
#. fr: L'un des avantages de la vie de gardien de phare, c'est de pouvoir se tenir sur le bord du promontoire pour observer la plage, lorsque la nuit tombe.
#. column 13: The Salt Strand
#. column 15: When struck by a fallen shard from Dalamud's outer shell, a massive amount of concentrated aether was released from just below the surface of the Rhotano Sea, immediately fusing with and crystallizing the towering fount of saltwater which was expelled during the impact. City<hyphen>state-funded exploratory forays into the inner crater have all yet to return...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162693:0:14"
msgid "\"Under the watchful gaze of the Wanderer, I cast a line to waters far below. Looking upon those pillars, grotesque and beautiful, my thoughts drift to that fateful day five years ago.\" Such were the fisher's words, and I would see as she saw."
msgstr "«Под бдительным взглядом Странника закидываю удочку вон в те воды, внизу. Глядя на эти причудливые, прекрасные столбы соли, невольно вспоминаю тот страшный день пять лет назад». Так говорила рыбачка. Я решила взглянуть на всё её глазами."

#. ja: 霊災時に砂浜に落着したダラガブの欠片が地脈を貫いた結果、エーテルが噴出し、偏属性クリスタルを形成した。その際、同時に海水の塩分が結晶化したらしく、ミルククラウンのような塩柱が残る結果となったようだ
#. de: Dalamud-Fragmente durchtrennten hier beim Einschlag große Äther-Adern, wodurch denaturierte Kristalle entstanden, die mit dem Meerwasser reagierten und mannigfaltige Salzformationen entstehen ließen.
#. fr: Un fragment de Dalamud tombé lors du Fléau a libéré l'éther du sol, provoquant la formation d'un imposant cristal corrompu qui, à son tour, a causé l'agglomération des sels de mer projetés vers le ciel sous la force de l'impact.
#. column 13: The Salt Strand
#. column 14: "Under the watchful gaze of the Wanderer, I cast a line to waters far below. Looking upon those pillars, grotesque and beautiful, my thoughts drift to that fateful day five years ago." Such were the fisher's words, and I would see as she saw.
#. macro: <hyphen> — a hyphen that does not break the line (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162693:0:15"
msgid "When struck by a fallen shard from Dalamud's outer shell, a massive amount of concentrated aether was released from just below the surface of the Rhotano Sea, immediately fusing with and crystallizing the towering fount of saltwater which was expelled during the impact. City<hyphen>state-funded exploratory forays into the inner crater have all yet to return..."
msgstr "Когда обломок оболочки Даламуда упал в море Ротано, под его поверхностью высвободилось огромное количество сконцентрированного эфира. Он тут же смешался с вырвавшимся при ударе столбом морской воды и обратился в кристаллы соли. Все экспедиции, снаряжённые городом<hyphen>государством исследовать кратер, до сих пор не вернулись..."

#. ja: レッドルースター農場の畑
#. de: Felder der Gockelburg
#. fr: Métairie du Coq rouge
#. column 14: "No romance in the farmin' life? Balderdash, I say! Rise at dawn, climb atop the gate, and look upon the dew-kissed fields below─then tell me there's any place in the realm ye'd rather be." Such were the farmer's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: The farmers on the Red Rooster Stead will rarely shy from testing their agricultural acumen on exotic crops or untested growing methods, and take pride in their willingness to sacrifice a harvest if it means a better yield an autumn hence. The plantation's name is said to be taken from the bloody cockfights held after nightfall by the gamekeeps.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162694:0:13"
msgid "Red Rooster Stead"
msgstr "Ферма Красного Петуха"

#. ja: ――ある農夫が見た景色。\n農夫の朝は早い。門の上に立ち、朝霧に濡れた畑を見て、地味な野良仕事に備えて心を奮い立たせるのが日課だ。
#. de: Der frühe Morgen ist des Feldarbeiters Mittag. Von oberhalb des Tores die geheimnisvoll verschleierten Felder zu überblicken, erfrischt den Geist und die Glieder wie nichts anderes.
#. fr: La vie de métayer requiert de se lever tôt, mais c'est aussi la chance d'admirer les baraques et les clôtures prendre forme dans la brume matinale, debout sur les tuiles.
#. column 13: Red Rooster Stead
#. column 15: The farmers on the Red Rooster Stead will rarely shy from testing their agricultural acumen on exotic crops or untested growing methods, and take pride in their willingness to sacrifice a harvest if it means a better yield an autumn hence. The plantation's name is said to be taken from the bloody cockfights held after nightfall by the gamekeeps.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162694:0:14"
msgid "\"No romance in the farmin' life? Balderdash, I say! Rise at dawn, climb atop the gate, and look upon the dew-kissed fields below─then tell me there's any place in the realm ye'd rather be.\" Such were the farmer's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Говорят, фермерская жизнь скучна? Чепуха! Встань на рассвете, заберись на ворота и взгляни на росистые поля внизу. А потом скажи, где ещё в этом мире тебе захотелось бы жить!» Так говорил фермер. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 一人の園芸師が設立した実験農場。作物の栽培はもちろん、ドードーやシープの飼育も行う。なお、農場名は、赤い鶏と白い鶏のどちらが強いか賭けを行ったところ、双方が血塗れで真っ赤になったという出来事に由来する
#. de: Die Gockelburg ist ein Versuchsbauernhof, der sich der Veredelung von Feldfrüchten und der Dodo- und Schafzucht verschrieben hat. Der Name stammt von den Hahnenkämpfen, die wie Ritterturniere aufgezogen wurden.
#. fr: Outre ses potagers expérimentaux, cette ex<shy>ploi<shy>ta<shy>tion fait aussi l'élevage de dodos et de moutons. Son nom viendrait d'un combat de coqs, un rouge et un blanc, qui aurait dégénéré en bagarre et fini avec les deux volailles et les spectateurs couverts de sang.
#. column 13: Red Rooster Stead
#. column 14: "No romance in the farmin' life? Balderdash, I say! Rise at dawn, climb atop the gate, and look upon the dew-kissed fields below─then tell me there's any place in the realm ye'd rather be." Such were the farmer's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162694:0:15"
msgid "The farmers on the Red Rooster Stead will rarely shy from testing their agricultural acumen on exotic crops or untested growing methods, and take pride in their willingness to sacrifice a harvest if it means a better yield an autumn hence. The plantation's name is said to be taken from the bloody cockfights held after nightfall by the gamekeeps."
msgstr "Фермеры с фермы Красного Петуха не боятся испытывать свои знания на редких культурах и новых способах выращивания. Они готовы пожертвовать урожаем, если это сулит более богатый сбор будущей осенью. Говорят, название фермы пошло от кровавых петушиных боёв, которые егеря устраивали после наступления темноты."

#. ja: ブルワーズ灯台
#. de: Leuchtturm Braubake
#. fr: Phare des Brasseurs
#. column 14: "When dawn breaks, I quench the flame and pour meself an ale. I step outside, and lose meself in the blue expanse above and below─me hard-earned reward for the ships I've seen to safety, I reckon." Such were the candlekeep's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: This relatively new lighthouse was built soon after the Calamity claimed Swiftperch Tower to ensure safe passage for trade vessels carrying shipments of dark stouts and blonde barleywines out of Aleport. In addition, the candlekeeps also keep watch for increasingly frequent rogue tidal waves caused by the stirrings of the Lord of the Whorl.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162695:0:13"
msgid "The Brewer's Beacon"
msgstr "Маяк пивоваров"

#. ja: ――ある灯台守が見た景色。\n青い空、青い海。船を導いていた灯台の灯りを消したあと、エールをひっかけながら見る海の眺めは最高だ。
#. de: Azurblauer Himmel, tiefblaues Meer: Das ist die majestätische Kulisse, die sich dem Wärter darbietet, sobald die Arbeit getan und das Leuchtfeuer gelöscht ist. Sind die Schiffe sicher vorüber, gibt es nichts Schöneres als ein Bier vor diesem atemberaubenden Ausblick.
#. fr: L'œil qui veille sur les navires la nuit est celui qui a la meilleure vue sur la baie, lorsque les premiers rayons de soleil font leur apparition.
#. column 13: The Brewer's Beacon
#. column 15: This relatively new lighthouse was built soon after the Calamity claimed Swiftperch Tower to ensure safe passage for trade vessels carrying shipments of dark stouts and blonde barleywines out of Aleport. In addition, the candlekeeps also keep watch for increasingly frequent rogue tidal waves caused by the stirrings of the Lord of the Whorl.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162695:0:14"
msgid "\"When dawn breaks, I quench the flame and pour meself an ale. I step outside, and lose meself in the blue expanse above and below─me hard-earned reward for the ships I've seen to safety, I reckon.\" Such were the candlekeep's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«На рассвете гашу огонь и наливаю себе эля. Выхожу наружу, любуюсь синевой над головой и под ногами. Думаю, заслужил я этот отдых — сколько кораблей благополучно провёл!» Так говорил смотритель. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 崩落した雨燕塔の代替として建設された灯台。エールポートに出入りする船を見守るため、ブルワー（醸造家）の灯台と呼ばれている。水神「リヴァイアサン」の津波を警戒して、海に設置された消波帯の様子が一望できる
#. de: Braubake - der Name deutet die Zugehörigkeit zu Bierhafen an - wurde nach dem Einsturz des Tölpelturms errichtet. Von hoch oben blickt man auf die Wellenbrecher, die die Küste vor Flutwellen schützen.
#. fr: Bâti pour remplacer la tour du Martinet détruite lors du Fléau, ce phare tire son nom du fait qu'il guide les navires passant par Port-aux-Ales. Il permet aussi d'observer les murs qui doivent protéger la côte contre les raz-de-marée du Primordial Léviathan.
#. column 13: The Brewer's Beacon
#. column 14: "When dawn breaks, I quench the flame and pour meself an ale. I step outside, and lose meself in the blue expanse above and below─me hard-earned reward for the ships I've seen to safety, I reckon." Such were the candlekeep's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162695:0:15"
msgid "This relatively new lighthouse was built soon after the Calamity claimed Swiftperch Tower to ensure safe passage for trade vessels carrying shipments of dark stouts and blonde barleywines out of Aleport. In addition, the candlekeeps also keep watch for increasingly frequent rogue tidal waves caused by the stirrings of the Lord of the Whorl."
msgstr "Этот сравнительно новый маяк построили вскоре после того, как Бедствие разрушило башню Свифтперч. Он должен был помогать торговым судам с тёмным стаутом и светлым ячменным вином безопасно добираться из Эльпорта. Смотрители маяка также следят за всё более частыми внезапными приливными волнами, вызванными пробуждением Владыки Вихря."

#. ja: 革細工師ギルド
#. de: Gerbergilde
#. fr: Guilde des tanneurs
#. column 14: "Knew it was my calling ever since I was knee-high to a goobbue. When cloudy days sunk my spirits, I'd sneak into the guild, climb as high as my legs could carry me, and watch the tanners and tawers at work below." Such were the craftsman's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Crafters for the realm-famous Atelier Fen-Yll, the Leatherworkers' Guild boasts the finest tawers and tanners in all Eorzea. In recent years, the workshop has come to be known for its Geva patterns, which outline methods of working and cutting hides, pelts, skins, and furs in a way that honors the elementals within by minimizing waste.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162696:0:13"
msgid "The Leatherworkers' Guild"
msgstr "Гильдия кожевников"

#. ja: ――ある革細工師が見た景色。\n子供だった頃、よく工房内を一望できる場所に立って、職人たちが働く姿を眺めたものだ。空が陰り、肌寒い日は特にな。
#. de: Von diesem hohen Beobachtungsposten aus hatte der Gerber als Kind das Tun in der Werkstatt bestens im Blick. Besonders stimmungsvoll fand er es hier, wenn sich draußen der Himmel mit Wolken zuzog.
#. fr: Le travail du cuir est une telle fierté à Gridania que les enfants grimpent souvent sur les cadres de séchage pour admirer les tanneurs à l'ouvrage, lorsqu'il fait gris l'après-midi.
#. column 13: The Leatherworkers' Guild
#. column 15: Crafters for the realm-famous Atelier Fen-Yll, the Leatherworkers' Guild boasts the finest tawers and tanners in all Eorzea. In recent years, the workshop has come to be known for its Geva patterns, which outline methods of working and cutting hides, pelts, skins, and furs in a way that honors the elementals within by minimizing waste.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162696:0:14"
msgid "\"Knew it was my calling ever since I was knee-high to a goobbue. When cloudy days sunk my spirits, I'd sneak into the guild, climb as high as my legs could carry me, and watch the tanners and tawers at work below.\" Such were the craftsman's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Ещё когда я был ниже гооббу, понял: вот моё призвание. В пасмурные дни, когда настроение было хуже некуда, я пробирался в гильдию, забирался повыше и смотрел, как там внизу работают кожевники и дубильщики». Так говорил ремесленник. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: グリダニアが誇る革細工師たちが、森の恵みを活かした作品作りに没頭するアトリエ。特に熟練のギルド員のみが出品を許されるブランド、「フェン・イル」の製品は名品として名高く、予約待ちの状況が続いている
#. de: Die gridanischen Gerber verarbeiten mit hoher Kunst<shy>fer<shy>tig<shy>keit die Materialien, die der Wald ihnen bietet, und verkaufen ihre Waren im Atelier Fen-Yll. Für die beliebtesten Stücke gibt es Wartelisten, so groß ist der Andrang.
#. fr: Le métier de la tannerie est une des plus grandes fiertés de Gridania. Pratiquant leur artisanat dans le respect des matériaux que leur fournit la forêt, les membres de cette guilde ont créé leur propre marque de produits de haute qualité, Les Atours de Fen-Yll.
#. column 13: The Leatherworkers' Guild
#. column 14: "Knew it was my calling ever since I was knee-high to a goobbue. When cloudy days sunk my spirits, I'd sneak into the guild, climb as high as my legs could carry me, and watch the tanners and tawers at work below." Such were the craftsman's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162696:0:15"
msgid "Crafters for the realm-famous Atelier Fen-Yll, the Leatherworkers' Guild boasts the finest tawers and tanners in all Eorzea. In recent years, the workshop has come to be known for its Geva patterns, which outline methods of working and cutting hides, pelts, skins, and furs in a way that honors the elementals within by minimizing waste."
msgstr "Гильдия кожевников — мастера прославленного на весь мир ателье Фен-Илль и лучшие кожевники Эорзеи. В последние годы мастерская знаменита выкройками Гевы: они учат обрабатывать и кроить шкуры, меха и кожи так, чтобы почти ничего не пропадало и духи природы оставались в почёте."

#. ja: アプカル滝
#. de: Apkallu-Fälle
#. fr: Chutes de l'Apkallu
#. column 14: "My favoritest place is where I can see the falling water. There's a secret path that only I know. I snuck out of bed to go there last night. Mum and Dad made me promise I wouldn't climb up there anymore─you won't tell them, will you?" Such were the little boy's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Named after a failed attempt by an ambitious Gridanian merchant to hatch and breed apkallus in the linn, Apkallu Falls is most remembered for serving as a place of meditation for the late Louisoix Leveilleur, Circle of Knowing Archon and hero of Eorzea.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162697:0:13"
msgid "Apkallu Falls"
msgstr "Водопад Апкаллу"

#. ja: ――ある少年が見た景色。\nざーざー流れる滝が、お気に入りの場所。寝たふりをして家を抜けだして、秘密の道を通って、大人が来れない高いところに行くんだ。
#. de: Manchmal, wenn er eigentlich im Bett sein müsste, stiehlt sich der Dreikäsehoch aus dem Haus, rennt den geheimen Weg entlang und betrachtet den Wasserfall von oben, wo kein Erwachsener sich je hinaufbegeben würde.
#. fr: Les garnements gridaniens sont bien agiles. Trompant la vigilance de leurs parents, ils vont se percher sur les lampadaires pour admirer le reflet des étoiles dans l'eau vive.
#. column 13: Apkallu Falls
#. column 15: Named after a failed attempt by an ambitious Gridanian merchant to hatch and breed apkallus in the linn, Apkallu Falls is most remembered for serving as a place of meditation for the late Louisoix Leveilleur, Circle of Knowing Archon and hero of Eorzea.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162697:0:14"
msgid "\"My favoritest place is where I can see the falling water. There's a secret path that only I know. I snuck out of bed to go there last night. Mum and Dad made me promise I wouldn't climb up there anymore─you won't tell them, will you?\" Such were the little boy's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Больше всего мне нравится место, откуда видно водопад. Я знаю тайную тропу. Вчера притворился, что лёг спать, а потом сбежал туда. Мама с папой взяли с меня слово больше туда не лазить. Ты ведь им не расскажешь?» Так говорил мальчуган. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 湧水が流れ落ちる小さな滝。その昔、この滝壺でアプカルという鳥の繁殖が試みられたことがあるため、そう呼ばれる。第六星暦末期にグリダニアを訪れた賢人ルイゾワが、思索の場として好んでいたことでも有名
#. de: Der beschauliche Wasserfall hat seinen Namen von den ersten Siedlern, die hier Apkallu-Vögel züchteten. Der Ort ist dafür bekannt, dass der Weise Louisoix sich gerne zum Nachdenken hierher zurückzog.
#. fr: Appréciées pour le son rassérénant qu'elles produisent, ces chutes d'eau tirent leur nom d'une tentative échouée d'élevage d'apkallus. À la fin de la 6e ère astrale, le sage Louisoix s'y rendait souvent pour méditer lors de ses visites à Gridania.
#. column 13: Apkallu Falls
#. column 14: "My favoritest place is where I can see the falling water. There's a secret path that only I know. I snuck out of bed to go there last night. Mum and Dad made me promise I wouldn't climb up there anymore─you won't tell them, will you?" Such were the little boy's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162697:0:15"
msgid "Named after a failed attempt by an ambitious Gridanian merchant to hatch and breed apkallus in the linn, Apkallu Falls is most remembered for serving as a place of meditation for the late Louisoix Leveilleur, Circle of Knowing Archon and hero of Eorzea."
msgstr "Водопады Апкаллу названы в честь гриданийского торговца, который тщетно пытался вывести и разводить апкаллу у подножия водопада. Но больше всего это место помнят как любимое место для размышлений Луизуа Левейера, архонта Круга познания и героя Эорзеи."

#. ja: ベントブランチ牧場
#. de: Gut Zwieselgrund
#. fr: Ranch de Brancharquée
#. column 14: "Cute little bugger, isn't he? The moogle, that is. Seein' him up there on a clear day, swayin' gently in the wind, it's enough to lull a man to slumber. Me, I settle for a stump and a moment's repose." Such were the stablehand's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Once Moogle's Gift Mounts was established and its rookery stocked with Ishgard's finest birds, it was not long before an entire settlement had grown up around the stables. The trademark balloon tethered to the main building is actually an Ixali war vessel claimed by chocobokeeps after it became tangled in a nearby tree and was abandoned by its riders.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162698:0:13"
msgid "Bentbranch Meadows"
msgstr "Луга Гнутых ветвей"

#. ja: ――ある牧童が見た景色。\nお天道様の日射しをうけて、気球のモーグリも気持ちよさそう。そんな日は、ついつい腰を下ろして休みたくなるね。
#. de: Die Züchterin, mit der ich mich unterhielt, macht es richtig: Wenn die Sonne auf den Mogry-Ballon scheint, setzt sie sich an diesen einladenden Ort und genießt ihre Mittagspause.
#. fr: Il n'est pas donné à tout le monde de voir les Mogs, mais il y en a un grand que chacun peut admirer tranquillement par un bel après-midi, en s'asseyant sur une souche.
#. column 13: Bentbranch Meadows
#. column 15: Once Moogle's Gift Mounts was established and its rookery stocked with Ishgard's finest birds, it was not long before an entire settlement had grown up around the stables. The trademark balloon tethered to the main building is actually an Ixali war vessel claimed by chocobokeeps after it became tangled in a nearby tree and was abandoned by its riders.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162698:0:14"
msgid "\"Cute little bugger, isn't he? The moogle, that is. Seein' him up there on a clear day, swayin' gently in the wind, it's enough to lull a man to slumber. Me, I settle for a stump and a moment's repose.\" Such were the stablehand's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Милый, правда? Я про мугла. В ясный день смотришь, как он покачивается на ветру, и так и клонит в сон. А я уж устроюсь на пеньке и немного отдохну». Так говорил конюх. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 「モーグリギフトマウンツ」が運営するチョコボ牧場。本場であるイシュガルドより招いた厩務員の指導の下、チョコボの安定的な繁殖に挑んでいる。看板代わりに掲げられた、モーグリ印のバルーンがトレードマーク
#. de: In dem überregional bekannten Gestüt „Mogry-Stolz“ zieht ein aus Ishgard stammender Züchter zuverlässige Arbeits-Chocobos groß. Markenzeichen des Guts ist der auffällige Mogry-Ballon.
#. fr: Ce ranch est géré par la compagnie des Montures Mog. Les chocobos y sont élevés sous les in<shy>struc<shy>tions d'un dresseur venu d'Ishgard, une nation dont les destriers à plumes font la fierté. Le ballon à têtes de Mog à l'entrée est un célèbre symbole de l'endroit.
#. column 13: Bentbranch Meadows
#. column 14: "Cute little bugger, isn't he? The moogle, that is. Seein' him up there on a clear day, swayin' gently in the wind, it's enough to lull a man to slumber. Me, I settle for a stump and a moment's repose." Such were the stablehand's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162698:0:15"
msgid "Once Moogle's Gift Mounts was established and its rookery stocked with Ishgard's finest birds, it was not long before an entire settlement had grown up around the stables. The trademark balloon tethered to the main building is actually an Ixali war vessel claimed by chocobokeeps after it became tangled in a nearby tree and was abandoned by its riders."
msgstr "После того как в конюшнях «Подарок муглов» поселили лучших ишгардских чокобо, вокруг быстро выросло целое поселение. Знаменитый воздушный шар у главного здания на самом деле — военный корабль иксалей. Конюхи чокобо прибрали его к рукам, когда тот застрял на дереве, а всадники бросили его."

#. ja: 十二神大聖堂
#. de: Dom der Einkehr
#. fr: Sanctuaire des Douze
#. column 14: "I've never been the pious type, but when the sun strikes those windows and the trees in the gardens glisten, even I find myself mouthing a prayer from time to time." Such were the botanist's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: This sky-scraping ivory cathedral was built following the Age of Endless Frost─a dark period in which the realm was overrun with famine and disease─to serve as a place of refuge and respite for all who sought succor. Soon after, however, it fell into ruin and was all but forgotten...until the advent of the Seventh Umbral Era saw need for its rise once again.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162699:0:13"
msgid "The Sanctum of the Twelve"
msgstr "Святилище Двенадцати"

#. ja: ――ある園芸師が見た景色。\n陽光を受けると泉の水が輝いて、庭園は荘厳な空気に満ちる。そんな光景を見れば、不信心なヤツだって、祈りを捧げたくなるだろう。
#. de: Wenn sich das strahlende Sonnenlicht im Wasser spiegelt, weiß die Gärtnerin, warum sie diesen Beruf gewählt hat: Nirgends fühlt sie sich wohler als in ihrem Blumengarten. Dafür dankt sie den Göttern.
#. fr: Lorsque la lumière matinale vient faire étinceler l'eau, alors l'air se remplit d'une atmosphère bénie qui force même les moins croyants à prier au seuil de la béatitude.
#. column 13: The Sanctum of the Twelve
#. column 15: This sky-scraping ivory cathedral was built following the Age of Endless Frost─a dark period in which the realm was overrun with famine and disease─to serve as a place of refuge and respite for all who sought succor. Soon after, however, it fell into ruin and was all but forgotten...until the advent of the Seventh Umbral Era saw need for its rise once again.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162699:0:14"
msgid "\"I've never been the pious type, but when the sun strikes those windows and the trees in the gardens glisten, even I find myself mouthing a prayer from time to time.\" Such were the botanist's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Я не из набожных, но когда солнце светит в эти окна, а деревья в саду блестят, даже я порой ловлю себя на том, что шепчу молитву». Так говорил ботаник. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 大氷雪時代の直後に、食糧難と病の流行に悩まされた人々が、十二神全ての加護を得ようと建設した古き大聖堂。第七霊災後の困難な時代に、ふたたび神の加護を得ようと、グリダニアの民が協力して修繕した
#. de: Nach dem Zeitalter des langen Eises baute die von Hunger geplagte Bevölkerung diesen Dom, um die Zwölf um Beistand zu bitten. Auch nach der Siebten Katastrophe beten die Gläubigen hier zu ihren Göttern.
#. fr: Bâti pour obtenir la protection des Douze contre les famines et les épidémies qui ont suivi la grande glaciation, ce vieil édifice longtemps délaissé a été restauré après le septième fléau avec l'aide des Gridaniens pour recevoir de nouveau la faveur des Dieux.
#. column 13: The Sanctum of the Twelve
#. column 14: "I've never been the pious type, but when the sun strikes those windows and the trees in the gardens glisten, even I find myself mouthing a prayer from time to time." Such were the botanist's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162699:0:15"
msgid "This sky-scraping ivory cathedral was built following the Age of Endless Frost─a dark period in which the realm was overrun with famine and disease─to serve as a place of refuge and respite for all who sought succor. Soon after, however, it fell into ruin and was all but forgotten...until the advent of the Seventh Umbral Era saw need for its rise once again."
msgstr "Этот устремлённый ввысь собор из белой слоновой кости построили после Великой стужи — мрачной эпохи голода и болезней. Он должен был стать убежищем для всех, кому нужна помощь. Вскоре собор пришёл в упадок и был почти забыт... пока Седьмая умбральная эра не заставила возродить его."

#. ja: シルフの仮宿
#. de: Sylphen-Zuflucht
#. fr: Le Refuge
#. column 14: "To know the sylph, you must be the sylph. I may lack for wings, but a short climb will put me in a similar position. Lights dancing in the dark before me, I ponder what mischief I might make─er, were I a sylph, that is." Such were the scholar's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Little is the solace granted to those sylphs who would voice their opposition to the summoning of the Lord of Levin. Little is the solace bequeathed upon those who would abandon their homes in the Sylphlands and shun their frenzied brethren. Thus, it is only through fraternity that those sylphs may ultimately find solace, however little it may be.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162700:0:13"
msgid "Little Solace"
msgstr "Малая Отрада"

#. ja: ――ある博物学者が見た景色。\n空を飛ぶシルフ族のキモチを、少しでも良く知りたいと、よじ登った屋根の上。闇夜にぼんやり浮かぶ街灯の美しさが忘れられない。
#. de: Hoch oben auf der Wipfelplattform fühlt sich der Forscher fast wie eine fliegende Sylphe. Besonders hübsch ist es hier am Abend, wenn die Lichter der Hütten den Wald erhellen.
#. fr: Même sans savoir voler, les humains peuvent, avec un peu d'agilité, grimper sur les branches pour admirer le paysage depuis le toit naturel d'une demeure sylphe, par une belle nuit.
#. column 13: Little Solace
#. column 15: Little is the solace granted to those sylphs who would voice their opposition to the summoning of the Lord of Levin. Little is the solace bequeathed upon those who would abandon their homes in the Sylphlands and shun their frenzied brethren. Thus, it is only through fraternity that those sylphs may ultimately find solace, however little it may be.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162700:0:14"
msgid "\"To know the sylph, you must be the sylph. I may lack for wings, but a short climb will put me in a similar position. Lights dancing in the dark before me, I ponder what mischief I might make─er, were I a sylph, that is.\" Such were the scholar's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Чтобы понять сильфа, надо самому стать сильфом. Крыльев у меня нет, но стоит забраться повыше — и я уже почти как они. Смотрю, как во тьме танцуют огоньки, и думаю, какую бы пакость устроил... то есть, если бы был сильфом». Так говорил учёный. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 雷神「ラムウ」の召喚に反対するシルフ族の一派が、仮住まいとして築いた集落。実と枝を魔法によって変形させることで、奇妙な形状の住居を形作り、樹木から吊っている。飛行可能な種族らしく、ハシゴなどは一切ない
#. de: Hier ließen sich die Sylphen nieder, die sich der Beschwörung des Primae Ramuh widersetzen. Mit ihrer Magie verwandeln sie die Pflanzen des Waldes zu sehenswerten hängenden Behausungen.
#. fr: Ayant fui leurs semblables, les Sylphes qui vivent ici sont opposés à l'invocation du Primordial Ramuh. Grâce à leur magie, ces êtres volants savent modeler les végétaux pour créer d'étranges habitations suspendues aux arbres, bien à l'abri des dangers.
#. column 13: Little Solace
#. column 14: "To know the sylph, you must be the sylph. I may lack for wings, but a short climb will put me in a similar position. Lights dancing in the dark before me, I ponder what mischief I might make─er, were I a sylph, that is." Such were the scholar's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162700:0:15"
msgid "Little is the solace granted to those sylphs who would voice their opposition to the summoning of the Lord of Levin. Little is the solace bequeathed upon those who would abandon their homes in the Sylphlands and shun their frenzied brethren. Thus, it is only through fraternity that those sylphs may ultimately find solace, however little it may be."
msgstr "Сильфам, которые выступили против призыва Владыки Молний, не на кого опереться. Не легче и тем, кто бросил дома в Сильфских землях и отвернулся от обезумевших сородичей. Только в кругу друзей они могут найти хоть какое-то утешение."

#. ja: ロイヤルプロムナード
#. de: Herrscherpromenade
#. fr: Promenade royale
#. column 14: "Come morning, when my watch is over, I stand upon the three plates of silver depicting the first three of our kind. Paying reverence to those who came before us, I salute my sworn brothers who stand before me." Such were the Sultansworn's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: In times when the sultan had sole rule over the city<hyphen>state, the Promenade would serve as an ersatz waiting chamber for those petitioners who sought audience with His Resplendence in the Fragrant Chamber. Now, with power in the hands of the Syndicate, the round is empty, save for the occasional tryst betwixt young nobles.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162701:0:13"
msgid "Royal Promenade"
msgstr "Королевская аллея"

#. ja: ――ある近衛騎士が見た景色。\n長い夜警を終え、三騎士を示す3枚の銀盤の上に立つ。交代の同僚に敬礼を交わし、吹き抜けから見える青空を見つつ、眠るために宿舎に戻るのだ。
#. de: Nach ihrer anstrengenden Nachtschicht stellen die Palastwachen sich auf eine der drei silbernen Platten, grüßen ihre Ablösung mit einem Salut, erhaschen über sich noch einen Blick auf den morgenroten Himmel und eilen dann zu ihren Zimmern in der Herberge.
#. fr: Il n'est pas rare de voir des lève-tôt profiter d'un beau ciel dégagé pour visiter la ville. Certains s'amusent à se tenir sur une des trois plaques argentées au pied d'un certain escalier, et à imiter le salut des sentinelles qui font la relève. Ah, ces touristes...
#. column 13: Royal Promenade
#. column 15: In times when the sultan had sole rule over the city<hyphen>state, the Promenade would serve as an ersatz waiting chamber for those petitioners who sought audience with His Resplendence in the Fragrant Chamber. Now, with power in the hands of the Syndicate, the round is empty, save for the occasional tryst betwixt young nobles.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162701:0:14"
msgid "\"Come morning, when my watch is over, I stand upon the three plates of silver depicting the first three of our kind. Paying reverence to those who came before us, I salute my sworn brothers who stand before me.\" Such were the Sultansworn's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Утром, окончив дозор, я встаю на одну из трёх серебряных плит с изображениями первых трёх наших братьев. Отдаю дань тем, кто был до нас, и приветствую товарищей, стоящих передо мной». Так говорил рыцарь Султаны. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: ウルダハ政庁層に築かれた遊歩道。王宮に面しているため、近衛兵団「銀冑団」の騎士が警備に就いている。王権が強かった時代には、王族に謁見しようとする人々で賑わったが、今では富裕層が散歩に訪れる程度だという
#. de: Der Zugang zu Ul'dahs Regierungsviertel wird von der Palastwache streng bewacht. Einst warteten die treuen Anhänger des Sultanats hier geduldig auf Audienz, heute flaniert der Geldadel über die Promenade.
#. fr: L'allée du district politique d'Ul'dah qui permet d'accéder au palais de la famille royale. Les casques d'argent sont chargés de sa sur<shy>veil<shy>lan<shy>ce. À l'époque où le pouvoir des sultans était encore important, l'endroit était toujours animé par la présence des suppliants attendant une audience. De nos jours, il sert surtout de lieu de promenade aux riches seigneurs de la Cité.
#. column 13: Royal Promenade
#. column 14: "Come morning, when my watch is over, I stand upon the three plates of silver depicting the first three of our kind. Paying reverence to those who came before us, I salute my sworn brothers who stand before me." Such were the Sultansworn's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. macro: <hyphen> — a hyphen that does not break the line (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162701:0:15"
msgid "In times when the sultan had sole rule over the city<hyphen>state, the Promenade would serve as an ersatz waiting chamber for those petitioners who sought audience with His Resplendence in the Fragrant Chamber. Now, with power in the hands of the Syndicate, the round is empty, save for the occasional tryst betwixt young nobles."
msgstr "Когда султан правил городом<hyphen>государством единолично, аллея служила залом ожидания для просителей, добивавшихся аудиенции у Её Лучезарности в Благоуханной палате. Теперь власть принадлежит синдикату, и аллея пустует — разве что молодые аристократы иногда назначают здесь свидания."

#. ja: ゴールドコート
#. de: Platz der Sultana
#. fr: Cour dorée
#. column 14: "Even the strings of the tightest purse loosen upon seeing my famed balancing act. From vaulted gardens I leap onto the eastmost streetlamp, then bask as dour, cloudy expressions break into smiles and a shower of gil." Such were the acrobat's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: A large atrium in the heart of Ul'dah, the Gold Court's opulence and scale make it a popular meeting place for the city's elite. The plaza was once reserved for the sultan's private balls, but has since been opened to the public due to a lack of funds to maintain the majestic hanging fountain at her center.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162702:0:13"
msgid "The Gold Court"
msgstr "Золотой двор"

#. ja: ――ある軽業師が見た景色。\nケチな市民から投げ銭を得るには、雲を吹き飛ばすような芸が必須。吹き抜けの庭を跳び、東の街灯に華麗に飛び乗り、道行く奴らを見渡してやろう。
#. de: Wer den geizigen Ul'dahnern als Straßenkünstler ein paar Gil entlocken möchte, muss auffallen. Auf dem Podest vor der östlichen Laterne an diesem kühlen Platz haben Publikum und Künstler sich immer gut im Blick.
#. fr: Les jeunes d'aujourd'hui ne savent plus quoi inventer pour s'occuper les jours où la pluie menace. La dernière fureur est d'aller se percher sur des endroits incongrus. Le lampadaire à l'est de la fontaine est très apprécié des plus audacieux, qui aiment scruter les environs de haut.
#. column 13: The Gold Court
#. column 15: A large atrium in the heart of Ul'dah, the Gold Court's opulence and scale make it a popular meeting place for the city's elite. The plaza was once reserved for the sultan's private balls, but has since been opened to the public due to a lack of funds to maintain the majestic hanging fountain at her center.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162702:0:14"
msgid "\"Even the strings of the tightest purse loosen upon seeing my famed balancing act. From vaulted gardens I leap onto the eastmost streetlamp, then bask as dour, cloudy expressions break into smiles and a shower of gil.\" Such were the acrobat's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Даже у самых прижимистых кошельки развязываются, когда они видят мой знаменитый номер! Прыгаю из крытой галереи на самый восточный фонарь — и любуюсь, как хмурые лица расплываются в улыбках, а вокруг сыплются гилы». Так говорил акробат. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: ウルダハの中心地にある吹き抜けの方庭。噴水を配した美しい庭は、涼を求める市民の憩いの場となっている。かつてはウルダハ王家の舞踏会場だったが、近年の王室財政では維持が困難となったため、市民に譲渡された
#. de: Die kühlen Mauern und der Springbrunnen dieses Treppenaufgangs im Herzen Ul'dahs laden besonders in der Mittagshitze zum Verweilen ein. Zur Blütezeit des Sultanats wurden hier höfische Tänze aufgeführt.
#. fr: La magnifique fontaine de cette place au centre d'Ul'dah attire les citadins en quête d'un peu de fraîcheur durant les journées torrides. L'endroit était autrefois une salle de bal de la famille royale, mais son entretien étant devenu trop coûteux pour un trésor s'amenuisant d'année en année, il a été récemment cédé à la ville.
#. column 13: The Gold Court
#. column 14: "Even the strings of the tightest purse loosen upon seeing my famed balancing act. From vaulted gardens I leap onto the eastmost streetlamp, then bask as dour, cloudy expressions break into smiles and a shower of gil." Such were the acrobat's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162702:0:15"
msgid "A large atrium in the heart of Ul'dah, the Gold Court's opulence and scale make it a popular meeting place for the city's elite. The plaza was once reserved for the sultan's private balls, but has since been opened to the public due to a lack of funds to maintain the majestic hanging fountain at her center."
msgstr "Этот просторный атриум в самом сердце Ульды поражает размахом и роскошью, поэтому здесь любят встречаться сливки общества. Прежде площадь предназначалась для закрытых балов султаны, но дворец больше не мог содержать великолепный подвесной фонтан в её центре и открыл сад для горожан."

#. ja: 交易都市「ウルダハ」
#. de: Ul'dah
#. fr: Ul'dah
#. column 14: "From a vantage point high above Nophica's Wells, I looked out upon Ul'dah in all its glory─truly a jewel in the desert, shining brighter than a sea of stars." Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as she saw.
#. column 15: The commercial hub of Ul'dah is organized strategically around the dome-shaped citadel at its center. Its towering fortifications and protective outer walls bedighted with myriad glass panes and colorful mosaics are visible for malms in all directions, and serve as a stark yet dazzling deterrent to would-be besiegers.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162703:0:13"
msgid "The Jewel of the Desert"
msgstr "Жемчужина пустыни"

#. ja: ――ある冒険者が見た景色。\nノフィカの井戸の足場の上から、砂都を見渡してみろ。そうすりゃ、星空にも勝るほど、まばゆく輝く「荒野の宝石」が見えるだろう。
#. de: Von der Spitze des Baugerüsts an Nophicas Brunnen bietet sich Abenteurern ein imposanter Anblick. Inmitten der Wüste glänzt die Perle der Wüste mit den Sternen am Nachthimmel um die Wette.
#. fr: Le "joyau du désert" est une vision magique la nuit. La lumière des étoiles pâlit devant la sienne. Le meilleur point de vue pour l'admirer serait en haut de l'échafaudage des sources de Nophica.
#. column 13: The Jewel of the Desert
#. column 15: The commercial hub of Ul'dah is organized strategically around the dome-shaped citadel at its center. Its towering fortifications and protective outer walls bedighted with myriad glass panes and colorful mosaics are visible for malms in all directions, and serve as a stark yet dazzling deterrent to would-be besiegers.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162703:0:14"
msgid "\"From a vantage point high above Nophica's Wells, I looked out upon Ul'dah in all its glory─truly a jewel in the desert, shining brighter than a sea of stars.\" Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as she saw."
msgstr "«Поднимись высоко над Источниками Нофики и взгляни на Ульду во всём её великолепии. Настоящая жемчужина пустыни — сияет ярче целого моря звёзд!» Так говорил искатель приключений. Я решил взглянуть на всё её глазами."

#. ja: 荒涼とした砂漠地帯ザナラーンにそびえる交易都市。高い城壁の向こうにドーム状屋根を持つ建物が林立する姿は、旅疲れた者には輝いて見えることだろう。その内側に富が溢れることもあり、「荒野の宝石」と呼ばれる
#. de: Das ul'dhische Handelszentrum ist konzentrisch um die kuppelförmige Zitadelle angelegt. Die hohen Mauern und Türme der Stadt, die von Myriaden bunter Fenster und Mosaike geziert werden, sind malmenweit zu sehen und flößen Ehrfurcht ein.
#. fr: La capitale marchande qui se dresse dans les terres désolées du Thanalan. Protégée par de hauts murs, seuls les plus grands bâtiments sont visibles de loin. Parce que leurs dômes brillent de mille feux sous la lumière du soleil, et que la ville regorge de richesses, elle est surnommée le joyau du désert.
#. column 13: The Jewel of the Desert
#. column 14: "From a vantage point high above Nophica's Wells, I looked out upon Ul'dah in all its glory─truly a jewel in the desert, shining brighter than a sea of stars." Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as she saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162703:0:15"
msgid "The commercial hub of Ul'dah is organized strategically around the dome-shaped citadel at its center. Its towering fortifications and protective outer walls bedighted with myriad glass panes and colorful mosaics are visible for malms in all directions, and serve as a stark yet dazzling deterrent to would-be besiegers."
msgstr "Торговый центр Ульды построен вокруг куполообразной цитадели. Высокие укрепления и наружные стены, украшенные множеством стеклянных вставок и яркими мозаиками, видны за многие мальмы. Их величественный, ослепительный вид должен отбить охоту осаждать город."

#. ja: シラディハ遺跡
#. de: Sil'dih-Ruinen
#. fr: Vestiges de Sil'dih
#. column 14: "The fog was so thick you could cut it with a blade. My foot slipped, and in an eyeblink I was sprawled out on a cliff, the ruins of a buried city before me. Sadly, the stinging pain in my arse detracted somewhat from my enjoyment of the scenery." Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: The city<hyphen>states of Ul'dah and Sil'dih coexisted for generations until four hundred years ago when bad blood festering betwixt the two sultanates culminated in the War of the Sisters─leaving Sil'dih a smoldering pile of rubble to be claimed by the shifting desert sands. The subsequent relocation of Ul'dah placed the city<hyphen>state nearly directly above her fallen sibling.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162704:0:13"
msgid "The Ruins of Sil'dih"
msgstr "Руины Сильдиха"

#. ja: ――ある冒険者が見た景色。\n想定外の霧で道に迷い、脚を滑らせ崖をずり落ちたとき、眼前に現れたのは亡国の残滓。いささか肝を冷やしたよ。
#. de: Als eine Abenteurerin einst in dichtem Nebel vom Wege abkam und einen Steilhang hinunterrutschte, fand sie sich unerwartet vor den Ruinen der verlorenen Stadt wieder. Vor Schreck wäre ihr fast das Herz in die Hose gerutscht.
#. fr: Un voyageur a raconté qu'il a failli perdre la vie en tombant d'une falaise à cause d'un brouillard matinal. Un rebord plus bas l'a heureusement sauvé, et une fois sa frayeur passée, il a pu admirer les ruines d'une Cité disparue.
#. column 13: The Ruins of Sil'dih
#. column 15: The city<hyphen>states of Ul'dah and Sil'dih coexisted for generations until four hundred years ago when bad blood festering betwixt the two sultanates culminated in the War of the Sisters─leaving Sil'dih a smoldering pile of rubble to be claimed by the shifting desert sands. The subsequent relocation of Ul'dah placed the city<hyphen>state nearly directly above her fallen sibling.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162704:0:14"
msgid "\"The fog was so thick you could cut it with a blade. My foot slipped, and in an eyeblink I was sprawled out on a cliff, the ruins of a buried city before me. Sadly, the stinging pain in my arse detracted somewhat from my enjoyment of the scenery.\" Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Туман был такой густой, хоть ножом режь. Подвернулась нога — и в мгновение ока я уже распластался на скале, а передо мной лежит погребённый город. Жаль только, задница так болела, что любоваться видом было трудновато». Так говорил искатель приключений. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 古都「シラディハ」の遺跡。約400年前にウルダハとの戦争に敗れたことで滅亡し、100年ほど経過するうちに砂に埋もれてしまった。その後、ウルダハが現在の位置へ遷都した結果、今では両者の一部が重なっている
#. de: Vor 400 Jahren wurde die Sultansstadt Sil'dih im „Krieg der Schwestern“ von Ul'dah vernichtet und fast vollständig vom Sand verschluckt. Das heutige Ul'dah steht teilweise auf ihren Ruinen.
#. fr: Les ruines de l'ancienne Cité de Sil'dih. Elle a été détruite par les Uldiens il y a quatre cents ans à l'issue d'une longue guerre, et en l'espace d'un siècle a été presque entièrement ensevelie par le sable du Thanalan. L'emplacement actuel d'Ul'dah empiète partiellement sur celui de Sil'dih.
#. column 13: The Ruins of Sil'dih
#. column 14: "The fog was so thick you could cut it with a blade. My foot slipped, and in an eyeblink I was sprawled out on a cliff, the ruins of a buried city before me. Sadly, the stinging pain in my arse detracted somewhat from my enjoyment of the scenery." Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. macro: <hyphen> — a hyphen that does not break the line (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162704:0:15"
msgid "The city<hyphen>states of Ul'dah and Sil'dih coexisted for generations until four hundred years ago when bad blood festering betwixt the two sultanates culminated in the War of the Sisters─leaving Sil'dih a smoldering pile of rubble to be claimed by the shifting desert sands. The subsequent relocation of Ul'dah placed the city<hyphen>state nearly directly above her fallen sibling."
msgstr "Города-государства Ульда и Сильдих мирно сосуществовали поколениями, пока четыре сотни лет назад давняя вражда между султанатами не вылилась в Войну сестёр. Сильдих превратился в дымящиеся руины, которые постепенно поглотили пески. Позже Ульду перенесли почти прямо над павшим городом-сестрой."

#. ja: グゥーブーの骸
#. de: Versteinerte Goobbue
#. fr: Le géant solitaire
#. column 14: "Merciful are the rains that fall, for they give succor to the thirsting land, and comfort the old wounds of one who journeyed too far from home." Such were the botanist's words, and I would see as she saw.
#. column 15: Local legend claims the Lonely Giant is everything from the ghost of a Sil'dihn sultan, to the prototype for a new model of Garlean machina. Ul'dahn scholars, however, simply believe him a Coerthan goobbue who lost his bearings during the chaos of the Calamity, and after a long journey through the Black Shroud, died of exhaustion upon reaching Thanalan.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162705:0:13"
msgid "The Lonely Giant"
msgstr "Одинокий гигант"

#. ja: ――ある園芸師が見た景色。\n渇きし大地に降り注ぐ慈雨は、美しき花々を咲き誇らせていた。まるで、座した骸を慰めるかのように。
#. de: Der Regen, der den trockenen Wüstenboden benetzt, lässt bunte Blumen sprießen. Fast scheint es, als wollten sie der versteinerten Gestalt, die hier ihre letzte Ruhestätte gefunden hat, Trost spenden.
#. fr: Les voyageurs qui s'abritent de la pluie dans un petit bosquet sont souvent touchés par la vision du corps sans vie d'un géant moussu. Il semble si seul lorsque la nuit approche. On aurait presque envie de le consoler...
#. column 13: The Lonely Giant
#. column 15: Local legend claims the Lonely Giant is everything from the ghost of a Sil'dihn sultan, to the prototype for a new model of Garlean machina. Ul'dahn scholars, however, simply believe him a Coerthan goobbue who lost his bearings during the chaos of the Calamity, and after a long journey through the Black Shroud, died of exhaustion upon reaching Thanalan.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162705:0:14"
msgid "\"Merciful are the rains that fall, for they give succor to the thirsting land, and comfort the old wounds of one who journeyed too far from home.\" Such were the botanist's words, and I would see as she saw."
msgstr "«Дожди милосердны: они поят иссохшую землю и врачуют старые раны того, кто забрёл слишком далеко от дома». Так говорил ботаник. Я решила взглянуть на всё её глазами."

#. ja: グゥーブーの骸の周囲に珍しい草花が繁茂する場所。霊災時にパニックに陥ったグゥーブーがクルザスより下山し、ここで力尽きたものと思われる。おそらく黒衣森を抜ける際に、様々な種子を付着させ運んできたのだろう
#. de: Der Geist eines sil'dhischen Sultans oder doch garleisches Kriegsgerät? Um den einsamen Giganten ranken sich viele Mythen. Vermutlich floh die Goobbue während einer Katastrophe aus Coerthas und starb nach dem langen Marsch durch den Finsterwald erschöpft in Thanalan.
#. fr: Les Uldiens pensent que ce goobbue du Coerthas a dû fuir paniqué lors du septième fléau, et a fini par mourir d'épuisement peu après avoir atteint le Thanalan. Cela ex<shy>pli<shy>que<shy>rait l'abondance de végétation originaire de Sombrelinceul ayant poussé près du cadavre<nbsp>: de nombreuses graines se sont pro<shy>ba<shy>ble<shy>ment accrochées à lui durant son passage dans la forêt.
#. column 13: The Lonely Giant
#. column 14: "Merciful are the rains that fall, for they give succor to the thirsting land, and comfort the old wounds of one who journeyed too far from home." Such were the botanist's words, and I would see as she saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162705:0:15"
msgid "Local legend claims the Lonely Giant is everything from the ghost of a Sil'dihn sultan, to the prototype for a new model of Garlean machina. Ul'dahn scholars, however, simply believe him a Coerthan goobbue who lost his bearings during the chaos of the Calamity, and after a long journey through the Black Shroud, died of exhaustion upon reaching Thanalan."
msgstr "Местные легенды называют Одинокого гиганта то призраком султана Сильдиха, то прототипом новой гарлеанской машины. Учёные из Ульды считают, что это коэртасский гооббу, сбившийся с пути во время Бедствия. Он прошёл через Чёрный Плющ, но, добравшись до Таналана, умер от изнеможения."

#. ja: 見えざる都
#. de: Die Unsichtbare Stadt
#. fr: La Cité invisible
#. column 14: "As I felled my quarry atop a great stone slab, my eyes drifted up to a city swallowed by the clouds and the mountain itself. I know not who once called it home, nor why it fell, but it was a sight to behold." Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Buried under nearly a malm of solid rock, if not for a gaping rent torn open by the Calamity, these ancient ruins may have gone undiscovered for another thousand summers. Scholars sent to Highbridge to study the site are currently of a mind that the structures are not a city, but in fact the tomb of one Lalafuto IV, famed sultan of Belah'dia.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162706:0:13"
msgid "The Invisible City"
msgstr "Невидимый город"

#. ja: ――ある冒険者が見た景色。\n討伐任務を終え、崩れ去った建物の上に立ち、ふと見上げると、そこには垂れ込める雲の下、岩から顔を出す遺跡が見えた。
#. de: Nach siegreichem Kampf ließ ein Abenteurer sich auf den Trümmern einer Stadt nieder. Als er aufblickte, ragte unter dem wolkenverhangenen Himmel ihr Gesicht hervor und war nicht länger unsichtbar.
#. fr: Certains aventuriers n'ayant pas peur des hauteurs recommandent d'admirer le matin les ruines d'une antique Cité, du haut d'un morceau de route brisé. La vue en vaudrait la peine d'après eux, même par temps couvert.
#. column 13: The Invisible City
#. column 15: Buried under nearly a malm of solid rock, if not for a gaping rent torn open by the Calamity, these ancient ruins may have gone undiscovered for another thousand summers. Scholars sent to Highbridge to study the site are currently of a mind that the structures are not a city, but in fact the tomb of one Lalafuto IV, famed sultan of Belah'dia.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162706:0:14"
msgid "\"As I felled my quarry atop a great stone slab, my eyes drifted up to a city swallowed by the clouds and the mountain itself. I know not who once called it home, nor why it fell, but it was a sight to behold.\" Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Я добил добычу на огромной каменной плите и поднял глаза. Надо мной, в облаках и недрах горы, проступал город. Не знаю, кто там жил и отчего он пал, но зрелище было незабываемое». Так говорил искатель приключений. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: バーニングウォールへのダラガブ片の落着は、地殻に巨大な裂け目を作りだした。そこから姿を現したのが、この壮麗な遺跡である。最新の研究によると、ベラフディア中期タタメフI世の宮殿ではないかと考えられている
#. de: Die Wucht des Aufpralls von Dalamud-Bruchstücken auf den Feuerwall legte auch diese prächtige Ruine frei. Forschern zufolge könnte es sich bei ihr um das Grab von Lalafuto I. handeln, einem belah'dischen Sultan.
#. fr: La chute de morceaux de Dalamud au Mur incandescent a créé une énorme crevasse, révélant des vestiges majestueux. Des recherches ont bien entendu été menées et les historiens pensent qu'il s'agirait de la tombe de Lalafuto IV, dirigeant de l'ancienne cité de Belah'dia.
#. column 13: The Invisible City
#. column 14: "As I felled my quarry atop a great stone slab, my eyes drifted up to a city swallowed by the clouds and the mountain itself. I know not who once called it home, nor why it fell, but it was a sight to behold." Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162706:0:15"
msgid "Buried under nearly a malm of solid rock, if not for a gaping rent torn open by the Calamity, these ancient ruins may have gone undiscovered for another thousand summers. Scholars sent to Highbridge to study the site are currently of a mind that the structures are not a city, but in fact the tomb of one Lalafuto IV, famed sultan of Belah'dia."
msgstr "Если бы Бедствие не раскололо землю, эти древние руины так и остались бы погребёнными под толщей камня почти в малм — возможно, ещё тысячу лет. Учёные, отправленные в Высокий мост исследовать развалины, считают, что это не город, а гробница Лалафуто IV, прославленного султана Белах'дии."

#. ja: ハイブリッジ
#. de: Hohenbrück
#. fr: Le Viaduc
#. column 14: "En route from Ul'dah to Gridania, I sought lodgings at Highbridge. Setting out at first light, I looked out upon the wise men of old─at least they looked wiser than me─and asked for guidance in my travels." Such were the merchant's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: After the Calamity rent eastern Thanalan asunder, one of the first projects commissioned by the Syndicate was the construction of a bridge to span the newly formed chasm and restore the trade route with lands transpontine. The city which has sprung up along its edges is populated almost solely by scholars investigating the nearby ruins of the Invisible City.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162707:0:13"
msgid "Highbridge"
msgstr "Высокий мост"

#. ja: ――ある商人が見た景色。\n砂都から森都へ向かう道中、石橋で一泊。翌日、朝日を受けた古の王たちは、実に荘厳であった。
#. de: Händler auf dem Weg von Thanalan zum Finsterwald rasten gerne an dieser Brücke. Der Blick auf die gewaltigen Könige im roten Licht der Morgensonne ist die Übernachtung in der Tat mehr als wert.
#. fr: Quand le temps est clair, rien de tel qu'une petite prière au bout d'une passerelle surplombant une crevasse sans fond pour bien commencer la journée !
#. column 13: Highbridge
#. column 15: After the Calamity rent eastern Thanalan asunder, one of the first projects commissioned by the Syndicate was the construction of a bridge to span the newly formed chasm and restore the trade route with lands transpontine. The city which has sprung up along its edges is populated almost solely by scholars investigating the nearby ruins of the Invisible City.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162707:0:14"
msgid "\"En route from Ul'dah to Gridania, I sought lodgings at Highbridge. Setting out at first light, I looked out upon the wise men of old─at least they looked wiser than me─and asked for guidance in my travels.\" Such were the merchant's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«По дороге из Ульды в Гриданию я остановился на ночлег в Высоком мосту. На рассвете отправился дальше и увидел мудрецов древности — во всяком случае, они выглядели мудрее меня, — а затем попросил их наставить меня в пути». Так говорил торговец. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: ザナラーンと黒衣森とを行き来するために作られた石橋。グリダニアとの重要な交易路であるため、銅刃団オーキッド連隊傘下の防衛部隊が駐屯している。また、「見えざる都」の学術調査を行う者たちのベース地でもある
#. de: Eine gewaltige Steinbrücke verbindet Thanalan mit dem Finsterwald. Die Orchideenkompanie der Messingklingen wacht über den Handelsplatz, der auch Basis für die Erforschung der Unsichtbaren Stadt ist.
#. fr: Ce pont a été construit afin de relier le Thanalan à la forêt de Sombrelinceul. Comme il s'agit d'une route commerciale essentielle entre Gridania et Ul'dah, le régiment de l'Orchidée des lames de cuivre y est stationné en permanence. Les archéologues étudiant les ruines de la Cité invisible ont également un camp à proximité.
#. column 13: Highbridge
#. column 14: "En route from Ul'dah to Gridania, I sought lodgings at Highbridge. Setting out at first light, I looked out upon the wise men of old─at least they looked wiser than me─and asked for guidance in my travels." Such were the merchant's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162707:0:15"
msgid "After the Calamity rent eastern Thanalan asunder, one of the first projects commissioned by the Syndicate was the construction of a bridge to span the newly formed chasm and restore the trade route with lands transpontine. The city which has sprung up along its edges is populated almost solely by scholars investigating the nearby ruins of the Invisible City."
msgstr "После того как Бедствие раскололо восточный Таналан, синдикат одним из первых дел распорядился построить мост через образовавшуюся пропасть и восстановить торговый путь в дальние земли. По краям моста вырос городок, где почти все жители — учёные, исследующие соседние руины Невидимого города."

#. ja: ささやきの谷
#. de: Flüsterklamm
#. fr: Canyon des Chuchotements
#. column 14: "Don't tell Baderon, but if ye ask me, ye'll find no better place to down a flagon of ale than where the water dances, keepin' ye cool on even the 'ottest summer's day." Such were the laborer's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Little more than a shallow valley but five years past, Woad Whisper Canyon was carved into a gaping gorge in a matter of moons after the Calamity drained Bronze Lake and dramatically altered the course of the Nym River. On hot days, laborers from both Summerford Farms and the Skylift will oft take respite in the cool mists of the falls...if not met by bandits.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162708:0:13"
msgid "Woad Whisper Canyon"
msgstr "Каньон Шёпота Уада"

#. ja: ――ある農夫から聞いた噂。\n取っておきの酒盛り場。常に水しぶきが舞い、太陽が照っても涼しいらしい。
#. de: Geheimtipp unter den Feldarbeitern: Nicht etwa eine Taverne, sondern hier sei der beste Ort, um sich - allein oder in geselliger Runde - eine Erfrischung zu gönnen. Die Dunstschleier schirmen die Hitze selbst an heißen Sommertagen ab.
#. fr: Le soleil rayonne parfois fort sur la Noscea centrale, mais les paysans locaux connaissent un endroit à l'ombre où se désaltérer en observant l'eau tomber.
#. column 13: Woad Whisper Canyon
#. column 15: Little more than a shallow valley but five years past, Woad Whisper Canyon was carved into a gaping gorge in a matter of moons after the Calamity drained Bronze Lake and dramatically altered the course of the Nym River. On hot days, laborers from both Summerford Farms and the Skylift will oft take respite in the cool mists of the falls...if not met by bandits.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162708:0:14"
msgid "\"Don't tell Baderon, but if ye ask me, ye'll find no better place to down a flagon of ale than where the water dances, keepin' ye cool on even the 'ottest summer's day.\" Such were the laborer's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Бадерону ни слова, но лучше места, чтобы опрокинуть кружечку эля, не сыскать. Вода пляшет, и даже в самую жару тут прохладно». Так говорил рабочий. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: オ・ゴモロ方面から流れる「ニーム川」の浸食によって作られた渓谷。幾筋もの細い滝が、ささやき声のような涼やかな水音を奏でている。谷が日射しを遮るため、酒盛りにぴったりの避暑地として地元民に愛されている
#. de: Vom in O'Ghomoro entspringenden Nym ins karge Gestein eingeschnitten entstand diese Schlucht mit ihren zahlreichen Wasserfällen, nachdem die Katastrophe den Fluss in neue Bahnen gezwungen hatte. Eine kühle Zuflucht vor der glühenden Sommerhitze.
#. fr: Prenant sa source près du volcan d'O'Ghomoro, la rivière de Nym a creusé cette gorge au cours du temps. Le doux murmure des nombreuses chutes d'eau et l'abri que prodigue cet endroit contre le soleil en font le lieu préféré des Limséens pour boire au frais.
#. column 13: Woad Whisper Canyon
#. column 14: "Don't tell Baderon, but if ye ask me, ye'll find no better place to down a flagon of ale than where the water dances, keepin' ye cool on even the 'ottest summer's day." Such were the laborer's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162708:0:15"
msgid "Little more than a shallow valley but five years past, Woad Whisper Canyon was carved into a gaping gorge in a matter of moons after the Calamity drained Bronze Lake and dramatically altered the course of the Nym River. On hot days, laborers from both Summerford Farms and the Skylift will oft take respite in the cool mists of the falls...if not met by bandits."
msgstr "Когда-то здесь была всего лишь неглубокая долина. Но после Бедствия воды Бронзового озера ушли, а русло реки Ним резко изменилось — за несколько месяцев образовался огромный каньон. В жаркие дни рабочие с ферм Саммерфорда и Небесного подъёмника приходят сюда передохнуть в прохладной дымке водопадов... если их не опередят разбойники."

#. ja: サマーフォード庄
#. de: Sommerfurt-Höfe
#. fr: Vergers d'Estival
#. column 14: Overheard at a tavern: "Erstwhile pirates taken to land, drunk on ale and tales of wenches and plunder, climb atop lamps as if they were manning the crow's nest of a great vessel..."
#. column 15: When Merlwyb Bloefhiswyn rose to Admiral, one of her first decrees included the clearing of large swaths of land for new Lominsan settlements. Summerford Farms and its expansive orange groves is one of those locations─its name is derived from the man-made crossings required when late spring runoff from Mt. O'Ghomoro causes the Rogue River to swell.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162709:0:13"
msgid "Summerford Farms"
msgstr "Фермы Саммерфорда"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\n元海賊は酒が入れば喧嘩を始める。ランプの上に登って高みの見物を決め込むのがいい。
#. de: Wie man ehemalige Piraten von ehrbaren Arbeitern unterscheidet? Ein Honigwein, und alle Manieren sind vergessen! Da sollte man die Lage lieber von Anfang an aus sicherer Höhe beobachten: von der Lampe aus.
#. fr: Être maraîcher n'a rien de palpitant quand on a vécu le sabre au clair, même si on peut utiliser une lampe en guise de nid-de-corbeau pour faire la vigie dans une salle.
#. column 13: Summerford Farms
#. column 15: When Merlwyb Bloefhiswyn rose to Admiral, one of her first decrees included the clearing of large swaths of land for new Lominsan settlements. Summerford Farms and its expansive orange groves is one of those locations─its name is derived from the man-made crossings required when late spring runoff from Mt. O'Ghomoro causes the Rogue River to swell.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162709:0:14"
msgid "Overheard at a tavern: \"Erstwhile pirates taken to land, drunk on ale and tales of wenches and plunder, climb atop lamps as if they were manning the crow's nest of a great vessel...\""
msgstr "Услышано в таверне: «Пираты, перебравшиеся на сушу, хлебнут эля да заведут истории про девиц и добычу. А после забираются на фонари, будто стоят на марсе большого корабля...»"

#. ja: メルウィブ提督が進める入植政策によって拓かれた集落。陸に上がった元海賊と、ベテラン農夫たちが協力して開拓を進めている。「ローグ川」がもたらす豊かな真水の恩恵を得て、ラノシアオレンジの栽培に成功したようだ
#. de: Im Zuge der Besiedlungspolitik Merlwybs erschlossen und nun von ehemaligen Piraten und erfahrenen Bauern (zumeist) in Eintracht bestellt. Prächtige La Noscea-Orangen zeugen von der Fruchtbarkeit des Bodens.
#. fr: Cette plantation, où collaborent anciens pirates et maraîchers de métier, a été créée dans le cadre de la politique de développement du territoire de l'amirale Bloefhiswyn. La rivière des requins en fait une terre propice à la culture des oranges noscéennes.
#. column 13: Summerford Farms
#. column 14: Overheard at a tavern: "Erstwhile pirates taken to land, drunk on ale and tales of wenches and plunder, climb atop lamps as if they were manning the crow's nest of a great vessel..."
msgctxt "Adventure:2162709:0:15"
msgid "When Merlwyb Bloefhiswyn rose to Admiral, one of her first decrees included the clearing of large swaths of land for new Lominsan settlements. Summerford Farms and its expansive orange groves is one of those locations─its name is derived from the man-made crossings required when late spring runoff from Mt. O'Ghomoro causes the Rogue River to swell."
msgstr "После того как Мервиб Блуфисвин стала адмиралом, одним из её первых указов стало расчистить большие участки земли для новых поселений Лимсы Ломинсы. Фермы Саммерфорда с обширными апельсиновыми рощами — одно из таких мест. Их название связано с рукотворными переправами: в конце весны талые воды с горы О'Гоморо разливают реку Разбойников."

#. ja: グレイフリート風車群
#. de: Die Graue Flotte
#. fr: Flotte grise
#. column 14: "I took refuge inside to get away from the rain. To my ill fortune, the beastmen had the same idea. Quickly, I climbed to the roof and plotted a course of escape. Quite a view, though staying alive was a far more pressing concern at the time." Such were the merchant's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Sitting high atop Widow Cliffs on the southeastern coast of Vylbrand, the Grey Fleet was built to harness the constant southerly winds funneled down through the Strait of Merlthor, and use them to power the many mills which grind the region's wheat and full its wool.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162710:0:13"
msgid "The Grey Fleet"
msgstr "Серая флотилия"

#. ja: ――ある商人から聞いた噂。\n雨宿りのために駆け込んだ建物に、蛮族がやって来た。慌てて屋根の上に登って、逃げ道を探したらしい。
#. de: Als ein Händler, der dort nachmittags vor Regen Zuflucht suchte, von Räubern überfallen wurde, flüchtete er aufs Dach und sah sich verzweifelt nach einem Fluchtweg um.
#. fr: Alors qu'il allait à la métairie du Coq rouge, un marchand tomba nez à nez avec des Kobolds. Fuyant à toutes jambes, il réussit à leur échapper en se réfugiant en haut d'une cabane. Seul sous la pluie, il resta un long moment à scruter l'horizon.
#. column 13: The Grey Fleet
#. column 15: Sitting high atop Widow Cliffs on the southeastern coast of Vylbrand, the Grey Fleet was built to harness the constant southerly winds funneled down through the Strait of Merlthor, and use them to power the many mills which grind the region's wheat and full its wool.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162710:0:14"
msgid "\"I took refuge inside to get away from the rain. To my ill fortune, the beastmen had the same idea. Quickly, I climbed to the roof and plotted a course of escape. Quite a view, though staying alive was a far more pressing concern at the time.\" Such were the merchant's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Забрался внутрь переждать дождь. Не повезло: зверолюди тоже решили укрыться там. Я мигом взобрался на крышу и стал искать путь к отступлению. Вид, конечно, отличный, да только тогда меня больше волновало, как бы остаться в живых». Так говорил торговец. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: レッドルースター農場で生産された小麦を挽いたり、羊毛を縮絨したりするために作られた風車。羽根車に帆船用の帆布を利用しているため、多くの風車が並ぶ姿を艦隊になぞらえ、「グレイフリート風車群」と呼ぶ
#. de: Mithilfe der Windmühlen wird das Korn der Gockelburg-Felder gemahlen und Schafswolle zu Filz gewalkt. Ihre mit kräftigem Segeltuch bespannten Flügel lassen sie im Dämmerlicht wie Schiffe erscheinen.
#. fr: Les moulins de ce site ont été construits pour moudre le blé et carder la laine produits à la métairie du Coq rouge. Vus de loin, ces bâtiments de pierre dont les ailes proviennent des voiles d'un navire s'apparentent à une imposante armada<nbsp>; d'où leur surnom de “Flotte grise”.
#. column 13: The Grey Fleet
#. column 14: "I took refuge inside to get away from the rain. To my ill fortune, the beastmen had the same idea. Quickly, I climbed to the roof and plotted a course of escape. Quite a view, though staying alive was a far more pressing concern at the time." Such were the merchant's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162710:0:15"
msgid "Sitting high atop Widow Cliffs on the southeastern coast of Vylbrand, the Grey Fleet was built to harness the constant southerly winds funneled down through the Strait of Merlthor, and use them to power the many mills which grind the region's wheat and full its wool."
msgstr "Высоко на скалах Вдовы, у юго-восточного побережья Вилбрандта, стоит Серая флотилия. Её построили, чтобы использовать постоянные южные ветра, которые приносит пролив Мерлтор. Ветряки здесь мелют пшеницу и валяют шерсть со всей округи."

#. ja: 隠れ滝
#. de: Verborgener Wasserfall
#. fr: Chute cachée
#. column 14: "The ogling from the men as they recline burns brighter than the summer sun. I don't mind much, provided they're handsome...and wealthy doesn't hurt either." Such were the young lady's words, and I would see as she saw.
#. column 15: Sheltered on three sides by towering cliffs, Hidden Falls can be found several score yalms upstream from where the Agelyss River empties into the Strait of Merlthor. Taken by its beauty, Ul'dahn plutocrat Gegeruju was quick to purchase the land and construct a stage upon which private performances for the magnate's favored clients are held.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162711:0:13"
msgid "Hidden Falls"
msgstr "Скрытый водопад"

#. ja: ――ある女性から聞いた噂。\n椅子に腰を下ろした客から注がれる視線は、照りつける太陽よりも熱いとのこと。
#. de: Ob ihr die Blicke derjenigen, die es sich hinter ihr bequem gemacht haben, nicht im Rücken brennen würden? - „Doch, schon ...“ (Aber der Blick aufs sanft wogende Meer entschädigt für vieles.)
#. fr: Fût-ce même pour une jolie danseuse, les regards insistants des hommes sont troublants, mais s'asseoir sous le soleil pour regarder la cascade redonne toujours du courage.
#. column 13: Hidden Falls
#. column 15: Sheltered on three sides by towering cliffs, Hidden Falls can be found several score yalms upstream from where the Agelyss River empties into the Strait of Merlthor. Taken by its beauty, Ul'dahn plutocrat Gegeruju was quick to purchase the land and construct a stage upon which private performances for the magnate's favored clients are held.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162711:0:14"
msgid "\"The ogling from the men as they recline burns brighter than the summer sun. I don't mind much, provided they're handsome...and wealthy doesn't hurt either.\" Such were the young lady's words, and I would see as she saw."
msgstr "«Мужчины развалятся в креслах и глаз с меня не сводят — взгляд жжёт ярче летнего солнца. Я не против, если красавчики... а богатство им тоже не повредит». Так говорила девушка. Я решила взглянуть на всё её глазами."

#. ja: 「アジェレス川」が作りだした滝。滝壺がある小さな浜辺には、富豪ゲゲルジュ氏が特別なゲストのために用意した宿泊施設が存在している。専属の踊り子たちによる、特別な接待が行われているとかいないとか
#. de: Vor dem Hintergrund des als Wasserfall herabstürzenden Agelyss ließ der vermögende Gegeruju eine Ferienanlage für handverlesene Gäste errichten, die nicht zuletzt wegen ihrer bildschönen Tänzerinnen gerühmt wird.
#. fr: Située à l'estuaire de la rivière d'Agelyss, cette chute donne naissance à un bassin où le seigneur Gegeruju a fait bâtir une cabane sur pilotis pour ses invités de marque. Les danseuses qui travaillent là leur prodigueraient toutes sortes de services spéciaux.
#. column 13: Hidden Falls
#. column 14: "The ogling from the men as they recline burns brighter than the summer sun. I don't mind much, provided they're handsome...and wealthy doesn't hurt either." Such were the young lady's words, and I would see as she saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162711:0:15"
msgid "Sheltered on three sides by towering cliffs, Hidden Falls can be found several score yalms upstream from where the Agelyss River empties into the Strait of Merlthor. Taken by its beauty, Ul'dahn plutocrat Gegeruju was quick to purchase the land and construct a stage upon which private performances for the magnate's favored clients are held."
msgstr "Со всех сторон Скрытый водопад обступают высокие скалы. Он находится в нескольких десятках ялмов выше места, где река Агелисс впадает в пролив Мерлтор. Красота этих мест так впечатлила ульданского богача Гегеруджу, что он поспешил выкупить землю и построить сцену для закрытых представлений перед избранными гостями."

#. ja: 白鴎塔
#. de: Sturmvogelturm
#. fr: Tour de la Mouette
#. column 14: "The rains may cloud our view, but they won't stop those who would invade our shores. And so we climb high, scouring the horizon for any sign of danger." Such were the lookout's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: One of three beacons built along the La Noscean coast in the Sixth Astral Era, Gullperch Tower is the easternmost─warning ships navigating the Strait of Merlthor of its deadly shallows, while also serving as a watchtower for pirate and Sahagin raids on Bloodshore.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162712:0:13"
msgid "Gullperch Tower"
msgstr "Башня Чайки"

#. ja: ――ある傭兵から聞いた噂。\n雨天時は見通しが悪くなる。だから、海からの脅威を警戒するには、高所から見張るのが一番だ。
#. de: Unwetter auf See rauben die Sicht und können auch großen Schiffen zum Verhängnis werden. Umso schwerer lastet die Verantwortung auf seinen Schultern, denn seine Warnzeichen von höchster Warte lotsen verlässlich auf sicheren Kurs.
#. fr: Les soldats du Maelstrom savent bien qu'il vaut mieux être haut perché pour apercevoir la moindre menace, notamment par mauvais temps.
#. column 13: Gullperch Tower
#. column 15: One of three beacons built along the La Noscean coast in the Sixth Astral Era, Gullperch Tower is the easternmost─warning ships navigating the Strait of Merlthor of its deadly shallows, while also serving as a watchtower for pirate and Sahagin raids on Bloodshore.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162712:0:14"
msgid "\"The rains may cloud our view, but they won't stop those who would invade our shores. And so we climb high, scouring the horizon for any sign of danger.\" Such were the lookout's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Дождь застилает обзор, но захватчиков он не остановит. Потому и забираемся повыше, чтобы высматривать опасность на горизонте». Так говорил дозорный. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: ラノシア特有の白い火山岩で作られた小塔。近海を航行する船に、水深が低いことを知らせる灯台であると同時に、サハギン族や海賊を見張るための監視塔でもある。近隣にカモメが多く生息するため、その名がつけられた
#. de: Ein aus dem weißen Vulkangestein La Nosceas errichteter Leuchtturm. Er warnt passierende Schiffe vor den Untiefen und die Küstenbevölkerung vor nahenden Piraten und Sahagin-Scharen.
#. fr: Cette tour bâtie avec de la roche volcanique typique de la Noscea sert à la fois de phare, indiquant la présence de récifs aux navires, et de poste de guet contre les pirates et les Sahuagins. Son nom vient des nombreuses colonies de mouettes dans les environs.
#. column 13: Gullperch Tower
#. column 14: "The rains may cloud our view, but they won't stop those who would invade our shores. And so we climb high, scouring the horizon for any sign of danger." Such were the lookout's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162712:0:15"
msgid "One of three beacons built along the La Noscean coast in the Sixth Astral Era, Gullperch Tower is the easternmost─warning ships navigating the Strait of Merlthor of its deadly shallows, while also serving as a watchtower for pirate and Sahagin raids on Bloodshore."
msgstr "Башня Чайки — один из трёх маяков, построенных на побережье Ла-Носкеи в Шестую астральную эру. Это самый восточный из них: он предупреждает суда в проливе Мерлтор об опасных мелях и служит дозорной башней, откуда следят за пиратами и набегами сахагинов на Кровавый берег."

#. ja: エールポートのリムレーン像
#. de: Llymlaen-Statue in Bierhafen
#. fr: Statue de Llymlaen
#. column 14: "I've no wife, an' no mind to take one─the only child I'll ever know is the ale I brew. And so, as the cargo ships pull out of the harbor, I say a prayer to the watcher of seas, that She'll see me sons safe to someone's belly somewhere." Such were the brewer's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Carved centuries past by a famous Roegadyn sculptor, this massive stone effigy located in the center of Aleport's lower plaza serves as hallowed ground upon which sailors might offer solemn prayers to the watcher of the seas before embarking on their journeys across the untamed deep.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162713:0:13"
msgid "The Navigator"
msgstr "Навигатор"

#. ja: ――ある醸造職人から聞いた噂。\n酒樽を積んだ船は、悠然と出港する。見送る人々は、美しき女神に祈りを捧げていた。
#. de: Gespräch mit einem Braumeister: Nichts sei erhebender anzusehen als das Auslaufen der Schiffe, schwer beladen mit ihrer kostbaren Fracht; wie sie unter dem beschützenden Blick der kühlen Göttin ihrem Bestimmungsort zuschippern. Gar nicht genug könne er ihr danken!
#. fr: Lorsque les navires sont chargés et prêts à appareiller, il n'est pas rare de voir les brasseurs locaux venir vénérer la Déesse dans les derniers rayons de soleil.
#. column 13: The Navigator
#. column 15: Carved centuries past by a famous Roegadyn sculptor, this massive stone effigy located in the center of Aleport's lower plaza serves as hallowed ground upon which sailors might offer solemn prayers to the watcher of the seas before embarking on their journeys across the untamed deep.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162713:0:14"
msgid "\"I've no wife, an' no mind to take one─the only child I'll ever know is the ale I brew. And so, as the cargo ships pull out of the harbor, I say a prayer to the watcher of seas, that She'll see me sons safe to someone's belly somewhere.\" Such were the brewer's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Жены у меня нет, да и не нужна. Единственное дитя, которое мне знакомо, — эль, что я варю. Вот торговые суда выходят из гавани, а я молюсь Покровительнице морей: пусть мои сынки благополучно доберутся до чьего-нибудь брюха». Так говорил пивовар. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 遠洋船が長期航海に備え、必要物資を補充するための港街「エールポート」。その中心には、航海の女神「リムレーン」の像が据えられている。著名なルガディン族彫刻家の手になる美しい女神が、今日も旅立つ船を見送る
#. de: Die „Lotsin“, Göttin der Weltmeere und der Seefahrer, von Meisterhand in weißen Marmor gemeißelt, wacht über die Überseeschiffer, die in Bierhafen nach strapaziöser Überfahrt ihre Vorräte aufstocken.
#. fr: Dressée au centre de Port-aux-Ales, point de ra<shy>vi<shy>tail<shy>le<shy>ment obligatoire pour les navires au long cours, la statue de Llymlaen, finement ouvragée par un sculpteur roegadyn de renom, est le lieu où les marins viennent prier avant d'embarquer pour le large.
#. column 13: The Navigator
#. column 14: "I've no wife, an' no mind to take one─the only child I'll ever know is the ale I brew. And so, as the cargo ships pull out of the harbor, I say a prayer to the watcher of seas, that She'll see me sons safe to someone's belly somewhere." Such were the brewer's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162713:0:15"
msgid "Carved centuries past by a famous Roegadyn sculptor, this massive stone effigy located in the center of Aleport's lower plaza serves as hallowed ground upon which sailors might offer solemn prayers to the watcher of the seas before embarking on their journeys across the untamed deep. "
msgstr "Эту огромную каменную статую несколько веков назад высек прославленный рогадинский скульптор. Она стоит в центре нижней площади Алепорта. Перед долгим путешествием по бурному морю моряки приходят сюда, чтобы вознести молитву Навигатору, покровительнице морей."

#. ja: 船の墓場
#. de: Schiffsfriedhof
#. fr: Cimetière de bateaux
#. column 14: "If yer wise, ye won't look too closely. It's not just flotsam the dark tides drag in, and there are sights what could haunt the bravest of men for life. Aye, ye'll not catch me dead going there─least of all at night." Such were the lighthouse keeper's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: For centuries, ships wrecked off the shores of southern Vylbrand have been carried upon currents to this quiet inlet─a timeless reminder of the deep's boundless wrath. So many are the wooden corpses which populate this watery lichyard, it is said that for every hull visible above the waves, a score more slumber beneath.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162714:0:13"
msgid "The Ship Graveyard"
msgstr "Кладбище кораблей"

#. ja: ――ある灯台守から聞いた噂。\n散乱する漂着物、忍び寄る恐ろしき気配。あんなところは、夜に行くべきではない。
#. de: Der Leuchtturmwärter: Vom Treibgut solle man lieber die Finger lassen, da bringe man nur Unglück über sich, und das Heulen und Pfeifen sei das Wehklagen verlorener Seelen. Kein Ort für einen Nachtspaziergang.
#. fr: Ô vous qui naviguez sur les flots, ne vous laissez pas envoûter par ses mots. Si vous la laissez vous charmer, votre navire finira dans ce charnier. Peu enviable est le destin de ces défunts, qui errent dans le noir au milieu des embruns.
#. column 13: The Ship Graveyard
#. column 15: For centuries, ships wrecked off the shores of southern Vylbrand have been carried upon currents to this quiet inlet─a timeless reminder of the deep's boundless wrath. So many are the wooden corpses which populate this watery lichyard, it is said that for every hull visible above the waves, a score more slumber beneath.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162714:0:14"
msgid "\"If yer wise, ye won't look too closely. It's not just flotsam the dark tides drag in, and there are sights what could haunt the bravest of men for life. Aye, ye'll not catch me dead going there─least of all at night.\" Such were the lighthouse keeper's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Если голова на плечах есть, лучше не приглядывайся. Тёмные воды приносят не только обломки, а некоторые зрелища и самого храброго до конца жизни преследовать будут. Не дождётесь, чтобы я туда сунулся — особенно ночью». Так говорил смотритель маяка. Я решил взглянуть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 海流によって流されてきた難破船が、静かに眠る入江。文字通り「船の墓場」そのものの光景が広がる。地元民の噂によると、その多くが伝説の魔物「セイレーン」によって惑わされた結果、難破したものだという
#. de: In der abgelegenen Bucht treibt die Strömung die Wracks verlassener Schiffe zusammen, von denen man munkelt, ihre Besatzungen hätten sich von der legendären Sirene ins Verderben locken lassen.
#. fr: Dans cette crique reposent les épaves des navires qui ont fait naufrage près des côtes noscéennes. Bien qu'ils aient été entraînés par le courant, de nombreux habitants semblent penser qu'ils ont été attirés dans ces lieux par une sirène. La brume persistante et les morts vivants qui errent sur les plages font de ce cimetière l'un des endroits les plus glauques d'Éorzéa.
#. column 13: The Ship Graveyard
#. column 14: "If yer wise, ye won't look too closely. It's not just flotsam the dark tides drag in, and there are sights what could haunt the bravest of men for life. Aye, ye'll not catch me dead going there─least of all at night." Such were the lighthouse keeper's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162714:0:15"
msgid "For centuries, ships wrecked off the shores of southern Vylbrand have been carried upon currents to this quiet inlet─a timeless reminder of the deep's boundless wrath. So many are the wooden corpses which populate this watery lichyard, it is said that for every hull visible above the waves, a score more slumber beneath."
msgstr "Уже много веков течения несут сюда, в тихую бухту, корабли, разбившиеся у южных берегов Вилбрандта. Они напоминают о безграничной ярости морской пучины. Деревянных остовов так много, что, по слухам, на каждый корпус над водой приходятся ещё два десятка под волнами."

#. ja: キャンプ・スカルバレー
#. de: Camp Schädeltal
#. fr: Camp de la vallée du Crâne
#. column 14: Overheard at an inn: "There's an outpost with quite a view of the land, but you'll want to steel yourself well if you mean to go there..."
#. column 15: Now a strategic outpost for the Maelstrom, Camp Skull Valley was once but a circle of tents occupied by a meager Yellowjacket unit charged with surveilling the area for kobold incursions. Those beastmen foolish enough to venture down from O'Ghomoro were slaughtered and beheaded─their skulls put on display as a warning to others.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162715:0:13"
msgid "Camp Skull Valley"
msgstr "Лагерь «Долина Черепов»"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\n防衛拠点は、敵を警戒するため見晴らしがいいらしい。だが、入り込む勇気はない。
#. de: Tavernenlegende zum Stützpunkt: Der Name gründet in einer wahren Begebenheit! Feinde können sich bei dem guten Ausblick gar nicht erst annähern, aber auch Verbündete dürfte das Betreten gehörigen Mut kosten.
#. fr: Une pointe de fierté ne fait jamais de mal à un soldat, notamment quand il s'agit de prouver son agilité en grimpant là où on peut bien surveiller l'ennemi.
#. column 13: Camp Skull Valley
#. column 15: Now a strategic outpost for the Maelstrom, Camp Skull Valley was once but a circle of tents occupied by a meager Yellowjacket unit charged with surveilling the area for kobold incursions. Those beastmen foolish enough to venture down from O'Ghomoro were slaughtered and beheaded─their skulls put on display as a warning to others.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162715:0:14"
msgid "Overheard at an inn: \"There's an outpost with quite a view of the land, but you'll want to steel yourself well if you mean to go there...\""
msgstr "Услышано в гостинице: «Есть там аванпост с отличным обзором, но прежде чем отправляться, советую набраться храбрости...»"

#. ja: 黒渦団の軍事拠点。かつては南下しようとするコボルド族への警告として、その頭骨を並べていたため、スカルバレーと呼ばれる。しかし、今ではハーフストーン一帯のサハギン族に対する防御拠点としての役割が強い
#. de: Vor dem Mahlstrom-Militärlager reihte man einst Kobold-Schädel auf, um die nach Süden vorstoßenden Kobolde abzuschrecken. Heute dient das Camp vor allem dem Schutz gegen die Sahagin in Halbstein.
#. fr: Tirant son nom de la coutume qu'avaient les soldats d'exposer les crânes d'intrus kobolds pour dissuader leurs camarades de venir plus bas dans la Noscea, cette base militaire du Maelstrom surveille désormais les activités des Sahuagins à Demipierre.
#. column 13: Camp Skull Valley
#. column 14: Overheard at an inn: "There's an outpost with quite a view of the land, but you'll want to steel yourself well if you mean to go there..."
msgctxt "Adventure:2162715:0:15"
msgid "Now a strategic outpost for the Maelstrom, Camp Skull Valley was once but a circle of tents occupied by a meager Yellowjacket unit charged with surveilling the area for kobold incursions. Those beastmen foolish enough to venture down from O'Ghomoro were slaughtered and beheaded─their skulls put on display as a warning to others."
msgstr "Ныне Лагерь Долины Черепов — важный форпост Мальстрёма. Когда-то здесь был лишь круг палаток и крошечный отряд жёлтых курток, следивший, не нагрянут ли кобольды. Тех зверолюдов, что осмеливались спуститься с О'Гоморо, убивали и обезглавливали, а их черепа выставляли напоказ в назидание остальным."

#. ja: 南北防波壁
#. de: Nord- und Süddamm
#. fr: Barrages du nord et du sud
#. column 14: Overheard at an alehouse: "When I've misplaced my goods, I climb atop the tents and scour the ground below. Offers a clear view, and you'd be surprised at how sturdy they are..."
#. column 15: Taking advantage of the chaos left in the Calamity's wake, a large force of Sahagin rose from the seas and laid claim to Halfstone, a distant Lominsan settlement on the far-western edge of La Noscea. To prevent any further swells of the beastman forces, a massive wall was erected between the enemy-occupied lowlands and the allied Skull Valley.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162716:0:13"
msgid "Tidegate"
msgstr "Врата Прилива"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\n大事な備品を無くしたとき、天幕によじ登って探した。意外と潰れないものだ。
#. de: Auf den Baldachin zu springen, soll ein beliebter Zeitvertreib der Wachen sein, und einer von ihnen ist darin absolute Spitze. Beeindruckend aber auch, wie robust der Stoff ist. Echte Qualitätsarbeit!
#. fr: Semblables en bien des points aux mâts et aux voiles des navires, les tentes des marchands limséens peuvent résister même au poids d'un Roegadyn.
#. column 13: Tidegate
#. column 15: Taking advantage of the chaos left in the Calamity's wake, a large force of Sahagin rose from the seas and laid claim to Halfstone, a distant Lominsan settlement on the far-western edge of La Noscea. To prevent any further swells of the beastman forces, a massive wall was erected between the enemy-occupied lowlands and the allied Skull Valley.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162716:0:14"
msgid "Overheard at an alehouse: \"When I've misplaced my goods, I climb atop the tents and scour the ground below. Offers a clear view, and you'd be surprised at how sturdy they are...\""
msgstr "Услышано в таверне: «Потеряю что-нибудь — забираюсь на палатку и оглядываю землю вокруг. Обзор отличный, а палатки, между прочим, куда прочнее, чем кажутся...»"

#. ja: サハギン族によって制圧されたハーフストーンと、スカルバレーとの境界に建造された黒渦団の防壁。サハギン族の攻勢を波に見立て「防波壁」と名付けられたが、文字通り寄せては返す波のような猛攻にさらされている
#. de: Der Nord- und Süddamm ist ein Schutzwall des Mahlstroms zwischen dem von den Sahagin eroberten Halbstein und Schädeltal, der die Horden der Sahagin von La Noscea abhalten soll - bisher erfolgreich.
#. fr: La colonie de Demipierre ayant été envahie par les Sahuagins, ces imposants remparts ont été bâtis afin de contenir les vagues d'assauts de ces hommes-poissons et de les empêcher de déferler dans la vallée du Crâne, ce qui leur vaut le nom de “barrages”.
#. column 13: Tidegate
#. column 14: Overheard at an alehouse: "When I've misplaced my goods, I climb atop the tents and scour the ground below. Offers a clear view, and you'd be surprised at how sturdy they are..."
msgctxt "Adventure:2162716:0:15"
msgid "Taking advantage of the chaos left in the Calamity's wake, a large force of Sahagin rose from the seas and laid claim to Halfstone, a distant Lominsan settlement on the far-western edge of La Noscea. To prevent any further swells of the beastman forces, a massive wall was erected between the enemy-occupied lowlands and the allied Skull Valley."
msgstr "Воспользовавшись хаосом после Бедствия, многочисленные сахагины поднялись из морских глубин и захватили Полукаменный край — отдалённое поселение Ла-Носкеи на её крайнем западе. Чтобы не дать зверолюдям продвинуться дальше, между занятыми врагом низинами и союзной Долиной черепов возвели огромную стену."

#. ja: キャンプ・ブロンズレイク
#. de: Camp Bronzesee
#. fr: Camp du lac d'Airain
#. column 14: Overheard at a tavern: "Nothing like feeling the cool breeze on your skin after a hot bath. The view's nothin' to sneeze at, either..."
#. column 15: The formation of great underwater fissures during the Calamity saw nearly half of the water comprising Bronze Lake vanish in the span of a single night. The result was the uncovering of ancient Nymian ruins submerged for thousands of years─most notably, the Wanderer's Palace, a temple dedicated to the god Oschon.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162717:0:13"
msgid "Camp Bronze Lake"
msgstr "Лагерь «Бронзовое озеро»"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\n湯あたりしたら、風に当たって涼むといい。そこから見える景色も風情があって最高だ。
#. de: Wen nach zu langem heißem Bad Benommenheit befällt, dem soll die kühle Abendbrise schnell wieder zu einem klaren Kopf verhelfen. Die grandiose Aussicht könnte allerdings aufs Neue schwindeln machen ...
#. fr: Les toits des bâtiments du sanatorium ne sont pas sans rappeler la forme des tonneaux de vin et donnent probablement une belle vue vers le couchant.
#. column 13: Camp Bronze Lake
#. column 15: The formation of great underwater fissures during the Calamity saw nearly half of the water comprising Bronze Lake vanish in the span of a single night. The result was the uncovering of ancient Nymian ruins submerged for thousands of years─most notably, the Wanderer's Palace, a temple dedicated to the god Oschon.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162717:0:14"
msgid "Overheard at a tavern: \"Nothing like feeling the cool breeze on your skin after a hot bath. The view's nothin' to sneeze at, either...\""
msgstr "Услышано в таверне: «После горячей ванны нет ничего лучше прохладного ветерка. Да и вид отсюда что надо...»"

#. ja: ブロンズレイクの水位が下がったことで、湖面に姿を現した古代都市「ニーム」時代の遺跡。温水が沸き出していたため、傷病兵向けの温泉地として整備された。療養所「ウォームワイン・サナトリウム」が併設されている
#. de: Das Sinken des Wasserspiegels ließ die malerischen Ruinen der Stadt Nym auftauchen. Heute lockt das heilsame Thermalwasser und der Warmwein des gleichnamigen Sanatoriums Kranke und Ruhesuchende von weither an.
#. fr: Situé près de vestiges de l'ancienne cité de Nym, que la baisse de niveau des eaux du lac d'Airain a révélés, ce camp est célèbre pour son installation du sanatorium du Vin chaud, qui prodigue des soins aux soldats blessés grâce à ces sources thermales.
#. column 13: Camp Bronze Lake
#. column 14: Overheard at a tavern: "Nothing like feeling the cool breeze on your skin after a hot bath. The view's nothin' to sneeze at, either..."
msgctxt "Adventure:2162717:0:15"
msgid "The formation of great underwater fissures during the Calamity saw nearly half of the water comprising Bronze Lake vanish in the span of a single night. The result was the uncovering of ancient Nymian ruins submerged for thousands of years─most notably, the Wanderer's Palace, a temple dedicated to the god Oschon."
msgstr "Во время Бедствия на дне озера образовались огромные трещины, и за одну ночь ушла почти половина воды. Так обнажились древние руины Нима, тысячи лет пролежавшие под водой. Самая примечательная из них — Дворец Странника, храм, посвящённый Ошону."

#. ja: サラオスの亡骸
#. de: Thalaos
#. fr: Thalaos
#. column 14: "Under the burning sun, I climbed to the tip of the ancient one and turned my thoughts to the days when it roamed the deep. This was when inspiration struck..." Such were the scholar's words, and I would see as she saw.
#. column 15: Though there is no proof to support the claim, rumor has these sun-bleached remains of a long-dead denizen of the deep are those of one of the legendary twin sea serpents believed to have been unleashed by the Navigator, Llymlaen, at the dawn of eras to fill the empty seas (the other being Perykos).
msgctxt "Adventure:2162718:0:13"
msgid "Thalaos"
msgstr "Талаос"

#. ja: ――ある博物学者から聞いた噂。\n勇壮なる大いなる存在に思いを馳せるには、そのよく晴れた日に先端に登るべし。
#. de: Gespräch mit einem Paläontologen: Wenn man dem grellen Himmel so nahe ist, durch nichts vom Erdboden getrennt als dem imposanten Rest eines so überwältigenden Wesens - dann scheinen die Grenzen von Naturgeschichte und Mythos zu verschwimmen.
#. fr: Le relief de la Haute-Noscea est pour le moins accidenté, ce qui n'est certainement pas bon pour les vertèbres, mais certains endroits offrent une vue fantastique.
#. column 13: Thalaos
#. column 15: Though there is no proof to support the claim, rumor has these sun-bleached remains of a long-dead denizen of the deep are those of one of the legendary twin sea serpents believed to have been unleashed by the Navigator, Llymlaen, at the dawn of eras to fill the empty seas (the other being Perykos).
msgctxt "Adventure:2162718:0:14"
msgid "\"Under the burning sun, I climbed to the tip of the ancient one and turned my thoughts to the days when it roamed the deep. This was when inspiration struck...\" Such were the scholar's words, and I would see as she saw."
msgstr "«Взобрался на самый кончик древнего великана под палящим солнцем и задумался о временах, когда он бороздил морские глубины. Тут-то меня и осенило...» Так говорил учёный. Я решила взглянуть на всё её глазами."

#. ja: 地表に露出した古代生物の巨大化石。かつて女神「リムレーン」が解き放った伝説の海蛇「サラオス」にちなみ、その名で呼ばれている。海洋生物の化石が存在する事実は、島がかつて海の底であったことを伺わせている
#. de: Das riesige Skelett eines marinen Urwesens, nach jahrtausendelanger Umklammerung vom Erdreich freigegeben. Man taufte das Fossil „Thalaos“, nach der einen der mythischen Seeschlangen, die Llymlaen einst losließ, um die leere See zu füllen. Die andere war übrigens Perykos.
#. fr: Ce fossile d'un animal préhistorique géant s'est vu donner le nom de Thalaos, un serpent de mer légendaire que la Déesse Lllymlaen aurait libéré autrefois. Ces imposants ossements tendraient à prouver que l'île de Vylbrand était autrefois sous la mer.
#. column 13: Thalaos
#. column 14: "Under the burning sun, I climbed to the tip of the ancient one and turned my thoughts to the days when it roamed the deep. This was when inspiration struck..." Such were the scholar's words, and I would see as she saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162718:0:15"
msgid "Though there is no proof to support the claim, rumor has these sun-bleached remains of a long-dead denizen of the deep are those of one of the legendary twin sea serpents believed to have been unleashed by the Navigator, Llymlaen, at the dawn of eras to fill the empty seas (the other being Perykos)."
msgstr "Хотя доказательств этому нет, ходят слухи, будто выцветшие под солнцем останки древнего морского чудовища принадлежат одному из двух легендарных морских змеев. По преданию, богиня-покровительница мореходов Ллимлейн выпустила их в пустые воды на заре времён. Вторым змеем был Перикос."

#. ja: ジジルン交易商店
#. de: Jijiroons Handelsposten
#. fr: Comptoir de Jijiroon
#. column 14: Overheard at a tavern: "Spent the night on that ledge, I did─anything to escape those shelled monstrosities. Wasn't a bad sight, though I can't say I enjoyed the trip down..."
#. column 15: Located on the eastern banks of Bronze Lake, Jijiroon's Trading Post is one of two makeshift markets peddling baubles and trinkets to those brave enough to venture that deep into kobold lands. The other is Memeroon's Trading Post, run by Jijiroon's estranged sibling, to whom the stubborn Qiqirn merchant hasn't spoken in twenty summers.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162719:0:13"
msgid "Jijiroon's Trading Post"
msgstr "Торговая лавка Джиджируна"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\n魔貝に追われて、よじ登って一夜を明かした。降りるときは、かなり勇気がいった。
#. de: Zweifellos außer Muschel-Reichweite, aber auch nicht der gemütlichste Ort, um eine nasskalte Nacht zu verbringen. Runterzukommen soll dagegen einfach gewesen sein.
#. fr: Le lac d'Airain n'est pas sans dangers, surtout la nuit. Heureusement, on peut toujours se percher sur d'anciennes ruines pour échapper aux monstres, mais attention à ne pas glisser.
#. column 13: Jijiroon's Trading Post
#. column 15: Located on the eastern banks of Bronze Lake, Jijiroon's Trading Post is one of two makeshift markets peddling baubles and trinkets to those brave enough to venture that deep into kobold lands. The other is Memeroon's Trading Post, run by Jijiroon's estranged sibling, to whom the stubborn Qiqirn merchant hasn't spoken in twenty summers.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162719:0:14"
msgid "Overheard at a tavern: \"Spent the night on that ledge, I did─anything to escape those shelled monstrosities. Wasn't a bad sight, though I can't say I enjoyed the trip down...\""
msgstr "Услышано в таверне: «Ночевал на том уступе — лишь бы спастись от этих чудищ в панцирях. Вид оттуда неплохой, а вот спускаться было страшновато...»"

#. ja: キキルン族商人「ジジルン」が営む交易商店。兄弟であるメメルンが運営する「メメルン交易商店」とは、ライバル関係にあり売上を競っているらしい。なぜ、人里はなれた地に出店を決意したのかは、よく解っていない
#. de: Der Qiqirn-Händler Jijiroon betreibt diesen Handelsposten in heftiger Konkurrenz mit dem seines Bruders Memeroon. Wie er an einem so abgelegenen Ort Profit machen kann, ist äußerst schleierhaft.
#. fr: Ce lieu d'échanges commerciaux est tenu par le Qiqirn Jijiroon, qui entretient une certaine rivalité avec son frère Memeroon, lui-même à la tête d'un éta<shy>blis<shy>se<shy>ment du même genre. Personne ne sait toutefois pourquoi il s'est installé dans un endroit aussi reculé.
#. column 13: Jijiroon's Trading Post
#. column 14: Overheard at a tavern: "Spent the night on that ledge, I did─anything to escape those shelled monstrosities. Wasn't a bad sight, though I can't say I enjoyed the trip down..."
msgctxt "Adventure:2162719:0:15"
msgid "Located on the eastern banks of Bronze Lake, Jijiroon's Trading Post is one of two makeshift markets peddling baubles and trinkets to those brave enough to venture that deep into kobold lands. The other is Memeroon's Trading Post, run by Jijiroon's estranged sibling, to whom the stubborn Qiqirn merchant hasn't spoken in twenty summers."
msgstr "Эту торговую лавку на восточном берегу Бронзового озера держит кикирн Джиджирун. Это один из двух временных рынков, где отважным путникам предлагают безделушки и побрякушки в глубине земель кобольдов. Другой принадлежит Мемеруну — брату, с которым Джиджирун не разговаривает уже двадцать лет."

#. ja: ニーム浮遊遺跡
#. de: Schwebende Stadt Nym
#. fr: Cité flottante de Nym
#. column 14: "There were islands floating in the sky, and crystals that shone like terrestrial stars. Even now, I wonder if it was but a dream..." Such were the fledgling adventurer's words, and I would see as she saw.
#. column 15: Suspended high above the foothills of Mt. O'Ghomoro is the Floating City of Nym─central hub of a lost civilization which prospered on Vylbrand during the Fifth Astral Era. The accepted theory as to how the city was torn from the realm involves the over-aspecting of corrupted wind crystals─a phenomenon witnessed late in the Sixth Astral Era.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162720:0:13"
msgid "The Floating City of Nym"
msgstr "Парящий город Ним"

#. ja: ――ある冒険者から聞いた噂。\n空に浮かぶ遺跡は忘れがたいほど神秘的。輝くクリスタルの光は、地上に光る星のよう。
#. de: Wie sich so massive Felsen in der Luft halten können, ist wahrlich rätselhaft - ein unvergesslicher Anblick, wenn die glimmenden Kristallspitzen vom opulenten Gold der Sonne überflutet werden, um danach erneut mit sanftem Schein die Nacht zu erhellen.
#. fr: Les ruines de l'ancienne Nym sont sûrement l'un des panorama les plus impressionnants d'Éorzéa, constellant le ciel de la Noscea.
#. column 13: The Floating City of Nym
#. column 15: Suspended high above the foothills of Mt. O'Ghomoro is the Floating City of Nym─central hub of a lost civilization which prospered on Vylbrand during the Fifth Astral Era. The accepted theory as to how the city was torn from the realm involves the over-aspecting of corrupted wind crystals─a phenomenon witnessed late in the Sixth Astral Era.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162720:0:14"
msgid "\"There were islands floating in the sky, and crystals that shone like terrestrial stars. Even now, I wonder if it was but a dream...\" Such were the fledgling adventurer's words, and I would see as she saw."
msgstr "«В небе плавали острова, а кристаллы сияли, словно земные звёзды. До сих пор гадаю: неужто мне всё это приснилось?..» Так говорил начинающий искатель приключений. Я решила взглянуть на всё её глазами."

#. ja: 第五星暦時代にバイルブランド島で栄えた、古代都市「ニーム」の遺跡。地脈のエーテルが偏属性クリスタル化した結果、風属性の力が強まり、遺跡の一部が浮遊してしまったようだ。その光景は、幻想的の一語に尽きる
#. de: Nym erlebte in der Fünften Ära des Lichts ihre Hochblüte. Dass ein Teil der Ruinen in die Luft emporgehoben wurde, liegt an der starken Windaspektiertheit der hier verfestigten denaturierten Kristalle.
#. fr: Ces ruines de l'ancienne cité de Nym, civilisation qui a fleuri sur l'île de Vylbrand à la 5e ère astrale, forment désormais un paysage fantastique du fait de cristaux corrompus, qui renforçant l'élément vent, font flotter une partie des vestiges.
#. column 13: The Floating City of Nym
#. column 14: "There were islands floating in the sky, and crystals that shone like terrestrial stars. Even now, I wonder if it was but a dream..." Such were the fledgling adventurer's words, and I would see as she saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162720:0:15"
msgid "Suspended high above the foothills of Mt. O'Ghomoro is the Floating City of Nym─central hub of a lost civilization which prospered on Vylbrand during the Fifth Astral Era. The accepted theory as to how the city was torn from the realm involves the over-aspecting of corrupted wind crystals─a phenomenon witnessed late in the Sixth Astral Era."
msgstr "Высоко над предгорьями горы О'Гоморо парит город Ним — центр древней цивилизации, процветавшей на Вилбрандте в Пятую астральную эру. Считается, что город оторвался от земли из-за чрезмерного влияния ветра на искажённые кристаллы ветра. Подобное явление наблюдали в конце Шестой астральной эры."

#. ja: キャンプ・オーバールック
#. de: Camp Ausblick
#. fr: Camp du Guet
#. column 14: Overheard at an inn: "You'll want to keep a wide berth of brigands and beastmen both. There's a crumbling gate, overrun by shrubbery. Makes for good cover, and offers an unobstructed view of the road below─two birds with one stone."
#. column 15: Manned by the “meanest shite-kickin' unit in the whole damn Maelstrom,” Camp Overlook serves as the base of operations for the Red Swallows─a privateer levy tasked with the surveillance of kobold activity in outer La Noscea and along the slopes of Mt. O'Ghomoro.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162721:0:13"
msgid "Camp Overlook"
msgstr "Лагерь «Дозор»"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\n輸送路を脅かす存在を警戒するには、壁の上の茂みに隠れて見張るといい。
#. de: Kein offizieller Aussichtsposten, aber zweifellos ein geeigneter Ort, um Gefahren für die Handelsstraße sofort zu sichten und zu beseitigen. Das Gestrüpp auf der Mauer bietet Sichtschutz (und der Frühschicht noch Gelegenheit für ein kurzes Schläfchen).
#. fr: Les Hirondelles écarlates savent que les buissons qui poussent sur les vieilles pierres nymiennes offrent une cachette idéale pour observer les ennemis.
#. column 13: Camp Overlook
#. column 15: Manned by the “meanest shite-kickin' unit in the whole damn Maelstrom,” Camp Overlook serves as the base of operations for the Red Swallows─a privateer levy tasked with the surveillance of kobold activity in outer La Noscea and along the slopes of Mt. O'Ghomoro.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162721:0:14"
msgid "Overheard at an inn: \"You'll want to keep a wide berth of brigands and beastmen both. There's a crumbling gate, overrun by shrubbery. Makes for good cover, and offers an unobstructed view of the road below─two birds with one stone.\""
msgstr "Слух, подслушанный в таверне: «Держись подальше и от разбойников, и от зверолюдей. Там есть полуразрушенные ворота, заросшие кустами. Удобное укрытие, да и дорогу внизу видно как на ладони. Двух зайцев одним выстрелом!»"

#. ja: 外地ラノシアに設営された黒渦団のキャンプ。海賊兵部隊「紅燕陸戦隊」が陣取り、高台からコボルド族の動向を監視している。南に目を向けると、ニーム時代のオシュオン神殿「ワンダラーパレス」も見下ろせる
#. de: Im äußeren La Noscea hat der Mahlstrom die Rotschwalben-Kundschafter postiert, um ein wachsames Auge auf die Aktivitäten der Kobolde zu haben. Im Süden erkennt man den Palast des Wanderers aus der nymischen Kultur.
#. fr: Ce camp du Maelstrom, établi sur une hauteur de Noscea extérieure afin de mieux observer les mouvements des Kobolds, est la base de l'unité spéciale des Hirondelles écarlates. Au sud, on aperçoit le Palais du Vagabond, ancien édifice nymien dédié au dieu Oschon.
#. column 13: Camp Overlook
#. column 14: Overheard at an inn: "You'll want to keep a wide berth of brigands and beastmen both. There's a crumbling gate, overrun by shrubbery. Makes for good cover, and offers an unobstructed view of the road below─two birds with one stone."
msgctxt "Adventure:2162721:0:15"
msgid "Manned by the “meanest shite-kickin' unit in the whole damn Maelstrom,” Camp Overlook serves as the base of operations for the Red Swallows─a privateer levy tasked with the surveillance of kobold activity in outer La Noscea and along the slopes of Mt. O'Ghomoro. "
msgstr "В лагере «Обзорный» расквартирован «самый лютый отряд засранцев во всём проклятом Мальстрёме». Это база Красных ласточек — отряда каперов, которому поручено следить за кобольдами во внешней Ла-Носкее и на склонах горы О'Гоморо."

#. ja: ウ・ガマロ武装鉱山
#. de: U'Ghamaro-Minen
#. fr: Mines d'U'Ghamaro
#. column 14: "Reeks of sulphur and slumgullion, for sure, but lookin' down from that furnace, I could swear there was somethin' almost beautiful about the place. Either that or the fumes have gotten to me head..." Such were the soldier's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: The brilliant rainbow-colored hues that permeate the otherwise bistre slopes of O'Ghomoro are a result of the endless flow of toxic slumgullion streaming forth from the labyrinthine warrens that make up U'Ghamaro Mines. As more kobolds arrive on the surface each day, there is a scramble to construct new forges to accommodate them.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162722:0:13"
msgid "U'Ghamaro Mines"
msgstr "Шахты У'Гамаро"

#. ja: ――ある兵士から聞いた噂。\n白昼堂々と行われた敵拠点への強襲作戦。溶鉱炉に登って、敵兵をコケにしたらしい。
#. de: Soldatenlegende: Der allerhöchste Triumph sei es gewesen, die Besiegten nach einer am helllichtem Tage geführten Attacke auf ihren Stützpunkt von ihrem eigenen Schmelzofen herab zu verhöhnen.
#. fr: Il faut admettre que les Kobolds ont du talent pour fabriquer des machines aussi hautes, malgré leur corps ratatiné. Leurs longs bras en font peut-être d'excellents escaladeurs.
#. column 13: U'Ghamaro Mines
#. column 15: The brilliant rainbow-colored hues that permeate the otherwise bistre slopes of O'Ghomoro are a result of the endless flow of toxic slumgullion streaming forth from the labyrinthine warrens that make up U'Ghamaro Mines. As more kobolds arrive on the surface each day, there is a scramble to construct new forges to accommodate them.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162722:0:14"
msgid "\"Reeks of sulphur and slumgullion, for sure, but lookin' down from that furnace, I could swear there was somethin' almost beautiful about the place. Either that or the fumes have gotten to me head...\" Such were the soldier's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Серой воняет — и серой, и какой-то дрянью, это точно. Но когда я глянул на всё с этой печи, место показалось мне почти красивым. Или это пары мне в голову ударили...» — так сказал солдат. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: コボルド族が築いた武装鉱山。その周辺は、豊富な硫黄と、しみ出した地下水や工業廃水がない交ぜとなり、独特の光景を作りだしている。人口爆発によって増えた労働力により、日々、拡張工事が進められているらしい
#. de: Von den Kobolden immer weiter ausgebaut und ausgebeutet scheinen diese Minen unerschöpflich. Fremdlinge sind nicht willkommen und Schwefel und Verhüttungsabwässer schaffen eine unwirtliche Umgebung.
#. fr: Près de ce réseau complexe de galeries créé par les Kobolds, le soufre s'est mélangé aux eaux souterraines et usées pour former un paysage unique. Ces hommes-taupes comptent une importante main-d'œuvre qui étend leur territoire in<shy>las<shy>sa<shy>ble<shy>ment.
#. column 13: U'Ghamaro Mines
#. column 14: "Reeks of sulphur and slumgullion, for sure, but lookin' down from that furnace, I could swear there was somethin' almost beautiful about the place. Either that or the fumes have gotten to me head..." Such were the soldier's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162722:0:15"
msgid "The brilliant rainbow-colored hues that permeate the otherwise bistre slopes of O'Ghomoro are a result of the endless flow of toxic slumgullion streaming forth from the labyrinthine warrens that make up U'Ghamaro Mines. As more kobolds arrive on the surface each day, there is a scramble to construct new forges to accommodate them."
msgstr "Пёстрые радужные разводы на склонах О'Гоморо, обычно цвета горького шоколада, — следствие нескончаемого потока ядовитой грязи из лабиринта шахт У'Гамаро. Кобольдов с каждым днём приходит всё больше, и для них спешно строят новые плавильни."

#. ja: 隠者の庵
#. de: Einsiedlerhütte
#. fr: Masure de l'ermite
#. column 14: "Someone actually lives there? I'll believe it when I meet the man. Still, you'll not find me complaining─it's a fine place to sit down and rest your weary legs for a spell." Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: While few have ever seen the lord of this humble hideaway which rests precariously on the edge of an unscalable precipice─let alone obtained his permission for entering the premises─that has not stopped travelers from taking full advantage of the respite the location offers, whether it be a dip in the steaming pools, or a few bells' slumber on the soft goosefeather bed.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162723:0:13"
msgid "The Hermit's Hovel"
msgstr "Приют отшельника"

#. ja: ――ある冒険者から聞いた噂。\n人嫌いの変わり者は、終始不在。勝手に座り込んで、休んでもバレはしない。
#. de: Ein Abenteurer erzählte mir, da der Einsiedler ohnehin nie da sei, könne man bei schlechtem Wetter ruhig in seine Hütte flüchten und es sich auf einem Stuhl bequem machen. Selbst die Nacht verbringe man dort ungestört.
#. fr: L'étrange propriétaire de ces lieux étant continuellement absent, il n'est pas rare d'y voir des personnes entrer dans sa demeure pour s'abriter de la pluie, lire des livres, ou encore regarder les étoiles la nuit venue.
#. column 13: The Hermit's Hovel
#. column 15: While few have ever seen the lord of this humble hideaway which rests precariously on the edge of an unscalable precipice─let alone obtained his permission for entering the premises─that has not stopped travelers from taking full advantage of the respite the location offers, whether it be a dip in the steaming pools, or a few bells' slumber on the soft goosefeather bed.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162723:0:14"
msgid "\"Someone actually lives there? I'll believe it when I meet the man. Still, you'll not find me complaining─it's a fine place to sit down and rest your weary legs for a spell.\" Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Там и правда кто-то живёт? Поверю, когда сам его встречу. Хотя жаловаться не на что: отличное место, чтобы присесть и дать ногам отдохнуть». Так сказал приключенец. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 北方にオ・ゴモロ山を望む場所に、ひっそりと建てられた庵。火山地帯だけあって温水が沸き出しており、敷地内には天然の露天風呂が作られている。庵の主は、ほとんど姿を現さないほど、放浪癖がある人物らしい
#. de: Von der abgeschiedenen Hütte überblickt man den nördlich gelegenen Vulkan O'Ghomoro, doch den scheuen Bewohner bekommt man kaum zu Gesicht. Heißes Wasser quillt aus der Erde in ein gemütliches Badebecken.
#. fr: Cette masure isolée jouit d'une vue imprenable sur le volcan d'O'Ghomoro. Située à côté d'une source d'eau chaude, elle s'offre le luxe d'avoir un bain à ciel ouvert sur son terrain. Vagabond dans l'âme, le pro<shy>prié<shy>taire des lieux est une personne mystérieuse dont on ne sait presque rien.
#. column 13: The Hermit's Hovel
#. column 14: "Someone actually lives there? I'll believe it when I meet the man. Still, you'll not find me complaining─it's a fine place to sit down and rest your weary legs for a spell." Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162723:0:15"
msgid "While few have ever seen the lord of this humble hideaway which rests precariously on the edge of an unscalable precipice─let alone obtained his permission for entering the premises─that has not stopped travelers from taking full advantage of the respite the location offers, whether it be a dip in the steaming pools, or a few bells' slumber on the soft goosefeather bed."
msgstr "Мало кому доводилось видеть хозяина скромного жилища на краю неприступного обрыва, не говоря уж о том, чтобы получить разрешение войти. Но это не мешает путникам отдыхать здесь: купаться в горячих источниках или спать на мягкой перине из гусиного пуха."

#. ja: カーラインカフェと大水車
#. de: Hexenstübchen und Wasserrad
#. fr: Don de Figaga
#. column 14: Overheard about town: "There's nothing quite like standing beside the mighty waterwheel, watching brave men and women as they come and go."
#. column 15: Nestled cozily within the inn known as the Roost lies the relaxing Carline Canopy, a haven for those seeking a respite from travel's travails or questing's quandaries. Figaga's Gift, the towering waterwheel found outside the café, powers the saws and lathes of the Carpenters' Guild, and is widely considered Gridania's grandest architectural achievement.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162724:0:13"
msgid "The Carline Canopy"
msgstr "Навес Карлайн"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\n去りゆく者を見送りながら、勇壮な水車が回る姿を見るのはオツなものだ。
#. de: Man muss schon ein bisschen klettern, um den besten Blick auf das Hexenstübchen und das sich unermüdlich drehende Wasserrad zu haben. Aber wie jeder Wanderer weiß: Das eigentliche Ziel jeder Reise ist der Weg selbst.
#. fr: La grande roue à eau tourne inlassablement, accueillant et reconduisant tous ceux qui passent par la porte du Blaireau bleu.
#. column 13: The Carline Canopy
#. column 15: Nestled cozily within the inn known as the Roost lies the relaxing Carline Canopy, a haven for those seeking a respite from travel's travails or questing's quandaries. Figaga's Gift, the towering waterwheel found outside the café, powers the saws and lathes of the Carpenters' Guild, and is widely considered Gridania's grandest architectural achievement.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162724:0:14"
msgid "Overheard about town: \"There's nothing quite like standing beside the mighty waterwheel, watching brave men and women as they come and go.\""
msgstr "Слух, подслушанный в городе: «Ничто не сравнится с тем, как стоишь у могучего водяного колеса и смотришь, как смелые люди приходят и уходят»."

#. ja: チャボアザミの名を冠した喫茶店「カーラインカフェ」。その横手には、エオルゼア最大の木造水車である「フィガガ大水車」が、心地よい音色を響かせながら回転し、動力を木工師ギルドの工房へと送っている
#. de: Miounnes Hexenstübchen ist ein behagliches Rasthaus für Reisende und Abenteurer. Nebenan plätschert gemütlich Figagas Wasserrad und versorgt die Zimmerer der nahe gelegenen Gilde mit Wasserkraft.
#. fr: Située non loin du café Aux Feuilles de carline, cette imposante roue à aube fournit une énergie précieuse et propre à la guilde des menuisiers. Elle est très appréciée des Gridaniens pour le bruit agréable et apaisant qu'elle produit au contact de l'eau.
#. column 13: The Carline Canopy
#. column 14: Overheard about town: "There's nothing quite like standing beside the mighty waterwheel, watching brave men and women as they come and go."
msgctxt "Adventure:2162724:0:15"
msgid "Nestled cozily within the inn known as the Roost lies the relaxing Carline Canopy, a haven for those seeking a respite from travel's travails or questing's quandaries. Figaga's Gift, the towering waterwheel found outside the café, powers the saws and lathes of the Carpenters' Guild, and is widely considered Gridania's grandest architectural achievement."
msgstr "В уютной гостинице «Гнездо» находится кафе «Навес Карлайн» — здесь можно передохнуть от тягот дороги и приключений. Высоченное водяное колесо Фигаги стоит рядом с кафе и приводит в движение пилы и токарные станки гильдии плотников. Многие считают его величайшим достижением гриданской архитектуры."

#. ja: 槍術士ギルド
#. de: Pikeniergilde
#. fr: Guilde des maîtres d'hast
#. column 14: "In my early days of training, I was told to study the movements of my seniors. Climbing to what I thought the perfect vantage point, I earned no praise, only thorough scolding from my instructor." Such were the guardsman's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Founded by legendary Wood Wailer captain Mistalle, the Lancers' Guild doubles as a headquarters for those who keep the peace within Gridania, and the greater peace without. It is to these “Wailing Barracks” that people come with matters whose resolution requires a polearm's edge, and justice meted out to those who have wronged the forest or forestborn.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162725:0:13"
msgid "The Lancers' Guild"
msgstr "Гильдия копейщиков"

#. ja: ――ある衛士から聞いた噂。\n技を盗めと言われたため、特等席で見物しようとしたが、馬鹿げたことは止めろと怒鳴られた。
#. de: Als mich ein Schauer überraschte, wollte ich die Zeit nutzen und mir Tricks im Umgang mit der Lanze abschauen, aber ein unwirscher Pikenier verscheuchte mich von meinem - zugegebenermaßen unangemessenen - Beobachtungsposten.
#. fr: Si la guilde est avant tout un lieu d'entraînement, rien n'empêche les badauds de venir regarder les maîtres manier leurs lances, à condition de rester dans un coin sans les incommoder.
#. column 13: The Lancers' Guild
#. column 15: Founded by legendary Wood Wailer captain Mistalle, the Lancers' Guild doubles as a headquarters for those who keep the peace within Gridania, and the greater peace without. It is to these “Wailing Barracks” that people come with matters whose resolution requires a polearm's edge, and justice meted out to those who have wronged the forest or forestborn.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162725:0:14"
msgid "\"In my early days of training, I was told to study the movements of my seniors. Climbing to what I thought the perfect vantage point, I earned no praise, only thorough scolding from my instructor.\" Such were the guardsman's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«В первые дни учёбы мне велели следить за движениями старших. Я забрался на место, откуда, как мне казалось, всё отлично видно, но вместо похвалы получил от наставника основательную выволочку». Так сказал стражник. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 名槍術士「ミスタル」によって創設された槍術士たちのギルド。奥にグリダニアの治安を守る「鬼哭隊」の屯所が設けられていることもあり、その道場では、ギルド員と鬼哭隊士とが共に汗を流す姿も見ることができる
#. de: Die Gilde wurde von dem berühmten Lanzenkämpfer Mistalle gegründet. Hier befindet sich auch das Hauptquartier des Klageregiments, das regelmäßig Übungen mit den Pikenieren durchführt.
#. fr: Fondée par le légendaire lancier Mistalle, la guilde des maîtres d'hast sert également de quartier général aux vigiles sombres, l'unité de sécurité publique gridanienne. Ces derniers s'y entraînent d'ailleurs ré<shy>gu<shy>liè<shy>re<shy>ment en compagnie des férus de la lance.
#. column 13: The Lancers' Guild
#. column 14: "In my early days of training, I was told to study the movements of my seniors. Climbing to what I thought the perfect vantage point, I earned no praise, only thorough scolding from my instructor." Such were the guardsman's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162725:0:15"
msgid "Founded by legendary Wood Wailer captain Mistalle, the Lancers' Guild doubles as a headquarters for those who keep the peace within Gridania, and the greater peace without. It is to these “Wailing Barracks” that people come with matters whose resolution requires a polearm's edge, and justice meted out to those who have wronged the forest or forestborn."
msgstr "Гильдию копейщиков основал легендарный капитан Лесных стражей Мисталь. Она также служит штабом тем, кто поддерживает порядок в Гридании и за её пределами. В эти «казармы Плача» приходят разбираться с делами, где нужны копьё и справедливое наказание для тех, кто обидел лес или его жителей."

#. ja: バノック練兵所
#. de: Der Stubben
#. fr: Le Bannock
#. column 14: "My subordinates have a knack for disappearing from time to time, but not to worry. Climb high and survey the stump below, and the shirkers in the shadows are soon revealed." Such were the guard captain's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Built around the stump of a fallen heavenspillar, the Bannock serves as training grounds for Order of the Twin Adder initiates. There are several theories regarding the origin of the area's name, some claiming it is taken from the hardtack issued to Grand Company recruits, others that it is derived from the training stump's resemblance to those selfsame rations.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162726:0:13"
msgid "The Bannock"
msgstr "Баннок"

#. ja: ――ある衛士から聞いた噂。\n姿を消した部下を見つけるのは簡単。切り株よりも上から見下ろせばいいだけだから。
#. de: Wenn er erst mal einen Punkt gefunden hat, der höher als der namensgebende Baumstumpf liegt, entgeht dem Besucher nichts mehr von dem geschäftigen Treiben - auch wenn die Soldaten eine Schlechtwetterpause einlegen.
#. fr: Les officiers gridaniens sont bien placés pour observer les nouvelles recrues s'entraîner, et si jamais certaines se cachent, il suffit de monter un peu plus haut pour les découvrir.
#. column 13: The Bannock
#. column 15: Built around the stump of a fallen heavenspillar, the Bannock serves as training grounds for Order of the Twin Adder initiates. There are several theories regarding the origin of the area's name, some claiming it is taken from the hardtack issued to Grand Company recruits, others that it is derived from the training stump's resemblance to those selfsame rations.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162726:0:14"
msgid "\"My subordinates have a knack for disappearing from time to time, but not to worry. Climb high and survey the stump below, and the shirkers in the shadows are soon revealed.\" Such were the guard captain's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Мои подчинённые то и дело куда-то пропадают, но ничего страшного. Заберись повыше, огляни пень внизу — и бездельников, притаившихся в тени, сразу заметишь». Так сказал капитан стражи. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 双蛇党が新兵育成のために新設した練兵所。黒衣森固有の巨大樹「天柱樹」の切り株を用いて、訓練場が作られている。この切り株が、扁平な丸パン「バノック」に似ていることから、「バノック練兵所」と名付けられた
#. de: Ausbildungsort für Rekruten der Bruderschaft der Morgenviper. Der Name Stubben bezieht sich auf den Stumpf eines Mammutbaums, der zu den legendären Himmelssäulen gehörte und nun als Trainingsstätte dient.
#. fr: Utilisant ingénieusement la souche d'un arbre géant, que les Gridaniens appellent “pilier céleste”, ce camp a été créé par l'ordre des Deux Vipères pour former ses jeunes recrues. Son nom vient de la ressemblance de cette plateforme avec un pain plat local.
#. column 13: The Bannock
#. column 14: "My subordinates have a knack for disappearing from time to time, but not to worry. Climb high and survey the stump below, and the shirkers in the shadows are soon revealed." Such were the guard captain's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162726:0:15"
msgid "Built around the stump of a fallen heavenspillar, the Bannock serves as training grounds for Order of the Twin Adder initiates. There are several theories regarding the origin of the area's name, some claiming it is taken from the hardtack issued to Grand Company recruits, others that it is derived from the training stump's resemblance to those selfsame rations."
msgstr "Баннок построен вокруг пня упавшего небесного столпа и служит тренировочной площадкой для новобранцев Ордена Двух Змей. Происхождение названия объясняют по-разному: одни считают, что оно пошло от сухарей, которыми кормят новобранцев Великих компаний, другие видят сходство пня с этими самыми сухарями."

#. ja: ハウケタ御用邸
#. de: Haukke-Herrenhaus
#. fr: Manoir des Haukke
#. column 14: "I fled as fast as my legs could carry me, till I stood atop massive tree roots with nowhere to run. The glow from the windows, so beautiful, yet so terrible..." Such were the madman's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Long frowned upon by the people of Gridania as a symbol of excess, the Seedseers would finally submit to pressure from the citizenry, selling the deed to the manor to Lady Amandine of House Dartancours. The word “Haukke” is of ancient Padjali origin and means, “to speak without words.”
msgctxt "Adventure:2162727:0:13"
msgid "Haukke Manor"
msgstr "Особняк Хаукке"

#. ja: ――ある冒険者から聞いた噂。\n妖異に追われ、気付いた時には大樹の根の上にいたらしい。振り返ると、窓からは不気味な光が漏れていた。
#. de: Ein unheimliches Licht sieht man aus den Fenstern des verfluchten Herrenhauses scheinen, wenn man auf die klauenartige Wurzel des großen Baums steigt. Aber wer hat dazu schon den Mut?
#. fr: Les storopers ont beau être des créatures végétales, ils ne savent pas grimper sur les grosses racines... À moins que ce soit la vue du manoir qui leur fasse peur.
#. column 13: Haukke Manor
#. column 15: Long frowned upon by the people of Gridania as a symbol of excess, the Seedseers would finally submit to pressure from the citizenry, selling the deed to the manor to Lady Amandine of House Dartancours. The word “Haukke” is of ancient Padjali origin and means, “to speak without words.”
msgctxt "Adventure:2162727:0:14"
msgid "\"I fled as fast as my legs could carry me, till I stood atop massive tree roots with nowhere to run. The glow from the windows, so beautiful, yet so terrible...\" Such were the madman's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Я бежал изо всех сил, пока не оказался на огромных корнях, а дальше бежать было некуда. Из окон лился свет — прекрасный, но такой жуткий...» Так сказал безумец. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 幻術皇の元御用邸。二代前の幻術皇が「贅沢過ぎる」として引き払い、名門ダルタンクール家の手に渡った。なお、「ハウケタ」とは古語で「黙して語れ」という意味で、精霊との言葉に寄らない対話の場であることを示す
#. de: Das Herrenhaus gehörte den Saatsehern, bis Stimmen laut wurden, eine derart luxuriöse Residenz sei zu weltlich für eine spirituelle Leitfigur. Daraufhin wurde das Haus an die Dartancours-Familie abgegeben. Haukke ist ein altes Padjal-Wort und bedeutet: „ohne Worte kommunizieren“.
#. fr: Ancienne résidence des Oracles, cette demeure luxueuse a été cédée à la riche famille des Dartancours il y a maintenant deux générations. Le mot “Haukke” désignerait en langue ancienne des rituels de communication silencieuse avec les esprits de la forêt.
#. column 13: Haukke Manor
#. column 14: "I fled as fast as my legs could carry me, till I stood atop massive tree roots with nowhere to run. The glow from the windows, so beautiful, yet so terrible..." Such were the madman's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162727:0:15"
msgid "Long frowned upon by the people of Gridania as a symbol of excess, the Seedseers would finally submit to pressure from the citizenry, selling the deed to the manor to Lady Amandine of House Dartancours. The word “Haukke” is of ancient Padjali origin and means, “to speak without words.”"
msgstr "Жители Гридании давно осуждали особняк как символ расточительства. В конце концов провидцы уступили настояниям горожан и продали его леди Амандины из дома Дартанкур. Слово «Хаукке» на древнем паджальском означает «говорить без слов»."

#. ja: 長老の木
#. de: Wächterbaum
#. fr: Arbre gardien
#. column 14: "When I feel I have lost my way, I look down upon the ancient arbor under the shining sun. I look down, and I listen." Such were the conjurer's words, and I would see as she saw.
#. column 15: Having seen over a thousand summers, the Guardian Tree is purportedly the oldest arbor in all the Black Shroud, and home to the great one─an elder elemental who watches and presides over the forest's denizens. The fruit borne by the tree resembles a plum and is sought after across the Three Great Continents for its curative properties.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162728:0:13"
msgid "The Guardian Tree"
msgstr "Древо-хранитель"

#. ja: ――ある幻術士から聞いた噂。\n天気の良い日には、精霊の声に耳を傾けるため森に向かう。大いなる古木を見下ろす場所に。
#. de: Bei schönem Wetter geht der Druide in den Wald, um den Stimmen der Gebieter zu lauschen. Am liebsten dorthin, von wo aus er auf den heiligen Baum herabblicken kann.
#. fr: Les jours de beau temps, on aperçoit souvent des attroupements de promeneurs observer ce majestueux végétal depuis les hauteurs.
#. column 13: The Guardian Tree
#. column 15: Having seen over a thousand summers, the Guardian Tree is purportedly the oldest arbor in all the Black Shroud, and home to the great one─an elder elemental who watches and presides over the forest's denizens. The fruit borne by the tree resembles a plum and is sought after across the Three Great Continents for its curative properties.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162728:0:14"
msgid "\"When I feel I have lost my way, I look down upon the ancient arbor under the shining sun. I look down, and I listen.\" Such were the conjurer's words, and I would see as she saw."
msgstr "«Когда я сбиваюсь с пути, то смотрю вниз, на древнее дерево под сияющим солнцем. Смотрю и слушаю». Так сказал чародей. И я хотел увидеть мир его глазами."

#. ja: 黒衣森で最も齢を重ねているという大樹で、グリダニアの道士たちが語るところによれば「森の大精霊」が棲まうという。樹齢は、千年を超えているともいわれており、その果実は「千年果実」と呼ばれ珍重されている
#. de: Den Druiden zufolge ist der älteste noch lebende Urbaum Gridanias von einem mächtigen Gebieter beseelt und über tausend Jahre alt, weshalb seine wertvollen Früchte Tausendjahrpflaumen genannt werden.
#. fr: Cet arbre est le plus ancien de la forêt de Sombrelinceul. Âgé de plus de mille ans, ses fruits appelés “prunes millénaires” sont gardés pré<shy>cieu<shy>se<shy>ment par les botanistes du Courtil. D'après les druides gridaniens, il abriterait le doyen des esprits.
#. column 13: The Guardian Tree
#. column 14: "When I feel I have lost my way, I look down upon the ancient arbor under the shining sun. I look down, and I listen." Such were the conjurer's words, and I would see as she saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162728:0:15"
msgid "Having seen over a thousand summers, the Guardian Tree is purportedly the oldest arbor in all the Black Shroud, and home to the great one─an elder elemental who watches and presides over the forest's denizens. The fruit borne by the tree resembles a plum and is sought after across the Three Great Continents for its curative properties."
msgstr "Говорят, Древо-хранитель — старейшее во всём Чёрном лесу. Ему больше тысячи лет, и в его кроне обитает Великий — древний элементаль, что присматривает за лесными жителями. Плоды дерева похожи на сливы и ценятся на всех трёх великих континентах за целебные свойства."

#. ja: 虹架けの滝
#. de: Regenbogenfall
#. fr: Cascade de l'arc-en-ciel
#. column 14: "Shimmering in the sun and mist, the bridge is a sign that for all the pain we have inflicted on our forest home, the elementals still grace us with their favor." Such were the conjurer's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: When struck by the rare sunbeams which happen to penetrate the thick canopy of the Black Shroud, the veil of fine mist created by one of the East Vein's myriad cataracts projects a brilliant rainbow which appears to connect the river's east and west banks. The grotto hidden behind the veil houses one of the forest's most sacred locations─Lifemend Stump.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162729:0:13"
msgid "Rainbow Bridge"
msgstr "Радужный мост"

#. ja: ――ある幻術士から聞いた噂。\n水と光が織りなす幻想的な橋は、人と森の精霊を繋ぐ融和の証と考えられている。
#. de: Ein Druide sagte mir, der von Licht und Wasser gezauberte Brückenbogen wäre ein Zeichen der Harmonie zwischen uns und den Gebietern.
#. fr: Lorsque le soleil brille de tous ses rayons, il n'est pas rare de voir des habitants de Gridania s'arrêter sur la passerelle pour observer le spectacle féerique offert par cette chute d'eau.
#. column 13: Rainbow Bridge
#. column 15: When struck by the rare sunbeams which happen to penetrate the thick canopy of the Black Shroud, the veil of fine mist created by one of the East Vein's myriad cataracts projects a brilliant rainbow which appears to connect the river's east and west banks. The grotto hidden behind the veil houses one of the forest's most sacred locations─Lifemend Stump.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162729:0:14"
msgid "\"Shimmering in the sun and mist, the bridge is a sign that for all the pain we have inflicted on our forest home, the elementals still grace us with their favor.\" Such were the conjurer's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Сверкая в солнечных лучах и тумане, мост напоминает: несмотря на всё, что мы причинили лесу, духи всё ещё благоволят нам». Так сказал чародейка. И я хотел увидеть мир её глазами."

#. ja: 黒衣森を流れる小川のひとつ、「東の葉脈」が作る滝。日射しの加減次第で虹が架かることがあるため、地元民からは「虹架けの滝」の愛称で呼ばれている。なお、滝の裏手には洞窟があり、再生の根株に通じている
#. de: Im Tiefen Wald fällt das Wasser der „Östlichen Blattader“ einige Yalme tief und verbirgt dabei einen Felsdurchgang, der zum Mogry-Stubben führt. Ab und an zaubert das Sonnenlicht dort Regenbögen.
#. fr: Cette cascade prend sa source dans la Veine de l'est, l'une des petites rivières qui coulent dans la forêt de Sombrelinceul. En raison de la quantité de gouttelettes qu'elle produit, un arc-en-ciel est la plupart du temps visible quand il fait beau. À son pied se cache une grotte qui permet d'accéder à la Souche de Résurrection.
#. column 13: Rainbow Bridge
#. column 14: "Shimmering in the sun and mist, the bridge is a sign that for all the pain we have inflicted on our forest home, the elementals still grace us with their favor." Such were the conjurer's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162729:0:15"
msgid "When struck by the rare sunbeams which happen to penetrate the thick canopy of the Black Shroud, the veil of fine mist created by one of the East Vein's myriad cataracts projects a brilliant rainbow which appears to connect the river's east and west banks. The grotto hidden behind the veil houses one of the forest's most sacred locations─Lifemend Stump."
msgstr "Если редкому солнечному лучу удаётся пробиться сквозь густую крону Чёрного леса, завеса мелких брызг над одним из многочисленных водопадов Восточной артерии превращается в яркую радугу. Кажется, будто она соединяет два берега. За водопадом скрыта пещера, где находится одно из самых священных мест леса — Пень возрождения."

#. ja: ゆりかごの大樹
#. de: Sprösslings-Wiege
#. fr: Le Berceau
#. column 14: "Flora or fauna, one cannot but marvel at the wonder of birth." Such were the scholar's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Illuminated in the soft glow of countless moonspores, the Seedbed is an ancient arbor-turned-nursery used by the sylphs to grow and incubate their offspring, also known as podlings.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162730:0:13"
msgid "The Seedbed"
msgstr "Колыбель"

#. ja: ――ある博物学者が見た景色。\n種族違えども、産まれ行く命を守らんとする意志は同じ。その光に未来を見た。
#. de: „Egal welches Lebewesen ich erforscht habe, eins hatten sie alle gemein: den Instinkt, neugeborenes Leben zu schützen", verriet mir der Gelehrte an diesem hell erleuchteten Ort.
#. fr: S'il y a une lueur d'espoir dans ce monde, c'est bien le fait que, quelle que soit l'espèce, le désir de protéger sa progéniture est le même.
#. column 13: The Seedbed
#. column 15: Illuminated in the soft glow of countless moonspores, the Seedbed is an ancient arbor-turned-nursery used by the sylphs to grow and incubate their offspring, also known as podlings.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162730:0:14"
msgid "\"Flora or fauna, one cannot but marvel at the wonder of birth.\" Such were the scholar's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Растение или зверь — рождение новой жизни всё равно вызывает восхищение». Так сказал учёный. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: シルフの種を包む繭、「シルフのゆりかご」を育む大樹。この樹なくして、シルフ族は繁殖できないため、非常に重要な場所といえる。それを見守るように、月光のような淡い光を放っているのは「ムーンスポア」である
#. de: Der Kokon birgt die Saat der Sylphen und ist für deren Fortpflanzung unerlässlich. Beschützt wird dieser äußerst wichtige Ort daher von den gespenstisch leuchtenden Mondsporen.
#. fr: C'est au cœur de ce grand arbre que sont déposées les cosses, c'est-à-dire les cocons contenant les bulbes de Sylphes, pour qu'elles se développent. Ce lieu crucial pour la survie de cette espèce est toujours baigné par la lumière sélénienne des sporelunes.
#. column 13: The Seedbed
#. column 14: "Flora or fauna, one cannot but marvel at the wonder of birth." Such were the scholar's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162730:0:15"
msgid "Illuminated in the soft glow of countless moonspores, the Seedbed is an ancient arbor-turned-nursery used by the sylphs to grow and incubate their offspring, also known as podlings."
msgstr "Колыбель — древнее дерево, превращённое в питомник. Сильфы растят здесь и высиживают потомство, которое называют росточками. Место залито мягким светом бесчисленных лунных спор."

#. ja: 酒房「バスカロンドラザーズ」
#. de: Buscarrons Horst
#. fr: Au Choix de Buscarron
#. column 14: "What was I doin' up there at dawn in the pourin' rain? Hells if I can remember, but it wasn't a bad view." Such were the drunkard's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: The Druthers is run by a disenfranchised ex-sentry-turned-tavernkeep and welcomes all manner of folk, from upstanding to unsavory, so long as they follow Buscarron Strongarm's simple rules of etiquette: sit down, forget your worries, and savor your ale.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162731:0:13"
msgid "Buscarron's Druthers"
msgstr "«Забегаловка Бускаррона»"

#. ja: ――ある酔客から聞いた噂。\n深酒をした翌日、豪雨にさらされた場所で目覚めた。どうやってたどり着いたのかは覚えていない。
#. de: Ein Patron erzählte mir, wie er nach einem Zechgelage nicht in seinem Bett erwachte, sondern unter freiem Himmel von Regen und Donner geweckt wurde. Eine missliche Situation, und der Abstieg stand noch bevor.
#. fr: Si chacun se désaltère librement ici, il est quand même préférable de rester vigilant. Certains imprudents se réveillent parfois frappés par l'orage, après une nuit arrosée.
#. column 13: Buscarron's Druthers
#. column 15: The Druthers is run by a disenfranchised ex-sentry-turned-tavernkeep and welcomes all manner of folk, from upstanding to unsavory, so long as they follow Buscarron Strongarm's simple rules of etiquette: sit down, forget your worries, and savor your ale.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162731:0:14"
msgid "\"What was I doin' up there at dawn in the pourin' rain? Hells if I can remember, but it wasn't a bad view.\" Such were the drunkard's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Что я делал там на рассвете, под проливным дождём? У чёрта на куличках, не помню. Зато вид был неплохой». Так сказал выпивоха. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 元哨兵バスカロンが営む酒場。懐の広いバスカロンが差配するこの店では、冒険者はおろか周辺を根城とするゴロツキの類いまでもが、平穏に酒を酌み交わす。この酒場は、一種のアジール（聖域・避難所）といえるだろう
#. de: Buscarron muss der geselligste Soldat sein, der jemals eine Schenke eröffnete. Abenteurer und gelegentlich auch Räuber kehren hier ein, um ihre Krüge zu leeren. Ein Zufluchtsort der besonderen Art.
#. fr: Ce bar, établi dans la Forêt du sud par un ancien soldat du nom de Buscarron, est un lieu de rendez-vous très apprécié par les aventuriers et les canailles des environs. C'est en quelque sorte un endroit sacré où chacun peut boire en toute tran<shy>quil<shy>li<shy>té.
#. column 13: Buscarron's Druthers
#. column 14: "What was I doin' up there at dawn in the pourin' rain? Hells if I can remember, but it wasn't a bad view." Such were the drunkard's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162731:0:15"
msgid "The Druthers is run by a disenfranchised ex-sentry-turned-tavernkeep and welcomes all manner of folk, from upstanding to unsavory, so long as they follow Buscarron Strongarm's simple rules of etiquette: sit down, forget your worries, and savor your ale."
msgstr "«Забегаловкой» управляет бывший караульный, а ныне трактирщик, лишившийся всех прав. Бускаррон Крепкорукий принимает гостей любого сорта — от почтенных людей до самых сомнительных. Условие у него простое: садись, забудь о заботах и смакуй эль."

#. ja: サウスシュラウド・ランディング
#. de: Luftschiff-Landeplatz (Südwald)
#. fr: Aérodrome de la Forêt du sud
#. column 14: Overheard at a tavern: "Bet the people who built that place never thought it would end up used like that."
#. column 15: Constructed by Highwind Skyways to serve as a landing for cargo airships, this location was quickly abandoned when the imperial presence in the area became too large to ignore. Now the site is used as a makeshift market where bandits and poachers peddle their ill-gotten wares far from the eyes of the law.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162732:0:13"
msgid "South Shroud Landing"
msgstr "Пристань Южного леса"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\n施設を放棄した連中は、まさかあんな使われ方をされるとは思わなかっただろう。
#. de: In der Taverne wurde gemunkelt, dass die Betreiber des Landeplatzes sicher nicht abgezogen wären, wenn sie geahnt hätten, wer sich später darin einnisten würde.
#. fr: Les dirigeants de la société Vols Hautvent ne s'attendaient pas à ce que leur installation tombe entre les mains de bandits sans foi ni loi. C'est d'autant plus regrettable que la vue est exquise depuis la plateforme d'embarquement.
#. column 13: South Shroud Landing
#. column 15: Constructed by Highwind Skyways to serve as a landing for cargo airships, this location was quickly abandoned when the imperial presence in the area became too large to ignore. Now the site is used as a makeshift market where bandits and poachers peddle their ill-gotten wares far from the eyes of the law.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162732:0:14"
msgid "Overheard at a tavern: \"Bet the people who built that place never thought it would end up used like that.\""
msgstr "Слух, подслушанный в таверне: «Наверняка те, кто всё это построил, и не думали, что место будет использоваться вот так»."

#. ja: ハイウィンド飛空社が設置した貨物輸送用の飛空艇発着場。ガレマール帝国軍の進出に伴い、空の安全が脅かされたため、あえなく閉鎖された。現在は、地元の密猟者たちが、密猟品を売買するための闇市に利用している
#. de: Aufgrund der Gefährdung durch die vorrückenden Garlear sah sich die Highwind-Fluggesellschaft gezwungen, den Landeplatz aufzugeben. Nun wird er von Wilderern als Umschlagsplatz genutzt.
#. fr: Originairement établi pour le transport de mar<shy>chan<shy>di<shy>ses par la société Vols Hautvent, cet aérodrome a dû fermer en raison des menaces que font peser les Garlemaldais sur les voies aériennes. Cet endroit est aujourd'hui le repaire des Griffecoeurl, qui l'utilisent pour trafiquer fourrures et autres produits braconnés.
#. column 13: South Shroud Landing
#. column 14: Overheard at a tavern: "Bet the people who built that place never thought it would end up used like that."
msgctxt "Adventure:2162732:0:15"
msgid "Constructed by Highwind Skyways to serve as a landing for cargo airships, this location was quickly abandoned when the imperial presence in the area became too large to ignore. Now the site is used as a makeshift market where bandits and poachers peddle their ill-gotten wares far from the eyes of the law."
msgstr "Компания «Высокие ветра» построила здесь причал для грузовых дирижаблей, но вскоре закрыла его: имперские войска в округе уже нельзя было игнорировать. Теперь здесь устроен рынок, где бандиты и браконьеры сбывают добычу подальше от глаз закона."

#. ja: ウルズの恵み
#. de: Urths Segen
#. fr: Le Don d'Urth
#. column 14: "Shrouded in mist, bathed in ephemeral light. I felt as if I'd left the forest behind and come to another world..." Such were the conjurer's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Ancient writings tell that in exchange for her lifeblood, Lady Urth was able to seal the Dark Divinity Odin in a crystalline prison beneath a bubbling wellspring. To honor her sacrifice, the land upon which she drew her last breath still bears her name.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162733:0:13"
msgid "Urth's Gift"
msgstr "Дар Урта"

#. ja: ――ある幻術士から聞いた噂。\n淡い光に包まれた聖なる森の一角。霧に包まれると、さらに神秘的な雰囲気となる。
#. de: Eine schweigsame Druidin geleitete mich an diesen Ort im heiligen Wald, der in ein fahles Licht getaucht ist. Besonders geheimnisvoll wirkte die Szenerie, als Nebel aufzog.
#. fr: Certains élémentalistes prétendent que la lumière fantastique de ce lieu sacré est encore plus surnaturelle lorsqu'elle se dissipe dans la brume.
#. column 13: Urth's Gift
#. column 15: Ancient writings tell that in exchange for her lifeblood, Lady Urth was able to seal the Dark Divinity Odin in a crystalline prison beneath a bubbling wellspring. To honor her sacrifice, the land upon which she drew her last breath still bears her name.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162733:0:14"
msgid "\"Shrouded in mist, bathed in ephemeral light. I felt as if I'd left the forest behind and come to another world...\" Such were the conjurer's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Окутанный туманом, залитый мимолётным светом. Казалось, я покинул лес и попал в другой мир...» Так сказала чародейка. И я хотел увидеть мир её глазами."

#. ja: エーテル濃い清らかな湧水地。聖典では、この地で「ウルズ」という名の聖女が、悪神「オーディン」に斬り殺されたと記されている。それゆえ「ウルズの恵み」と呼ばれているが、この伝承が真実かどうかは解っていない
#. de: Diese natürliche Quelle strotzt nur so von ätherischer Energie. Die Schriften behaupten, dass Odin hier einst die heilige Urth mit seinem Schwert erschlug, und er dafür von der Kraft eines Kristalls in Urths Quelle gefesselt wurde, wo er immer noch schlummern soll.
#. fr: Si l'on en croit les textes sacrés, cette source fortement chargée en éther se situe à l'endroit où la sainte appelée Urth aurait été tuée par Odin, le Chevalier des ombres, ce qui lui vaut son nom actuel. Nul ne sait toutefois si cette légende est vraie.
#. column 13: Urth's Gift
#. column 14: "Shrouded in mist, bathed in ephemeral light. I felt as if I'd left the forest behind and come to another world..." Such were the conjurer's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162733:0:15"
msgid "Ancient writings tell that in exchange for her lifeblood, Lady Urth was able to seal the Dark Divinity Odin in a crystalline prison beneath a bubbling wellspring. To honor her sacrifice, the land upon which she drew her last breath still bears her name."
msgstr "Согласно древним писаниям, леди Урт пожертвовала кровью, чтобы заточить тёмное божество Одина в кристальную темницу под бьющим из-под земли источником. В память о её подвиге земля, где она испустила последний вздох, носит её имя."

#. ja: クォーリーミル
#. de: Mühlenbruch
#. fr: Moulin de la Carrière
#. column 14: "As I was cleaning out the chimneys, I could not help but be struck by the view below. My village may be a humble one, but there's nowhere else I'd call home." Such were the hunter's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Once a deal had been struck between the Gelmorrans and the elementals allowing their return to the forest surface, the Elezen began unearthing large quantities of boulders to build the foundations of their new city, Gridania. The waterwheels of Quarrymill were raised to power the hammers which rendered the massive stones into workable blocks.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162734:0:13"
msgid "Quarrymill"
msgstr "Куарримилл"

#. ja: ――ある猟師から聞いた噂。\n地元こそが最高の景色。煤を除去しているときに見る、集落は心暖まるものがある。
#. de: Mit leuchtenden Augen erzählte mir der Jäger davon, wie er in den frühen Morgenstunden alles vom Ruß reinigt und dabei verzückt auf die Siedlung blickt. Zu Hause ist es doch am schönsten!
#. fr: "Nul n'est mieux que chez soi", disait ce vieil homme. On raconte qu'il prenait un plaisir fou à contempler son village adoré lorsqu'il réparait sa toiture ou ramonait sa cheminée, les matins de beau temps.
#. column 13: Quarrymill
#. column 15: Once a deal had been struck between the Gelmorrans and the elementals allowing their return to the forest surface, the Elezen began unearthing large quantities of boulders to build the foundations of their new city, Gridania. The waterwheels of Quarrymill were raised to power the hammers which rendered the massive stones into workable blocks.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162734:0:14"
msgid "\"As I was cleaning out the chimneys, I could not help but be struck by the view below. My village may be a humble one, but there's nowhere else I'd call home.\" Such were the hunter's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Чистил я как-то дымоходы и залюбовался видом внизу. Деревенька у нас скромная, но другого дома мне не надо». Так сказал охотник. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 南部森林にある小村。森都「グリダニア」の建設時に、切り出した石材を製材するための水車場として拓かれた歴史を持つ。その役目を終えた今では、豊かな森の恵みを得る猟師たちの村に生まれ変わっているようだ
#. de: Einst wurden hier im Südwald mithilfe eines Wasserrads Steine für den Aufbau Gridanias geschliffen, doch diese Funktion gehört der Geschichte an. Heute leben in dem kleinen Weiler Jäger und Sammler.
#. fr: Ce hameau de la Forêt du sud tient son nom des moulins à eau qui servaient à couper la pierre extraite des carrières lorsque Gridania a été fondée. Aujourd'hui, les tailleurs de pierre ont cédé la place aux chasseurs qui profitent des bienfaits que la nature leur offre.
#. column 13: Quarrymill
#. column 14: "As I was cleaning out the chimneys, I could not help but be struck by the view below. My village may be a humble one, but there's nowhere else I'd call home." Such were the hunter's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162734:0:15"
msgid "Once a deal had been struck between the Gelmorrans and the elementals allowing their return to the forest surface, the Elezen began unearthing large quantities of boulders to build the foundations of their new city, Gridania. The waterwheels of Quarrymill were raised to power the hammers which rendered the massive stones into workable blocks."
msgstr "После того как жители Гельморры договорились с элементалями и получили разрешение вернуться на поверхность леса, элезены принялись добывать камни для фундамента нового города — Гридании. На водяных мельницах Куарримилла установили молоты, которые дробили огромные валуны на подходящие для строительства блоки."

#. ja: イクサル軍伐採所
#. de: Ixal-Kahlhieb
#. fr: Site de déboisement ixal
#. column 14: "I stood there atop the butchered arbor, my fist trembling in anger. Those who would harm our forest home must be shown no quarter." Such were the sentry's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: The Ixal have never taken well their banishment from the Black Shroud, and to this day continue to fell the hoary sentinels growing on the forest's outskirts. Too heavy to drag back to their settlements in Natalan or faraway Xelphatol, the ill-gotten lumber is tied to balloons buoyed with Ixali airstones and flown to the beast tribe's homeland under the cover of night.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162735:0:13"
msgid "Ixali Logging Grounds"
msgstr "Лесосека иксалов"

#. ja: ――ある哨兵から聞いた噂。\n切り出され、打ち込まれた木の上に立ち、怒りに震える。森の現状を現す光景らしい。
#. de: Eine aufgebrachte Wachfrau erzählte mir, wie sie das Ausmaß des Unrechts, das die Ixal dem Wald zufügen, zum ersten Mal begriff: Auf einem in die Erde getriebenen Baumstamm stehend musste sie dem räuberischen Abtransport hilflos zusehen.
#. fr: Un éclaireur des Deux Vipères a découvert un endroit bien perché d'où il peut observer les Ixali charger les rondins de bois qu'ils subtilisent à la forêt.
#. column 13: Ixali Logging Grounds
#. column 15: The Ixal have never taken well their banishment from the Black Shroud, and to this day continue to fell the hoary sentinels growing on the forest's outskirts. Too heavy to drag back to their settlements in Natalan or faraway Xelphatol, the ill-gotten lumber is tied to balloons buoyed with Ixali airstones and flown to the beast tribe's homeland under the cover of night.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162735:0:14"
msgid "\"I stood there atop the butchered arbor, my fist trembling in anger. Those who would harm our forest home must be shown no quarter.\" Such were the sentry's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Стоял я на поваленном дереве, кулак от злости дрожал. Тем, кто губит наш лесной дом, спуску давать нельзя». Так сказал часовой. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 黒衣森に不法侵入したイクサル族の伐採部隊が、樹木を切り出している伐採所。イクサル族は根拠地の大渓谷「ゼルファトル」から、クルザスの「ナタラン入植地」経由で装甲気球を送り込み、木材の搬出を行っている
#. de: Ein Feldlager der vogelartigen Ixal. Die Ixal fällen die erhabenen Bäume des Waldes der Einkehr und transportieren das geraubte Holz mit gepanzerten Ballons nach Natalan in Coerthas oder bis ins ferne Xelphatol-Tal.
#. fr: S'étant emparés de cet endroit pour en exploiter les ressources forestières, les Ixali transportent le bois à l'aide de ballons renforcés qu'ils ont fait parvenir depuis leurs terres natales des vallées de Xelphatol via leur colonie de Natalan dans le Coerthas.
#. column 13: Ixali Logging Grounds
#. column 14: "I stood there atop the butchered arbor, my fist trembling in anger. Those who would harm our forest home must be shown no quarter." Such were the sentry's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162735:0:15"
msgid "The Ixal have never taken well their banishment from the Black Shroud, and to this day continue to fell the hoary sentinels growing on the forest's outskirts. Too heavy to drag back to their settlements in Natalan or faraway Xelphatol, the ill-gotten lumber is tied to balloons buoyed with Ixali airstones and flown to the beast tribe's homeland under the cover of night."
msgstr "Изгнанные из Чёрной чащи иксалы до сих пор рубят вековые деревья на её окраинах. Слишком тяжёлую древесину не дотащить до поселений в Наталане или далёком Кселфатоле, поэтому ночью её привязывают к воздушным шарам, наполненным иксальскими аэрокамнями, и отправляют на родину зверолюдов."

#. ja: メテオの陰地
#. de: Meteoritenkrater
#. fr: Ombrage du Météore
#. column 14: "I don't like it, I can tell you that. That crescent...whatever it is...protruding into the sky. It doesn't belong there. It doesn't belong nowhere in this world." So were the guard's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Coined by the learned men of Garlond Ironworks, these massive rings were used to dampen spiritual energies, preventing the focusing of power required to wield magicks. No less than five, each measuring hundreds of yalms across, were required to keep Bahamut silent for three full eras...but even then they proved insufficient.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162736:0:13"
msgid "Fallen Neurolink"
msgstr "Упавший нейролинк"

#. ja: ――ある衛士から聞いた噂。\n天を衝く三日月型の異物。その異質な存在感には、ただただ圧倒されるばかりだ。
#. de: Eine der Wachen sprach ehrfurchtsvoll von dem sichelförmigen Gebilde, das hier vom Himmel gefallen war. Seine fremdartige Präsenz sei einfach überwältigend.
#. fr: Cet immense objet en forme de croissant de lune est l'une des nombreuses traces visibles du septième fléau. Les plus jeunes s'amusent à tester leur courage en allant l'observer la nuit.
#. column 13: Fallen Neurolink
#. column 15: Coined by the learned men of Garlond Ironworks, these massive rings were used to dampen spiritual energies, preventing the focusing of power required to wield magicks. No less than five, each measuring hundreds of yalms across, were required to keep Bahamut silent for three full eras...but even then they proved insufficient.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162736:0:14"
msgid "\"I don't like it, I can tell you that. That crescent...whatever it is...protruding into the sky. It doesn't belong there. It doesn't belong nowhere in this world.\" So were the guard's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Не нравится он мне, скажу как есть. Эта штуковина в форме полумесяца торчит в небо... Что бы это ни было, ему там не место. Да нигде ему места нет». Так сказал стражник. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 月の衛星「ダラガブ」内に封じられていた、古の蛮神を包んでいた拘束具の一部。第七霊災の際に、黒衣森上空に飛来した黒き蛮神の身体から剥落し、この地に堕ちてきたという。第七霊災の爪痕のひとつといえる
#. de: Als Bahamut sein kosmisches Gefängnis absprengte, um Eorzea zu verwüsten, stürzte ein Fragment davon auf den Südwald herab. Der Krater zeugt bis heute von den Schrecken der Siebten Katastrophe.
#. fr: Cette structure est un fragment de Dalamud, l'immense geôle qui emprisonnait le Primordial Bahamut. Les gens pensent qu'il s'est détaché du corps du dragon lorsqu'il a survolé la forêt de Sombrelinceul au moment du septième fléau. L'Ombrage du Météore est l'une des nombreuses traces visibles de la terrible catastrophe qui a frappé Éorzéa.
#. column 13: Fallen Neurolink
#. column 14: "I don't like it, I can tell you that. That crescent...whatever it is...protruding into the sky. It doesn't belong there. It doesn't belong nowhere in this world." So were the guard's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162736:0:15"
msgid "Coined by the learned men of Garlond Ironworks, these massive rings were used to dampen spiritual energies, preventing the focusing of power required to wield magicks. No less than five, each measuring hundreds of yalms across, were required to keep Bahamut silent for three full eras...but even then they proved insufficient."
msgstr "Учёные из Гарлондских мастерских назвали эти огромные кольца нейролинками. Они подавляли духовную энергию и не позволяли сосредоточить силу, необходимую для применения магии. Чтобы держать Бахамута взаперти, понадобилось не меньше пяти таких колец, каждое шириной в сотни ялмов. Их хватило на три полных эры — но и этого оказалось мало."

#. ja: アルダースプリングス
#. de: Erlenbrunnen
#. fr: Sources de l'Aulne
#. column 14: "So there I was, starin' out over those naked tree limbs. Was feelin' brave, so I thought I'd see just how far I could go. As it turns out? Pretty far." Such were the mountaineer's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Once a vast grove of giant alders, the flames of the Calamity reduced the area to a charred graveyard, leaving nothing of the ancient holt but its name.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162737:0:13"
msgid "Alder Springs"
msgstr "Ольховые ключи"

#. ja: ――ある山師から聞いた噂。\n心臓が強いと自負するなら、限界まで先へ進むといい。突き出した根の先っぽまで。
#. de: Ein Bergmann riet mir, bis an das Ende einer freiliegenden Wurzel zu gehen, um das stille, in Wolken gehüllte Tal zu betrachten - solange ich nur festen Schrittes und schwindelfrei sei.
#. fr: Les mineurs de la Forêt du nord aiment parfois éprouver leur courage en allant jusqu'au bout de vieilles racines suspendues dans le vide.
#. column 13: Alder Springs
#. column 15: Once a vast grove of giant alders, the flames of the Calamity reduced the area to a charred graveyard, leaving nothing of the ancient holt but its name.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162737:0:14"
msgid "\"So there I was, starin' out over those naked tree limbs. Was feelin' brave, so I thought I'd see just how far I could go. As it turns out? Pretty far.\" Such were the mountaineer's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Иду я как-то, смотрю на голые ветви. Храбрости набрался и решил проверить, как далеко смогу забраться. Оказалось — довольно далеко». Так сказал горец. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: かつては「アルダースプリング」と呼ばれるほど、多くのハンノキが茂る森林地帯だったが、第七霊災を境に状況は一変。ダラガブの破片が落着した際の衝撃で大地が引き裂かれ、今でも無残な傷跡を晒している
#. de: Einst stand in dieser Gegend ein uralter Erlenwald, doch während der Siebten Katastrophe gingen Splitter von Dalamud zu Boden und verwüsteten die Landschaft bis heute.
#. fr: Autrefois une dense forêt d'aulnes, qui lui a valu son nom, ce lieu désolé a pris son visage actuel lors du septième fléau, notamment à cause de fragments de Dalamud qui ont déchiré le sol et dont on peut encore voir la marque ici et là aujourd'hui.
#. column 13: Alder Springs
#. column 14: "So there I was, starin' out over those naked tree limbs. Was feelin' brave, so I thought I'd see just how far I could go. As it turns out? Pretty far." Such were the mountaineer's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162737:0:15"
msgid "Once a vast grove of giant alders, the flames of the Calamity reduced the area to a charred graveyard, leaving nothing of the ancient holt but its name."
msgstr "Когда-то здесь росли могучие ольхи. Но огонь Бедствия превратил лес в выжженную пустошь, и от древней рощи осталось лишь название."

#. ja: カステッルム・マリヌム
#. de: Castrum Marinum
#. fr: Castrum Marinum
#. column 14: "Say what you will about our foe, you can't deny that the architecture of their outposts has a certain ghastly charm. I would have enjoyed the sunset a while longer, but the cohort doesn't take kindly to tourists." Such were the scout's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Situated atop the roiling Rhotano Sea between Aldenard and the eastern coast of Vylbrand, Castrum Marinum serves as the southernmost outpost for the Garlean Empire's XIVth Legion. The cohort stationed on this man-made floating island is primarily tasked with the resupplying of imperial army cohorts deployed in the La Noscea and Thanalan theaters.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162738:0:13"
msgid "Castrum Marinum"
msgstr "Каструм Маринум"

#. ja: ――ある兵士から聞いた噂。\n強行偵察中、高所から望む敵補給基地は、沈みゆく陽光に照らされ不気味に光っていた。
#. de: Von einem Soldaten hörte ich, dass die Befestigungsanlage in der Abendsonne unheimlich leuchtet, wenn man sie von einem hohen Punkt aus betrachtet. Wie Recht er doch hatte.
#. fr: Les soldats en mission de reconnaissance se cachent parfois en hauteur aux avant-postes garlemaldais pour mieux espionner l'ennemi. Ils peuvent même apercevoir une place forte impériale au loin si le ciel est particulièrement dégagé, mais la vue est plutôt sinistre lorsque le soleil se couche.
#. column 13: Castrum Marinum
#. column 15: Situated atop the roiling Rhotano Sea between Aldenard and the eastern coast of Vylbrand, Castrum Marinum serves as the southernmost outpost for the Garlean Empire's XIVth Legion. The cohort stationed on this man-made floating island is primarily tasked with the resupplying of imperial army cohorts deployed in the La Noscea and Thanalan theaters.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162738:0:14"
msgid "\"Say what you will about our foe, you can't deny that the architecture of their outposts has a certain ghastly charm. I would have enjoyed the sunset a while longer, but the cohort doesn't take kindly to tourists.\" Such were the scout's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Что ни говори о враге, у их форпостов есть свой жутковатый шарм. Я бы ещё полюбовался закатом, но легионеры туристов не жалуют». Так сказал разведчик. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: アルデナード小大陸とバイルブランド島を隔てる「ロータノ海」に浮かぶ、ガレマール帝国軍の物資中継基地。その名称は、そのものズバリ「洋上の補給基地」を示す。帝国軍第XIV軍団所属の第X歩兵大隊が駐屯する
#. de: Der südlichste Versorgungsstützpunkt der Garlear thront über der Rhotano-See, die Vylbrand von Aldenard trennt. Die X. Kohorte der XIV. Legion ist hier stationiert. Sie beliefert Truppen in La Noscea und Thanalan.
#. fr: Une base de l'Empire située dans la mer de Rhotano, entre le continent d'Aldenard et l'île de Vylbrand, servant prin<shy>ci<shy>pa<shy>le<shy>ment de relais pour les ressources destinées aux autre bases garlemaldaises. Son nom signifie “place forte maritime”. La 10e unité d'infanterie de la 14e légion impériale y est stationnée.
#. column 13: Castrum Marinum
#. column 14: "Say what you will about our foe, you can't deny that the architecture of their outposts has a certain ghastly charm. I would have enjoyed the sunset a while longer, but the cohort doesn't take kindly to tourists." Such were the scout's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162738:0:15"
msgid "Situated atop the roiling Rhotano Sea between Aldenard and the eastern coast of Vylbrand, Castrum Marinum serves as the southernmost outpost for the Garlean Empire's XIVth Legion. The cohort stationed on this man-made floating island is primarily tasked with the resupplying of imperial army cohorts deployed in the La Noscea and Thanalan theaters. "
msgstr "Посреди бурного Моря Ротано, между Алденардом и восточным побережьем Вилбранда, возвышается Крепость Маринум — самый южный форпост XIV легиона Гарлеанской империи. Расположенная на искусственном плавучем острове когорта снабжает войска империи, действующие в Ла-Носкее и Таналане."

#. ja: ベスパーベイのロロリト像
#. de: Bucht des Abendsterns
#. fr: Baie des Vêpres
#. column 14: Overheard in a tavern: "Go where the wealthy go and do what they do, and sooner or later their good fortune will rub off on you. That said, the merchant wasn't too happy when I climbed atop his estate for a better view..."
#. column 15: A bustling port city strategically situated on the western coast of Thanalan and maintained using funds generously provided by Syndicate chairman Lolorito, Vesper Bay serves as a gateway in and out of sultanate-controlled lands. The colossal bronze statue in the main plaza is said to be an exact likeness of said chairman (when viewed from afar).
msgctxt "Adventure:2162739:0:13"
msgid "Vesper Bay"
msgstr "Залив Веспер"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\n金持ちの家の上で、大金持ちのまねごとを。これで金運が増せばいいのだが。
#. de: Angeblich soll es den Gilbeutel füllen, wenn man sich in dieser malerischen Stadt auf das Dach der Residenz eines wohlhabenden Geschäftsmannes stellt, um einen noch wohlhabenderen Geschäftsmann nachzuahmen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'il fait beau, on voit parfois des petits malins profitant de leur temps libre l'après-midi pour aller se percher sur l'une des maisons d'un port animé, et imiter un des plus riches marchands uldiens.
#. column 13: Vesper Bay
#. column 15: A bustling port city strategically situated on the western coast of Thanalan and maintained using funds generously provided by Syndicate chairman Lolorito, Vesper Bay serves as a gateway in and out of sultanate-controlled lands. The colossal bronze statue in the main plaza is said to be an exact likeness of said chairman (when viewed from afar).
msgctxt "Adventure:2162739:0:14"
msgid "Overheard in a tavern: \"Go where the wealthy go and do what they do, and sooner or later their good fortune will rub off on you. That said, the merchant wasn't too happy when I climbed atop his estate for a better view...\""
msgstr "Слух, подслушанный в таверне: «Делай, как богачи, бывай там же, где они, и, может, их удача перейдёт к тебе. Правда, купец не обрадовался, когда я забрался на крышу его поместья, чтобы посмотреть получше...»"

#. ja: ウルダハの海の玄関口として建設された港町。中央広場の銅像は、アルデナード商会ロロリト会長を模したもの。港湾施設の整備に莫大な費用を投じたことを称えたものだが、その容姿を巡っては美化しすぎとの声もある
#. de: Ul'dahs Tor zu Eorzeas Märkten. Der Vorsitzende der Ostaldenard-Handelsgesellschaft, Lolorito, hat hier viel Geld investiert. Ihm zu Ehren errichtete man eine Statue, die viele allerdings für zu schmeichelhaft halten.
#. fr: La baie des Vêpres est le port principal du commerce maritime uldien. Une statue à l'effigie du seigneur Lolorito, l'homme à la tête de la Firme du commerce de l'Aldenard oriental, a été érigée en son centre en signe de gratitude pour sa généreuse par<shy>ti<shy>ci<shy>pa<shy>tion à la con<shy>struc<shy>tion des docks. Elle ne fait pas l'unanimité cependant, et certains pensent qu'il est exagérément embelli.
#. column 13: Vesper Bay
#. column 14: Overheard in a tavern: "Go where the wealthy go and do what they do, and sooner or later their good fortune will rub off on you. That said, the merchant wasn't too happy when I climbed atop his estate for a better view..."
msgctxt "Adventure:2162739:0:15"
msgid "A bustling port city strategically situated on the western coast of Thanalan and maintained using funds generously provided by Syndicate chairman Lolorito, Vesper Bay serves as a gateway in and out of sultanate-controlled lands. The colossal bronze statue in the main plaza is said to be an exact likeness of said chairman (when viewed from afar)."
msgstr "Залив Веспер — оживлённый порт на западном побережье Таналана и важные ворота в земли султаната и обратно. Его содержат на щедрые средства Лолорито, главы Синдиката. Говорят, огромная бронзовая статуя на главной площади — его точное подобие. Если смотреть издалека."

#. ja: ブラックブラッシュ停留所
#. de: Kohlenstaub-Bahnhof
#. fr: Gare de Roncenoire
#. column 14: "A modern marvel she may be, but a right bitch to keep runnin'. I couldn't tell you how many hours I've spent surveyin' from all directions and altitudes. You can have the view, just give me a good night's sleep!" Such were the railroad man's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: A marvel of modern innovation, the steam engine has transformed the mining industry, increasing efficiency and profits thrice over. It has also led to the transformation of what was once a thinly manned aetheryte outpost into a thriving crossroads of labor and commerce─a new pillar to support the thriving Ul'dahn economy.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162740:0:13"
msgid "Black Brush Station"
msgstr "Станция Чёрная щётка"

#. ja: ――ある鉄道員から聞いた噂。\n設備の保守点検は辛い。夜半までかかり、高所から施設を点検することもある。
#. de: Die Bahninspekteure hier haben es wahrlich nicht leicht. Manchmal werden sie sogar mitternachts die Hänge hinauf gejagt, um von oben zu überprüfen, ob alles mit rechten Dingen zugeht. Und erst all der Staub.
#. fr: Les ouvriers de Roncenoire sont parfois obligés de vérifier l'état des pylônes autour de la gare durant une tempête de poussière pour s'assurer qu'ils ne sont pas endommagés, et ce même la nuit. Imaginez-vous un peu là-haut !
#. column 13: Black Brush Station
#. column 15: A marvel of modern innovation, the steam engine has transformed the mining industry, increasing efficiency and profits thrice over. It has also led to the transformation of what was once a thinly manned aetheryte outpost into a thriving crossroads of labor and commerce─a new pillar to support the thriving Ul'dahn economy.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162740:0:14"
msgid "\"A modern marvel she may be, but a right bitch to keep runnin'. I couldn't tell you how many hours I've spent surveyin' from all directions and altitudes. You can have the view, just give me a good night's sleep!\" Such were the railroad man's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Может, она и чудо техники, но поддерживать её в рабочем состоянии — та ещё морока. Не сосчитать, сколько часов я потратил на осмотры с разных сторон и высот. Забирайте себе вид, только дайте мне наконец выспаться!» Так сказал железнодорожник. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 以前は銅刃団の駐屯地に過ぎなかったが、アマジナ鉱山社が鉄道を敷設し、停留所を設けたことで様相が一変した。採掘された鉱石を製錬するための最新式高熱炉が設置され、ウルダハの産業を支える働きを見せている
#. de: Ursprünglich bloß ein Stützpunkt der Messingklingen, floriert die Siedlung seit dem Anschluss an das Schienennetz der Amajina Bergbau AG. Mit einem modernen Schmelzofen werden die Bodenschätze direkt verarbeitet.
#. fr: Roncenoire était autrefois une simple garnison des lames de cuivre, mais depuis la con<shy>struc<shy>tion d'un service ferroviaire par Amajina et Fils et d'une gare dans la région, l'endroit a rapidement changé et est devenu un lieu important pour l'industrie métallurgique d'Ul'dah.
#. column 13: Black Brush Station
#. column 14: "A modern marvel she may be, but a right bitch to keep runnin'. I couldn't tell you how many hours I've spent surveyin' from all directions and altitudes. You can have the view, just give me a good night's sleep!" Such were the railroad man's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162740:0:15"
msgid "A marvel of modern innovation, the steam engine has transformed the mining industry, increasing efficiency and profits thrice over. It has also led to the transformation of what was once a thinly manned aetheryte outpost into a thriving crossroads of labor and commerce─a new pillar to support the thriving Ul'dahn economy."
msgstr "Чудо современной техники — паровой двигатель — в корне изменило горное дело, утроив его эффективность и прибыль. А ещё благодаря ему прежний безлюдный форпост у эфирита превратился в оживлённый центр труда и торговли, став новой опорой процветающей экономики Ульды."

#. ja: ナル大門
#. de: Tor des Nald
#. fr: Porte de Nald
#. column 14: Overheard on the streets: "Lost me job, me family─and any coin I could spend to drown me sorrows. And so I stood atop the canvas, looking out over the wasteland of me life."
#. column 15: One of three main portals accessible by the general populace, the Gate of Nald is wide enough for two fully burdened chocobo carriages to enter abreast and still leave room for the flanking gateguards. Her Royal Majesty Nanamo Ul Namo has commanded that the portcullis remain open night and day, so as to welcome all who would partake of Ul'dah's wonders.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162741:0:13"
msgid "Gate of Nald"
msgstr "Врата Нальда"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\n仕事も酒を飲む金もないときは、ぼーっとするしかない。布の上で、荒野を眺めながら。
#. de: Ein Trinker riet mir, wenn ich weder Arbeit noch genügend Geld für die Taverne hätte, ließe es sich auf dem Stoffdach hervorragend entspannen. Die umliegende Wildnis böte einen herrlichen Anblick.
#. fr: Pour les enfants, les vrais plaisirs sont les plus simples. Jamais je n'oublierai l'émerveillement sur le visage de ces jeunes réfugiés qui regardaient défiler les caravanes de marchandises, assis sur les toiles de leurs tentes.
#. column 13: Gate of Nald
#. column 15: One of three main portals accessible by the general populace, the Gate of Nald is wide enough for two fully burdened chocobo carriages to enter abreast and still leave room for the flanking gateguards. Her Royal Majesty Nanamo Ul Namo has commanded that the portcullis remain open night and day, so as to welcome all who would partake of Ul'dah's wonders.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162741:0:14"
msgid "Overheard on the streets: \"Lost me job, me family─and any coin I could spend to drown me sorrows. And so I stood atop the canvas, looking out over the wasteland of me life.\""
msgstr "Слух, подслушанный на улице: «Потерял работу, семью — да и последние деньги, чтоб залить горе. Вот и стоял на полотнище, глядя на пустошь своей жизни»."

#. ja: ウルダハの主門のひとつ。同都市の守護神「ナルザル」のうち、生者の世界を司る「ナル神」の名が付けられている。交易都市だけに、商品を満載した2台のチョコボキャリッジがすれ違えるほど、その門の幅は広い
#. de: Eines der Haupttore Ul'dahs ist Nald geweiht, dem diesseitigen Aspekt der dualen Gottheit Nald'thal. Das Tor ist so breit, dass es zwei Chocobo-Kutschen nebeneinander passieren können.
#. fr: Cette porte est l'une des trois entrées principales d'Ul'dah. Suffisamment large pour y faire passer deux caravanes en même temps (Cité du commerce oblige), elle a été baptisée ainsi en l'honneur de la divinité tutélaire de la nation. Nald est le dieu qui veille sur le monde des vivants.
#. column 13: Gate of Nald
#. column 14: Overheard on the streets: "Lost me job, me family─and any coin I could spend to drown me sorrows. And so I stood atop the canvas, looking out over the wasteland of me life."
msgctxt "Adventure:2162741:0:15"
msgid "One of three main portals accessible by the general populace, the Gate of Nald is wide enough for two fully burdened chocobo carriages to enter abreast and still leave room for the flanking gateguards. Her Royal Majesty Nanamo Ul Namo has commanded that the portcullis remain open night and day, so as to welcome all who would partake of Ul'dah's wonders."
msgstr "Врата Нальда — одни из главных ворот Ульды. Они названы в честь Нальда, одного из двух покровителей города, который правит миром живых. Город торговый, так что ворота широки: рядом могут проехать две гружёные кареты с чокобо."

#. ja: バーニングウォール
#. de: Der Feuerwall
#. fr: Le Mur incandescent
#. column 14: Overheard in an alehouse: "Standing atop the crystal affords you the best view of the place, if you're brave enough to make the climb..."
#. column 15: Once an unscalable precipice severing eastern Thanalan from the Grand Wake, the Burning Wall earned its name for the deep-red glow it would emit each evening as the sun set. Toppled by the Calamity, that cliff no longer exists─in its place a queer forest of crystalline sentinels and malformed creatures shunned by nature itself.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162742:0:13"
msgid "The Burning Wall"
msgstr "Пылающая стена"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\n絶景を見たと自慢したいなら、クリスタルの上から辺りを一望するといいだろう。
#. de: Bei einem kühlen Bier erzählt man sich gerne, dass die Aussicht hier am schönsten sei, wenn man seinen Blick oben von einer Kristallspitze in die Runde schweifen lässt.
#. fr: Il paraît qu'un cristal faisant face à une presqu'île est l'endroit idéal pour se baigner dans la lumière d'un après-midi ensoleillé, et admirer le paysage alentour.
#. column 13: The Burning Wall
#. column 15: Once an unscalable precipice severing eastern Thanalan from the Grand Wake, the Burning Wall earned its name for the deep-red glow it would emit each evening as the sun set. Toppled by the Calamity, that cliff no longer exists─in its place a queer forest of crystalline sentinels and malformed creatures shunned by nature itself.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162742:0:14"
msgid "Overheard in an alehouse: \"Standing atop the crystal affords you the best view of the place, if you're brave enough to make the climb...\""
msgstr "Слух, подслушанный в пивной: «С вершины кристалла отсюда вид лучше всего. Если хватит смелости забраться...»"

#. ja: 月の衛星「ダラガブ」から剥落した破片が地脈を貫いた結果、大規模なエーテル流出が発生。これが結晶化し、炎のようにうねった形状のまま偏属性クリスタルとして固着した。第七霊災の壮絶さを今に伝える光景である
#. de: Ein Bruchstück des Mondes Dalamud riss den Erdboden auf und setzte Unmengen an Äther frei. Dieser kristallisierte flammenförmig und erzählt so selbst heute noch eindrucksvoll von der Siebten Katastrophe.
#. fr: Lorsque des morceaux de Dalamud se sont violemment écrasés dans la région, de nombreux courants éthérés souterrains se sont écoulés vers la surface pour finalement se cristalliser. Leur forme allongée et leur couleur rappelant celles des flammes ont donné son nom au Mur incandescent. Ces cristaux sont un rappel terrible de la violence du septième fléau.
#. column 13: The Burning Wall
#. column 14: Overheard in an alehouse: "Standing atop the crystal affords you the best view of the place, if you're brave enough to make the climb..."
msgctxt "Adventure:2162742:0:15"
msgid "Once an unscalable precipice severing eastern Thanalan from the Grand Wake, the Burning Wall earned its name for the deep-red glow it would emit each evening as the sun set. Toppled by the Calamity, that cliff no longer exists─in its place a queer forest of crystalline sentinels and malformed creatures shunned by nature itself."
msgstr "Когда-то неприступная скала отделяла восточную часть Таналана от Великой расщелины. По вечерам на закате она отливала густым красным светом — отсюда и название «Горящая стена». Бедствие обрушило скалу, и теперь на её месте раскинулся диковинный лес из кристаллических изваяний и уродливых созданий, отвергнутых самой природой."

#. ja: ゴールドバザー
#. de: Goldbasar
#. fr: Bazar doré
#. column 14: "A ghost town? Hah! Mark my words, I'll make my fortune there. When the sun is high, I climb atop the fencing and survey the land for untapped veins of ore." Such were the miner's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Once a waypoint for traders making the journey between Gridania and Ul'dah, the rise of settlements such as Camp Drybone and Highbridge have all but rendered the once prospering hamlet a ghost town. Rumors of mythril deposits in the nearby mountains and treasure in the ruins of the Invisible City, however, may work to rekindle this dying ember.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162743:0:13"
msgid "The Golden Bazaar"
msgstr "Золотой базар"

#. ja: ――ある採掘師から聞いた噂。\n寂れた場所で狙うのは一攫千金。柵の上に登り、日が高いうちに試掘場所を探すらしい。
#. de: Fleißige Minenarbeiter suchen ihr Glück in luftiger Höhe. Vom Palisadenzaun aus halten sie Ausschau nach vielversprechenden Erzadern. Davon hält sie auch die sengende Mittagshitze nicht ab. Der Ruf des Goldes ist zu verlockend.
#. fr: Certains mineurs aiment monter sur l'échafaudage à l'entrée de la mine d'un petit village pour profiter de la lumière du soleil matinal, avant de commencer leur longue journée souterraine.
#. column 13: The Golden Bazaar
#. column 15: Once a waypoint for traders making the journey between Gridania and Ul'dah, the rise of settlements such as Camp Drybone and Highbridge have all but rendered the once prospering hamlet a ghost town. Rumors of mythril deposits in the nearby mountains and treasure in the ruins of the Invisible City, however, may work to rekindle this dying ember.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162743:0:14"
msgid "\"A ghost town? Hah! Mark my words, I'll make my fortune there. When the sun is high, I climb atop the fencing and survey the land for untapped veins of ore.\" Such were the miner's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Город-призрак? Ха! Вот увидите, я там разбогатею. В полдень забираюсь на ограду и высматриваю в земле неразработанные жилы руды». Так сказал шахтёр. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: ウルダハのハムレット。かつては交易の中継地として市が立ち賑わっていたが、東方交易の中断のあおりを受け寂れてしまった。周辺一帯に優良な霊銀鉱床が眠っているとの噂があり、鉱業での振興が期待されているようだ
#. de: Seit Stilllegung der östlichen Handelsroute ist vom einstigen Glanz dieses ul'dhischen Weilers nicht mehr viel zu spüren. Aufschwung erhofft man sich von angeblich reichen Erzadern, die hier im Gestein schlummern sollen.
#. fr: Ce village était autrefois un centre animé du négoce uldien, mais il dépérit lentement depuis l'arrêt du commerce avec l'Orient. Les habitants espèrent cependant un renouveau d'activité si les rumeurs sur la présence de riches filons de mithril dans la région s'avèrent exactes.
#. column 13: The Golden Bazaar
#. column 14: "A ghost town? Hah! Mark my words, I'll make my fortune there. When the sun is high, I climb atop the fencing and survey the land for untapped veins of ore." Such were the miner's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162743:0:15"
msgid "Once a waypoint for traders making the journey between Gridania and Ul'dah, the rise of settlements such as Camp Drybone and Highbridge have all but rendered the once prospering hamlet a ghost town. Rumors of mythril deposits in the nearby mountains and treasure in the ruins of the Invisible City, however, may work to rekindle this dying ember."
msgstr "Когда-то здесь останавливались торговцы, ездившие между Гриданией и Ульдой. Но с появлением поселений вроде Лагеря Сухой Кости и Высокого моста деревушка почти опустела. Впрочем, слухи о залежах мириала в окрестных горах и сокровищах в руинах Невидимого города могут раздуть угасающий уголёк новой жизни."

#. ja: ザルの祠
#. de: Thals Rast
#. fr: Sursis de Thal
#. column 14: "Those who do not pay proper obeisance will find their fortunes all too fleeting. Those who do will feel the tears of mercy washing over them like the pouring rains." Such were the initiate's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Overseer of wealth in the afterlife, proper obeisance to the Trader Thal is required for those who wish to take belongings accumulated in this world to the hereafter. Thal's Respite is oft used by stout devotees of the Order of Nald'thal as a place of fasting and prayer, but its distance from Ul'dah prevents all but the most affluent from making the journey.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162744:0:13"
msgid "Thal's Respite"
msgstr "Прибежище Тала"

#. ja: ――ある聖職者から聞いた噂。\n来世の利益を得たいなら、静かに祈るといい。豪雨のような懺悔の涙が、魂を救うとのこと。
#. de: Wer auf Wohlstand im Jenseits hofft, muss sich gut mit Thal stellen. Wenn einem ins Gebet vertieft die Reue wie Regen von den Wangen tropft, ist die Seele der Rettung einen Schritt näher.
#. fr: Il est toujours conseillé d'offrir une prière à Thal avant de pénétrer dans son sanctuaire. Un torrent de larmes dans l'obscurité, né d'un repentir sincère, ne peut que plaire au dieu du monde des morts.
#. column 13: Thal's Respite
#. column 15: Overseer of wealth in the afterlife, proper obeisance to the Trader Thal is required for those who wish to take belongings accumulated in this world to the hereafter. Thal's Respite is oft used by stout devotees of the Order of Nald'thal as a place of fasting and prayer, but its distance from Ul'dah prevents all but the most affluent from making the journey.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162744:0:14"
msgid "\"Those who do not pay proper obeisance will find their fortunes all too fleeting. Those who do will feel the tears of mercy washing over them like the pouring rains.\" Such were the initiate's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Не воздашь почестей как следует — богатство быстро утечёт сквозь пальцы. А кто воздаст, того омоют милосердные слёзы, будто ливень». Так сказал послушник. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 双子の神「ナルザル」のうち、死後の世界を司る「ザル神」を祀る祠。断食祈祷を行うための「ナル・ザル教団」の施設が併設されている。かつては多くの巡礼者が訪れたが、近年では訪れる者の数は減っているようだ
#. de: Thal wacht über den Wohlstand im Jenseits und ist daher die erste Anlaufstelle für reiche Ul'dahner, die an diesem Ort zu fasten und zu beten pflegen. Wäre der Ort nur nicht so abgelegen.
#. fr: Cet autel est dédié à Thal, le dieu du monde des morts et jumeau de Nald. L'ordre de Nald'thal y a fait construire des ins<shy>tal<shy>la<shy>tions destinées à ses membres pour qu'ils puissent jeûner et prier. Les pèlerins visitaient fréquemment l'endroit autrefois, mais leur nombre s'est considérablement réduit ces dernières années.
#. column 13: Thal's Respite
#. column 14: "Those who do not pay proper obeisance will find their fortunes all too fleeting. Those who do will feel the tears of mercy washing over them like the pouring rains." Such were the initiate's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162744:0:15"
msgid "Overseer of wealth in the afterlife, proper obeisance to the Trader Thal is required for those who wish to take belongings accumulated in this world to the hereafter. Thal's Respite is oft used by stout devotees of the Order of Nald'thal as a place of fasting and prayer, but its distance from Ul'dah prevents all but the most affluent from making the journey."
msgstr "Тал, Торговец, властвует над богатствами загробного мира. Чтобы забрать накопленное в этой жизни с собой, нужно воздать ему должные почести. Верные последователи ордена Налд'тала часто приходят в Пристанище Тала поститься и молиться, но из-за дальнего пути из Ульды добраться сюда могут лишь самые состоятельные."

#. ja: ナルの祠
#. de: Nalds Besinnung
#. fr: Thébaïde de Nald
#. column 14: "Those who do not pay proper obeisance will find fortune ever elusive. Those who do will see the fog lifted, and know the joys of abundance." Such were the initiate's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Overseer of wealth and commerce upon the corporeal plane, it is believed that through fervent worship of the Trader Nald, one will reap immeasurable fortune in one's living years. Prince and pauper alike once made pilgrimages to this remote place of prayer in search of prosperity...until, that is, Milvaneth Sacrarium opened a new (toll-based) temple within Ul'dah.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162745:0:13"
msgid "Nald's Reflection"
msgstr "Отражение Нальда"

#. ja: ――ある聖職者から聞いた噂。\n現世の利益を得たいなら、盛大に祈るといい。霧中に彷徨う魂は、喜捨によって救われるそうだ。
#. de: Wer auf Wohlstand im Diesseits hofft, muss sich gut mit Nald stellen. Gebete werden die durch den Nebel der weltlichen Verblendung vom Weg abgekommene Seele erretten.
#. fr: Il est toujours conseillé d'offrir une prière à Nald avant de pénétrer dans son sanctuaire. Les âmes égarées dans un brouillard d'incertitude seront peut-être guidées par la lumière d'une nouvelle aube.
#. column 13: Nald's Reflection
#. column 15: Overseer of wealth and commerce upon the corporeal plane, it is believed that through fervent worship of the Trader Nald, one will reap immeasurable fortune in one's living years. Prince and pauper alike once made pilgrimages to this remote place of prayer in search of prosperity...until, that is, Milvaneth Sacrarium opened a new (toll-based) temple within Ul'dah.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162745:0:14"
msgid "\"Those who do not pay proper obeisance will find fortune ever elusive. Those who do will see the fog lifted, and know the joys of abundance.\" Such were the initiate's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Не воздашь почестей как следует — удача будет ускользать. А кто воздаст, тот увидит, как туман рассеивается, и познает радость изобилия». Так сказал послушник. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 双子の神「ナルザル」のうち、現世を司る「ナル神」を祀る祠。詣でれば現世利益があるという話だが、富裕層は都市内の「ミルバネス礼拝堂」で販売している護符を買うだけで満足してしまうため、巡礼する者は稀である
#. de: Nald gebietet über das Diesseits. Er soll seinen Anhängern zu Reichtum verhelfen, doch viele Kaufleute begnügen sich mittlerweile damit, Talismane in der Minerva-Kapelle in Ul'dah zu erstehen.
#. fr: Cet autel est dédié à Nald, le dieu du monde des vivants et jumeau de Thal. Visiter l'endroit porterait chance dans les affaires commerciales, mais les riches marchands de la Cité se contentant simplement d'acheter des talismans au sanctuaire de Milvaneth à Ul'dah, les pèlerins sont rares.
#. column 13: Nald's Reflection
#. column 14: "Those who do not pay proper obeisance will find fortune ever elusive. Those who do will see the fog lifted, and know the joys of abundance." Such were the initiate's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162745:0:15"
msgid "Overseer of wealth and commerce upon the corporeal plane, it is believed that through fervent worship of the Trader Nald, one will reap immeasurable fortune in one's living years. Prince and pauper alike once made pilgrimages to this remote place of prayer in search of prosperity...until, that is, Milvaneth Sacrarium opened a new (toll-based) temple within Ul'dah."
msgstr "Считается, что усердное поклонение Нальду, Торговцу, который ведает богатством и торговлей в мире живых, сулит несметные богатства. Некогда сюда, в далёкое святилище, за удачей приходили и принцы, и бедняки... пока в Ульде не открылось Святилище Милванет, где продают защитные амулеты."

#. ja: ザハラク戦陣
#. de: Zahar'ak
#. fr: Zahar'ak
#. column 14: "Some call the sight bleak, but to me it's a thing of beauty. The winds pound away at the hills, but strong we stand─our gaze locked on our foe." Such were the sentry's words, and I would see what he saw.
#. column 15: Loosely translated as “land of perseverance,” Zahar'ak is a forward stronghold for the Amalj'aa host based in Zanr'ak. The beast tribe believes the scorched plains of Thanalan to be hallowed ground blessed by the cleansing flames of their primal deity, Ifrit, and as such are intent on driving from the land all whom they deem invaders.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162746:0:13"
msgid "Zahar'ak"
msgstr "Захар'ак"

#. ja: ――ある兵士から聞いた噂。\n荒野の風は岩をも削る。風化した柱状の岩の上で、ひたすらに敵陣を監視するらしい。
#. de: Der Wüstenwind ist geduldiger als jede Armee und besiegt sogar Stein. Davon zeugt ein säulenartig geschliffener Felsen, von dessen Spitze man den Feind bei klarem Himmel vortrefflich im Blick hat.
#. fr: Un pilier de pierre face au camp amalj'aa est un lieu de choix pour observer les faits et gestes des hommes-lézards. Et la vue est particulièrement belle lorsque le soleil se lève.
#. column 13: Zahar'ak
#. column 15: Loosely translated as “land of perseverance,” Zahar'ak is a forward stronghold for the Amalj'aa host based in Zanr'ak. The beast tribe believes the scorched plains of Thanalan to be hallowed ground blessed by the cleansing flames of their primal deity, Ifrit, and as such are intent on driving from the land all whom they deem invaders.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162746:0:14"
msgid "\"Some call the sight bleak, but to me it's a thing of beauty. The winds pound away at the hills, but strong we stand─our gaze locked on our foe.\" Such were the sentry's words, and I would see what he saw."
msgstr "«Кому-то этот вид кажется унылым, а я нахожу его прекрасным. Ветер точит холмы, но мы стоим крепко и не сводим глаз с врага». Так сказал часовой. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 「不退転」を意味するアマルジャ語で呼ばれている、アマルジャ軍の戦陣。彼らは南ザナラーンのザンラク一帯を、焔神「イフリート」によって焼き清められた聖地と考えており、歴史的にウルダハと衝突を繰り返してきた
#. de: In der Sprache der Amalj'aa bedeutet Zahar'ak „Unbeugsamkeit“. Für die Echsen ist die Region Zanr'ak durch Ifrits Flammen geheiligtes Land. Deshalb versuchen sie, die Ul'dahner von dort fernzuhalten.
#. fr: Le nom de ce camp de l'armée amalj'aa signifie “résolution in<shy>é<shy>bran<shy>la<shy>ble” dans la langue de ces hommes-bêtes. Ils croient que Zanr'ak est une région sacrée, purifiée par le feu de leur dieu, le Primordial Ifrit, d'où le conflit territorial avec Ul'dah.
#. column 13: Zahar'ak
#. column 14: "Some call the sight bleak, but to me it's a thing of beauty. The winds pound away at the hills, but strong we stand─our gaze locked on our foe." Such were the sentry's words, and I would see what he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162746:0:15"
msgid "Loosely translated as “land of perseverance,” Zahar'ak is a forward stronghold for the Amalj'aa host based in Zanr'ak. The beast tribe believes the scorched plains of Thanalan to be hallowed ground blessed by the cleansing flames of their primal deity, Ifrit, and as such are intent on driving from the land all whom they deem invaders."
msgstr "Захар'ак на языке амалджа означает «земля стойкости». Это передовая крепость воинства, обосновавшегося в Занраке. Здешние зверолюды считают выжженные равнины Таналан священной землёй, очищенной пламенем их праймального божества Ифрита, и стремятся изгнать всех, кого считают захватчиками."

#. ja: ビエルゴズ・ストライク
#. de: Byregots Schlag
#. fr: Foreuse de Byregot
#. column 14: "After a fortnight of wandering, I found myself under the searing sun, looking out upon the ruins of Allag. It was then I swore to myself: I will not succumb─not this day." Such were the wayfarer's words, and I would see what he saw.
#. column 15: According to the Sons of Saint Coinach, the Sagolii Desert was once a verdant sea of lush plains capable of sustaining great civilizations, as is evidenced by the ruins recently discovered in the area. How such a place devolved into a lifeless desert remains a mystery, but recent disaster tells us an ancient calamity is the likely culprit.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162747:0:13"
msgid "The Sagolii Desert"
msgstr "Пустыня Саголии"

#. ja: ――ある採掘師から聞いた噂。\n強烈な日射しと廃熱にやられヘタばりそうだが、古代アラグの遺跡は宝の山だ。
#. de: Ein Minenarbeiter klagte mir sein Leid, dass ihm bei der Gluthitze oft die Zunge aus dem Hals hinge, doch die allagischen Ruinen und die darin verborgenen Schätze wären die Mühe wert.
#. fr: Vue de loin, cette machine semble extrêmement résistante et fiable... mais les apparences sont parfois trompeuses. Malgré son aspect robuste, elle souffre de la chaleur torride du désert au même titre que les hommes (et parfois plus).
#. column 13: The Sagolii Desert
#. column 15: According to the Sons of Saint Coinach, the Sagolii Desert was once a verdant sea of lush plains capable of sustaining great civilizations, as is evidenced by the ruins recently discovered in the area. How such a place devolved into a lifeless desert remains a mystery, but recent disaster tells us an ancient calamity is the likely culprit.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162747:0:14"
msgid "\"After a fortnight of wandering, I found myself under the searing sun, looking out upon the ruins of Allag. It was then I swore to myself: I will not succumb─not this day.\" Such were the wayfarer's words, and I would see what he saw."
msgstr "«Две недели бродил — и вот стою под палящим солнцем, смотрю на руины Аллага. Тогда я поклялся себе: не сдамся. Не сегодня». Так сказал путник. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: アマジナ鉱山社が、砂に埋没した古代アラグ時代の遺跡を掘り起こすために設置した大型採掘機。工神「ビエルゴ」の大槌による一撃に見立て、勇ましい名が付けられているが、熱に弱い採掘機はトラブル続きのようだ
#. de: Mit der Maschine lässt die Amajina Bergbau AG in der Wüste nach allagischen Ruinen graben. Dafür, dass sie nach dem göttlichen Erbauer benannt ist, erweist sie sich ganz schön anfällig gegen Überhitzung.
#. fr: Cette immense machine de forage a été construite par la société des Bons filons d'Amajina et Fils dans le but de déterrer les vestiges de l'ancien empire d'Allag. Conçue pour frapper le sol tel le puissant maillet du dieu dont elle tire le nom, les nombreux problèmes de surchauffe qu'elle rencontre rendent son utilisation par<shy>ti<shy>cu<shy>liè<shy>rement délicate.
#. column 13: The Sagolii Desert
#. column 14: "After a fortnight of wandering, I found myself under the searing sun, looking out upon the ruins of Allag. It was then I swore to myself: I will not succumb─not this day." Such were the wayfarer's words, and I would see what he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162747:0:15"
msgid "According to the Sons of Saint Coinach, the Sagolii Desert was once a verdant sea of lush plains capable of sustaining great civilizations, as is evidenced by the ruins recently discovered in the area. How such a place devolved into a lifeless desert remains a mystery, but recent disaster tells us an ancient calamity is the likely culprit."
msgstr "По словам Сыновей святого Койнаха, когда-то пустыня Саголии была зелёной равниной, способной прокормить великие цивилизации. Об этом говорят недавно найденные здесь руины. Почему цветущий край превратился в безжизненную пустыню, неизвестно, но недавняя катастрофа наводит на мысль, что причиной могло стать древнее бедствие."

#. ja: カルン埋没寺院
#. de: Versunkener Tempel von Qarn
#. fr: Temple enseveli de Qarn
#. column 14: Overheard in a tavern: "...Ah, a fellow antiquarian! There's a slanted stone slab that affords you the best vantage point of the ruins."
#. column 15: Most scholars of ancient Belah'dian civilization claim this twisting labyrinth of complex chambers to be a place of worship dedicated to the sun goddess, Azeyma. Recent diggings, however, have uncovered older chambers buried beneath the new containing relics not of the Sixth Astral Era, suggesting that the temple may have been built by a different people.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162748:0:13"
msgid "The Sunken Temple of Qarn"
msgstr "Затонувший храм Карна"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\n当時の構造を調べるには、傾いた遺構の上に登って確認するのが手っ取り早い。
#. de: Die Struktur dieser lange Zeit vergessenen heiligen Stätte erkennt man Gerüchten zufolge am besten, wenn man den schiefen Turm erklimmt und sie von seinem Dach aus betrachtet.
#. fr: Il paraît que des archéologues ont trouvé un endroit parfait pour étudier la structure de certaines ruines, lorsque le ciel est dégagé et le soleil suffisamment haut. Ce serait une ancienne tour brisée. Plus d'un se serait blessé en glissant du toit cependant.
#. column 13: The Sunken Temple of Qarn
#. column 15: Most scholars of ancient Belah'dian civilization claim this twisting labyrinth of complex chambers to be a place of worship dedicated to the sun goddess, Azeyma. Recent diggings, however, have uncovered older chambers buried beneath the new containing relics not of the Sixth Astral Era, suggesting that the temple may have been built by a different people.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162748:0:14"
msgid "Overheard in a tavern: \"...Ah, a fellow antiquarian! There's a slanted stone slab that affords you the best vantage point of the ruins.\""
msgstr "Слух, подслушанный в таверне: «А, коллега-антиквар! Там есть наклонная каменная плита, с которой на руины открывается лучший вид»."

#. ja: 古代都市「ベラフディア」時代の遺跡。ベラフディアで守護神として崇められていた太陽の女神「アーゼマ」を祀る神殿であり、歴代の王たちが長年の時をかけて、威信を示すために増改築を繰り返してきたようだ
#. de: Eine belah'dische Ruine, die der Sonnengöttin Azeyma geweiht ist. Mehrere Herrscher brauchte es, um diese prachtvolle Anlage, die ein Zeichen unerschütterlichen Glaubens ist, zu vollenden.
#. fr: Ce temple est un vestige de l'ancienne cité de Belah'dia, dédié à la déesse du soleil Azeyma, vénérée par les Belahdiens. Leurs rois ont ajouté au fil des générations de nouvelles sections plus magnifiques les unes que les autres, pro<shy>ba<shy>ble<shy>ment pour afficher leur importance plutôt que par piété.
#. column 13: The Sunken Temple of Qarn
#. column 14: Overheard in a tavern: "...Ah, a fellow antiquarian! There's a slanted stone slab that affords you the best vantage point of the ruins."
msgctxt "Adventure:2162748:0:15"
msgid "Most scholars of ancient Belah'dian civilization claim this twisting labyrinth of complex chambers to be a place of worship dedicated to the sun goddess, Azeyma. Recent diggings, however, have uncovered older chambers buried beneath the new containing relics not of the Sixth Astral Era, suggesting that the temple may have been built by a different people."
msgstr "Большинство учёных, изучающих древнюю цивилизацию Белад'дии, считают этот лабиринт запутанных залов храмом богини солнца Азимы. Однако недавние раскопки открыли под новыми помещениями более древние, где нашли реликвии эпохи, предшествовавшей Шестой астральной эре. Возможно, храм построил другой народ."

#. ja: ミノタウロスマルム
#. de: Minotauren-Malm
#. fr: Malm du Minotaure
#. column 14: "Beads of sweat flying from their broad shoulders, massive muscles tightening and loosening─no, I've not seen a finer sight in all the realm." Such were the warrioress's words, and I would see what she saw.
#. column 15: Local legend has that long ago, a young goatherd leading his pack to water at Forgotten Springs was set upon and chased a full malm through these caves by a minotaur. There has yet to be a second sighting of the creature, but the stories are enough to frighten away most who would consider passage through this trading post used by the Seventy-Seven Caravans.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162749:0:13"
msgid "Minotaur Malm"
msgstr "Лига Минотавра"

#. ja: ――ある兵士から聞いた噂。\n熱波如きで訓練を休むのは愚か者。真の漢は、気合で乗り越え、肉体を鍛え続ける。その姿こそ絶景。
#. de: Der Soldat vertrat vehement die Meinung, bei Gluthitze dürfe man sich nicht schonen, sondern man müsse sich voller Entschlossenheit zusammenreißen und umso härter trainieren.
#. fr: Les soldats, les vrais, ne craignent pas la morsure du soleil. Ils s'exercent jour et nuit pour être prêts lorsque l'heure de l'ultime bataille arrivera. Les regarder ainsi s'entraîner a quelque chose de motivant.
#. column 13: Minotaur Malm
#. column 15: Local legend has that long ago, a young goatherd leading his pack to water at Forgotten Springs was set upon and chased a full malm through these caves by a minotaur. There has yet to be a second sighting of the creature, but the stories are enough to frighten away most who would consider passage through this trading post used by the Seventy-Seven Caravans.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162749:0:14"
msgid "\"Beads of sweat flying from their broad shoulders, massive muscles tightening and loosening─no, I've not seen a finer sight in all the realm.\" Such were the warrioress's words, and I would see what she saw."
msgstr "«Капли пота летят с широких плеч, могучие мышцы то напрягаются, то расслабляются... Нет, прекраснее зрелища во всём мире не сыскать». Так сказала воительница. Я решил посмотреть на всё её глазами."

#. ja: 東アルデナード商会などの大資本に対抗するために、中小規模の旅商人たちが結成した「隊商互助会」の交易所。危険でリスクが高い「サゴリー砂漠」方面との交易拠点として、第七霊災後に設営されたという
#. de: Um das Monopol der Ostaldenard-Handelsgesellschaft zu brechen, gründeten kleinere Händler die 77 Karawanen. Dieser Handelsposten dient ihnen als Basis für ihre riskanten Geschäfte in der Sagolii-Wüste.
#. fr: Établi après le septième fléau par les Soixante-dix-sept caravanes, le Malm du Minotaure est le principal lieu d'échange de mar<shy>chan<shy>di<shy>ses du désert de Sagolii. Sans ce poste de traite, les populations locales seraient dans l'incapacité de survivre dans ce milieu hostile.
#. column 13: Minotaur Malm
#. column 14: "Beads of sweat flying from their broad shoulders, massive muscles tightening and loosening─no, I've not seen a finer sight in all the realm." Such were the warrioress's words, and I would see what she saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162749:0:15"
msgid "Local legend has that long ago, a young goatherd leading his pack to water at Forgotten Springs was set upon and chased a full malm through these caves by a minotaur. There has yet to be a second sighting of the creature, but the stories are enough to frighten away most who would consider passage through this trading post used by the Seventy-Seven Caravans."
msgstr "Старая легенда гласит: давным-давно минотавр напал на юного пастуха, который гнал коз на водопой к Забытым источникам, и целую лигу гнал его сквозь эти пещеры. Больше чудовище никто не видел, но одной этой истории хватает, чтобы отпугнуть почти всех, кто хотел бы пройти через торговый пост Семидесяти семи караванов."

#. ja: 東方監視塔
#. de: Östlicher Wachturm
#. fr: Tour de guet est
#. column 14: "On the watch, slumber's siren call is your greatest foe. When I feel myself drifting off at my post, I envision my commander standing before me, and put the fear of the gods in myself." Such were the sentry's words, and I would see what he saw.
#. column 15: To power their legions of warmachina, the Garleans require a steady supply of the aether-based fuel known as ceruleum. Bluefog housing the largest deposit in Eorzea, the Empire has begun their own mining operation but a stone's throw from the Allied refineries, heightening tensions in the area and prompting the construction of two watchtowers.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162750:0:13"
msgid "East Watchtower"
msgstr "Восточная дозорная башня"

#. ja: ――ある兵士から聞いた噂。\n見張りの敵は己の眠気。眠くなったらどうするか。旗先に立ってビシッと敬礼、この度胸試しで眠気を覚ます。
#. de: Der größte Feind des Wächters ist die Müdigkeit. Um sie zu vertreiben, haben die Soldaten am Wachturm einen Trick: Auf die Spitze des Fahnenmasts stellen und zackig salutieren! Garantiert nichts für schwache Nerven.
#. fr: Les soldats en manque de frissons s'amusent parfois à saluer le soleil qui se lève en se perchant sur la bannière d'une tour.
#. column 13: East Watchtower
#. column 15: To power their legions of warmachina, the Garleans require a steady supply of the aether-based fuel known as ceruleum. Bluefog housing the largest deposit in Eorzea, the Empire has begun their own mining operation but a stone's throw from the Allied refineries, heightening tensions in the area and prompting the construction of two watchtowers.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162750:0:14"
msgid "\"On the watch, slumber's siren call is your greatest foe. When I feel myself drifting off at my post, I envision my commander standing before me, and put the fear of the gods in myself.\" Such were the sentry's words, and I would see what he saw."
msgstr "«На дозоре главный враг — сон. Когда чувствую, что клюю носом, представляю перед собой командира и как следует пугаю себя». Так сказал часовой. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: ガレマール帝国軍第XIV軍団が、魔導兵器の燃料を確保するために築いた資源採掘拠点、「カストルム・メリディアヌム」を監視するための物見塔。不滅隊の哨兵が駐在し、昼夜を問わず対岸の動きを見張っている
#. de: Die Garlear benötigen Unmengen an Erdseim für ihre Kampf<shy>maschinen. Dieser wird in Castrum Meridianum gefördert. Seitdem ist die Lage in der Region gespannt, wie dieser eorzäische Wachturm beweist.
#. fr: Cette tour a été érigée afin de surveiller Castrum Meridianum, la forteresse garlemaldaise permettant à la 14e légion impériale de protéger l'extraction et l'ex<shy>ploi<shy>ta<shy>tion de céruleum. Des sentinelles des Immortels y montent la garde jour et nuit.
#. column 13: East Watchtower
#. column 14: "On the watch, slumber's siren call is your greatest foe. When I feel myself drifting off at my post, I envision my commander standing before me, and put the fear of the gods in myself." Such were the sentry's words, and I would see what he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162750:0:15"
msgid "To power their legions of warmachina, the Garleans require a steady supply of the aether-based fuel known as ceruleum. Bluefog housing the largest deposit in Eorzea, the Empire has begun their own mining operation but a stone's throw from the Allied refineries, heightening tensions in the area and prompting the construction of two watchtowers."
msgstr "Для боевых машин гарлеанским легионам нужно постоянное топливо — церулеум, вещество на основе эфира. В Синем тумане находятся крупнейшие залежи Эорзеи. Империя начала добывать его всего в двух шагах от союзных перерабатывающих заводов, обострив напряжённость в регионе и вынудив построить две сторожевые башни."

#. ja: 青燐水パイプライン
#. de: Erdseim-Leitung
#. fr: Céruléoducs
#. column 14: "My duties include keeping the portcullis well oiled. A right fine view on a clear day, but don't lose your balance─it's a long way down." Such were the soldier's words, and I would see what he saw.
#. column 15: Even before airships and engines were commonplace in Eorzea, Amajina & Sons Mineral Concern recognized the potential value of ceruleum and laid claim to nearly all of the untapped deposits in northern Thanalan. In an ironic twist, for many years before the Garlean invasion, the Concern's biggest customer was, in fact, the imperial army.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162751:0:13"
msgid "Ceruleum Pipeline"
msgstr "Трубопровод церулеума"

#. ja: ――ある兵士から聞いた噂。\n落とし格子の整備には時間がかかる。晴れていれば眺めはいいが、落っこちたら一大事だ。
#. de: Die Wartung der Fallgitter ist beschwerlich. An wolkenlosen Tagen hat man von oben einen überwältigenden Ausblick, doch wer vor lauter Staunen nicht aufpasst und runterfällt, sieht nur noch Radieschen von unten.
#. fr: La vue du haut d'une herse est paraît-il incomparable, même la nuit si aucun nuage ne cache la lumière des étoiles. Gare cependant à la chute...
#. column 13: Ceruleum Pipeline
#. column 15: Even before airships and engines were commonplace in Eorzea, Amajina & Sons Mineral Concern recognized the potential value of ceruleum and laid claim to nearly all of the untapped deposits in northern Thanalan. In an ironic twist, for many years before the Garlean invasion, the Concern's biggest customer was, in fact, the imperial army.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162751:0:14"
msgid "\"My duties include keeping the portcullis well oiled. A right fine view on a clear day, but don't lose your balance─it's a long way down.\" Such were the soldier's words, and I would see what he saw."
msgstr "«В мои обязанности входит смазывать опускную решётку. В ясный день отсюда чудесный вид, только не теряйте равновесия — падать высоко». Так сказал солдат. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 採取された青燐水を精製所まで送るためのパイプライン。エオルゼアにおいても、飛空艇をはじめ青燐機関の利用は広がりつつあり、燃料需要が増大傾向にある。アマジナ鉱山社は巨費を投じて、設備を拡充しているようだ
#. de: Weit vor dem Einzug von Maschinen in Eorzea sicherte sich die Amajina Bergbau AG wohlweislich die Förderrechte für Erdseim. Ironischerweise waren bis zum Krieg gegen Garlemald ausgerechnet die Garlear ihr größter Abnehmer.
#. fr: Ces pipe-lines sont utilisés pour acheminer le céruleum brut jusqu'à l'usine de céruleum pour qu'il y soit raffiné. L'utilisation des machines utilisant ce carburant, à commencer par les aéronefs, se répand de plus en plus en Éorzéa. La société minière Amajina et Fils a notamment investi d'énormes sommes d'argent pour moderniser ses équipements.
#. column 13: Ceruleum Pipeline
#. column 14: "My duties include keeping the portcullis well oiled. A right fine view on a clear day, but don't lose your balance─it's a long way down." Such were the soldier's words, and I would see what he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162751:0:15"
msgid "Even before airships and engines were commonplace in Eorzea, Amajina & Sons Mineral Concern recognized the potential value of ceruleum and laid claim to nearly all of the untapped deposits in northern Thanalan. In an ironic twist, for many years before the Garlean invasion, the Concern's biggest customer was, in fact, the imperial army."
msgstr "Ещё до того, как дирижабли и двигатели стали обычным делом в Эорзее, Горнорудная компания «Амажина и сыновья» разглядела выгоду в церулеуме и застолбила почти все неразведанные месторождения Северного Таналана. Ирония в том, что долгие годы до вторжения гарлеанцев главным покупателем компании была именно имперская армия."

#. ja: ブルーフォグ
#. de: Blauer Dunst
#. fr: Brumebleue
#. column 14: "Fog ain't supposed to be blue, least not where I come from─gives me the creeps. On such rare occasions as it clears up, I look upon the valley from on high. Simple pleasure, but it keeps me from losin' my bloody mind." Such were the laborer's words, and I would see what he saw.
#. column 15: Though abundant on the northern continent of Ilsabard, only a handful of ceruleum deposits have ever been discovered on Aldenard, the largest being buried under the Sea of Spires in northern Thanalan. Ceruleum is a highly unstable substance and will begin to evaporate when in contact with air, resulting in the bluish haze from which this area earns its name.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162752:0:13"
msgid "Bluefog"
msgstr "Синяя мгла"

#. ja: ――ある作業員から聞いた噂。\n青い霧は、未だに慣れない。霧が晴れたら作業をサボって、高所から渓谷を一望する方が好きだ。
#. de: Der blaue Dunst kann einem ganz schön aufs Gemüt schlagen. Wenn sich der Nebel lichtet, erklimmen die Arbeiter daher gerne eine hohe Stelle und blicken von dort auf die Schlucht hinab.
#. fr: Les ouvriers de l'usine de céruleum profitent parfois d'une éclaircie lors de leur pause de l'après-midi pour aller admirer en hauteur la crevasse insondable à l'ouest de leur lieu de travail.
#. column 13: Bluefog
#. column 15: Though abundant on the northern continent of Ilsabard, only a handful of ceruleum deposits have ever been discovered on Aldenard, the largest being buried under the Sea of Spires in northern Thanalan. Ceruleum is a highly unstable substance and will begin to evaporate when in contact with air, resulting in the bluish haze from which this area earns its name.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162752:0:14"
msgid "\"Fog ain't supposed to be blue, least not where I come from─gives me the creeps. On such rare occasions as it clears up, I look upon the valley from on high. Simple pleasure, but it keeps me from losin' my bloody mind.\" Such were the laborer's words, and I would see what he saw."
msgstr "«Где я вырос, туману не положено быть синим. Жуть берёт. Когда он наконец рассеивается, я забираюсь повыше и любуюсь долиной. Простая радость, зато с ума не сойдёшь». Так сказал рабочий. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 北ザナラーンの渓谷地帯は、エオルゼアでも指折りの青燐水埋蔵量を誇る場所として知られている。青燐水採掘時に生じるガスの影響で、青みを帯びた霧「ブルーフォグ」が立ちこめる光景は、この地の名物ともいえるもの
#. de: Das nördliche Thanalan verfügt mit über die größten Erdseim-Reserven in ganz Eorzea, die jedoch im Vergleich zu den Vorkommen auf Ilsabard geradezu kümmerlich wirken. Beim Abbau des Rohstoffs tritt bläulicher Nebel hervor, der der Region ihren Namen gab.
#. fr: La région ravinée du Thanalan septentrional est riche en céruleum, et son ex<shy>ploi<shy>ta<shy>tion y est intensive. Un gaz bleuâtre se dégageant durant l'extraction de ce carburant, l'endroit a fini par être appelé Brumebleue.
#. column 13: Bluefog
#. column 14: "Fog ain't supposed to be blue, least not where I come from─gives me the creeps. On such rare occasions as it clears up, I look upon the valley from on high. Simple pleasure, but it keeps me from losin' my bloody mind." Such were the laborer's words, and I would see what he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162752:0:15"
msgid "Though abundant on the northern continent of Ilsabard, only a handful of ceruleum deposits have ever been discovered on Aldenard, the largest being buried under the Sea of Spires in northern Thanalan. Ceruleum is a highly unstable substance and will begin to evaporate when in contact with air, resulting in the bluish haze from which this area earns its name."
msgstr "На северном континенте Илсабард церулеума в избытке, а вот на Алденарде нашли всего несколько месторождений. Крупнейшее залегает под Морем шпилей в Северном Таналане. Церулеум крайне нестабилен и начинает испаряться при соприкосновении с воздухом, образуя голубоватую дымку, давшую название этой местности."

#. ja: ラウバーン緩衝地
#. de: Raubahns Trutz
#. fr: La Poussée de Raubahn
#. column 14: "Even in the wind and swirling snow, the talons are unmistakable, clutching toward the skies. Don't ask what compelled me to climb to the very tip of one, but I can tell you the sight was something to behold." Such were the sentry's words, and I would see what he saw.
#. column 15: In the final days of the Sixth Astral Era, the ceruleum fields of northern Thanalan proved to be one of the most hotly contested areas in all Eorzea, with the Empire amassing a giant host outside of Bluefog to seize control of the local fuel refineries. Though outnumbered three to one, Raubahn and his army succeeded in “pushing” back the enemy.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162753:0:13"
msgid "Raubahn's Push"
msgstr "Толчок Раубана"

#. ja: ――ある兵士から聞いた噂。\n厚い雲が覆っていても、ダラガブの爪はよく目立つ。哨戒任務でよく訪れる場所らしい。
#. de: Die Patrouillen an diesem Ort wissen sich bei dichtem Nebel zu helfen. Denn Dalamuds Klauen sind selbst dann nicht zu übersehen und erleichtern die Orientierung.
#. fr: D'après certains soldats, les Griffes de Dalamud sont un excellent endroit pour observer la région, même lorsque le temps est nuageux. Ils s'y rendent souvent le matin pour espionner les mouvements ennemis.
#. column 13: Raubahn's Push
#. column 15: In the final days of the Sixth Astral Era, the ceruleum fields of northern Thanalan proved to be one of the most hotly contested areas in all Eorzea, with the Empire amassing a giant host outside of Bluefog to seize control of the local fuel refineries. Though outnumbered three to one, Raubahn and his army succeeded in “pushing” back the enemy.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162753:0:14"
msgid "\"Even in the wind and swirling snow, the talons are unmistakable, clutching toward the skies. Don't ask what compelled me to climb to the very tip of one, but I can tell you the sight was something to behold.\" Such were the sentry's words, and I would see what he saw."
msgstr "«Даже в метель с ветром когти сразу заметны — так и тянутся к небу. Не спрашивай, зачем я забрался на самый кончик одного из них. Скажу только, зрелище было что надо». Так сказал часовой. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 第七霊災の混乱に乗じ、帝国軍が北ザナラーンへと侵攻した際、不滅隊のラウバーン局長は戦力的に劣りながらも奮戦し、青燐精製所をかろうじて死守した。結果的に生じた両陣営の中間地を、「ラウバーン緩衝地」と呼ぶ
#. de: Als die Garlear am Ende der Sechsten Ära des Lichts in der Hoffnung auf Erdseim ins nördliche Thanalan einfielen, bissen sie sich am Widerstand der Legion der Unsterblichen die Zähne aus, die hier unter Raubahns Kommando kämpfte.
#. fr: Lorsque l'armée impériale tenta de profiter du chaos consécutif au septième fléau, les Immortels menés par le général Raubahn réussirent à repousser l'assaut sur l'usine de céruleum, malgré un désavantage numérique non négligeable. La portion de terrain entre les deux places fortes ennemies est appelée depuis “La Poussée de Raubahn”.
#. column 13: Raubahn's Push
#. column 14: "Even in the wind and swirling snow, the talons are unmistakable, clutching toward the skies. Don't ask what compelled me to climb to the very tip of one, but I can tell you the sight was something to behold." Such were the sentry's words, and I would see what he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162753:0:15"
msgid "In the final days of the Sixth Astral Era, the ceruleum fields of northern Thanalan proved to be one of the most hotly contested areas in all Eorzea, with the Empire amassing a giant host outside of Bluefog to seize control of the local fuel refineries. Though outnumbered three to one, Raubahn and his army succeeded in “pushing” back the enemy."
msgstr "В последние дни Шестой астральной эры месторождения церулеума в Северном Таналане стали одним из самых ожесточённо оспариваемых мест Эорзеи. Империя собрала огромное войско у Синего тумана, чтобы захватить местные перерабатывающие заводы. Раубан и его армия уступали врагу втрое, но всё же сумели его «оттеснить»."

#. ja: アマジナ霊銀山跡
#. de: Verlassene Amajina-Mithrilmine
#. fr: Mine de mithril abandonnée
#. column 14: "I didn't know what those madmen were going to do with me, and I wasn't about to find out. When the fog descended, I snuck out across a collapsed pillar. Lucky to be alive, though I do wish I'd had the luxury to enjoy the view." Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see what he saw.
#. column 15: The discovery of mythril in a small copper mine in Bluefog triggered the Great Rush which saw would-be prospectors flock to the Sea of Spires in search of quick and easy fortune. The veins that ran through the mountains, however, were not deep, and it was but ten summers before the mines ceased to yield the precious metal, forcing many to abandon their claims.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162754:0:13"
msgid "Abandoned Amajina Mythril Mine"
msgstr "Заброшенная шахта мириала «Амаджина»"

#. ja: ――ある冒険者から聞いた噂。\n不気味な連中に捕まりかけたことがある。霧に紛れ逃げ出して、崩れた柱を伝って脱出したらしい。
#. de: Der Abenteurer wurde von üblen Gesellen gefangen genommen, doch bei Nebel gelang ihm die Flucht über eine umgestürzte Säule.
#. fr: Perdu dans un épais brouillard, cet aventurier ne s'attendait pas à tomber nez à nez avec des sectateurs. Pris en chasse, il réussit à leur échapper en sautant sur un pilier du haut d'une bâtisse, et en y restant jusqu'à ce qu'ils l'oublient.
#. column 13: Abandoned Amajina Mythril Mine
#. column 15: The discovery of mythril in a small copper mine in Bluefog triggered the Great Rush which saw would-be prospectors flock to the Sea of Spires in search of quick and easy fortune. The veins that ran through the mountains, however, were not deep, and it was but ten summers before the mines ceased to yield the precious metal, forcing many to abandon their claims.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162754:0:14"
msgid "\"I didn't know what those madmen were going to do with me, and I wasn't about to find out. When the fog descended, I snuck out across a collapsed pillar. Lucky to be alive, though I do wish I'd had the luxury to enjoy the view.\" Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see what he saw."
msgstr "«Я не знал, что эти безумцы со мной сделают, и выяснять не собирался. Когда спустился туман, я незаметно выбрался по обрушившейся колонне. Повезло, что жив остался. Жаль, полюбоваться видом не успел». Так сказал приключенец. Я решил посмотреть на всё его глазами."

#. ja: 20年ほど前に放棄された廃坑。アマジナ鉱山社を躍進させた「ミスリルラッシュ」の舞台としても知られる一大ミスリル鉱山だったが、鉱脈が尽き閉鎖された。今では、カルト教団「最後の群民」のアジトと化している
#. de: Die Mine der Amajina-Bergbau AG wurde vor etwa 20 Jahren geschlossen, nachdem man sie im großen Mithrilrausch restlos ausgebeutet hatte. Heute dient sie dem Kult der „Jünger Dalamuds“ als Unterschlupf.
#. fr: Cette mine, qui a fait la fortune des Bons filons d'Amajina et Fils durant la “ruée vers le mithril”, a fermé ses portes il y a de cela une vingtaine d'années, après que ses filons ont été com<shy>plè<shy>te<shy>ment épuisés. Aujourd'hui, elle sert de repaire aux Survivalistes.
#. column 13: Abandoned Amajina Mythril Mine
#. column 14: "I didn't know what those madmen were going to do with me, and I wasn't about to find out. When the fog descended, I snuck out across a collapsed pillar. Lucky to be alive, though I do wish I'd had the luxury to enjoy the view." Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see what he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162754:0:15"
msgid "The discovery of mythril in a small copper mine in Bluefog triggered the Great Rush which saw would-be prospectors flock to the Sea of Spires in search of quick and easy fortune. The veins that ran through the mountains, however, were not deep, and it was but ten summers before the mines ceased to yield the precious metal, forcing many to abandon their claims. "
msgstr "Открытие мифрила в небольшой медной шахте у Синего Тумана положило начало великой лихорадке: толпы старателей устремились к Морю Шпилей в надежде быстро и легко разбогатеть. Но рудные жилы в горах залегали неглубоко, и уже через десять лет шахты перестали давать драгоценный металл. Многие были вынуждены оставить свои участки."

#. ja: 剣ヶ峰
#. de: Der Schwertrücken
#. fr: L'Épée
#. column 14: "I suppose the view is impressive, yes, but it's rare that I have a moment to appreciate it. Too much work to be done before the sun goes down." Such were the draughtsman's words, and I would see what he saw.
#. column 15: As is described in the <i>Enchiridion</i>, to ensure the realm of man did not drift apart from the firmament, Halone struck the Nail through both, ever binding the two. And though assailed on all sides by great metal shards fallen from the lesser moon Dalamud's crust, the ancient peak remained standing, a testament to the land's life force.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162755:0:13"
msgid "The Nail"
msgstr "Гвоздь"

#. ja: ――ある技師から聞いた噂。\n整備作業は、日暮れまでに終える必要がある。周辺の景色など、見ているヒマはない。
#. de: Die Justierungsarbeiten müssen bis Sonnenuntergang beendet sein, deswegen haben die hier beschäftigten Astrologen keine Gelegenheit, die unvergessliche Aussicht zu genießen.
#. fr: Les astrologues ishgardais doivent finir leurs préparatifs avant le coucher du soleil, mais ils sont souvent récompensés par un fabuleux panorama.
#. column 13: The Nail
#. column 15: As is described in the <i>Enchiridion</i>, to ensure the realm of man did not drift apart from the firmament, Halone struck the Nail through both, ever binding the two. And though assailed on all sides by great metal shards fallen from the lesser moon Dalamud's crust, the ancient peak remained standing, a testament to the land's life force.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162755:0:14"
msgid "\"I suppose the view is impressive, yes, but it's rare that I have a moment to appreciate it. Too much work to be done before the sun goes down.\" Such were the draughtsman's words, and I would see what he saw."
msgstr "«Вид, конечно, впечатляет, да только любоваться им некогда. До заката ещё столько работы». Так говорил чертёжник. Я решил взглянуть на мир его глазами."

#. ja: クルザス中央高地のそびえ立つ高峰。正教の聖典では、天界と地上を繋ぎ止める釘として、ハルオーネが振り下ろした剣だとされている。しかし、ダラガブ片が突き刺さった結果、その刃のような稜線は変貌してしまった
#. de: Der Kirche zufolge trieb Halone ein Schwert in das Hochland von Coerthas, um Himmel und Erde zu verbinden: der Berg Schwertrücken. Seit Dalamuds Absturz ist seine Klingenform kaum noch zu erkennen.
#. fr: L'Enchiridion, le livre sacré de la religion ishgardaise, décrit cet imposant pic dressé au cœur du Coerthas central comme l'épée de Halone. La déesse l'aurait plantée là pour lier le ciel et la terre. Un immense morceau de Dalamud défigure désormais cette montagne.
#. column 13: The Nail
#. column 14: "I suppose the view is impressive, yes, but it's rare that I have a moment to appreciate it. Too much work to be done before the sun goes down." Such were the draughtsman's words, and I would see what he saw.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162755:0:15"
msgid "As is described in the <i>Enchiridion</i>, to ensure the realm of man did not drift apart from the firmament, Halone struck the Nail through both, ever binding the two. And though assailed on all sides by great metal shards fallen from the lesser moon Dalamud's crust, the ancient peak remained standing, a testament to the land's life force."
msgstr "Как сказано в <i>Энхиридионе</i>, Халоне пронзила Гвоздём и землю, и небосвод, чтобы они не разошлись, и навеки скрепила их. Древний пик устоял, хотя со всех сторон его осыпали огромные металлические обломки, отколовшиеся от коры меньшей луны Даламуда. Такова жизненная сила этой земли."

#. ja: アドネール占星台
#. de: Observatorium
#. fr: Observatoire
#. column 14: Overheard at a tavern: "It wasn't what you could call me finest hour. I slipped and fell, and snagged me garments on something-or-another. I was enjoying the sight─till I realized how damned ridiculous I'd look if anyone came upon me. Dusted meself off and went on me way."
#. column 15: Three hundred years ago, Ishgardian astrologian Adaunel the Younger convinced the Holy See that he could predict the comings and goings of the Dravanian Horde by studying the movements of the heavens, and thus secured funding for the construction of the First Dicasterial Observatorium of Aetherial and Astrological Phenomena and its grand astroscope.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162756:0:13"
msgid "The Observatorium"
msgstr "Обсерваторий"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\n滑って落ちて、ひっかかった。九死一生とは、まさにこの事を言うのだろう。
#. de: Mein Gesprächspartner erzählte, wie er um eine Haaresbreite dem Tod entkam, als er stolperte und in die Tiefe stürzte, doch wie durch ein Wunder nicht auf dem Boden aufschlug. An jenem Tag soll es sehr neblig gewesen sein.
#. fr: La vie ne tient qu'à un fil. Tous les astrologues de l'Observatoire connaissent l'histoire de cet homme qui est resté suspendu au-dessus du vide toute la nuit après avoir malencontreusement chuté des escaliers.
#. column 13: The Observatorium
#. column 15: Three hundred years ago, Ishgardian astrologian Adaunel the Younger convinced the Holy See that he could predict the comings and goings of the Dravanian Horde by studying the movements of the heavens, and thus secured funding for the construction of the First Dicasterial Observatorium of Aetherial and Astrological Phenomena and its grand astroscope.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162756:0:14"
msgid "Overheard at a tavern: \"It wasn't what you could call me finest hour. I slipped and fell, and snagged me garments on something-or-another. I was enjoying the sight─till I realized how damned ridiculous I'd look if anyone came upon me. Dusted meself off and went on me way.\""
msgstr "«Не самый славный мой час, скажу я вам. Поскакнул, свалился, зацепился одеждой за что-то. Любовался видом, пока не понял, до чего же глупо буду выглядеть, если кто меня увидит. Отряхнулся и пошёл себе дальше». Так рассказывал тот чертёжник. Я решил взглянуть на мир его глазами."

#. ja: エオルゼア最大の天体望遠鏡を備えた占星台。天体の運行を観測することで、ドラゴン族の動きを予測するために作られた。その名は、イシュガルドの歴史に残る偉大な占星術士、「アドネール」に由来しているという
#. de: Im Observatorium für Ätherische und Astrologische Phänomene verfolgen die Astrologen Ishgards mit dem leistungsstärksten Teleskop Eorzeas den Lauf der Gestirne, um die Pläne der Drachen vorherzusagen.
#. fr: Cet édifice a été construit il y a trois cents ans à la demande d'Adaunel, un illustre astronome ishgardais qui prétendait pouvoir prédire les actions des Dravaniens en lisant dans les astres. Équipé de la plus grande lunette astronomique d'Éorzéa, ce bâtiment fait la fierté des amoureux des étoiles.
#. column 13: The Observatorium
#. column 14: Overheard at a tavern: "It wasn't what you could call me finest hour. I slipped and fell, and snagged me garments on something-or-another. I was enjoying the sight─till I realized how damned ridiculous I'd look if anyone came upon me. Dusted meself off and went on me way."
msgctxt "Adventure:2162756:0:15"
msgid "Three hundred years ago, Ishgardian astrologian Adaunel the Younger convinced the Holy See that he could predict the comings and goings of the Dravanian Horde by studying the movements of the heavens, and thus secured funding for the construction of the First Dicasterial Observatorium of Aetherial and Astrological Phenomena and its grand astroscope."
msgstr "Триста лет назад ишгардский астролог Адоанель Младший убедил Святейший Престол, что по движению небесных тел можно предсказывать набеги драконьей орды. Так он добился средств на строительство Первой дикастерии эфирных и астрологических явлений с её огромным астрооптиком."

#. ja: ドラゴン族の骸
#. de: Skelett des Drachen
#. fr: Cadavre de dragon
#. column 14: "From on high, I looked down upon the dread carcass. Ah, to have been the hero who pierced the wyrm's heart with a ballista that day! The mere thought stirred my blood on the coldest of days." Such were the knight's words, and I would see what he saw.
#. column 15: In years past, the hot alpine summers would have seen this fallen Dravanian outflyer blown with maggots and reduced to bones in a matter of days. Now, in the endless winter wrought by the Calamity, the carcass rests in the permafrost under a thick blanket of snow, perfectly preserved since the day he was pierced through the heart by a ballista.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162757:0:13"
msgid "The Frozen Fang"
msgstr "Замёрзший клык"

#. ja: ――ある騎兵から聞いた噂。\nその骸を見ると、どんなに寒い日でも、バリスタがドラゴンを貫いた瞬間を思い出し、熱くなる。
#. de: Ein Ritter, den ich am Skelett traf, sagte mir, dass auch an schneereichen Wintertagen sein Herz von feuriger Glut erfüllt ist, wenn er an den Moment zurückdenkt, als die Haubitze seines Vetters den Drachen niederstreckte.
#. fr: Tuer un dragon d'un tir de baliste rend un chevalier tellement fier qu'il n'hésitera pas à faire le funambule, même en plein blizzard, pour regarder son trophée.
#. column 13: The Frozen Fang
#. column 15: In years past, the hot alpine summers would have seen this fallen Dravanian outflyer blown with maggots and reduced to bones in a matter of days. Now, in the endless winter wrought by the Calamity, the carcass rests in the permafrost under a thick blanket of snow, perfectly preserved since the day he was pierced through the heart by a ballista.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162757:0:14"
msgid "\"From on high, I looked down upon the dread carcass. Ah, to have been the hero who pierced the wyrm's heart with a ballista that day! The mere thought stirred my blood on the coldest of days.\" Such were the knight's words, and I would see what he saw."
msgstr "«С высоты я смотрел на жуткую тушу. Ах, вот бы мне тогда стать героем, что пронзил баллистой сердце дракона! От одной этой мысли кровь закипает даже в самый лютый мороз». Так говорил рыцарь. Я решил взглянуть на мир его глазами."

#. ja: ホワイトブリム前哨地から放たれた対竜バリスタによって、打ち落とされたドラゴン族の骸。クルザスの厳しい寒さにより凍り付いたため、ほとんど腐敗していない。まるで雪の中で眠っているかのようにも見える
#. de: Die gut erhaltenen Überreste eines Drachen geben Zeugnis von der Feuerkraft der Drachenhaubitzen an der Weißenfels-Front. Aus der Entfernung scheint es, als schlummere der Drache inmitten der Wolken.
#. fr: Abattu grâce à un tir de baliste, ce dragon est allé s'écraser au fond d'une crevasse jouxtant le poste de L'Arête blanche. Les basses températures préservent la carcasse de la décomposition, donnant l'impression qu'elle peut se relever à tout moment.
#. column 13: The Frozen Fang
#. column 14: "From on high, I looked down upon the dread carcass. Ah, to have been the hero who pierced the wyrm's heart with a ballista that day! The mere thought stirred my blood on the coldest of days." Such were the knight's words, and I would see what he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162757:0:15"
msgid "In years past, the hot alpine summers would have seen this fallen Dravanian outflyer blown with maggots and reduced to bones in a matter of days. Now, in the endless winter wrought by the Calamity, the carcass rests in the permafrost under a thick blanket of snow, perfectly preserved since the day he was pierced through the heart by a ballista."
msgstr "В прежние годы, когда в альпийских долинах стояло жаркое лето, останки павшего дракона за несколько дней облепили бы личинки, и от него остались бы одни кости. Теперь же, в бесконечную зиму, что принесло Бедствие, туша лежит в вечной мерзлоте под толстым снежным одеялом, сохранившись с того самого дня, когда баллиста пронзила ей сердце."

#. ja: 皇都「イシュガルド」
#. de: Ishgard
#. fr: Sainte Cité d'Ishgard
#. column 14: "I look upon my homeland, its proud spires soaring in the azure, and swear a silent oath. My spear shall not leave my hand until the last dread wyrm has fallen." Such were the knight's words, and I would see what he saw.
#. column 15: For the past thousand years, Ishgard has waged a bloody war with the dragons of Dravania. To fend off the enemy horde, a complex web of defenses, magical and corporeal, has been added piecemeal to the city proper's outer walls, transforming her into an impenetrable bastion, while at the same time, isolating her and her people from the outside world.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162758:0:13"
msgid "The Holy See of Ishgard"
msgstr "Святой Престол Ишгарда"

#. ja: ――ある騎兵から聞いた噂。\n蒼天に浮かぶ故郷を見て、決意を新たにする。厳しさを増す戦いに備えるために。
#. de: Ishgard sieht schweren Zeiten entgegen - doch beim Anblick der stolzen Festung vor dem eisblauen Himmel erneuern die Ritter der Morgenwache tief in ihrem Herzen den Eid, den sie auf ihr heiliges Reich leisteten.
#. fr: Le chevalier chargé de sonner les mâtines est souvent récompensé par une vue imprenable sur la sainte Cité.
#. column 13: The Holy See of Ishgard
#. column 15: For the past thousand years, Ishgard has waged a bloody war with the dragons of Dravania. To fend off the enemy horde, a complex web of defenses, magical and corporeal, has been added piecemeal to the city proper's outer walls, transforming her into an impenetrable bastion, while at the same time, isolating her and her people from the outside world.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162758:0:14"
msgid "\"I look upon my homeland, its proud spires soaring in the azure, and swear a silent oath. My spear shall not leave my hand until the last dread wyrm has fallen.\" Such were the knight's words, and I would see what he saw."
msgstr "«Гляжу на родину: гордые шпили взмывают в синеву. И молча даю себе клятву: не выпущу копья из рук, пока не падёт последний страшный дракон». Так говорил рыцарь. Я решил взглянуть на мир его глазами."

#. ja: 宗教都市「イシュガルド」。ドラゴン族の襲来に備え、城壁と魔法障壁が幾重にも張り巡らされているほか、対竜バリスタを備えた尖塔が乱立している。イシュガルド正教の教皇が住まう宮殿があるため、皇都とも呼ばれる
#. de: Von Mauern und magischen Barrieren umgeben, trotzen die Ritter Ishgards der eisigen Kälte und den Angriffen der Drachen. Ishgard ist außerdem Sitz des Papstes, der in einem ansehnlichen Palast residiert.
#. fr: Capitale du peuple très religieux que sont les Ishgardais, la sainte Cité est non seulement protégée par de puissants remparts et des barrières magiques, mais aussi pourvue de tours de guet armées de balistes pour se défendre contre ses ennemis, les dragons.
#. column 13: The Holy See of Ishgard
#. column 14: "I look upon my homeland, its proud spires soaring in the azure, and swear a silent oath. My spear shall not leave my hand until the last dread wyrm has fallen." Such were the knight's words, and I would see what he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162758:0:15"
msgid "For the past thousand years, Ishgard has waged a bloody war with the dragons of Dravania. To fend off the enemy horde, a complex web of defenses, magical and corporeal, has been added piecemeal to the city proper's outer walls, transforming her into an impenetrable bastion, while at the same time, isolating her and her people from the outside world."
msgstr "Уже тысячу лет Ишгард ведёт кровопролитную войну с драконами Дравании. Чтобы сдержать вражескую орду, город постепенно окружили сложной сетью укреплений — магических и обычных. Так он стал неприступной крепостью, но вместе с тем оказался отрезан от внешнего мира, как и его жители."

#. ja: 巨石の丘
#. de: Rothbruch
#. fr: Coteaux rocheux
#. column 14: "In the shadow of those unholy rocks, the mightiest giant will look as a dwarf. Yet from the right vantage point, even one of humble stature can look upon them all." Such were the knight's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Before the Calamity, Boulder Downs was a vast sloped lea littered with moraine deposited by realm-swallowing glaciers long receded. The rain of debris that accompanied the fall of Dalamud, however, transformed the landscape into a frozen wasteland pocked with gaping impact craters and peculiar dark matter formations.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162759:0:13"
msgid "Boulder Downs"
msgstr "Валуны"

#. ja: ――ある騎兵から聞いた噂。\n近づけば見上げるほどの巨石も、そこに行けば、全体像を見下ろすことができるらしい。
#. de: Der Wachsoldat ließ mich nur für einen Moment auf die Zinne, doch er wollte mir den Blick auf das von den letzten Sonnenstrahlen berührte Rothbruch nicht verwehren.
#. fr: Pour avoir une bonne vue de cet ensemble de débris de Dalamud, il faut assurément un œil perçant et haut placé.
#. column 13: Boulder Downs
#. column 15: Before the Calamity, Boulder Downs was a vast sloped lea littered with moraine deposited by realm-swallowing glaciers long receded. The rain of debris that accompanied the fall of Dalamud, however, transformed the landscape into a frozen wasteland pocked with gaping impact craters and peculiar dark matter formations.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162759:0:14"
msgid "\"In the shadow of those unholy rocks, the mightiest giant will look as a dwarf. Yet from the right vantage point, even one of humble stature can look upon them all.\" Such were the knight's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«В тени этих проклятых скал даже величайший великан покажется карликом. Но с удачной точки и невысокому человеку открывается вид на все разом». Так говорил рыцарь. Я решил взглянуть на мир его глазами."

#. ja: 剣ヶ峰の麓に広がる丘で、かつて大きな岩が点在していたため「巨石の丘」と呼ばれていた。今では月の衛星「ダラガブ」の外殻を覆っていたダークマターが、奇妙な形状で固着し、新たな奇岩となり丘を覆っている
#. de: Am Fuße des Schwertrückens erstrecken sich rote Felswände, aus denen man einst rotschimmernde Steine brach. Nach der Katastrophe verformte sich der Fels unter dem Einfluss dunkler Materie auf bizarre Weise.
#. fr: Cette colline qui s'étend au pied de L'Épée était autrefois jonchée d'énormes rochers, origines de son nom. C'est désormais la matière sombre de la surface du satellite Dalamud qui s'y accumule sous d'étranges formes, créant un paysage pour le moins singulier.
#. column 13: Boulder Downs
#. column 14: "In the shadow of those unholy rocks, the mightiest giant will look as a dwarf. Yet from the right vantage point, even one of humble stature can look upon them all." Such were the knight's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162759:0:15"
msgid "Before the Calamity, Boulder Downs was a vast sloped lea littered with moraine deposited by realm-swallowing glaciers long receded. The rain of debris that accompanied the fall of Dalamud, however, transformed the landscape into a frozen wasteland pocked with gaping impact craters and peculiar dark matter formations."
msgstr "До Бедствия Валунные холмы были обширным пологим лугом, усеянным моренными отложениями, оставленными давно отступившими ледниками, некогда поглотившими целые земли. Но вместе с падением Даламуда сюда обрушился дождь обломков, превративший окрестности в ледяную пустошь с огромными воронками и причудливыми скоплениями тёмной материи."

#. ja: ハルオーネの秘石
#. de: Halone-Signum
#. fr: L'Œil de la Conquérante
#. column 14: "Dragons, heretics─I've stared into the eye of many a foe. Stone has no eyes, yet no other gaze can pierce me to the very depths of my soul." Such were the knight's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: A place holy to all Ishgardians, it is believed that when a man stands within this hidden grotto, the Fury Herself will reach deep into the darkest recesses of his soul and lay out his sins before him, allowing the man to repent those failings. Monument Tower was built nearby to protect this hallowed ground from the taint of dragons and heretics.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162760:0:13"
msgid "The Fury's Gaze"
msgstr "Взор Фурии"

#. ja: ――ある騎兵から聞いた噂。\n聖なる石の前に立つと、天よりの視線を感じる。きっと、身が引き締まる思いをするだろう。
#. de: Ein Ritter sprach ehrfürchtig von seiner ersten Pilgerfahrt zum Heiligen Stein. Vielleicht lag es an der erhabenen Aura, vielleicht an dem strengen Schneetreiben, aber er fühlte sich, als würde die Göttin des Krieges selbst auf ihn herunterblicken.
#. fr: Même l'Ishgardais le plus fidèle ne saurait contempler la déesse de trop près s'il ne veut pas s'attirer la tempête de son courroux.
#. column 13: The Fury's Gaze
#. column 15: A place holy to all Ishgardians, it is believed that when a man stands within this hidden grotto, the Fury Herself will reach deep into the darkest recesses of his soul and lay out his sins before him, allowing the man to repent those failings. Monument Tower was built nearby to protect this hallowed ground from the taint of dragons and heretics.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162760:0:14"
msgid "\"Dragons, heretics─I've stared into the eye of many a foe. Stone has no eyes, yet no other gaze can pierce me to the very depths of my soul.\" Such were the knight's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Сколько врагов я ни встречал — драконов, еретиков, — смотрел им прямо в глаза. У камня глаз нет, а всё равно ничей взор так не пронзает мне душу до самого дна». Так говорил рыцарь. Я решил взглянуть на мир его глазами."

#. ja: 戦争の女神「ハルオーネ」の神印が浮き出した聖なる石。ハルオーネを主神とするイシュガルド正教にとって、この秘石がある洞穴は重要な聖地である。それゆえ、「秘石の塔」という監視塔まで建造し、防衛に努めている
#. de: Man kommt, um einen Stein zu sehen, doch wenn man geht, hat man Ehrfurcht und Demut gelernt. Die Gläubigen von Ishgard verehren diesen Stein, der das Signum der Kriegsgöttin Halone trägt, als Heiligtum.
#. fr: Pour les vénérateurs de la déesse de la guerre que sont les Ishgardais, la grotte où se trouve cette pierre sacrée marquée du symbole de la Conquérante est un lieu sain. C'est d'ailleurs pour la protéger qu'ils ont bâti la tour de l'Œil non loin de là.
#. column 13: The Fury's Gaze
#. column 14: "Dragons, heretics─I've stared into the eye of many a foe. Stone has no eyes, yet no other gaze can pierce me to the very depths of my soul." Such were the knight's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162760:0:15"
msgid "A place holy to all Ishgardians, it is believed that when a man stands within this hidden grotto, the Fury Herself will reach deep into the darkest recesses of his soul and lay out his sins before him, allowing the man to repent those failings. Monument Tower was built nearby to protect this hallowed ground from the taint of dragons and heretics."
msgstr "Это место свято для всех ишгардцев. Говорят, стоит человеку войти в эту потаённую пещеру — и сама Фурия заглянет в самые тёмные уголки его души, укажет на грехи и даст возможность покаяться. Чтобы защитить святыню от драконов и еретиков, неподалёку возвели Сторожевую башню."

#. ja: スノークローク大氷壁
#. de: Schneekleid
#. fr: Manteneige
#. column 14: "As I stood there, my thoughts turned to those left behind in the west. The sun shone strong, yet it could not keep my tears from turning to ice on my cheeks." Such were the researcher's words, and I would see as she saw.
#. column 15: The bitter cold which swept over the Coerthas highlands following the Calamity did not only blanket the region in snow and ice, but transformed the water of Twinpools and the Swiftrun into a mountainous flow of ice─a flow which has slowly crept through the western Coerthas highlands and now has completely engulfed Gargoyle Crossing, preventing passage.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162761:0:13"
msgid "Snowcloak"
msgstr "Снежный покров"

#. ja: ――ある調査員から聞いた噂。\n西の端で思うのは、西方に残された人々のことばかり。陽光でも凍った涙は溶けはしない。
#. de: Der Forscher erzählte, wie er am Westrand stand und voll tiefer Trauer an jene dachte, die im Westen zurückgelassen wurden. Seine Tränen, die selbst im Sonnenlicht gefroren, werden nicht so schnell wieder auftauen.
#. fr: Nombreuses sont les personnes qui vont se recueillir à cet endroit le matin. Toutes prient Halone afin qu'elle protège leurs proches bloqués à l'ouest. Même si le soleil brille dans le ciel, le froid empêche leurs larmes de couler.
#. column 13: Snowcloak
#. column 15: The bitter cold which swept over the Coerthas highlands following the Calamity did not only blanket the region in snow and ice, but transformed the water of Twinpools and the Swiftrun into a mountainous flow of ice─a flow which has slowly crept through the western Coerthas highlands and now has completely engulfed Gargoyle Crossing, preventing passage.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162761:0:14"
msgid "\"As I stood there, my thoughts turned to those left behind in the west. The sun shone strong, yet it could not keep my tears from turning to ice on my cheeks.\" Such were the researcher's words, and I would see as she saw."
msgstr "«Стоял я там, а думы всё о тех, кто остался на западе. Солнце припекало, а слёзы на щеках всё равно превращались в лёд». Так рассказывала исследовательница. Я решил взглянуть на мир её глазами."

#. ja: 第七霊災による属性変動に伴い、クルザス地域は急激に寒冷化した。そして、わずか5年で形作られたのが、天を覆わんばかりの氷の壁である。この「大氷壁」の存在により、クルザス西部との陸路は寸断されて久しい
#. de: Die massive Eiswand blockiert den Landweg ins südliche Coerthas. Sie entstand, als sich Coerthas vor fünf Jahren durch die ätherischen Verwerfungen der Siebten Katastrophe schlagartig abkühlte.
#. fr: Cet immense mur de glace s'est formé suite au dérèglement élémentaire provoqué par le septième fléau. En seulement cinq ans, sa paroi est devenue si dure et épaisse qu'il est désormais impossible de la percer pour accéder au Coerthas occidental.
#. column 13: Snowcloak
#. column 14: "As I stood there, my thoughts turned to those left behind in the west. The sun shone strong, yet it could not keep my tears from turning to ice on my cheeks." Such were the researcher's words, and I would see as she saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162761:0:15"
msgid "The bitter cold which swept over the Coerthas highlands following the Calamity did not only blanket the region in snow and ice, but transformed the water of Twinpools and the Swiftrun into a mountainous flow of ice─a flow which has slowly crept through the western Coerthas highlands and now has completely engulfed Gargoyle Crossing, preventing passage."
msgstr "После Бедствия Коэртас сковал лютый холод. Снег и лёд покрыли землю, а воды Двойных озёр и Быстрой реки застыли и превратились в ледяной поток, который медленно полз по западному Коэртасу. Теперь он полностью поглотил Переправу горгулий, преградив путь."

#. ja: キャンプ・ドラゴンヘッド
#. de: Camp Drachenkopf
#. fr: Camp de la Tête du dragon
#. column 14: "Clearing the parapets after a snowfall is arduous work, but gazing out over the hoar-kissed peaks, a man might forget his aches and pains for a while." So were the knight's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Its name taken from a rocky outcropping said to be the head of a Dravanian king turned to stone by the almighty hand of Halone, this outpost acts as the Coerthas central highlands' southernmost line of defense for the Holy See, tasked with fending off Ixali raids from Natalan, skirmishes by heretic factions, and the occasional yeti scare.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162762:0:13"
msgid "Camp Dragonhead"
msgstr "Лагерь Драконьей Головы"

#. ja: ――ある騎兵から聞いた噂。\n雪降ろしは重労働だが、見晴らしだけは抜群だ。屋根を白から緑に変える日々が続く。
#. de: Der Schnee erschwert die Arbeit der Wachleute Ishgards, aber er verwandelt die Umgebung in eine zauberhaft ruhige Märchenlandschaft. Wer die Abgeschiedenheit sucht, findet sie höher als das höchste Feuer.
#. fr: Il est important de déblayer la neige des chemins de ronde et des toits, ne serait-ce que pour redonner leur jolie couleur verte aux tuiles.
#. column 13: Camp Dragonhead
#. column 15: Its name taken from a rocky outcropping said to be the head of a Dravanian king turned to stone by the almighty hand of Halone, this outpost acts as the Coerthas central highlands' southernmost line of defense for the Holy See, tasked with fending off Ixali raids from Natalan, skirmishes by heretic factions, and the occasional yeti scare.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162762:0:14"
msgid "\"Clearing the parapets after a snowfall is arduous work, but gazing out over the hoar-kissed peaks, a man might forget his aches and pains for a while.\" So were the knight's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«После снегопада расчищать стены — тяжкий труд. Но взглянешь на покрытые инеем вершины, и на время забудешь про боль да усталость». Так говорил рыцарь. Я решил взглянуть на мир его глазами."

#. ja: 皇都「イシュガルド」を守る防衛拠点。名門「フォルタン家」の騎兵団が駐屯し、ドラゴン族や異端者、さらには東方から侵入してきたイクサル族を警戒している。その名は、付近にある竜の頭部に似た姿の大岩に由来する
#. de: Von dieser Burg aus kämpfen Ritter des Hauses Fortemps verbissen gegen Drachen, Häretiker und aus Osten eindringende Ixal. Ein wie ein Drachenkopf geformter Fels gibt dem Lager seinen Namen.
#. fr: Cette forteresse, située près d'un rocher en forme de tête de dragon, est un important poste de défense de la sainte Cité d'Ishgard. Les chevaliers de la maison Fortemps stationnés là surveillent de près les Dravaniens, les hérétiques et les Ixali.
#. column 13: Camp Dragonhead
#. column 14: "Clearing the parapets after a snowfall is arduous work, but gazing out over the hoar-kissed peaks, a man might forget his aches and pains for a while." So were the knight's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162762:0:15"
msgid "Its name taken from a rocky outcropping said to be the head of a Dravanian king turned to stone by the almighty hand of Halone, this outpost acts as the Coerthas central highlands' southernmost line of defense for the Holy See, tasked with fending off Ixali raids from Natalan, skirmishes by heretic factions, and the occasional yeti scare."
msgstr "Этот форпост назван в честь скального выступа, похожего на голову дракона. Говорят, его окаменил могучей рукой сама Халон. Здесь, на южной границе Центрального нагорья Курхаса, ишгардцы обороняют Святой Престол от нападений иксалов из Наталана, стычек с еретиками, а порой — и от налётов йети."

#. ja: スチールヴィジル
#. de: Stählerne Wacht
#. fr: Vigile d'Acier
#. column 14: Overheard in a tavern: "...Bollocks, I say! Ye haven't truly seen the Vigil until ye've seen it from that very spot. Ye'll be wantin' to tread carefully, mind ye."
#. column 15: One of four citadel watchtowers built along the Sea of Clouds, the Steel Vigil warned the Holy See of aerial attacks for centuries before being razed and gutted by the Dravanian Horde and their vile commander, Svara. Now, only the outer walls remain, leaving a bitter reminder of the dragons' destructive power.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162763:0:13"
msgid "The Steel Vigil"
msgstr "Стальной дозор"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\nスチールヴィジルの状況が知りたいなら、足下に気をつけながら様子を覗うべきだ。
#. de: In einer Stallung riet man mir, dass, wenn ich einen Blick auf die Stählerne Wacht zu werfen beabsichtigte, ich dem schmalsten Pfad folgen sollte.
#. fr: La forteresse n'est plus qu'une ruine, mais les murs qui restent debout fournissent un excellent point d'observation par beau temps.
#. column 13: The Steel Vigil
#. column 15: One of four citadel watchtowers built along the Sea of Clouds, the Steel Vigil warned the Holy See of aerial attacks for centuries before being razed and gutted by the Dravanian Horde and their vile commander, Svara. Now, only the outer walls remain, leaving a bitter reminder of the dragons' destructive power.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162763:0:14"
msgid "Overheard in a tavern: \"...Bollocks, I say! Ye haven't truly seen the Vigil until ye've seen it from that very spot. Ye'll be wantin' to tread carefully, mind ye.\""
msgstr "В таверне подслушал: «Да чушь всё это! Не видал ты Дозора по-настоящему, пока не поглядел на него вот с этого места. Только смотри под ноги, ага?»"

#. ja: 破壊された対ドラゴン要塞。西方の「ストーンヴィジル」と対を成す、イシュガルド防衛の双璧と呼ばれていた。しかし、黄竜「スヴァラ」に率いられたドラゴン族に蹂躙され、今や外郭の一部を遺すだけの廃墟となっている
#. de: Die Stählerne Wacht bildete zusammen mit drei weiteren Wachtürmen eine Verteidigungslinie entlang des Wolkenmeers, bis der gelbe Drache Svara und seine Horden sie in eine Ruine verwandelten. Heute bestehen nur noch einzelne Teile.
#. fr: Cette forteresse formait avec le Vigile de Pierre un élément important du système de défense mis au point par les Ishgardais pour repousser les Dravaniens. Elle fut toutefois réduite à l'état de ruines lors d'un assaut du puissant dragon Svara et de sa horde.
#. column 13: The Steel Vigil
#. column 14: Overheard in a tavern: "...Bollocks, I say! Ye haven't truly seen the Vigil until ye've seen it from that very spot. Ye'll be wantin' to tread carefully, mind ye."
msgctxt "Adventure:2162763:0:15"
msgid "One of four citadel watchtowers built along the Sea of Clouds, the Steel Vigil warned the Holy See of aerial attacks for centuries before being razed and gutted by the Dravanian Horde and their vile commander, Svara. Now, only the outer walls remain, leaving a bitter reminder of the dragons' destructive power."
msgstr "Стальной дозор — одна из четырёх крепостных башен, построенных вдоль Моря Облаков. Столетиями она предупреждала Святой Престол о воздушных атаках, пока драконья орда и её мерзкий предводитель Свара не сравняли её с землёй. Теперь уцелели лишь наружные стены — горькое напоминание о разрушительной мощи драконов."

#. ja: カストルム・セントリ
#. de: Castrum Centri
#. fr: Castrum Centri
#. column 14: "It's unnatural, is what it is─roads and towers made of metal─and yet I couldn't avert my eyes. Then I heard the great steel beast rousing in the distance, and thought I'd best be on my way." Such were the scout's words, and I would see as he saw.
#. column 15: Castrum Centri was erected with material salvaged from the ruins of Castrum Novum─the Garlean Empire's first major outpost in Eorzea, constructed in the final year of the Sixth Astral Era by VIIth Legion legatus Nael van Darnus. It houses several ceruleum mining pits, a magitek manufactory, and the Phantom Train, used to transport ordnance to outlying castra.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162764:0:13"
msgid "Castrum Centri"
msgstr "Каструм Центри"

#. ja: ――ある脱走兵から聞いた噂。\n基地の内側には、発着場がある。物資が運び出されるのを見送る日々だった。
#. de: Ein Deserteur berichtete mir, dass sich in dem Militärlager ein moderner Landeplatz befinden soll. In unheimlichem Licht sah er gerne zu, wie die Frachtschiffe landeten und starteten.
#. fr: Un bon cheminot ne doit pas avoir peur de prendre un peu de hauteur pour contrôler les opérations de chargement/déchargement de ses marchandises.
#. column 13: Castrum Centri
#. column 15: Castrum Centri was erected with material salvaged from the ruins of Castrum Novum─the Garlean Empire's first major outpost in Eorzea, constructed in the final year of the Sixth Astral Era by VIIth Legion legatus Nael van Darnus. It houses several ceruleum mining pits, a magitek manufactory, and the Phantom Train, used to transport ordnance to outlying castra.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162764:0:14"
msgid "\"It's unnatural, is what it is─roads and towers made of metal─and yet I couldn't avert my eyes. Then I heard the great steel beast rousing in the distance, and thought I'd best be on my way.\" Such were the scout's words, and I would see as he saw."
msgstr "«Неправильное это зрелище — дороги и башни из металла, а глаз всё равно не оторвать. Потом услышал, как вдали просыпается стальной зверь, и решил, что пора уносить ноги». Так рассказывал разведчик. Я решил взглянуть на мир его глазами."

#. ja: ガレマール帝国軍の資源採掘拠点。ネール率いる第VII軍団が築いた拠点「カストルム・ノヴム」を元に、霊災後に侵攻してきた第XIV軍団が改装した。鉱石輸送用の鉄道、通称「魔列車」の停車場が設けられている
#. de: Das garleische Militärlager wurde aus Überresten von Castrum Novum errichtet, das Nael van Darnus kurz vor der Siebten Katastrophe als ersten Stützpunkt in Eorzea erbaut hatte. Nun überwacht hier die XIV. Legion den Abbau von Rohstoffen und deren Abtransport mit dem Phantomzug.
#. fr: Cette base est l'un des principaux sites d'extraction minière des Garlemaldais. Anciennement appelée Castrum Novum, elle a été bâtie par la 7e légion de Nael van Darnus puis réaménagée par la 14e légion de Gaius après le Fléau. Elle dispose d'une gare ferroviaire qui accueille un train de transport de mar<shy>chan<shy>di<shy>ses surnommé le “train fantôme”.
#. column 13: Castrum Centri
#. column 14: "It's unnatural, is what it is─roads and towers made of metal─and yet I couldn't avert my eyes. Then I heard the great steel beast rousing in the distance, and thought I'd best be on my way." Such were the scout's words, and I would see as he saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162764:0:15"
msgid "Castrum Centri was erected with material salvaged from the ruins of Castrum Novum─the Garlean Empire's first major outpost in Eorzea, constructed in the final year of the Sixth Astral Era by VIIth Legion legatus Nael van Darnus. It houses several ceruleum mining pits, a magitek manufactory, and the Phantom Train, used to transport ordnance to outlying castra."
msgstr "Каструм Центри построили из материалов, уцелевших среди руин Каструм Новума — первого крупного опорного пункта Гарлеанской империи в Эорзее. Его возвёл легат VII легиона Наэль ван Дарнус в последний год Шестой Звёздной эры. Здесь находятся несколько церулевых шахт, мастерская магитека и станция Призрачного поезда, доставляющего боеприпасы в отдалённые каструмы."

#. ja: クリスタルタワー
#. de: Kristallturm
#. fr: Tour de Cristal
#. column 14: "It was a scene not of this world: a forest of crystal, and in the distance a spire that stretched so high it could have touched the heavens..." Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as she saw.
#. column 15: As if somehow beckoned forth from its hypogeal prison by the events of the Calamity, this sky-scraping spire now commands the Mor Dhonan horizon. Through their research, the Sons of Saint Coinach have determined that the monolith, also known as Syrcus Tower, was constructed to collect and store the endless energies of the sun.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162765:0:13"
msgid "The Crystal Tower"
msgstr "Кристальная башня"

#. ja: ――ある冒険者から聞いた噂。\n木々までもがクリスタルと化した地から、天を衝くクリスタルの柱が見えるらしい。
#. de: Eine bizarre Landschaft: sogar die Bäume wurden in Kristalle verwandelt. Der Turm selbst ragt wie eine aus Diamant geschliffene Lanze in den Himmel.
#. fr: Les aventuriers du Glas des revenants s'accordent tous pour dire que la Tour de Cristal est plus belle la nuit, sous un ciel dégagé.
#. column 13: The Crystal Tower
#. column 15: As if somehow beckoned forth from its hypogeal prison by the events of the Calamity, this sky-scraping spire now commands the Mor Dhonan horizon. Through their research, the Sons of Saint Coinach have determined that the monolith, also known as Syrcus Tower, was constructed to collect and store the endless energies of the sun.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162765:0:14"
msgid "\"It was a scene not of this world: a forest of crystal, and in the distance a spire that stretched so high it could have touched the heavens...\" Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as she saw."
msgstr "«Это было зрелище не из нашего мира: целый лес из кристаллов, а вдали — шпиль такой высоты, будто он пронзает небеса...» Так рассказывала искательница приключений. Я решил взглянуть на мир её глазами."

#. ja: 第七霊災を境に、突如として地表に姿を現したクリスタルの巨塔。学術組織「聖コイナク財団」の調査によると、その正体は古代アラグ文明が築いたエネルギー集積装置であり、「シルクスの塔」と呼ばれていたとのこと
#. de: Der Kristallturm erschien durch die große Katastrophe wie aus dem Nichts. Sankt Coinach-Forscher fanden heraus, dass die Allager ihn erbaut hatten, um Sonnenenergie zu speichern. Auch als Turm von Syrcus bekannt.
#. fr: Apparu lors du Fléau, cet immense édifice trône désormais au milieu du Mor Dhona. Des recherches conduites par la Fondation de Saint-Coinach ont révélé qu'il s'agit de la Tour de Syrcus, que l'ancien empire d'Allag avait bâtie pour recueillir l'énergie solaire.
#. column 13: The Crystal Tower
#. column 14: "It was a scene not of this world: a forest of crystal, and in the distance a spire that stretched so high it could have touched the heavens..." Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see as she saw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162765:0:15"
msgid "As if somehow beckoned forth from its hypogeal prison by the events of the Calamity, this sky-scraping spire now commands the Mor Dhonan horizon. Through their research, the Sons of Saint Coinach have determined that the monolith, also known as Syrcus Tower, was constructed to collect and store the endless energies of the sun."
msgstr "Будто Бедствие вызвало эту башню из подземной темницы, и теперь её шпиль до самого неба виден над Мор-Дхоной. Исследователи из Сынов Святого Койнаха выяснили, что монолит, известный также как Башня Сиркуса, построили для сбора и хранения бесконечной солнечной энергии."

#. ja: 早霜峠
#. de: Früher Frost
#. fr: Hâtegel
#. column 14: "In fields of crystal, I stood tall atop one of the stones and took in the view in all its shimmering desolation." Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see what he saw.
#. column 15: The fall of the <i>Agrius</i> into Silvertear Falls not only drained the magnificent multi-tiered lake, but instantly crystallized the majority of the region's flora─a result of mass quantities of ceruleum fuel reacting with aether released upon Midgardsormr's death. What remains is a brilliant-yet-dead landscape akin to a twisted garden pocked with blooming geodes.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162766:0:13"
msgid "Rathefrost"
msgstr "Перевал Ратефрост"

#. ja: ――ある冒険者から聞いた噂。\n大規模な結晶化現象がもたらしたのは、一面の青。クリスタルの上より一望できる。
#. de: Die Kristallisierung verfärbte einen Teil der Oberfläche in ein schimmerndes Blau. Ein Abenteurer führte mich auf einen ausgewucherten Kristall, der mir einen guten Blick auf die Umgebung bot.
#. fr: C'est au pied d'un arbre cristallisé, qu'on aurait paraît-il la meilleure vue d'ensemble de ce paysage fantastique.
#. column 13: Rathefrost
#. column 15: The fall of the <i>Agrius</i> into Silvertear Falls not only drained the magnificent multi-tiered lake, but instantly crystallized the majority of the region's flora─a result of mass quantities of ceruleum fuel reacting with aether released upon Midgardsormr's death. What remains is a brilliant-yet-dead landscape akin to a twisted garden pocked with blooming geodes.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162766:0:14"
msgid "\"In fields of crystal, I stood tall atop one of the stones and took in the view in all its shimmering desolation.\" Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see what he saw."
msgstr "«Среди кристаллических полей я встал на один из камней и огляделся. Вокруг сверкала мёртвая пустошь...» Так рассказывал искатель приключений. Я решил взглянуть на мир его глазами."

#. ja: 飛空戦艦「アグリウス」の墜落によって、大規模な結晶化現象が引き起こされた場所。草すら結晶化しており、この峠を歩くとシャリシャリと霜を踏みしめたような音がなる。そのため「早霜峠」と呼ばれるようになった
#. de: Der beiderseits fatale Zusammenprall der Agrius mit Midgardsormr hatte eine großflächige Kristallisierung des Äthers zur Folge. Sogar das Gras knirscht unter den Füßen derjenigen, die den Pass überschreiten, so als schreite man über ewigen Frost.
#. fr: La chute de l'aéronef garlemaldais l'Agrius a engendré un mystérieux phénomène de cristallisation de grande ampleur à cet endroit, touchant jusqu'à la végétation, qu'on dirait gelée. C'est d'ailleurs ce qui vaut son nom à ce col montagneux.
#. column 13: Rathefrost
#. column 14: "In fields of crystal, I stood tall atop one of the stones and took in the view in all its shimmering desolation." Such were the adventurer's words, and I would see what he saw.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162766:0:15"
msgid "The fall of the <i>Agrius</i> into Silvertear Falls not only drained the magnificent multi-tiered lake, but instantly crystallized the majority of the region's flora─a result of mass quantities of ceruleum fuel reacting with aether released upon Midgardsormr's death. What remains is a brilliant-yet-dead landscape akin to a twisted garden pocked with blooming geodes."
msgstr "Падение <i>«Агриуса»</i> в Серебряное озеро не только осушило великолепное многоярусное озеро, но и в одночасье обратило в кристалл большую часть местной растительности. Всё из-за того, что огромное количество церулевого топлива вступило в реакцию с эфиром, высвободившимся после гибели Мидгардсормра. Теперь здесь сверкает мёртвый пейзаж, похожий на исковерканный сад, усеянный раскрытыми жеодами."

#. ja: 黙約の塔
#. de: Hüter des Sees
#. fr: Gardien du lac
#. column 14: Overheard in a tavern: "I was an adventurer meself, aye. Till that day when, from atop a tree, I saw that ungodly thing─that twisted mass of metal and scale. Ran from the lake as fast as my legs could carry me. Reckoned I'd be safer livin' the rest of my days out of a bottle."
#. column 15: Maintaining a silent vigil over Silvertear Lake, the Keeper is wrought from the wreckage of the imperial flagship, the <i>Agrius</i>, and the entangled remains of Midgardsormr. For many religious and mythological enthusiasts, it stands as proof of the existence of the gods. For most people, however, it serves as a grim reminder of the horrific power of Garlemald.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162767:0:13"
msgid "The Keeper of the Lake"
msgstr "Хранитель озера"

#. ja: ――酒場で耳にした噂話。\n「アグリウス」は一見の価値があるが湖畔は危険。じっくり眺めたいなら、木登りを勧める。
#. de: Die Ufer des Sees sind tückisch ... Wer die Agrius in Ruhe betrachten möchte, tut gut daran, sich in einem Baum niederzulassen.
#. fr: Cette épave colossale n'est pas sans nous rappeler quelles sont les ramifications des actes commis au crépuscule de la 6e ère.
#. column 13: The Keeper of the Lake
#. column 15: Maintaining a silent vigil over Silvertear Lake, the Keeper is wrought from the wreckage of the imperial flagship, the <i>Agrius</i>, and the entangled remains of Midgardsormr. For many religious and mythological enthusiasts, it stands as proof of the existence of the gods. For most people, however, it serves as a grim reminder of the horrific power of Garlemald.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162767:0:14"
msgid "Overheard in a tavern: \"I was an adventurer meself, aye. Till that day when, from atop a tree, I saw that ungodly thing─that twisted mass of metal and scale. Ran from the lake as fast as my legs could carry me. Reckoned I'd be safer livin' the rest of my days out of a bottle.\""
msgstr "«Сам я был искателем приключений, ага. Пока однажды не увидел с верхушки дерева эту нечестивую громадину — переплетение металла и чешуи. Удрал от озера так быстро, как только ноги унесли. Решил, что безопаснее коротать остаток дней за бутылкой»."

#. ja: あたかも塔のように屹立する、艦首から湖に墜落したガレマール帝国軍の飛空戦艦、「アグリウス」の残骸。古来より銀泪湖の守り神として信仰を集めてきた、幻龍「ミドガルズオルム」の亡骸が巻きついている
#. de: Wie eine bizarre Skulptur ragt das Wrack des garleischen Luftschlachtschiffs Agrius aus dem Silbertränensee, umschlungen von den Überresten des einstigen Hüters des Sees, dem Drachen Midgardsormr.
#. fr: Serrée dans les anneaux du dragon Midgardsormr, qu'on appelle aussi le “dieu gardien de Pleurargent”, et dressée au milieu du lac, cette monstrueuse épave est tout ce qui reste de l'Agrius, un gigantesque aéronef que Garlemald avait lancé à l'assaut d'Éorzéa.
#. column 13: The Keeper of the Lake
#. column 14: Overheard in a tavern: "I was an adventurer meself, aye. Till that day when, from atop a tree, I saw that ungodly thing─that twisted mass of metal and scale. Ran from the lake as fast as my legs could carry me. Reckoned I'd be safer livin' the rest of my days out of a bottle."
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162767:0:15"
msgid "Maintaining a silent vigil over Silvertear Lake, the Keeper is wrought from the wreckage of the imperial flagship, the <i>Agrius</i>, and the entangled remains of Midgardsormr. For many religious and mythological enthusiasts, it stands as proof of the existence of the gods. For most people, however, it serves as a grim reminder of the horrific power of Garlemald."
msgstr "Безмолвно возвышаясь над Серебряным озером, Хранитель сложен из обломков имперского флагмана «<i>Агриус</i>» и переплетённых останков Мидгардсормра. Для многих любителей религии и мифов он служит доказательством существования богов. Для большинства же это мрачное напоминание о чудовищной мощи Гарлемальда."

#. ja: ファルコンネスト
#. de: Falkenhorst
#. fr: Nid du faucon
#. column 14: From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: From its humble origins as a lonely cluster of barracks nestled in the mountains of western Coerthas, the village of Falcon's Nest grew and prospered until the Calamity came and the icy winter took its deathly toll. Its name derives from the falconers who reside there with their snow white charges, defending their mountain home from the Dravanian threat.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162768:0:13"
msgid "Falcon's Nest"
msgstr "Соколиное гнездо"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nクルザス西部高地のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des westlichen Hochlands von Coerthas blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe les Hautes terres du Coerthas occidental d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Falcon's Nest
#. column 15: From its humble origins as a lonely cluster of barracks nestled in the mountains of western Coerthas, the village of Falcon's Nest grew and prospered until the Calamity came and the icy winter took its deathly toll. Its name derives from the falconers who reside there with their snow white charges, defending their mountain home from the Dravanian threat.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162768:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины западных нагорий Курхаса я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: 哨兵の兵舎から発展したクルザス西部高地の山村。第七霊災以後の寒冷化の被害が大きく、多くの凍死者が出た。村名は、ドラゴン族を警戒するために、村に鷹匠が常駐し、無数の白隼を飼っていたことに由来する
#. de: Falkenhorst geht auf eine einsame Ansammlung simpler Baracken in den Bergen von West-Coerthas zurück, die sich zu einem blühenden Dorf entwickelte - bis die Katastrophe hereinbrach und der brutale Winter seinen Blutzoll forderte. Seinen Namen hat es von den Falknern, die hier ihre schneeweißen Zöglinge aufsteigen und nach Drachen Ausschau halten lassen.
#. fr: Ce hameau de montagne s'était à l'origine développé autour d'un petit poste de garde. Hélas, on y déplora de nombreuses pertes à cause du refroidissement brutal qui survint après le septième fléau. Le nom de la bourgade vient de la présence ancestrale de nombreuses familles de fauconniers dans la région<nbsp>: on y élevait des gerfauts pour surveiller les allées et venues des dragons.
#. column 13: Falcon's Nest
#. column 14: From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162768:0:15"
msgid "From its humble origins as a lonely cluster of barracks nestled in the mountains of western Coerthas, the village of Falcon's Nest grew and prospered until the Calamity came and the icy winter took its deathly toll. Its name derives from the falconers who reside there with their snow white charges, defending their mountain home from the Dravanian threat."
msgstr "Когда-то на месте этого поселения в горах западного Курхаса стояли лишь одинокие казармы. Со временем деревня Соколиное гнездо разрослась и процвела, пока не пришло Бедствие и морозная зима не унесла множество жизней. Название она получила от сокольничих: те живут здесь со своими белоснежными соколами и защищают горный дом от драконов."

#. ja: キャンプ・リバーズミート
#. de: Camp Zweistrom
#. fr: Camp des Deux-Rivières
#. column 14: From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: Once a key military outpost for the Ishgardian forces, this strategic location where the waters of the Swiftrun and the Coerthas flow together is home to a lone aetheryte shard, which has stood abandoned in the years since the Calamity.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162769:0:13"
msgid "Camp Riversmeet"
msgstr "Лагерь Слияния рек"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nクルザス西部高地のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des westlichen Hochlands von Coerthas blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe les Hautes terres du Coerthas occidental d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Camp Riversmeet
#. column 15: Once a key military outpost for the Ishgardian forces, this strategic location where the waters of the Swiftrun and the Coerthas flow together is home to a lone aetheryte shard, which has stood abandoned in the years since the Calamity.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162769:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины западных нагорий Курхаса я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: イシュガルドの騎兵団が駐屯していた露営地。エーテライトが置かれた拠点であったが、霊災後に放棄された。クルザス川とスウィフトラン川が合流する場所に作られたため、「川が出会う場所」という意味の名を持つ
#. de: Dieser verlassene Ishgarder Außenposten befand sich in strategisch wichtiger Lage dort, wo der Schnellenstrom und der Coerthas zusammenfließen. Von seiner einstigen Bedeutung zeugen heute die Überreste des Ätheryten, der durch die Katastrophe vom Netz getrennt wurde.
#. fr: Un bivouac désaffecté où des chevaliers ishgardais étaient jadis stationnés. Une éthérite y avait également été installée, mais elle fut abandonnée après la calamité. Le campement surplombe le confluent de deux rivières, la Vivaigue et la Coerthas, ce qui lui a donné son nom.
#. column 13: Camp Riversmeet
#. column 14: From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162769:0:15"
msgid "Once a key military outpost for the Ishgardian forces, this strategic location where the waters of the Swiftrun and the Coerthas flow together is home to a lone aetheryte shard, which has stood abandoned in the years since the Calamity."
msgstr "Когда-то здесь располагался важный военный лагерь ишгардских сил. В стратегическом месте слияния рек Свифтран и Коэртас до сих пор стоит одинокий осколок эфирита, заброшенный после Бедствия."

#. ja: 臥竜島
#. de: Träumender Drache
#. fr: Île de Rêvedragon
#. column 14: From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: What appears to be an island floating amidst the icy waters of Ashpool is said to have once been a living, breathing dragon─magicked into slumber by the Holy See until ash enveloped its body and its limbs turned nigh unto stone.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162770:0:13"
msgid "The Dreaming Dragon"
msgstr "Дремлющий дракон"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nクルザス西部高地のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des westlichen Hochlands von Coerthas blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe les Hautes terres du Coerthas occidental d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: The Dreaming Dragon
#. column 15: What appears to be an island floating amidst the icy waters of Ashpool is said to have once been a living, breathing dragon─magicked into slumber by the Holy See until ash enveloped its body and its limbs turned nigh unto stone.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162770:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины западных нагорий Курхаса я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: 今や凍り付いた湖、アッシュプールにある島。強大なドラゴン族を鎮めるため、教皇庁の法術団が魔法で眠らせ続けたところ、いつしかその身体に灰が付着し岩となり、ついには島になってしまったと伝えられている
#. de: Was aussieht wie eine gigantische Felsinsel in den eisigen Wassern des Aschenpfuhls soll einst ein quicklebendiger Drache gewesen sein, dort durch Wirken der Kurie in eine magische Starre gezwungen, bis Asche seinen Körper bedeckte und seine Glieder sich in Stein wandelten.
#. fr: Une île au milieu de Cendrétang. La légende veut qu'après une dure bataille au bord du lac désormais gelé, un immense dragon ait été maintenu dans un profond sommeil par la magie de légistes ishgardais. La bête a dormi si longtemps que la cendre qui s'était déposée sur sa peau s'est changée en pierre et qu'il a fini par devenir cet îlot à la forme étrange.
#. column 13: The Dreaming Dragon
#. column 14: From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162770:0:15"
msgid "What appears to be an island floating amidst the icy waters of Ashpool is said to have once been a living, breathing dragon─magicked into slumber by the Holy See until ash enveloped its body and its limbs turned nigh unto stone."
msgstr "На острове посреди ледяных вод Пепельного озера, говорят, некогда жил настоящий дракон. Святой Престол усыпил его магией, и пепел постепенно облепил тело, а конечности почти превратились в камень."

#. ja: ダスクヴィジル
#. de: Abendrot-Wacht
#. fr: Vigile du Crépuscule
#. column 14: From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: The Calamity was not kind to this once-proud watchtower, from which Ser Yuhelmeric and the brave knights of House Durendaire once stood watch against the encroaching Horde. Since the walls fell and the chill took hold, it has come to be inhabited by all manner of fell beasts, and gods only know what else.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162771:0:13"
msgid "The Dusk Vigil"
msgstr "Дозор Сумерек"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nクルザス西部高地のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des westlichen Hochlands von Coerthas blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe les Hautes terres du Coerthas occidental d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: The Dusk Vigil
#. column 15: The Calamity was not kind to this once-proud watchtower, from which Ser Yuhelmeric and the brave knights of House Durendaire once stood watch against the encroaching Horde. Since the walls fell and the chill took hold, it has come to be inhabited by all manner of fell beasts, and gods only know what else.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162771:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины западных нагорий Курхаса я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: イシュガルドの対竜要塞「ダスクヴィジル」。元々は、ユヘルメリック卿率いるデュランデル家の騎兵団が駐屯していたが、霊災時に城壁の一部が崩壊。その後の寒冷化により氷に閉ざされ、今や魔物の巣窟と化している
#. de: Die Katastrophe hat der einst mächtigen Bastion übel mitgespielt. Vor vielen Generationen hielten Yuhelmeric und seine furchtlosen Ritter hier die herannahende Drachenbrut in Schach, doch seit die Mauern geborsten und der Frost eingekehrt ist, haben sich die scheußlichsten Kreaturen dort niedergelassen.
#. fr: À l'instar des autres Vigiles, ce bastion de la lutte anti-dragons fut édifié pour défendre Ishgard contre ses ennemis héréditaires. Des chevaliers de la maison Durendaire y étaient autrefois postés sous les ordres de sire Yuhelmeric. Le Fléau ayant détruit une partie des remparts, le froid a enfermé la place forte dans un cercueil de glace. Abandonnée, elle est aujourd'hui infestée de créatures maléfiques.
#. column 13: The Dusk Vigil
#. column 14: From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162771:0:15"
msgid "The Calamity was not kind to this once-proud watchtower, from which Ser Yuhelmeric and the brave knights of House Durendaire once stood watch against the encroaching Horde. Since the walls fell and the chill took hold, it has come to be inhabited by all manner of fell beasts, and gods only know what else."
msgstr "Бедствие не пощадило эту некогда гордую сторожевую башню. Здесь сэр Юхельмерик и отважные рыцари дома Дюрандэр несли дозор, сдерживая наступление драконьей Орды. После обрушения стен и наступления холодов башню заселили всевозможные злобные твари, да боги знают кто ещё."

#. ja: ゴルガニュ牧場
#. de: Gorgagne-Höfe
#. fr: Bergeries de Gorgagne
#. column 14: From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: Ser Gorgagne was a proud knight and bannerman of House Durendaire, until the fateful day when the heir of that house vanished from sight while under his care, never to be seen again. Devastated by the loss of the boy and his own failing, he put aside his blade and built this farm, where he quietly lived out the rest of his days.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162772:0:13"
msgid "Gorgagne Mills"
msgstr "Мельницы Горгани"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nクルザス西部高地のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des westlichen Hochlands von Coerthas blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe les Hautes terres du Coerthas occidental d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Gorgagne Mills
#. column 15: Ser Gorgagne was a proud knight and bannerman of House Durendaire, until the fateful day when the heir of that house vanished from sight while under his care, never to be seen again. Devastated by the loss of the boy and his own failing, he put aside his blade and built this farm, where he quietly lived out the rest of his days.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162772:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины западных нагорий Курхаса я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: デュランデル家に仕える騎士、ゴルガニュ卿が建てた牧場。武術師範として手塩にかけて指導していたデュランデル家の嫡男が、旅の最中に行方不明になったことで、彼は失意のうちに引退を決意。この牧場を建てたという
#. de: Gorgagne war ein stolzer Ritter und Bannerherr des Hauses Durendaire, bis eines Tages der älteste Sohn und Erbe des Hauses, dessen Obacht Gorgange oblag, verschwand und nie wieder gesehen wurde. Aus Sühne wählte der in Ungnade gefallene Ritter die Verbannung, tauschte sein Schwert gegen eine Pflugschar und beendete sein Leben als einfacher Bauer.
#. fr: Cette ferme fut bâtie par sire Gorgagne, un chevalier servant la maison Durendaire. S'étant impliqué dans l'éducation du fils aîné des Durendaire en qualité de maître d'armes, l'homme fut pro<shy>fon<shy>dé<shy>ment affecté par la disparition brutale de celui-ci lors d'un voyage. L'héritier ne donna plus jamais signe de vie, et sire Gorgagne, abattu, renonça à sa carrière militaire pour se consacrer à cette ex<shy>ploi<shy>ta<shy>tion.
#. column 13: Gorgagne Mills
#. column 14: From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162772:0:15"
msgid "Ser Gorgagne was a proud knight and bannerman of House Durendaire, until the fateful day when the heir of that house vanished from sight while under his care, never to be seen again. Devastated by the loss of the boy and his own failing, he put aside his blade and built this farm, where he quietly lived out the rest of his days."
msgstr "Сэр Горгань был гордым рыцарем и знаменосцем дома Дюрандэр, пока однажды наследник дома, за которого он отвечал, не пропал без вести. Больше его никто не видел. Не вынеся утраты мальчика и собственного промаха, Горгань сложил меч и построил эту ферму. Здесь он тихо прожил остаток своих дней."

#. ja: ヘムロック
#. de: Tannenhöhe
#. fr: Les Pruches
#. column 14: From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: Once a bustling village and home to the woodcutters who plied their trade in the western highlands of Coerthas, this settlement─named for the large evergreens unique to the area─was abandoned when the chill came, and remains a ghost town to this day.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162773:0:13"
msgid "Hemlock"
msgstr "Болиголов"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nクルザス西部高地のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des westlichen Hochlands von Coerthas blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe les Hautes terres du Coerthas occidental d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Hemlock
#. column 15: Once a bustling village and home to the woodcutters who plied their trade in the western highlands of Coerthas, this settlement─named for the large evergreens unique to the area─was abandoned when the chill came, and remains a ghost town to this day.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162773:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины западных нагорий Курхаса я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: クルザス西部高地に存在する廃村。元々は、周辺一帯にて林業を営む、木樵たちの集落であったが、霊災後の寒冷化に伴い放棄された。なお、「ヘムロック」という村名は、この地域特有のマツ科の針葉樹（ツガ）にちなむ
#. de: Früher war Tannenhöhe eine lebendige Siedlung, die den Holzfällern, die in den Bergen des westlichen Coerthas ihrer Arbeit nachgingen, als Basis diente, doch als Eis und Schnee kamen, zogen sich die Bewohner zurück und kamen nicht wieder.
#. fr: Déserté suite au grand refroidissement d'après le Fléau, ce hameau était jadis un village de bûcherons qui vivaient du bois des nombreux conifères des environs. Ce sont d'ailleurs eux qui lui ont donné son nom de <i>pruches</i> ou pérusses, de l'appellation locale de ces pins emblématiques de la région.
#. column 13: Hemlock
#. column 14: From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162773:0:15"
msgid "Once a bustling village and home to the woodcutters who plied their trade in the western highlands of Coerthas, this settlement─named for the large evergreens unique to the area─was abandoned when the chill came, and remains a ghost town to this day."
msgstr "Когда-то здесь была оживлённая деревня лесорубов, работавших в западных нагорьях Курхаса. Поселение назвали в честь местных высоких хвойных деревьев. Когда пришли холода, жители ушли, и с тех пор деревня стоит заброшенной."

#. ja: イエティの棲処
#. de: Knochenfeld
#. fr: Lit d'os
#. column 14: From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: It remains to be confirmed whether, as the tales say, yetis prefer to slumber atop makeshift bedding fashioned from the remains of their victims─in large part because prominent naturalists have been reluctant to do the fieldwork necessary to corroborate this claim.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162774:0:13"
msgid "The Bed of Bones"
msgstr "Ложе костей"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nクルザス西部高地のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des westlichen Hochlands von Coerthas blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe les Hautes terres du Coerthas occidental d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: The Bed of Bones
#. column 15: It remains to be confirmed whether, as the tales say, yetis prefer to slumber atop makeshift bedding fashioned from the remains of their victims─in large part because prominent naturalists have been reluctant to do the fieldwork necessary to corroborate this claim.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162774:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины западных нагорий Курхаса я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: イエティたちの棲処。すり鉢状になった崖が風を防ぐため、自然とこの場所に集まったようだ。ただし、現時点では有力なボスが現れていないらしく、群れとしてのまとまりに欠け、各々のイエティが別個に行動している
#. de: An Lagerfeuern erzählt man sich Geschichten, nach denen Yetis hier die Überreste ihrer Opfer verscharren und gelegentlich Knochen wie sprießende Pflanzen aus dem Erdreich hervorbrechen, doch wurde das angebliche Phänomen nie wissenschaftlich untersucht.
#. fr: Selon certaines rumeurs, les yétis pré<shy>fé<shy>re<shy>raient dormir sur des couches improvisées qu'ils con<shy>fec<shy>tion<shy>neraient avec les ossements de leurs victimes. Nul ne saurait confirmer ou infirmer ceci, notamment du fait que les plus grands naturalistes sont peu enthousiastes à l'idée d'aller vérifier sur place.
#. column 13: The Bed of Bones
#. column 14: From high atop the western highlands of Coerthas, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162774:0:15"
msgid "It remains to be confirmed whether, as the tales say, yetis prefer to slumber atop makeshift bedding fashioned from the remains of their victims─in large part because prominent naturalists have been reluctant to do the fieldwork necessary to corroborate this claim. "
msgstr "Предстоит ещё выяснить, правда ли йети, как гласят предания, любят спать на постелях, которые мастерят из останков своих жертв. Главным образом потому, что именитые натуралисты не спешат отправляться туда и проверять эти рассказы."

#. ja: グナースの塚
#. de: Loth ast Gnath
#. fr: Loth ast Gnath
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: Built from a highly viscous blend of Dravanian clay and saliva, the nests of the Gnath are surprisingly stable, able to withstand the harsh elements of the Dravanian forelands. The smoke that rises from the mound-like structures is believed to be a sort of incense with a scent that, for reasons unknown, keeps would-be dragon invaders at bay.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162775:0:13"
msgid "Loth ast Gnath"
msgstr "Лот аст Гнат"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n高地ドラヴァニアのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Dravanischen Vorlands blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe l'Avant-pays dravanien d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Loth ast Gnath
#. column 15: Built from a highly viscous blend of Dravanian clay and saliva, the nests of the Gnath are surprisingly stable, able to withstand the harsh elements of the Dravanian forelands. The smoke that rises from the mound-like structures is believed to be a sort of incense with a scent that, for reasons unknown, keeps would-be dragon invaders at bay.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162775:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины Драванских предгорий я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: 優れた狩猟民族であるグナース族の暮らす集落。分泌液と土を混ぜ合わせて作った蟻塚のような住居が林立している。建物の煙突から立ち上るのは、特殊な香草を燃やした煙であり、ドラゴン族を避ける効果があるという
#. de: Die Nestbauten der Gnath, geformt aus Lehm und Speichel, sind erstaunlich stabil und bieten Schutz vor der harschen Witterung des Dravanischen Vorlands. Der Rauch, der aus den schlotartigen Hügeln steigt, ist ein Räucherharz, das aus unbekannten Gründen geeignet ist, die Drachen fernzuhalten.
#. fr: Construits grâce à un mélange d'argile et de salive, les nids des Gnathes se montrent étonnamment solides. Ils sont notamment capables de résister aux intempéries de l'Avant-pays dravanien. La fumée qui s'élève de ces structures serait une sorte d'encens dont la fonction serait de repousser les dragons.
#. column 13: Loth ast Gnath
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162775:0:15"
msgid "Built from a highly viscous blend of Dravanian clay and saliva, the nests of the Gnath are surprisingly stable, able to withstand the harsh elements of the Dravanian forelands. The smoke that rises from the mound-like structures is believed to be a sort of incense with a scent that, for reasons unknown, keeps would-be dragon invaders at bay."
msgstr "Гнёзда гнатов построены из густой смеси драванской глины и слюны. Удивительно прочные, они выдерживают суровый климат Драванских предгорий. Дым, поднимающийся из этих холмов, считают чем-то вроде благовоний. Говорят, его запах почему-то отпугивает драконов."

#. ja: 不浄の集落
#. de: Kleiner Annex
#. fr: Annexe Mineure
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: The shattered ruins of a once-proud city. The official stance of the Holy See is that it was a settlement of heretics, razed to the ground by Halone in an act of divine retribution, though scholars disagree on the historical accuracy of this interpretation.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162776:0:13"
msgid "Anyx Minor"
msgstr "Малый Аникс"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n高地ドラヴァニアのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Dravanischen Vorlands blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe l'Avant-pays dravanien d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Anyx Minor
#. column 15: The shattered ruins of a once-proud city. The official stance of the Holy See is that it was a settlement of heretics, razed to the ground by Halone in an act of divine retribution, though scholars disagree on the historical accuracy of this interpretation.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162776:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины Драванских предгорий я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: 市街地跡と思しき遺跡群。イシュガルド教皇庁の見解では、異端者勢力が築いた「不浄の集落」であり、「戦神ハルオーネの神罰により滅びた」ものとされている。これが、歴史的事実なのか否かについては定かではない
#. de: Die Ruinen einer ehemals stolzen Stadt. Die offizielle Doktrin der Kurie sagt, dass hier eine Siedlung der Häretiker stand und von Halone in einem Akt göttlicher Einmischung dem Erdboden gleichgemacht wurde. Unabhängige Historiker bestreiten diese Darstellung.
#. fr: Ces ruines seraient les vestiges d'une grande cité disparue, mais selon la version officielle du Saint-Siège, il s'agirait de hameaux où vivaient autrefois des hérétiques et que Halone la Conquérante aurait rasés dans un acte de vengeance divine. De nombreux érudits contestent toutefois cette vision de l'Histoire.
#. column 13: Anyx Minor
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162776:0:15"
msgid "The shattered ruins of a once-proud city. The official stance of the Holy See is that it was a settlement of heretics, razed to the ground by Halone in an act of divine retribution, though scholars disagree on the historical accuracy of this interpretation."
msgstr "Разрушенные руины некогда гордого города. Святой Престол утверждает, что здесь было поселение еретиков, стёртое с лица земли Халон в наказание за грехи. Учёные же сомневаются в исторической достоверности этой версии."

#. ja: 不浄の三塔
#. de: Trinär-Annex
#. fr: Annexe Trine
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: Three towers unique in that they appear to have been built to house both man and dragon, an architectural oddity which would seem to corroborate the Holy See's position that they were erected by heretic witches for themselves and their dragon consorts.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162777:0:13"
msgid "Anyx Trine"
msgstr "Тройной Аникс"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n高地ドラヴァニアのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Dravanischen Vorlands blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe l'Avant-pays dravanien d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Anyx Trine
#. column 15: Three towers unique in that they appear to have been built to house both man and dragon, an architectural oddity which would seem to corroborate the Holy See's position that they were erected by heretic witches for themselves and their dragon consorts.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162777:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины Драванских предгорий я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: 正教の教えにて、魔女たちが建てた「異端の塔」とされる建造物。人向けの設備と、竜が停泊するための設備とを兼ね備える、極めて珍しい建築様式となっている。事実、現在ではドラゴン族たちの棲処となっているようだ
#. de: Drei Türme von einer Bauart, die es sowohl Drachen als auch Elezen gestattet, sie zu bewohnen. Diese architektonische Besonderheit würde die Deutung der Kurie stützen, nach der ketzerische Hexen die Türme erbauten, um dort mit ihren verbündeten Drachen zu hausen.
#. fr: Ces trois tours se distinguent par le fait qu'elles semblent avoir été bâties pour accueillir à la fois des humains et des dragons. Cette particularité architecturale tendrait à corroborer la position du Saint-Siège selon laquelle elles auraient été érigées par des sorcières hérétiques pour elles-mêmes et leurs conjoints draconiques.
#. column 13: Anyx Trine
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162777:0:15"
msgid "Three towers unique in that they appear to have been built to house both man and dragon, an architectural oddity which would seem to corroborate the Holy See's position that they were erected by heretic witches for themselves and their dragon consorts."
msgstr "Эти три башни устроены так, словно в них могли жить и люди, и драконы. Столь необычная архитектура, похоже, подтверждает мнение Святого Престола: башни построили ведьмы-еретики для себя и своих драконьих супругов."

#. ja: 悲嘆の飛泉
#. de: Hundertfacher Schrei
#. fr: Les Cent Râles
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: The rushing river has all but swallowed these ancient ruins at the base of Sohm Al, which now serve as a nest to all manner of beastkin who find sustenance in its waters, and the dragons who find sustenance in said beastkin.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162778:0:13"
msgid "The Hundred Throes"
msgstr "Сто Стонов"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n高地ドラヴァニアのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Dravanischen Vorlands blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe l'Avant-pays dravanien d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: The Hundred Throes
#. column 15: The rushing river has all but swallowed these ancient ruins at the base of Sohm Al, which now serve as a nest to all manner of beastkin who find sustenance in its waters, and the dragons who find sustenance in said beastkin.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162778:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины Драванских предгорий я оглядел весь мир во всей её красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: 霊峰ソーム・アルの麓に存在する、巨大な古の建造物。今では破壊され、川の流れに呑み込まれつつあり、野生の魔物や獣たちにとっては、貴重な水場となっている。また、それらを捕らえるため、ドラゴン族も現れるようだ
#. de: Der reißende Fluss hat große Teile der alten Ruinen am Fuße des Sohm Al mit sich gerissen. Dort hausen nun Ungeheuer, die sich von kleineren Lebewesen in den Wassern ernähren, und Drachen, die sich von den Ungeheuern ernähren.
#. fr: Le puissant courant de la rivière a presque emporté entièrement ces anciennes ruines situées au pied de Sohm Al. Désormais, cet endroit est habité par toutes sortes de créatures qui se nourrissent des poissons et autres formes de vie, et par les dragons qui chassent ces premières.
#. column 13: The Hundred Throes
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162778:0:15"
msgid "The rushing river has all but swallowed these ancient ruins at the base of Sohm Al, which now serve as a nest to all manner of beastkin who find sustenance in its waters, and the dragons who find sustenance in said beastkin."
msgstr "Бурная река почти поглотила древние руины у подножия Сом-Ал. Теперь здесь обитают всевозможные зверолюди, которые находят пищу в её водах, и драконы, охотящиеся на них."

#. ja: 光輪の祭壇
#. de: Halo
#. fr: Halo
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I whispered a prayer to the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: This ancient altar sits in the fiery depths of Mourn. Once adorned by statues depicting a girl and a dragon, only the latter has survived to the present age. Lift your eyes above the structure, and the base of the floating peak of Sohm Al can be seen.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162779:0:13"
msgid "Halo"
msgstr "Ореол"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n高地ドラヴァニアのいずこかにあり。\nその場で祈りを捧げるべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Dravanischen Vorlands betete ich für das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Ce magnifique endroit de l'Avant-pays dravanien, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges, est un lieu idéal pour prier.
#. column 13: Halo
#. column 15: This ancient altar sits in the fiery depths of Mourn. Once adorned by statues depicting a girl and a dragon, only the latter has survived to the present age. Lift your eyes above the structure, and the base of the floating peak of Sohm Al can be seen.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162779:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I whispered a prayer to the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины Драванских предгорий я прошептал молитву миру во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: 溶岩流れるモーン大岩窟の奥底に存在する祭壇。竜と女性をモチーフにしたらしい彫像が置かれているが、女性像は破壊されて久しいようだ。そこから直上を見上げれば、ソーム・アル浮遊山の底を見ることができるだろう
#. de: Dieser uralte Altar befindet sich in den feurigen Tiefen von Mourn. Von den zwei Statuen eines Mädchens und eines Drachen, die ihn einst einrahmten, ist nur die letztere erhalten. Wer einen Blick nach oben riskiert, erkennt die Unterseite des schwebenden Gipfels von Sohm Al.
#. fr: Cet ancien autel est situé dans les profondeurs ardentes de Morne. Il était autrefois décoré de deux statues, l'une à l'effigie d'une jeune femme et l'autre d'un dragon, mais seule la seconde existe encore de nos jours. En levant les yeux à cet endroit, il est possible d'observer le pic flottant de Sohm Al.
#. column 13: Halo
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I whispered a prayer to the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162779:0:15"
msgid "This ancient altar sits in the fiery depths of Mourn. Once adorned by statues depicting a girl and a dragon, only the latter has survived to the present age. Lift your eyes above the structure, and the base of the floating peak of Sohm Al can be seen."
msgstr "Этот древний алтарь находится в огненных глубинах Скорби. Когда-то его украшали статуи девушки и дракона, но до наших дней уцелела только последняя. Если поднять глаза над алтарём, можно увидеть основание парящей вершины Сом-Ал."

#. ja: テイルフェザー
#. de: Fiederhag
#. fr: La Penne
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: Founded by hunters who came to the frontiers in hopes of snaring the wild chocobos of the forest, this settlement and those who call it home are shielded from the eyes of the dragons by the canopy of the majestic caelumtrees that rise high above it.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162780:0:13"
msgid "Tailfeather"
msgstr "Хвостовое перо"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n高地ドラヴァニアのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Dravanischen Vorlands blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe l'Avant-pays dravanien d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Tailfeather
#. column 15: Founded by hunters who came to the frontiers in hopes of snaring the wild chocobos of the forest, this settlement and those who call it home are shielded from the eyes of the dragons by the canopy of the majestic caelumtrees that rise high above it.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162780:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины Драванских предгорий я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: 野生のチョコボを求めて、秘境「チョコボの森」へとやってきた猟師たちの集落。森に林立する七天樹の樹冠によって、上空を舞うドラゴン族の目から隠れられるため、かろうじて人が生活できる状態となっている
#. de: Fallensteller und Jäger, die es auf wilde Chocobos abgesehen hatten, gründeten diese Waldsiedlung, die durch das Blätterwerk der majestätischen Siebenhimmelbäume vor den Blicken der Drachen geschützt ist.
#. fr: Créé par des chasseurs qui sont venus en ces lieux reculés dans l'espoir d'attraper les chocobos sauvages de la forêt alentour, ce hameau et ses habitants sont astucieusement protégés des regards hostiles des dragons grâce aux branches et aux feuillages des majestueux toucheciels.
#. column 13: Tailfeather
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162780:0:15"
msgid "Founded by hunters who came to the frontiers in hopes of snaring the wild chocobos of the forest, this settlement and those who call it home are shielded from the eyes of the dragons by the canopy of the majestic caelumtrees that rise high above it."
msgstr "Это поселение основали охотники, пришедшие на край света ловить диких чокобо в лесу. Высокие кроны величественных небесных деревьев скрывают их и их жилища от глаз драконов."

#. ja: ソーム・アル
#. de: Sohm Al
#. fr: Sohm Al
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: Of all the mighty peaks that comprise Abalathia's Spine, none rise higher than Sohm Al, the highest point in all Eorzea. It is held as a sacred land by the dragons, who are said to journey here when they feel their life slipping away. Formed not of stone but solid crystal, the massive mountain floating above the ground below is a marvelous sight to behold.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162781:0:13"
msgid "Sohm Al"
msgstr "Сом-Ал"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n高地ドラヴァニアのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Dravanischen Vorlands blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe l'Avant-pays dravanien d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Sohm Al
#. column 15: Of all the mighty peaks that comprise Abalathia's Spine, none rise higher than Sohm Al, the highest point in all Eorzea. It is held as a sacred land by the dragons, who are said to journey here when they feel their life slipping away. Formed not of stone but solid crystal, the massive mountain floating above the ground below is a marvelous sight to behold.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162781:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины Драванских предгорий я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: 西アバラシア山脈に座す、エオルゼアの最高峰。死期を悟ったドラゴン族が訪れる「終焉の地」であり、彼らにとっては聖地と呼べる。山全体が巨大なクリスタルであり、山腹から山頂にかけてが空中に浮かぶ姿は圧巻
#. de: Der höchste der vielen eindrucksvollen Gipfel von Abalathias Rückgrat und der höchste Ort Eorzeas. Für die Drachen ist er heiliger Boden und die letzte Ruhestätte, wenn sie sich auf die letzte Reise begeben. Der schwebende Gipfel ist nicht aus Stein, sondern purem Kristall, und ein unvergesslicher Anblick.
#. fr: De tous les monts qui forment la chaîne d'Abalathia, aucun ne s'élève aussi haut que le pic de Sohm Al, le toit d'Éorzéa. Il est considéré comme une terre sacrée par les dragons, qui s'y rendent lorsqu'ils sentent leur dernière heure arrivée. La vue de cette imposante montagne formée de cristal et non de roche, et qui flotte dans le ciel, est quelque chose d'inoubliable.
#. column 13: Sohm Al
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian forelands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162781:0:15"
msgid "Of all the mighty peaks that comprise Abalathia's Spine, none rise higher than Sohm Al, the highest point in all Eorzea. It is held as a sacred land by the dragons, who are said to journey here when they feel their life slipping away. Formed not of stone but solid crystal, the massive mountain floating above the ground below is a marvelous sight to behold."
msgstr "Среди могучих вершин хребта Абалатия нет выше Сом-Ал — это высочайшая точка всей Эорзеи. Драконы считают эту землю священной и, по преданию, приходят сюда, когда чувствуют приближение смерти. Огромная гора, парящая над землёй, сложена не из камня, а из цельного кристалла. Зрелище поистине дивное."

#. ja: モグモグホーム
#. de: Moglingen
#. fr: Nid-Mog
#. column 14: From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: A settlement that sits curiously atop Sohm Al, the tallest peak in Eorzea, in the heart of the dragons' demesne. What pact might the moogles have made with the great wyrm Hraesvelgr to allow them to live here in peace?
msgctxt "Adventure:2162782:0:13"
msgid "Moghome"
msgstr "Могдом"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nドラヴァニア雲海のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Gipfeln der Wallenden Nebel blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe L'Écume des cieux de Dravania d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Moghome
#. column 15: A settlement that sits curiously atop Sohm Al, the tallest peak in Eorzea, in the heart of the dragons' demesne. What pact might the moogles have made with the great wyrm Hraesvelgr to allow them to live here in peace?
msgctxt "Adventure:2162782:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины Бурлящих туманов я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: エオルゼア最高峰の「ソーム・アル」山頂に存在するモーグリ族の集落。ドラヴァニア雲海は、基本的にドラゴン族の領域であるが、この地のモーグリ族は聖竜「フレースヴェルグ」と盟約を交わすことで暮らしているようだ
#. de: Das Dorf der Mogrys ist ausgerechnet auf Sohm Al gelegen, dem höchsten Berg Eorzeas und Herz des Herrschaftsgebiets der Drachen. Welche Absprache die Mogrys mit Hraesvelgr getroffen haben, um hier in Frieden leben zu können, bleibt ihr Geheimnis.
#. fr: Cette colonie de Mogs est curieusement installée au sommet de Sohm Al, la plus haute montagne d'Éorzéa, au cœur du domaine des dragons. Sans doute ces créatures poilues ont-elles conclu un pacte avec le dragon ancien Hraesvelgr pour obtenir sa protection et le droit de vivre à cet endroit.
#. column 13: Moghome
#. column 14: From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162782:0:15"
msgid "A settlement that sits curiously atop Sohm Al, the tallest peak in Eorzea, in the heart of the dragons' demesne. What pact might the moogles have made with the great wyrm Hraesvelgr to allow them to live here in peace?"
msgstr "Поселение, чудом устроенное на вершине Сом Аля — высочайшей горы Эорзеи, в самом сердце владений драконов. Какой договор заключили муглы с великим змеем Хресвельгром, чтобы жить здесь в мире?"

#. ja: ドラゴンズエアリー
#. de: Nest des Drachen
#. fr: L'Aire
#. column 14: From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: Vicious aetheric storms rage in Nidhogg's lair, keeping out all those who would dare disturb the great wyrm in his slumber─be it one of years or centuries.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162783:0:13"
msgid "The Aery"
msgstr "Драконье гнездо"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nドラヴァニア雲海のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Gipfeln der Wallenden Nebel blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe L'Écume des cieux de Dravania d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: The Aery
#. column 15: Vicious aetheric storms rage in Nidhogg's lair, keeping out all those who would dare disturb the great wyrm in his slumber─be it one of years or centuries.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162783:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины Бурлящих туманов я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: 邪竜「ニーズヘッグ」が棲まう「竜の巣」。主である邪竜の魔力によって、常に雷雲をまとい簡単には近づくことができない。数十年から百年単位の活動周期を持つニーズヘッグは、休眠期に入るとこの場所で眠りにつくようだ
#. de: Heimtückische Ätherstürme toben in Nidhoggs Höhle und halten all diejenigen fern, die es wagen sollten, den Hohen Drachen in seinem Schlaf zu stören - ein Schlaf, der mal ein Jahr, mal ein Jahrhundert dauern kann.
#. fr: De violentes tempêtes éthéréennes font continuellement rage autour du repaire de Nidhogg, empêchant d'approcher tous ceux qui chercheraient à déranger le dragon ancien dans son sommeil, fût-il de quelques années ou de plusieurs siècles.
#. column 13: The Aery
#. column 14: From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162783:0:15"
msgid "Vicious aetheric storms rage in Nidhogg's lair, keeping out all those who would dare disturb the great wyrm in his slumber─be it one of years or centuries."
msgstr "В логове Нидхёгга бушуют свирепые эфирные бури, не позволяя никому потревожить великого дракона во сне — хоть тому суждено продлиться годы, хоть столетия."

#. ja: サルウーム・カシュ
#. de: Tharl Oom Khash
#. fr: Tharl Oom Khash
#. column 14: From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: An ancient structure half-consumed by crystal, its name means “crystal from remorse” in the tongue of dragons. From the sheer mass of crystallization, it has been posited that an entity possessed of aetheric power to rival the seven great wyrms laid down its life here...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162784:0:13"
msgid "Tharl Oom Khash"
msgstr "Тарл Ум Каш"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nドラヴァニア雲海のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Gipfeln der Wallenden Nebel blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe L'Écume des cieux de Dravania d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Tharl Oom Khash
#. column 15: An ancient structure half-consumed by crystal, its name means “crystal from remorse” in the tongue of dragons. From the sheer mass of crystallization, it has been posited that an entity possessed of aetheric power to rival the seven great wyrms laid down its life here...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162784:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины Бурлящих туманов я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: ドラゴン語で「悔恨よりいずるクリスタル」を意味する名の遺跡。破壊された建造物が、半ばクリスタルに埋もれている。その結晶量から推測するに、かつて七大天竜級の魔力を持つ存在が、この地で果てた可能性があるが……
#. de: Der Name dieses uralten Gebildes bedeutet „Kristall der Reue“ in der Sprache der Drachen, und es ist tatsächlich zur Hälfte von Kristallen verschlungen. Aufgrund der immensen Kristallisation wird gemutmaßt, dass ein gigantisches Geschöpf mit einer ätherischen Präsenz, die den sieben Hohen Drachen gleichkommt, hier sein Leben ausgehaucht haben könnte.
#. fr: Cet ancien édifice, dont le nom signifierait “cristal issu du remords” dans la langue des dragons, est à moitié absorbé par des formations de cette matière. De par le degré de cristallisation, certains postulent qu'un être qui possédait un pouvoir capable de rivaliser avec celui des sept dragons anciens a perdu la vie à cet endroit.
#. column 13: Tharl Oom Khash
#. column 14: From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162784:0:15"
msgid "An ancient structure half-consumed by crystal, its name means “crystal from remorse” in the tongue of dragons. From the sheer mass of crystallization, it has been posited that an entity possessed of aetheric power to rival the seven great wyrms laid down its life here..."
msgstr "Древнее сооружение наполовину поглощено кристаллом. На языке драконов его название означает «кристалл из сожаления». Судя по огромному количеству кристаллов, здесь, возможно, погибло существо, чья эфирная мощь могла сравниться с мощью семи великих драконов..."

#. ja: 白亜の宮殿
#. de: Kreidetempel
#. fr: Zénith
#. column 14: From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: A majestic fortress in Hraesvelgr's domain, watched over at the great wyrm's behest by the moogles who make their home in the Churning Mists. Though the years─a thousand of them─have taken their toll, it still stands proud and strong, stirring the hearts of all who lay eyes upon it.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162785:0:13"
msgid "Zenith"
msgstr "Зенит"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nドラヴァニア雲海のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Gipfeln der Wallenden Nebel blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe L'Écume des cieux de Dravania d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Zenith
#. column 15: A majestic fortress in Hraesvelgr's domain, watched over at the great wyrm's behest by the moogles who make their home in the Churning Mists. Though the years─a thousand of them─have taken their toll, it still stands proud and strong, stirring the hearts of all who lay eyes upon it.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162785:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины Бурлящих туманов я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: 聖竜「フレースヴェルグ」の領域にある壮麗なる宮殿。雲海のモーグリ族が、聖竜との盟約に基づいて手入れしているが、千年の時に抗うことはできず、風化が進んでいる。それでもなお、見る者の心を惹き付けてやまない
#. de: Diese Festung liegt in Hraesvelgrs Domäne und wird auf Geheiß des Drachen von den Mogrys bewacht, die ihr Zuhause in den Wallenden Nebeln haben. Obwohl die Zeit - eintausend Jahre - ihren Tribut gefordert hat, erstrahlt der Tempel noch immer in Ehrfurcht gebietendem Glanz.
#. fr: Cette majestueuse forteresse, située au centre même du domaine de Hraesvelgr, est gardée par les Mogs qui vivent dans L'Écume des cieux, selon un pacte conclu entre le dragon ancien et ces créatures. Malgré le millier d'années qui s'est écoulé, l'édifice continue de se dresser bravement, forçant le respect de tous ceux qui posent les yeux dessus.
#. column 13: Zenith
#. column 14: From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162785:0:15"
msgid "A majestic fortress in Hraesvelgr's domain, watched over at the great wyrm's behest by the moogles who make their home in the Churning Mists. Though the years─a thousand of them─have taken their toll, it still stands proud and strong, stirring the hearts of all who lay eyes upon it."
msgstr "Величественная крепость во владениях Фресвельга. По приказу великого дракона за ней присматривают моглы, живущие в Бурлящих туманах. Тысяча лет не прошла бесследно, но крепость всё ещё гордо возвышается и трогает сердца тех, кто на неё взглянет."

#. ja: ランドロード像
#. de: Der Verirrte Grundherr
#. fr: L'Isolé
#. column 14: From high atop the Churning Mists, I whispered a prayer to the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: This colossus stands on an island in Greensward. Its name was bestowed by the moogles, who believe it to be a statue of the “king of the land-dwellers,” though no records remain that could shed light on the identity of this individual, and whether or not he ever truly walked the realm.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162786:0:13"
msgid "The Lost Landlord"
msgstr "Затерянный землевладелец"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nドラヴァニア雲海のいずこかにあり。\nその場で祈りを捧げるべし。
#. de: Von Gipfeln der Wallenden Nebel betete ich für das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Ce magnifique endroit de L'Écume des cieux de Dravania, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges, est un lieu idéal pour prier.
#. column 13: The Lost Landlord
#. column 15: This colossus stands on an island in Greensward. Its name was bestowed by the moogles, who believe it to be a statue of the “king of the land-dwellers,” though no records remain that could shed light on the identity of this individual, and whether or not he ever truly walked the realm.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162786:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Churning Mists, I whispered a prayer to the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины Бурлящих туманов я прошептал молитву миру во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: グリーンスウォード島に隣接する浮島に存在する巨大な人物像。モーグリ族は「地上人の王」と考えているらしく、「ランドロード像」と呼ばれている。しかし、記録が失われた今、何者を象ったものなのかは解っていない
#. de: Dieser Koloss erhebt sich auf einer Insel gleich neben Grünwarte. Den Namen erhielt er von den Mogrys, die glaubten, dass die Statue den „König der Bodenbewohner“ darstellt. Doch niemand weiß, ob die Statue ein bloßes Kunstwerk ist oder eine tatsächliche Person abbildet.
#. fr: Cet imposant monument se dresse sur une île adjacente à celle appelée Clos-Vert. Les Mogs l'appelle L'Isolé car ils pensent qu'il s'agit d'une statue à l'effigie d'un “roi des habitants de la terre qui se serait perdu”. Il n'existe toutefois aucun document qui pourrait permettre d'établir l'identité de cet individu.
#. column 13: The Lost Landlord
#. column 14: From high atop the Churning Mists, I whispered a prayer to the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162786:0:15"
msgid "This colossus stands on an island in Greensward. Its name was bestowed by the moogles, who believe it to be a statue of the “king of the land-dwellers,” though no records remain that could shed light on the identity of this individual, and whether or not he ever truly walked the realm."
msgstr "Эта исполинская статуя стоит на острове неподалёку от Зелёного луга. Муглы дали ей имя Потерянный владелец: они считают, что она изображает «короля жителей земли». Записей, которые могли бы раскрыть, кто этот человек и существовал ли он на самом деле, не сохранилось."

#. ja: 手紙の家
#. de: Haus der Blätter
#. fr: Maison des lettreux
#. column 14: From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: The thousand-year-old ruins of a tower said to have been built by the hand of man and dragon in the days before the war. Even now, as it lies crumbling in ruin, one can still make out the letters engraved in its walls, which have led the moogles to give it the name by which it is now commonly known.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162787:0:13"
msgid "The House of Letters"
msgstr "Дом букв"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nドラヴァニア雲海のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Gipfeln der Wallenden Nebel blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe L'Écume des cieux de Dravania d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: The House of Letters
#. column 15: The thousand-year-old ruins of a tower said to have been built by the hand of man and dragon in the days before the war. Even now, as it lies crumbling in ruin, one can still make out the letters engraved in its walls, which have led the moogles to give it the name by which it is now commonly known.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162787:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высокой вершины Бурлящих туманов я оглядел весь мир во всей его красе.\nИ увидел такое, о чём будут слагать песни, пока не умолкнут песни."

#. ja: 古の昔に、人と竜とが協力して造り上げたと思しき遺跡。半ば瓦礫と化した建物のあちこちに、文字が刻まれていたため、現地のモーグリ族は「手紙の家」と呼んでいる。そこには千年前の遺物が、今なお遺されているという
#. de: Die eintausend Jahre alten Ruinen eines Turms, der vor dem Krieg von Drachen und Ishgardern errichtet wurde. Selbst jetzt, da er in Trümmern liegt, lassen sich noch die Buchstaben seiner Wandinschriften erkennen. Die Mogry gaben diesem Ort seinen Namen, denn die Inschriften, die sie nicht entziffern konnten, erinnerten sie an die Blätter eines Briefes.
#. fr: Ces murs vieux de mille ans sont tout ce qu'il reste d'une tour qui aurait été bâtie par les humains et les dragons avant qu'ils ne se déclarent la guerre. Les lettres gravées que l'on peut encore deviner sur certaines de ces vieilles pierres ont amené les Mogs à donner à ces vestiges le nom qu'on leur connaît ac<shy>tu<shy>el<shy>le<shy>ment.
#. column 13: The House of Letters
#. column 14: From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162787:0:15"
msgid "The thousand-year-old ruins of a tower said to have been built by the hand of man and dragon in the days before the war. Even now, as it lies crumbling in ruin, one can still make out the letters engraved in its walls, which have led the moogles to give it the name by which it is now commonly known."
msgstr "Руины башни, которой около тысячи лет. Говорят, до войны её построили люди вместе с драконами. Башня давно обрушилась, но на стенах всё ещё можно различить вырезанные буквы — за них моглы и прозвали это место Домом букв."

#. ja: 飛竜泊
#. de: Drachen<shy>korridor
#. fr: La Roquerie
#. column 14: From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: As the moogles tell it, the place known as the Rookery was once a bustling skyport where wayfarers came and went on the backs of trained wyverns. These days, the buildings remain, but the only dragons in sight are the vicious minions of Nidhogg.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162788:0:13"
msgid "The Rookery"
msgstr "Драконье гнездовье"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nドラヴァニア雲海のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Gipfeln der Wallenden Nebel blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe L'Écume des cieux de Dravania d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: The Rookery
#. column 15: As the moogles tell it, the place known as the Rookery was once a bustling skyport where wayfarers came and went on the backs of trained wyverns. These days, the buildings remain, but the only dragons in sight are the vicious minions of Nidhogg.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162788:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высоты Клубящихся туманов я любовался величием края. И увидел там зрелище, о котором будут петь, пока звучат песни."

#. ja: モーグリ族に伝わる伝承によれば、飛竜ワイバーンの背に乗るために、多くの人が訪れたという「空の港」。今なお堅牢な建造物の一部が遺っているが、そこに棲まうドラゴン族は、人と見れば襲いかかる邪竜の眷属ばかりだ
#. de: Der Drachen<shy>korridor war einst ein Zugang zum Himmel - ein geschäftiger Ort, an dem Reisende auf abgerichteten Wyvern in die Lüfte stiegen und landeten. Dieser Tage landen hier nur noch Diener Nidhoggs.
#. fr: D'après les dires des Mogs, l'endroit connu sous le nom de la Roquerie était autrefois un port animé par lequel de nombreux voyageurs allaient et venaient à dos de wyverne. Si certes les bâtiments continuent d'exister, les dragons que l'on peut y voir de nos jours ne sont autres que de dangereux serviteurs de Nidhogg.
#. column 13: The Rookery
#. column 14: From high atop the Churning Mists, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162788:0:15"
msgid "As the moogles tell it, the place known as the Rookery was once a bustling skyport where wayfarers came and went on the backs of trained wyverns. These days, the buildings remain, but the only dragons in sight are the vicious minions of Nidhogg."
msgstr "По рассказам муглов, Драконье гнездовье когда-то было оживлённым небесным портом: путники прибывали сюда и отправлялись дальше на спинах обученных виверн. Здания стоят и поныне, но из драконов здесь встречаются лишь свирепые прислужники Нидхёгга."

#. ja: キャンプ・クラウドトップ
#. de: Camp Wolkenwipfel
#. fr: Camp de Cime-des-nuages
#. column 14: From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: An outpost manned by the Rose Knights of House Haillenarte, who stand watch against Dravanian incursions from atop the floating islets in the sky. Boasts the <i>Protector</i>, a mighty airship that would avail the Ishgardians greatly in their battle against the Horde were it ever repaired to full strength.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162789:0:13"
msgid "Camp Cloudtop"
msgstr "Лагерь Облачная вершина"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nアバラシア雲海のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Wolkenmeeres blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe L'Écume des cieux d'Abalathia d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Camp Cloudtop
#. column 15: An outpost manned by the Rose Knights of House Haillenarte, who stand watch against Dravanian incursions from atop the floating islets in the sky. Boasts the <i>Protector</i>, a mighty airship that would avail the Ishgardians greatly in their battle against the Horde were it ever repaired to full strength.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162789:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высоты Моря облаков я любовался величием края. И увидел там зрелище, о котором будут петь, пока звучат песни."

#. ja: アインハルト家の「薔薇騎兵団」が駐屯する拠点。浮島を利用することで、高空からドラゴン族を監視するために設立された。なお、新造飛空艇「プロテクトゥール号」が配備されているが、故障続きで戦闘能力は皆無らしい
#. de: Ein Außenposten, der mit den Rosenkavalleristen des Hauses Haillenarte bemannt ist, die unablässig Ausschau nach Angreifern aus Dravania halten. Der ganze Stolz des Postens ist die <i>Protektor</i>, ein gewaltiges Luftschiff, das den Ishgardern einen erheblichen Vorteil im Luftkampf verschaffen könnte, wenn es nur vollständig einsatzfähig wäre.
#. fr: Cet avant-poste occupé par les chevaliers de la Rose, de la maison Haillenarte, a pour principale fonction de prévenir toute incursion des Dravaniens par le biais des îles qui flottent dans le ciel. C'est également là que se trouve le Protecteur, un puissant aéronef qui donnerait un important avantage aux Ishgardais s'il n'était pas sujet à des pannes répétées.
#. column 13: Camp Cloudtop
#. column 14: From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162789:0:15"
msgid "An outpost manned by the Rose Knights of House Haillenarte, who stand watch against Dravanian incursions from atop the floating islets in the sky. Boasts the <i>Protector</i>, a mighty airship that would avail the Ishgardians greatly in their battle against the Horde were it ever repaired to full strength."
msgstr "Здесь расположился отряд Розовых рыцарей дома Эйнхардт, стерегущий небесные острова от вторжений драконов Дравании. Главная гордость лагеря — могучий дирижабль <i>«Защитник»</i>. Почини его как следует — и ишгардцам будет куда легче сражаться с Ордой."

#. ja: 渡り鳥の営巣地
#. de: Das Genist
#. fr: Le Nidifice
#. column 14: From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I allowed myself a moment's doze.\nI awoke to a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: A nest of great migratory birds that travel with the seasons from the Near East to Eorzea and back again in search of warmer climes. It is here that they lay their eggs, raise their young, and teach them to take to the skies before making the journey anew.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162790:0:13"
msgid "The Nidifice"
msgstr "Гнездовье"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nアバラシア雲海のいずこかにあり。\nその場で居眠りをするべし。
#. de: In den Höhen des Wolkenmeeres erlaubte ich mir einen Augenblick der Müdigkeit. Und was ich beim Aufwachen erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Ce magnifique endroit de L'Écume des cieux d'Abalathia, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges, est un lieu idéal pour somnoler.
#. column 13: The Nidifice
#. column 15: A nest of great migratory birds that travel with the seasons from the Near East to Eorzea and back again in search of warmer climes. It is here that they lay their eggs, raise their young, and teach them to take to the skies before making the journey anew.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162790:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I allowed myself a moment's doze.\nI awoke to a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высоты Моря облаков я позволил себе ненадолго задремать. Проснулся — а передо мной зрелище, о котором будут петь, пока звучат песни."

#. ja: 近東地域からエオルゼアへと、季節毎に移動する渡り鳥の営巣地。寒さを逃れるようにして、やって来た怪鳥たちは、この地で産卵し、子育てをする。そして、ヒナたちが飛び方を覚えて巣立つと東の空へと帰っていく
#. de: Große Wandervögel nisten hier während ihres Zugs vom Nahen Osten nach Eorzea und zurück. Jungvögel, die in den tückischen Winden des Wolkenmeeres flügge werden, meistern den Rest der Wegstrecke ohne Probleme.
#. fr: C'est à cet endroit que divers oiseaux, qui voyagent entre le Proche-Orient et Éorzéa, viennent faire leurs nids. Là, ils pondent leurs œufs, élevent leurs petits et finalement leur apprennent à prendre leur envol, pour ainsi poursuivre le cycle inlassable de leurs migrations.
#. column 13: The Nidifice
#. column 14: From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I allowed myself a moment's doze.\nI awoke to a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162790:0:15"
msgid "A nest of great migratory birds that travel with the seasons from the Near East to Eorzea and back again in search of warmer climes. It is here that they lay their eggs, raise their young, and teach them to take to the skies before making the journey anew."
msgstr "В поисках тепла большие перелётные птицы каждый сезон кочуют с Ближнего Востока в Эорзею и обратно. Здесь они откладывают яйца, растят птенцов и учат их летать, а затем снова отправляются в путь."

#. ja: ヴール・シアンシラン
#. de: Voor Sian Siran
#. fr: Voor Sian Siran
#. column 14: From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: A spring formed from moisture in the atmosphere accumulated and solidified by the power of water crystals. It is said that the knight who first discovered these ethereal waters shared the story with a wandering minstrel, who declared it to be the legendary paradise of Voor Sian Siran. However, this claim has been met with some skepticism, given the minstrel's penchant for embellishment.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162791:0:13"
msgid "Voor Sian Siran"
msgstr "Воор Сиан Сиран"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nアバラシア雲海のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Wolkenmeeres blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe L'Écume des cieux d'Abalathia d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Voor Sian Siran
#. column 15: A spring formed from moisture in the atmosphere accumulated and solidified by the power of water crystals. It is said that the knight who first discovered these ethereal waters shared the story with a wandering minstrel, who declared it to be the legendary paradise of Voor Sian Siran. However, this claim has been met with some skepticism, given the minstrel's penchant for embellishment.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162791:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высоты Моря облаков я любовался величием края. И увидел там зрелище, о котором будут петь, пока звучат песни."

#. ja: 水属性クリスタルの作用で、大気中の水分が集められ作られた泉。この美しい泉を発見した騎兵たちは、吟遊詩人が語り継ぐ、伝説上の景勝地「ヴール・シアンシラン」にちなんで、そう呼ぶことに決めたという
#. de: Eine Wasserquelle, genährt von der Feuchtigkeit der Luft und mannshohen Was<shy>ser<shy>kris<shy>tal<shy>len. Der Ritter, der sie zuerst erblickte, teilte seine wundersame Entdeckung mit einem Barden, der die Erscheinung in einer umgehend komponierten Ballade mit dem legendären Paradies von Voor Sian Siran verglich.
#. fr: Cette source s'est formée à partir de l'humidité de l'atmosphère, qui s'est accumulée sous l'effet de cristaux d'eau. Le chevalier qui a découvert cet endroit fabuleux en aurait fait part à un ménestrel errant, et celui-ci aurait alors composé un chant où il a comparé la beauté des lieux au paradis légendaire de Voor Sian Siran.
#. column 13: Voor Sian Siran
#. column 14: From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162791:0:15"
msgid "A spring formed from moisture in the atmosphere accumulated and solidified by the power of water crystals. It is said that the knight who first discovered these ethereal waters shared the story with a wandering minstrel, who declared it to be the legendary paradise of Voor Sian Siran. However, this claim has been met with some skepticism, given the minstrel's penchant for embellishment."
msgstr "Источник, возникший благодаря кристаллам воды: они собирают и уплотняют влагу из воздуха. Говорят, рыцарь, первым обнаруживший эти дивные воды, рассказал о них странствующему менестрелю. Тот провозгласил источник легендарным раем Воор Сиан Сиран. Правда, менестрелю этому была свойственна склонность приукрашивать, так что его словам верят не все."

#. ja: モック・ウーグル島
#. de: Mok Oogl
#. fr: Île Mok Oogl
#. column 14: From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: An island whose name, in the tongue of the Vanu Vanu, translates to “a noise heard on high.” On the island stands a monument engraved with a mark of moogle design, but no sign of the creatures themselves, leaving its origins clouded in mystery.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162792:0:13"
msgid "Mok Oogl Island"
msgstr "Остров Мок Угл"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nアバラシア雲海のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Wolkenmeeres blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe L'Écume des cieux d'Abalathia d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Mok Oogl Island
#. column 15: An island whose name, in the tongue of the Vanu Vanu, translates to “a noise heard on high.” On the island stands a monument engraved with a mark of moogle design, but no sign of the creatures themselves, leaving its origins clouded in mystery.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162792:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высоты Моря облаков я любовался величием края. И увидел там зрелище, о котором будут петь, пока звучат песни."

#. ja: バヌバヌ語で「高い場所にある音」を意味する「モック・ウーグル」と名付けられた島。そこには、モーグリ族が好む意匠が刻まれた碑石が残されているが、彼らの姿はない。どのような歴史を持つ場所なのだろうか
#. de: Der Name der Insel bedeutet in der Sprache der Vanu Vanu so viel wie „Klang der Höhe“. Das mit einem Mogry-Symbol versehene Monument ist ein Rätsel, haben die flatternden Kreaturen doch nie diese Insel bewohnt.
#. fr: Sur cette île, dont le nom signifie “bruit venu d'en haut” dans la langue des Vanu Vanu, se trouve un monument portant un dessin d'origine mog. Il faut toutefois préciser qu'aucune de ces créatures poilues ne semble vivre dans les environs, ce qui laisse une grande part de mystère quant à l'origine de l'édifice.
#. column 13: Mok Oogl Island
#. column 14: From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162792:0:15"
msgid "An island whose name, in the tongue of the Vanu Vanu, translates to “a noise heard on high.” On the island stands a monument engraved with a mark of moogle design, but no sign of the creatures themselves, leaving its origins clouded in mystery."
msgstr "Название острова на языке вану-вану означает «звук, слышимый в вышине». Здесь стоит памятник с изображением мугла, но самих муглов поблизости нет. Откуда он взялся — загадка."

#. ja: 舞い降りた羽根の屋敷
#. de: Haus der Gefallenen Feder
#. fr: Maison de la Plume tombée
#. column 14: From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: Among the most sacred locations of the Vanu Vanu, this is said to be the spot where a single feather from Bismarck, ruler of the clouds, fell to the surface. In recent years, the elder of the violent Vundu tribe has claimed it as his seat of power, from which he rules with an iron claw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162793:0:13"
msgid "Hall of the Fallen Plume"
msgstr "Чертог упавшего пера"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nアバラシア雲海のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Wolkenmeeres blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe L'Écume des cieux d'Abalathia d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Hall of the Fallen Plume
#. column 15: Among the most sacred locations of the Vanu Vanu, this is said to be the spot where a single feather from Bismarck, ruler of the clouds, fell to the surface. In recent years, the elder of the violent Vundu tribe has claimed it as his seat of power, from which he rules with an iron claw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162793:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высоты Моря облаков я любовался величием края. И увидел там зрелище, о котором будут петь, пока звучат песни."

#. ja: 雲神「ビスマルク」の羽根が、舞い降りてきたという伝承が語り部によって語り継がれている、バヌバヌ族の聖地のひとつ。現在は、ブンド族の長老の屋敷が建てられており、権力の象徴として利用されている
#. de: Eine der heiligsten Stätten der Vanu Vanu. Hier soll eine einzelne Feder des Primae Bismarck vom Himmel gefallen und den Boden berührt haben. Der Älteste des aggressiven Stammes der Vundo hat diesen Ort zu seinem Sitz gemacht und herrscht von hier aus mit eiserner Kralle.
#. fr: Ce bâtiment, qui compte parmi les lieux les plus sacrés pour les Vanu Vanu, a été construit à l'endroit où une plume de Bismarck, le Migrateur des brumes, serait tombée. C'est là que l'ancien de la tribu agressive des Vundu aurait choisi d'asseoir son pouvoir.
#. column 13: Hall of the Fallen Plume
#. column 14: From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162793:0:15"
msgid "Among the most sacred locations of the Vanu Vanu, this is said to be the spot where a single feather from Bismarck, ruler of the clouds, fell to the surface. In recent years, the elder of the violent Vundu tribe has claimed it as his seat of power, from which he rules with an iron claw."
msgstr "Одно из самых священных мест вану-вану. По преданию, именно здесь на землю упало перо Бисмарка, владыки облаков. В последние годы тут обосновался старейшина воинственного племени вунду и правит отсюда железной рукой."

#. ja: オク・ブンド・ヴァナ
#. de: Ok' Vundo Vana
#. fr: Ok' Vundu Vana
#. column 14: From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: Roughly translating as “high home of the Vundu,” this village is home to the Vanu Vanu's aggressive Vundu tribe. Exceedingly proud, the Vundu believe that the voices of those who live highest in the skies will be heard loud and clear by the ruler of the clouds.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162794:0:13"
msgid "Ok' Vundu Vana"
msgstr "Ок' Вунду Вана"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nアバラシア雲海のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Wolkenmeeres blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe L'Écume des cieux d'Abalathia d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Ok' Vundu Vana
#. column 15: Roughly translating as “high home of the Vundu,” this village is home to the Vanu Vanu's aggressive Vundu tribe. Exceedingly proud, the Vundu believe that the voices of those who live highest in the skies will be heard loud and clear by the ruler of the clouds.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162794:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высоты Моря облаков я любовался величием края. И увидел там зрелище, о котором будут петь, пока звучат песни."

#. ja: バヌバヌ族の主流氏族「ブンド」の根拠地。バヌバヌ語で「オク」は「村」、「ヴァナ」は「高所」を示す。高い場所ほど、雲神に声が届きやすいと考えられているため、標高の高いこの場所は、彼らにとって重要な意味を持つ
#. de: Grob übersetzt „hohes Dorf der Vundo“ - und tatsächlich ist dieses Dorf Heimat des aggressiven Stammes der Vundo. Diese Vanu Vanu glauben, dass die Stimmen derer, die den höchsten Punkt im Himmel bewohnen, vom Herrscher der Wolken, Bismarck, erhört werden.
#. fr: Se traduisant à peu près par “haut village des Vundu”, Ok' Vundu Vana est le domicile de la tribu de Vanu Vanu la plus agressive. D'un tempérament fier, les Vundu croient que les voix de ceux qui vivent à l'endroit le plus élevé dans les cieux seront mieux entendues par le Migrateur des brumes.
#. column 13: Ok' Vundu Vana
#. column 14: From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162794:0:15"
msgid "Roughly translating as “high home of the Vundu,” this village is home to the Vanu Vanu's aggressive Vundu tribe. Exceedingly proud, the Vundu believe that the voices of those who live highest in the skies will be heard loud and clear by the ruler of the clouds."
msgstr "Здесь живёт племя вунду — воинственная ветвь вану-вану. Название деревни примерно означает «высокий дом вунду». Гордые вунду верят: чем выше живёшь, тем лучше владыка облаков услышит твой голос."

#. ja: ヘネガの坩堝
#. de: Hengrs Schmelztiegel
#. fr: Creuset de Hengr
#. column 14: From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: This oddly shaped isle, floating in the eastern reaches of the Sea of Clouds, is named for the witch Hengr, a figure of Coerthan faerie tales whose cauldron its shape is said to resemble. In recent years, it has become a gathering place for the notoriously territorial toco tocos.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162795:0:13"
msgid "Hengr's Crucible"
msgstr "Горнило Хенгр"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nアバラシア雲海のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Wolkenmeeres blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe L'Écume des cieux d'Abalathia d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Hengr's Crucible
#. column 15: This oddly shaped isle, floating in the eastern reaches of the Sea of Clouds, is named for the witch Hengr, a figure of Coerthan faerie tales whose cauldron its shape is said to resemble. In recent years, it has become a gathering place for the notoriously territorial toco tocos.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162795:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высоты Моря облаков я любовался величием края. И увидел там зрелище, о котором будут петь, пока звучат песни."

#. ja: アバラシア雲海の東部に位置する、奇妙な形の浮島。この島を発見したイシュガルドの騎士が、クルザス地方の童謡に登場する魔女「ヘネガ」の坩堝に見立てて、そう名付けた。今ではトコトコの群生地としても知られている
#. de: Die merkwürdig geformte Insel am östlichen Rand des Wolkenmeers ist nach der Hexe Hengr benannt, einer coerthischen Märchengestalt, und soll ihrem Kessel ähnlich sehen. In letzter Zeit haben sich hier die sehr territorialen Tokotokos niedergelassen, die ihr neues Revier erbittert verteidigen.
#. fr: Située dans la partie orientale de L'Écume des cieux d'Abalathia, cette île à la forme par<shy>ti<shy>cu<shy>liè<shy>re doit son nom à la sorcière Hengr, un personnage de conte de fées du Coerthas qui aurait un chaudron de forme similaire. Depuis quelque temps, elle est devenue le territoire de tocos tocos très agressifs.
#. column 13: Hengr's Crucible
#. column 14: From high atop the Sea of Clouds, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162795:0:15"
msgid "This oddly shaped isle, floating in the eastern reaches of the Sea of Clouds, is named for the witch Hengr, a figure of Coerthan faerie tales whose cauldron its shape is said to resemble. In recent years, it has become a gathering place for the notoriously territorial toco tocos."
msgstr "Этот остров причудливой формы парит в восточной части Моря облаков. Его назвали в честь ведьмы Хенгр из коэртских сказок: говорят, очертания острова напоминают её котёл. В последние годы он стал излюбленным местом крайне территориальных токотоко."

#. ja: 大工房アーキテクトン
#. de: Arkhitekton
#. fr: L'Arkhitékton
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: Once home to Sharlayan masters who fashioned aetherytes within its halls, this workshop is now home to the Illuminati, a nasty band of goblins who would wield the ancient technologies within for their own nefarious ends.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162796:0:13"
msgid "The Arkhitekton"
msgstr "Архитектон"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n低地ドラヴァニアのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Dravanischen Hinterlands blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe l'Arrière-pays dravanien d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: The Arkhitekton
#. column 15: Once home to Sharlayan masters who fashioned aetherytes within its halls, this workshop is now home to the Illuminati, a nasty band of goblins who would wield the ancient technologies within for their own nefarious ends.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162796:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высоты Драванских низин я любовался величием края. И увидел там зрелище, о котором будут петь, пока звучат песни."

#. ja: シャーレアン人の匠たちが集まる大工房だった場所。かつては、ここでエーテライトの製造を行っていた。しかし、今では知識の独占をもくろむゴブリン族の科学者集団「青の手」が占拠し、要塞化を進めているようだ
#. de: Einst bauten die Sharlayaner Ätheryten in dieser Werkstatt, doch nun wird sie von den berüchtigten Goblins der Indigohand bewohnt, die die technischen Hin<shy>ter<shy>lass<shy>en<shy>schaf<shy>ten für ihre diabolischen Pläne missbrauchen.
#. fr: Autrefois atelier géant où les Sharlayanais construisaient une éthérite, ce bâtiment est désormais sous le contrôle de la Main indigo, une société secrète de Gobelins mégalomanes qui aimeraient avoir le monopole de toutes les technologies et con<shy>nais<shy>san<shy>ces existantes en Éorzéa.
#. column 13: The Arkhitekton
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162796:0:15"
msgid "Once home to Sharlayan masters who fashioned aetherytes within its halls, this workshop is now home to the Illuminati, a nasty band of goblins who would wield the ancient technologies within for their own nefarious ends."
msgstr "Когда-то в этих мастерских трудились шаллаянские мастера, создававшие эфириты. Теперь здесь обосновалась «Синяя рука» — шайка гоблинов, которая намерена пустить древние технологии на свои грязные дела."

#. ja: シャーレアン学士街
#. de: Akademie-Viertel
#. fr: Quartier académique
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: This Sharlayan settlement stretches across the western banks of the Thaliak. Home to Saint Mocianne's Arboretum and a center for education and scholarly pursuits, it hearkens back to the cities of learning that flourished in bygone times.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162797:0:13"
msgid "The Answering Quarter"
msgstr "Квартал Ответов"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n低地ドラヴァニアのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Dravanischen Hinterlands blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe l'Arrière-pays dravanien d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: The Answering Quarter
#. column 15: This Sharlayan settlement stretches across the western banks of the Thaliak. Home to Saint Mocianne's Arboretum and a center for education and scholarly pursuits, it hearkens back to the cities of learning that flourished in bygone times.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162797:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высоты Драванских низин я любовался величием края. И увидел там зрелище, о котором будут петь, пока звучат песни."

#. ja: 植民都市「シャーレアン」のうち、サリャク河西岸に広がる一帯。聖モシャーヌ植物園をはじめとする研究、教育機関が集中した場所で、かつては多くの研究者や学士が集っていた。在りし日の「学術都市」を偲ばせる場所だ
#. de: Diese verlassene Siedlung der Sharlayaner erstreckt sich am Westufer des Flusses Thaliak. Sie beherbergt das Sankt Mocianne-Arboretum und war ein Zentrum für Bildung und Wissenschaft. Sie geht zurück auf die Städte des Lernens, die in längst vergangenen Zeiten existierten.
#. fr: Située sur la berge ouest de la rivière Thaliak, cette partie de la cité de Sharlayan se distingue par son Arboretum Sainte-Mocianne et la présence de nombreux bâtiments voués à l'éducation, montrant à quel point le savoir et la magie étaient importants pour les gens de cette nation.
#. column 13: The Answering Quarter
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162797:0:15"
msgid "This Sharlayan settlement stretches across the western banks of the Thaliak. Home to Saint Mocianne's Arboretum and a center for education and scholarly pursuits, it hearkens back to the cities of learning that flourished in bygone times."
msgstr "Поселение шаллаянцев раскинулось по западному берегу Талиака. Здесь находятся дендрарий Святой Мосианны и другие научные и учебные заведения. Квартал напоминает о былых городах, где процветала наука."

#. ja: セノタフ大石碑
#. de: Zenotaph
#. fr: Cénotaphe
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: A towering monolith erected in tribute to the great scholars who have passed on, leaving behind the knowledge that has shaped the realm. The names of countless men of learning are etched in the mighty stone, along with the motto of Sharlayan: “Knowledge Seeks No Man.”
msgctxt "Adventure:2162798:0:13"
msgid "The Cenotaph"
msgstr "Кенотаф"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n低地ドラヴァニアのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Dravanischen Hinterlands blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe l'Arrière-pays dravanien d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: The Cenotaph
#. column 15: A towering monolith erected in tribute to the great scholars who have passed on, leaving behind the knowledge that has shaped the realm. The names of countless men of learning are etched in the mighty stone, along with the motto of Sharlayan: “Knowledge Seeks No Man.”
msgctxt "Adventure:2162798:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высоты Драванских низин я любовался величием края. И увидел там зрелище, о котором будут петь, пока звучат песни."

#. ja: 知識を後世に伝えて死んでいった、多数の先人たちの偉業を今に伝えるために、戒めとともに築かれた大石碑。知の都「シャーレアン」のモットー「知識は人を求めず」と共に、歴代の大賢人の名が刻まれている
#. de: Ein steil emporragender Monolith, der in Erinnerung an die großen Denker einstiger Tage errichtet wurde, deren Theorien Eorzea maßgeblich geprägt haben. Zusammen mit dem Sharlayaner Motto „Wissen suchet nicht den Geist“ sind die Namen zahlloser Gelehrter in den Stein gemeißelt.
#. fr: Cet imposant monolithe a été érigé en l'honneur des grands érudits qui ont contribué à la quête de con<shy>nais<shy>san<shy>ces ayant permis la création de Sharlayan. Il porte notamment la longue liste de leurs noms, en plus de la devise de la cité<nbsp>: “Le savoir ne cherche pas l'homme”.
#. column 13: The Cenotaph
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162798:0:15"
msgid "A towering monolith erected in tribute to the great scholars who have passed on, leaving behind the knowledge that has shaped the realm. The names of countless men of learning are etched in the mighty stone, along with the motto of Sharlayan: “Knowledge Seeks No Man.”"
msgstr "Высокий монолит воздвигли в память о великих учёных, ушедших из жизни, но оставивших знания, изменившие мир. На камне высечены имена бесчисленных мудрецов и девиз Шарлаяна: «Знание не ищет человека»."

#. ja: 知神の水瓶
#. de: Kippender Krug
#. fr: L'Aiguière inclinée
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: The spot where the melted snows of Abalathia's Spine flow emerge from their source to descend down the mountain, forming the countless tributaries that come together as the mighty Thaliak River. The name is said to come from the deity whose name the river bears and the magicked pitcher from which poured the waters of knowledge.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162799:0:13"
msgid "The Tipped Ewer"
msgstr "Наклонённый кувшин"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n低地ドラヴァニアのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Dravanischen Hinterlands blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe l'Arrière-pays dravanien d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: The Tipped Ewer
#. column 15: The spot where the melted snows of Abalathia's Spine flow emerge from their source to descend down the mountain, forming the countless tributaries that come together as the mighty Thaliak River. The name is said to come from the deity whose name the river bears and the magicked pitcher from which poured the waters of knowledge.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162799:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высоты Драванских низин я любовался величием края. И увидел там зрелище, о котором будут петь, пока звучат песни."

#. ja: サリャク河の大瀑布。アバラシア山脈の雪解け水が地下水となり、山を下るにつれて無数の支流となって合流し、低地に入り大河となる。その名は、知神「サリャク」が掲げた「知識の水」を生む魔法の水瓶に由来している
#. de: Der Ort, an dem zahlreiche Schmelzwasserläufe aus Abalathias Rückgrat hervortreten, die Hänge hinablaufen und schließlich zum mächtigen Thaliak-Fluss zusammenfließen. Der Name leitet sich von dem Krug des Gottes Thaliak ab, aus dem sich der Fluss der Weisheit ergoss.
#. fr: Cet endroit est celui où les cours d'eau qui sont nourris par les neiges fondues des montagnes d'Abalathia se rejoignent pour devenir la puissante rivière Thaliak. Le nom serait une référence à une cruche magique de laquelle le dieu du savoir aurait versé les eaux du savoir en Éorzéa.
#. column 13: The Tipped Ewer
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162799:0:15"
msgid "The spot where the melted snows of Abalathia's Spine flow emerge from their source to descend down the mountain, forming the countless tributaries that come together as the mighty Thaliak River. The name is said to come from the deity whose name the river bears and the magicked pitcher from which poured the waters of knowledge."
msgstr "Здесь талые воды с хребта Абалатия выходят из-под земли и стекают по склону, образуя бесчисленные притоки могучей реки Талиак. Говорят, название места связано с богом, чьё имя носит река, и волшебным кувшином, из которого лились воды знания."

#. ja: グブラ幻想図書館
#. de: Große Gubal-Bibliothek
#. fr: Grande bibliothèque de Gubal
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: A massive library constructed by the Sharlayans to house the wealth of knowledge they had amassed in their travels across the realm. Though the vast majority of the tomes that once lined its shelves were carried back to the motherland in the exodus, it is said forbidden texts still slumber in sealed-off vaults below.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162800:0:13"
msgid "Great Gubal Library"
msgstr "Большая библиотека Губал"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n低地ドラヴァニアのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Dravanischen Hinterlands blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe l'Arrière-pays dravanien d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: Great Gubal Library
#. column 15: A massive library constructed by the Sharlayans to house the wealth of knowledge they had amassed in their travels across the realm. Though the vast majority of the tomes that once lined its shelves were carried back to the motherland in the exodus, it is said forbidden texts still slumber in sealed-off vaults below.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162800:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высоты Драванских низин я любовался величием края. И увидел там зрелище, о котором будут петь, пока звучат песни."

#. ja: 植民都市「シャーレアン」が、各地で集積した知識を保管するために建造した大図書館。「大撤収」により放棄された際、重要な書物は北洋の本国に持ち去られたが、今でも地下の「禁書庫」には稀少な書物が眠るという
#. de: Eine gigantische Bibliothek, die die Sharlayaner bauten, um all das Wissen zu horten, das sie während ihrer Reisen durch Eorzea gesammelt hatten. Viele Schriften nahmen die Bibliotheksherren beim großen Auszug mit zurück in ihre Heimat, doch noch immer sollen verbotene Bücher in einer versiegelten Kammer in den Kellern des Gebäudes schlummern.
#. fr: Cet édifice massif avait été construit par les Sharlayanais pour conserver les myriades de livres et autres documents qu'ils avaient accumulés au cours de leurs pérégrinations en Éorzéa. Bien que la majorité des ouvrages qui y étaient entreposés aient été emportés lors de l'exode, il resterait de nombreux textes interdits dans des salles scellées magiquement.
#. column 13: Great Gubal Library
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162800:0:15"
msgid "A massive library constructed by the Sharlayans to house the wealth of knowledge they had amassed in their travels across the realm. Though the vast majority of the tomes that once lined its shelves were carried back to the motherland in the exodus, it is said forbidden texts still slumber in sealed-off vaults below."
msgstr "Шаллаянцы построили эту огромную библиотеку, чтобы хранить знания, собранные в странствиях по свету. Во время исхода почти все книги с полок увезли на родину, но, говорят, в запертых подземных хранилищах до сих пор покоятся запретные тексты."

#. ja: オーン原生林
#. de: Orn-Busch
#. fr: Étendue d'Orn
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: A primeval forest that stretches across the northern reaches of the Dravanian hinterlands, its rich verdure sustained by the pristine waters of the Thaliak. Nigh untouched by the hand of man, its wilds stand between those who would make their way to Sharlayan without braving a trek across the forelands.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162801:0:13"
msgid "The Orn Wild"
msgstr "Дикая чаща Орн"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n低地ドラヴァニアのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Dravanischen Hinterlands blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: Lorsqu'on observe l'Arrière-pays dravanien d'un point surélevé, on peut apercevoir ce magnifique endroit, dont la beauté pourrait inspirer des chants aux bardes jusqu'à la fin des âges.
#. column 13: The Orn Wild
#. column 15: A primeval forest that stretches across the northern reaches of the Dravanian hinterlands, its rich verdure sustained by the pristine waters of the Thaliak. Nigh untouched by the hand of man, its wilds stand between those who would make their way to Sharlayan without braving a trek across the forelands.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162801:0:14"
msgid "From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung."
msgstr "С высоты Драванских низин я любовался величием края. И увидел там зрелище, о котором будут петь, пока звучат песни."

#. ja: 低地ドラヴァニアの北に広がる原生林。水量豊かなサリャク河に支えられ、ほとんど手付かずの大自然が残っている。高地ドラヴァニアを経由せずシャーレアンを目指すなら、河を遡上し、この原生林を抜けてくる必要がある
#. de: Ein urzeitlicher Wald, der sich im nördlichen Teil des Dravanischen Hinterlands erstreckt. Die üppige Natur wird gespeist von den klaren Wassern des Thaliak-Flusses. Fast gänzlich unberührt, stellen die wilden Tiere in dieser Region ein ernstes Hindernis für jeden dar, der Sharlayan ohne Abstecher durch das Vorland erreichen möchte.
#. fr: Située aux confins septentrionaux de l'Arrière-pays dravanien et irriguée par les eaux pures de la rivière Thaliak, cette large étendue est couverte par une luxuriante forêt, à laquelle l'homme n'a jamais touché et qui barre la route à quiconque voudrait atteindre Sharlayan sans traverser l'Avant-pays dravanien.
#. column 13: The Orn Wild
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162801:0:15"
msgid "A primeval forest that stretches across the northern reaches of the Dravanian hinterlands, its rich verdure sustained by the pristine waters of the Thaliak. Nigh untouched by the hand of man, its wilds stand between those who would make their way to Sharlayan without braving a trek across the forelands."
msgstr "Первобытный лес раскинулся на севере Драванских низин, а его буйная зелень питается чистыми водами Талиака. Человек почти не тронул эти места. Тем, кто хочет попасть в Шаллаян, не пересекая предгорья, придётся пробираться через здешнюю глушь."

#. ja: 聖モシャーヌ植物園
#. de: Sankt Mocianne-Arboretum
#. fr: Arboretum Sainte-Mocianne
#. column 14: From high atop the Dravanian hinterlands, I looked out upon the realm in all her glory.\nThere I saw a sight that will be sung of for as long as songs are sung.
#. column 15: This botanical garden built by the Sharlayans once was home to fauna and flora collected from across the realm, the study of which yielded numerous discoveries regarding our natural world. Sadly, it was abandoned in the exodus, the teeming life within left to run wild and unchecked.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162802:0:13"
msgid "Saint Mocianne's Arboretum"
msgstr "Дендрарий Святой Мосианны"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n低地ドラヴァニアのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Von den Höhen des Dravanischen Hinterlands blickte ich herab auf das Land, wie es dalag in seiner ganzen Schönheit. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
