#. column 15: The Beehive is a place of noise and excitement─a little sting to invigorate the safe, pampered lives of Eulmore's free citizens. Regardless of gender, this establishment's bonded workers are often called “honeybees,” while the owner reigns above them as “queen.”
msgctxt "Adventure:2162900:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through the city of Eulmore, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Странствуя по Юлмору, я замер, поражённый открывшимся видом. Его стоило запечатлеть на бумаге, чтобы другие не прошли мимо такой красоты."

#. ja: 安穏な生活を送るユールモアの自由市民に対し、蜂のひと刺しのような刺激を与えることを目的に開設された娯楽施設。ここで働く者は男女を問わず「ミツバチ」と呼ばれ、支配人は「クイーンビー」の称号で呼ばれるという
#. de: Wenn den freien Bürgern von Eulmore der Sinn nach aufregender Unterhaltung steht, gehen sie in das Lustspielhaus. Die Tänze und frivolen Theaterstücke, die dort aufgeführt werden, versetzen so manchen fettleibigen Besucher in größere Aufregung, als es ein echter Bienenstock je könnte.
#. fr: Ce lieu de récréation a été créé afin d'apporter un peu de piquant au quotidien de la classe d'habitants d'Eulmore connue sous le nom de “Libérés”. Ceux qui travaillent à La Ruche sont communément appelés les “abeilles” et leur gérante la “reine des abeilles”.
#. column 13: The Beehive
#. column 14: In my wanderings through the city of Eulmore, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162900:0:15"
msgid "The Beehive is a place of noise and excitement─a little sting to invigorate the safe, pampered lives of Eulmore's free citizens. Regardless of gender, this establishment's bonded workers are often called “honeybees,” while the owner reigns above them as “queen.”"
msgstr "Пчелиный улей — шумное и весёлое место, маленький укус, призванный взбодрить сытых и беззаботных свободных жителей Юлмора. Работников здесь, независимо от пола, зовут «пчёлками», а хозяйка носит титул «королевы»."

#. ja: ジョッブ砦
#. de: Jobb-Feste
#. fr: Fort Jobb
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Lakeland, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: Once the forward base of a long-faded knightly order, these ruins were repurposed to serve as a defensive outpost for the Crystarium guard. The architectural remnants of the Church of the First Light now merely hint at the majesty of a bygone era.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162901:0:13"
msgid "Fort Jobb"
msgstr "Форт Джобб"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nレイクランドのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Seenlands gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Grand-Lac que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Fort Jobb
#. column 15: Once the forward base of a long-faded knightly order, these ruins were repurposed to serve as a defensive outpost for the Crystarium guard. The architectural remnants of the Church of the First Light now merely hint at the majesty of a bygone era.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162901:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through Lakeland, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Лейкленду я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: クリスタリウムの防衛を担う城塞群のひとつ。元々は、レイクランド連邦時代に拓かれた騎士修道会用の拠点であり、その廃墟を利用して形作られている。今や崩れ去った光耀教会の跡地が、往時の姿を偲ばせる程度だ
#. de: Diese Festung ist Teil des Verteidigungssystems von Crystarium. Zur Zeit des Seenland-Bündnisses als Stützpunkt für einen Ritterorden erbaut, wurde die Ruine umgebaut, um ihre heutige Funktion zu erfüllen. Wie prachtvoll die Kirche des Strahlenden Lichts gewesen sein muss, die einst in der Feste stand, lässt sich anhand der Überreste kaum noch erahnen.
#. fr: Cette forteresse fait partie du système de défense de Cristarium. Bâtie originellement à l'époque de la Fédération de Grand-Lac comme base pour un ordre religieux militaire, elle a été réaménagée pour sa fonction actuelle et on y devine à peine les vestiges du passage de l'église de l'Aurore.
#. column 13: Fort Jobb
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Lakeland, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162901:0:15"
msgid "Once the forward base of a long-faded knightly order, these ruins were repurposed to serve as a defensive outpost for the Crystarium guard. The architectural remnants of the Church of the First Light now merely hint at the majesty of a bygone era."
msgstr "Когда-то здесь располагалась передовая база давно исчезнувшего рыцарского ордена. Теперь развалины служат оборонительным постом стражи Кристариума. Остатки церкви Первого Света лишь намекают на былое величие."

#. ja: ラディスカ物見塔
#. de: Radiscas Rundturm
#. fr: Garde de Radisca
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Lakeland, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: Located in the center of Lakeland, this watchtower is named in honor of a soldier who saved countless lives when he warned of a flying swarm of sin eaters. The soldier himself was slain in battle, having chosen to remain at the tower and delay the eaters' pursuit.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162902:0:13"
msgid "Radisca's Round"
msgstr "Башня Радиски"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nレイクランドのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Seenlands gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Grand-Lac que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Radisca's Round
#. column 15: Located in the center of Lakeland, this watchtower is named in honor of a soldier who saved countless lives when he warned of a flying swarm of sin eaters. The soldier himself was slain in battle, having chosen to remain at the tower and delay the eaters' pursuit.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162902:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through Lakeland, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Лейкленду я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: レイクランド中央に置かれた物見塔。ラディスカとは、かつて罪喰いの大群が飛来するのを発見し、人々を避難させることで多くの人命を救った兵の名である。しかし、彼自身は足止めのため塔に残り、戦死してしまったという
#. de: Dieser Wachturm im Zentrum des Seenlands ist nach einem Soldaten benannt, dessen Heldenmut viele Leben rettete. Als er eine herannahende Horde von Sünden<shy>ver<shy>tilgern erspähte, schlug er Alarm und blieb alleine zurück, um bis zum letzten Atemzug zu kämpfen und den anderen die Flucht zu ermöglichen.
#. fr: Cette tour de guet située au centre de Grand-Lac porte le nom d'un soldat qui a héroïquement sauvé la vie de nombreuses personnes en donnant l'alerte et en affrontant jusqu'à son dernier souffle une immense horde de purgateurs qu'il avait repérée.
#. column 13: Radisca's Round
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Lakeland, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162902:0:15"
msgid "Located in the center of Lakeland, this watchtower is named in honor of a soldier who saved countless lives when he warned of a flying swarm of sin eaters. The soldier himself was slain in battle, having chosen to remain at the tower and delay the eaters' pursuit."
msgstr "Эта сторожевая башня в центре Лейкленда названа в честь солдата, который спас множество жизней, предупредив о летящей сюда стае пожирателей грехов. Сам он пал в бою: остался у башни, чтобы задержать преследователей."

#. ja: ラクサン城
#. de: Burg Selard
#. fr: Château de Ganlag
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Lakeland, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: In the old tongue of the elves, “Laxan” is the word for “Lakeland,” and it is here that the region's erstwhile king set his throne. The castle is also infamous as the site of a historical conflict, where the Shadowkeeper led a force of elven dissidents in a final, bloody uprising.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162903:0:13"
msgid "Laxan Loft"
msgstr "Замок Лаксан"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nレイクランドのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Seenlands gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Grand-Lac que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Laxan Loft
#. column 15: In the old tongue of the elves, “Laxan” is the word for “Lakeland,” and it is here that the region's erstwhile king set his throne. The castle is also infamous as the site of a historical conflict, where the Shadowkeeper led a force of elven dissidents in a final, bloody uprising.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162903:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through Lakeland, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Лейкленду я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: かつてのレイクランド連邦の王城。「光の氾濫」の直前に、エルフ族の守旧派を率いて立ち上がった「影の王」なる人物が、最期の戦いに身を投じた場所としても有名。なお、ラクサンとはレイクランドを示す古エルフ語である
#. de: Diese Burg, die einst vom Seenland-Bündnis erbaut wurde, gilt als der Ort, an dem ein Elf, der als Schattenkönig bekannt war, seine letzte Schlacht an der Spitze der konservativen Elfen führte, kurz bevor die Lichtflut über die Welt hereinbrach. „Selard“ bedeutet in der alten Sprache der Elfen „Seenland“.
#. fr: Autrefois bâti par la Fédération de Grand-Lac, ce château est réputé pour être le lieu où un personnage connu sous le nom de roi de l'Ombre a livré sa dernière bataille à la tête des Elfes conservateurs, juste avant le déluge de Lumière. “Ganlag” serait d'ailleurs l'ancien nom elfique de Grand-Lac.
#. column 13: Laxan Loft
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Lakeland, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162903:0:15"
msgid "In the old tongue of the elves, “Laxan” is the word for “Lakeland,” and it is here that the region's erstwhile king set his throne. The castle is also infamous as the site of a historical conflict, where the Shadowkeeper led a force of elven dissidents in a final, bloody uprising."
msgstr "На древнем эльфийском «лаксан» означает «Лейкленд». Здесь некогда находилась резиденция местного короля. Замок печально известен кровавым восстанием: перед самым Потопом Света Повелитель теней возглавил мятежных эльфов в их последнем бою."

#. ja: オスタル厳命城
#. de: Ostalls Befehl
#. fr: L'Impératif d'Ostall
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Lakeland, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: The well-preserved remnants of a fortress dating back to the glory days of Lakeland. This imposing structure was named in honor of one Ser Ostall, who, according to the tales, ordered his men to stand their ground against a ravening horde of sin eaters. The knight himself refused to fall, holding off the abominations until the smallfolk had reached safe refuge.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162904:0:13"
msgid "The Ostall Imperative"
msgstr "Неотвратимый приказ Остала"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nレイクランドのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Seenlands gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Grand-Lac que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: The Ostall Imperative
#. column 15: The well-preserved remnants of a fortress dating back to the glory days of Lakeland. This imposing structure was named in honor of one Ser Ostall, who, according to the tales, ordered his men to stand their ground against a ravening horde of sin eaters. The knight himself refused to fall, holding off the abominations until the smallfolk had reached safe refuge.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162904:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through Lakeland, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Лейкленду я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: 廃墟と化したレイクランド連邦の城塞。エルフ族の騎士、オスタルは迫りくる罪喰いの大群を前に、民を護るため一歩も退いてはならないと部下たちに厳命、徹底抗戦を貫いた。現在の名は、その故事に基づくものである
#. de: Diese verlassene Festung, die auf die Zeit des Seenland-Bündnisses zurückgeht, verdankt ihren Namen dem berühmten Elfenritter Ostall, der seinen Männern dort einst einen schicksalshaften Befehl gab. Im Angesicht eines riesigen Schwarms von Sünden<shy>ver<shy>tilgern befahl er, keinen Schritt zurückzuweichen und bis zum bitteren Ende Widerstand zu leisten, um möglichst viele Zivilisten zu retten.
#. fr: Cette forteresse abandonnée datant de l'époque de la Fédération de Grand-Lac tire son nom du fameux ordre que le chevalier elfe Ostall donna à ses hommes, l'ordre étant de se battre sans faiblir face aux hordes de purgateurs afin de protéger le peuple.
#. column 13: The Ostall Imperative
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Lakeland, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162904:0:15"
msgid "The well-preserved remnants of a fortress dating back to the glory days of Lakeland. This imposing structure was named in honor of one Ser Ostall, who, according to the tales, ordered his men to stand their ground against a ravening horde of sin eaters. The knight himself refused to fall, holding off the abominations until the smallfolk had reached safe refuge."
msgstr "Хорошо сохранившиеся руины крепости времён расцвета Лейкленда. По преданию, рыцарь сэр Осталл приказал своим людям не отступать перед свирепой ордой пожирателей грехов. Сам он тоже не отступил и сдерживал чудовищ, пока простые люди не добрались до укрытия."

#. ja: 責苦の監獄
#. de: Kerkerplatte
#. fr: Suppliciante
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Lakeland, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: These crumbling ruins are all that remains of a Lakeland prison. To the east, at the base of the cliff, can be seen another memory of the past─the domiciles of the prison wardens. Once known by a less-somber name, “Mortal Irons” is thought to better reflect the settlement's abandoned state and the transient fate of its residents.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162905:0:13"
msgid "The Hour of Certain Durance"
msgstr "Час неминуемой кары"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nレイクランドのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Seenlands gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
