#. ja: 始まりの湖の湖畔にある漁村。ウィード島、ブリック島、ノット島、ラップ島という4つの島を橋で結ぶことで構成されている。しかめっ面の漁師たちが多いことから、自虐的に「不機嫌」なる奇妙な村名が付けられることとなった
#. de: Dieses Fischerdorf am Ufer des Quellsees wurde von seinen Bewohnern so genannt, weil sie selbst einsehen, dass ihr entbehrungsreiches Leben sie grantig macht. Es erstreckt sich über vier kleine Inseln namens Unkrauthügel, Backsteininsel, Buckel und Brandungsfels, die allesamt durch Brücken miteinander verbunden sind.
#. fr: Ce village de pêcheurs bâti au bord du lac de L'Origine a été appelé ainsi par ses habitants parce qu'ils aiment se dire, non sans humour, maussades. Il est relié par un réseau de ponts aux îles d'Ivraie, de Briquetière, d'Embossée et d'Écumante, lesquelles le constituent.
#. column 13: Sullen
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Lakeland, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162906:0:15"
msgid "Weed, Brick, Knot, and Lap─the fishing village of Sullen sprawls across these four small islands, its bridges connecting each location to the next, and thence to the shore of the Source itself. The settlement's name, it seems, was agreed upon as a self-deprecating nod to the oft-creased brows of its resident fishermen."
msgstr "Рыбацкая деревня Унылое раскинулась на четырёх островках — Виде, Кирпиче, Узле и Лапе. Мосты соединяют их друг с другом, а затем и с берегом Истока. Название, похоже, выбрали в шутку: у местных рыбаков вечно нахмуренные лица."

#. ja: クラックシェル海岸
#. de: Splittermuschelstrand
#. fr: Plage des Coquilles brisées
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: When questioned on the rather prosaic name of this coastline, the inhabitants of nearby Stilltide simply point to the carpet of broken seashells. In earlier days, they say the beach was crowded with the comings and goings of local fishermen, but now it is mostly the boots of barbaric hobgoblins leaving tracks along the pebbled shore.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162907:0:13"
msgid "Cracked Shell Beach"
msgstr "Пляж битых ракушек"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nコルシア島のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Kholusias gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Kholusia que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Cracked Shell Beach
#. column 15: When questioned on the rather prosaic name of this coastline, the inhabitants of nearby Stilltide simply point to the carpet of broken seashells. In earlier days, they say the beach was crowded with the comings and goings of local fishermen, but now it is mostly the boots of barbaric hobgoblins leaving tracks along the pebbled shore.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162907:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Холусии я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: 近隣の漁村「スティルタイド」の住人が、割れた貝殻が多いからという、もっとも過ぎる理由で名付けた砂浜。昔は、多くの漁師が行き交っていたが、治安が乱れた昨今では野蛮なホブゴブリンがうろつくようになってしまった
#. de: Dieser Sandstrand wurde von den einfallslosen Bewohnern des nahegelegenen Fischerdorfes Stillwasser so benannt, weil es dort viele zerbrochene Muscheln gibt. Früher gingen die Fischer dort gerne spazieren, doch heutzutage treiben dort Hobgoblins ihr Unwesen und machen die Gegend unsicher.
#. fr: Cette plage a été nommée ainsi par les habitants du proche village de Douceonde pour la simple raison qu'on y trouve de nombreuses coquilles brisées. Si de nombreux pêcheurs s'y croisaient autrefois, ils sont désormais remplacés par de farouches hobgobelins.
#. column 13: Cracked Shell Beach
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162907:0:15"
msgid "When questioned on the rather prosaic name of this coastline, the inhabitants of nearby Stilltide simply point to the carpet of broken seashells. In earlier days, they say the beach was crowded with the comings and goings of local fishermen, but now it is mostly the boots of barbaric hobgoblins leaving tracks along the pebbled shore."
msgstr "Когда у жителей Тихого прилива спрашивают, почему побережье так прозаично назвали, они просто указывают на груды расколотых раковин. Прежде пляж был полон местных рыбаков, а теперь по галечному берегу оставляют следы главным образом дикие хобгоблины."

#. ja: ホワイトオイルフォールズ
#. de: Weißölfälle
#. fr: Chute de l'Huile blanche
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: This waterfall marks the midpoint of Watts River. The sluggish current sends water over the cliff with little force, the cascade cleaving closely to the rock as it plunges down from an impressive height. Upon observing this almost-viscous flow, a renowned poet is said to have likened the falls to an enormous trickle of oil.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162908:0:13"
msgid "White Oil Falls"
msgstr "Водопад Белого масла"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nコルシア島のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Kholusias gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Kholusia que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: White Oil Falls
#. column 15: This waterfall marks the midpoint of Watts River. The sluggish current sends water over the cliff with little force, the cascade cleaving closely to the rock as it plunges down from an impressive height. Upon observing this almost-viscous flow, a renowned poet is said to have likened the falls to an enormous trickle of oil.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162908:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Холусии я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: ワッツリバーの中程にある落差の大きな滝。川が絶妙な速度で流れているため、さしたる飛沫を上げないまま、まっすぐに水が崖上から落ちてくる。その様子を見た高名な詩人が、油の滝と喩えたことで、そう呼ばれるようになった
#. de: Dieser große Wasserfall, der durch einen Höhenunterschied in der Mitte des Watts entstanden ist, zeichnet sich dadurch aus, dass das Wasser aufgrund der langsamen Fließgeschwindigkeit des Flusses senkrecht fällt, ja geradezu wie Öl hinabläuft. Diese Besonderheit inspirierte einen berühmten Dichter dazu, dem Wasserfall seinen Namen zu geben.
#. fr: Cette grande chute formée par une différence de niveau du terrain en plein milieu du cours de la Watts se distingue par le fait que l'eau tombe verticalement sans provoquer d'éclaboussures à cause de l'élégance avec laquelle coule la rivière. C'est ce qui a inspiré son nom à un illustre poète.
#. column 13: White Oil Falls
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162908:0:15"
msgid "This waterfall marks the midpoint of Watts River. The sluggish current sends water over the cliff with little force, the cascade cleaving closely to the rock as it plunges down from an impressive height. Upon observing this almost-viscous flow, a renowned poet is said to have likened the falls to an enormous trickle of oil."
msgstr "Этот водопад находится посреди реки Уоттс. Течение здесь медленное, поэтому вода почти без брызг стекает по скале с большой высоты. Увидев этот вязкий поток, знаменитый поэт, говорят, сравнил его с ручьём масла."

#. ja: ゲートタウン
#. de: Torstadt
#. fr: Le Vestibule
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: Gatetown is a haphazard mess of shacks and lean-tos─the result of refugees throwing up shelters as they await their chance to embrace the comforts of Eulmore. Though living conditions can best be described as “abysmal,” the regular distribution of meol and minimal risk of eater attacks has only seen the population increase over time.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162909:0:13"
msgid "Gatetown"
msgstr "Городок у ворот"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nコルシア島のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Kholusias gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Kholusia que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Gatetown
#. column 15: Gatetown is a haphazard mess of shacks and lean-tos─the result of refugees throwing up shelters as they await their chance to embrace the comforts of Eulmore. Though living conditions can best be described as “abysmal,” the regular distribution of meol and minimal risk of eater attacks has only seen the population increase over time.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162909:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Холусии я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: ユールモアへの移住を望む難民が寄り集まったことで、自然と形成された貧民街。住環境は劣悪の一語に尽きるが、それでも罪喰いに襲われるリスクが少なく、食糧メオルの配給もあるため人口は増加傾向が続いてきた
#. de: Die Flüchtlinge, die vor der verheißungsvollen Stadt des Vergnügens auf Einlass hoffen, haben eine Hüttenstadt errichtet, in der sie vor Angriffen der Sünden<shy>ver<shy>tilger geschützt sind und mit Meol versorgt werden.
#. fr: Ce quartier d'habitations modestes s'est na<shy>tu<shy>rel<shy>le<shy>ment formé du fait du ras<shy>sem<shy>ble<shy>ment de réfugiés désireux de s'installer à Eulmore. Bien que les conditions de vie y soient par<shy>ti<shy>cu<shy>liè<shy>rement mauvaises, le faible risque d'être attaqué par des purgateurs et la dis<shy>tri<shy>bu<shy>tion quotidienne de méol font que la population continue d'augmenter.
#. column 13: Gatetown
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162909:0:15"
msgid "Gatetown is a haphazard mess of shacks and lean-tos─the result of refugees throwing up shelters as they await their chance to embrace the comforts of Eulmore. Though living conditions can best be described as “abysmal,” the regular distribution of meol and minimal risk of eater attacks has only seen the population increase over time."
msgstr "Беженцы, надеющиеся попасть в Юлмор, сами собой образовали этот беспорядочный городок из лачуг и навесов. Условия здесь, мягко говоря, ужасные, но мэол раздают регулярно, а грехоеды почти не нападают — вот население и продолжает расти."

#. ja: ライト村
#. de: Werfting
#. fr: Cherpant
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: A farming village in the southern reaches of Kholusia. The residents of Wright have refused the largesse of Eulmore, preferring instead to subsist upon barley, vegetables, and other crops cultivated through time-honored methods. Their independence cost them dearly, however, when the appearance of a stray sin eater ended in unspeakable slaughter.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162910:0:13"
msgid "Wright"
msgstr "Райт"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nコルシア島のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Kholusias gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Kholusia que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Wright
#. column 15: A farming village in the southern reaches of Kholusia. The residents of Wright have refused the largesse of Eulmore, preferring instead to subsist upon barley, vegetables, and other crops cultivated through time-honored methods. Their independence cost them dearly, however, when the appearance of a stray sin eater ended in unspeakable slaughter.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162910:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Холусии я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: コルシア島の南部にある農村。メオルの配給を拒んだ農民たちが、昔ながらの手法で大麦や各種野菜の栽培で生計を立てている。しかし、一年ほど前に、はぐれ罪喰いの襲撃を受け、多大な犠牲を出したこともあった
#. de: Ein Bauerndorf im Süden von Kholusia. Die Bewohner ernähren sich von Getreide und Gemüse und lehnen die Meol-Gaben Eulmores ab. Doch mehr und mehr Alteingesessene verlassen das Dorf, seit ein Überfall der Sünden<shy>ver<shy>tilger vor einem Jahr viele Opfer forderte.
#. fr: Situé dans le sud de l'île de Kholusia, ce village est habité par des fermiers qui ont préféré continuer de cultiver l'orge et les légumes à l'ancienne plutôt que de recevoir du méol. Toutefois nombre d'entre eux ont été massacrés lors de l'attaque d'un purgateur errant il y a environ un an.
#. column 13: Wright
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162910:0:15"
msgid "A farming village in the southern reaches of Kholusia. The residents of Wright have refused the largesse of Eulmore, preferring instead to subsist upon barley, vegetables, and other crops cultivated through time-honored methods. Their independence cost them dearly, however, when the appearance of a stray sin eater ended in unspeakable slaughter."
msgstr "Деревня Райт стоит на юге Холусии. Её жители отказались от щедрот Юлмора и предпочли жить за счёт ячменя, овощей и прочих культур, выращенных по старинке. За независимость пришлось дорого заплатить: появление отбившегося от стаи пожирателя грехов обернулось страшной резнёй."

#. ja: ラダー大昇降機
#. de: Die Leiter
#. fr: L'Échelle
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: This enormous mechanism facilitates travel between Kholusia's lowlands and highlands. Its gears once driven by the tireless Talos of Daedalus Stoneworks, the apparatus fell into disrepair after said company retired its operations in the region─a development which all but halted trade with the highland dwarves.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162911:0:13"
msgid "The Ladder"
msgstr "Лестница"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nコルシア島のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Kholusias gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Kholusia que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: The Ladder
#. column 15: This enormous mechanism facilitates travel between Kholusia's lowlands and highlands. Its gears once driven by the tireless Talos of Daedalus Stoneworks, the apparatus fell into disrepair after said company retired its operations in the region─a development which all but halted trade with the highland dwarves.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162911:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Холусии я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: コルシア島の高地と低地を結ぶ、巨大な昇降機。かつてはダイダロス社のタロースを動力として、昇降機を動かしていたが、同社が撤退したことで長らく放置されていた。その昔は、ドワーフ族との交易の要衝であったという
#. de: Ein gigantischer Aufzug verbindet das Tiefland von Kholusia mit seinem Hochland. Hebe-Taloi der Daedalus-Steinhauerei besorgen den Antrieb, doch seit der Lichtflut stehen sie ungewartet und bewegungslos da. Einst wurde über die Leiter geschäftiger Handel mit den Zwergen getrieben.
#. fr: Cette immense installation permet de relier le plateau et la plaine de Kholusia. Elle était autrefois actionnée par les talos de la firme Daedalus, mais depuis le retrait de cette dernière, l'Échelle est laissée à l'abandon et ne sert même plus de lieu de commerce avec les Nains.
#. column 13: The Ladder
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162911:0:15"
msgid "This enormous mechanism facilitates travel between Kholusia's lowlands and highlands. Its gears once driven by the tireless Talos of Daedalus Stoneworks, the apparatus fell into disrepair after said company retired its operations in the region─a development which all but halted trade with the highland dwarves."
msgstr "Этот огромный механизм связывает низины Кулусии с нагорьем. Когда-то подъёмник приводили в движение неутомимые талосы компании «Дедалова каменоломня», но после ухода компании механизм пришёл в негодность. Торговля с горными дворфами почти прекратилась."

#. ja: トメラの村
#. de: Tomra
#. fr: Tomra
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: One of the dwarven settlements which dot the slopes of Mt. Gulg, Tomra is home to a sizable branch of the Tholl family. Every building is constructed on a scale to cater to the diminutive inhabitants, giving taller races the impression of a village built in miniature.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162912:0:13"
msgid "Tomra"
msgstr "Томра"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nコルシア島のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Kholusias gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Kholusia que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Tomra
#. column 15: One of the dwarven settlements which dot the slopes of Mt. Gulg, Tomra is home to a sizable branch of the Tholl family. Every building is constructed on a scale to cater to the diminutive inhabitants, giving taller races the impression of a village built in miniature.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162912:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Холусии я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: グルグ火山周辺に点在するドワーフ族の集落のひとつで、トルー一家に属す者たちが暮らしている。小柄なドワーフ族に合わせた建物が立ち並ぶため、他種族の者にとってはミニチュアの街並みにも見えることだろう
#. de: Nah am Fuße des Gulgs haben die Zwerge der Tholl-Sippe ihr Dorf. Ihre kleinen Behausungen sind für die großgewachsenen Völker eher ungeeignet, aber putzig anzuschauen.
#. fr: Tomra est un des hameaux nains situés autour du Mont Gulg et est le lieu de résidence des Tholl. Ses habitations sont adaptées à la taille et au mode de vie de ces mineurs nains, ce qui fait qu'elles peuvent passer pour des reproductions miniatures aux yeux des visiteurs d'autres races.
#. column 13: Tomra
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162912:0:15"
msgid "One of the dwarven settlements which dot the slopes of Mt. Gulg, Tomra is home to a sizable branch of the Tholl family. Every building is constructed on a scale to cater to the diminutive inhabitants, giving taller races the impression of a village built in miniature."
msgstr "Томра — одно из поселений дварфов на склонах горы Гулг, где живёт большая ветвь семьи Тру. Все здания здесь под стать невысоким жителям, поэтому для высокорослых народов деревня кажется игрушечной."

#. ja: ドヴェルグの煙突
#. de: Duergars Schlot
#. fr: Trou du Duergar
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: The far end of the Dwarven Hollows opens up into a great, crater-like expanse. Geysers here spew volcanically heated water high into the air, spraying the uncaring dwarves as they mine deposits of sulphur and other valuable minerals.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162913:0:13"
msgid "The Duergar's Tewel"
msgstr "Сопло Дверга"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nコルシア島のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Kholusias gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Kholusia que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: The Duergar's Tewel
#. column 15: The far end of the Dwarven Hollows opens up into a great, crater-like expanse. Geysers here spew volcanically heated water high into the air, spraying the uncaring dwarves as they mine deposits of sulphur and other valuable minerals.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162913:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Холусии я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: ドワーフの洞窟を抜けた先にある吹き抜けのような場所で、グルグ火山の火山活動の影響により、定期的に温水が吹き出す間欠泉となっている。その周辺では、硫黄などが産するため、ドワーフ族にとっては重要な場所である
#. de: Hinter einer Zwergenhöhle öffnet sich das Gestein, um dem dampfenden Schlot Platz zu machen. Immer wieder stößt er Fontänen heißen Wassers aus und bildet schwefelige Ablagerungen. Eine Freude für die Zwerge der Gogg-Sippe.
#. fr: Au-delà des mines naines se trouve un étrange et profond précipice duquel des eaux chaudes jaillissent ré<shy>gu<shy>liè<shy>re<shy>ment des geysers du fait de l'activité volcanique du Mont Gulg. La roche du lieu contenant des minerais tels que le souffre, il s'agit d'un lieu d'extraction important pour les mineurs nains.
#. column 13: The Duergar's Tewel
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Kholusia, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162913:0:15"
msgid "The far end of the Dwarven Hollows opens up into a great, crater-like expanse. Geysers here spew volcanically heated water high into the air, spraying the uncaring dwarves as they mine deposits of sulphur and other valuable minerals."
msgstr "В конце Дворфийских пещер открывается огромная впадина, похожая на кратер. Гейзеры выбрасывают в воздух разогретую вулканом воду, обливая дворфов, которые невозмутимо добывают здесь серу и другие ценные минералы."

#. ja: 隊商の野営地
#. de: Roter Karawanenhof
#. fr: Caravansérail rouge
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: This amaro roost was established by Crystarium merchants plying their trade in Amh Araeng. Tucked within the foreboding walls of Qasr Sharl, the waypoint and its stockpiled goods are well protected from both predators and windblown sands.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162914:0:13"
msgid "The Red Serai"
msgstr "Красный караван-сарай"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nアム・アレーンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Amh Araeng gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations en Amh Araeng que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: The Red Serai
#. column 15: This amaro roost was established by Crystarium merchants plying their trade in Amh Araeng. Tucked within the foreboding walls of Qasr Sharl, the waypoint and its stockpiled goods are well protected from both predators and windblown sands.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162914:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Странствуя по Амх-Араэну, я замер, поражённый открывшимся видом. Его стоило запечатлеть на бумаге, чтобы другие не прошли мимо такой красоты."

#. ja: クリスタリウムの隊商たちが、アム・アレーンとの間を行き来する際の中継地点として設けたアマロ用の発着場。集積した資材を守りやすいように、ナバスアレン王国の要塞、「カスール・シャル」の跡地を利用している
#. de: Von der einstigen Festung Qasr Sharl des Königreichs von Nabaath Areng starten heute lange Handelskarawanen, die Waren zwischen Crystarium und Amh Araeng hin und her transportieren. Auch ein Amaro-Flugsteg wurde eingerichtet.
#. fr: Ce poste sert de relais à amaros pour les marchands de Cristarium qui se rendent en Amh Araeng. Il a été établi dans les ruines de la citadelle de Qasr Sharl, bâtie autrefois par le royaume de Nabaath Areng, afin de mieux protéger les matériaux et produits qui y sont entreposés.
#. column 13: The Red Serai
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162914:0:15"
msgid "This amaro roost was established by Crystarium merchants plying their trade in Amh Araeng. Tucked within the foreboding walls of Qasr Sharl, the waypoint and its stockpiled goods are well protected from both predators and windblown sands."
msgstr "Эту стоянку амаро устроили торговцы из Кристариума, ведущие дела в Амх-Араэне. Она укрыта за грозными стенами крепости Каср-Шарл, поэтому и караван, и припасы надёжно защищены от хищников и песчаных бурь."

#. ja: モルド・スーク
#. de: Mordh Souq
#. fr: Mord Souq
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: The Mord have long dwelled in Amh Araeng, and this “souq” or “city” serves as a marketplace to display the curious wares they gather from every corner of the badlands. Merchants and collectors from across Norvrandt can be seen here purchasing ores, oddities, and the relics of Nabaath Areng.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162915:0:13"
msgid "Mord Souq"
msgstr "Рынок Морд"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nアム・アレーンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Amh Araeng gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations en Amh Araeng que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Mord Souq
#. column 15: The Mord have long dwelled in Amh Araeng, and this “souq” or “city” serves as a marketplace to display the curious wares they gather from every corner of the badlands. Merchants and collectors from across Norvrandt can be seen here purchasing ores, oddities, and the relics of Nabaath Areng.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162915:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Странствуя по Амх-Араэну, я замер, поражённый открывшимся видом. Его стоило запечатлеть на бумаге, чтобы другие не прошли мимо такой красоты."

#. ja: 古くからアム・アレーンで暮らす獣人種族、モルド族の集落。「スーク」とは市場を示す言葉であり、モルド族が荒野の方々から集めた品物が並んでいる。鉱物やナバスアレンの遺物を求めるなら、真っ先に立ち寄るべき場所だ
#. de: In dieser Siedlung leben die wilden Mordh, die von alters her  in Amh Araeng heimisch sind. „Souq“ bedeutet Markt, und hier verkaufen die Mordh allerlei Waren, die sie aus den ver<shy>schie<shy>den<shy>sten Winkeln des Ödlands mitgebracht haben. Ein Besuch im Souq empfiehlt sich für jeden, der nach Erzen oder Relikten aus dem Königreich Nabaath Areng sucht.
#. fr: Ce hameau est prin<shy>ci<shy>pa<shy>le<shy>ment occupé par les Mords, un peuple d'hommes-bêtes présent en Amh Araeng depuis des âges reculés. Le terme “souq” signifie marché et c'est à cet endroit que les marchands mords vendent des produits qui affluent de diverses régions. C'est un lieu incontournable pour tous ceux qui recherchent du minerai ou des reliques du royaume de Nabaath Areng.
#. column 13: Mord Souq
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162915:0:15"
msgid "The Mord have long dwelled in Amh Araeng, and this “souq” or “city” serves as a marketplace to display the curious wares they gather from every corner of the badlands. Merchants and collectors from across Norvrandt can be seen here purchasing ores, oddities, and the relics of Nabaath Areng."
msgstr "Морд издавна живут в Амх-Араэне. На этом «суке», то есть рынке, они выставляют диковинные товары, собранные по всей пустоши. Сюда приезжают торговцы и коллекционеры со всего Норвранта за рудами, редкостями и реликвиями Набас-Арэнга."

#. ja: アム・マリク新宮殿
#. de: Palast von Amh Malik
#. fr: Nouveau palais d'Amh Malik
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: In the common tongue, “amh malik” translates into “majestic king,” and it was within this royal residence that was housed the core of Nabaath Areng's political and military might. When the Flood came, however, it was halted moments too late─half the palace toppled before a titanic wave of Light like a sand castle caught by the tide.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162916:0:13"
msgid "The Pristine Palace of Amh Malik"
msgstr "Дворец Амх-Малика"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nアム・アレーンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Amh Araeng gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations en Amh Araeng que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: The Pristine Palace of Amh Malik
#. column 15: In the common tongue, “amh malik” translates into “majestic king,” and it was within this royal residence that was housed the core of Nabaath Areng's political and military might. When the Flood came, however, it was halted moments too late─half the palace toppled before a titanic wave of Light like a sand castle caught by the tide.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162916:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Странствуя по Амх-Араэну, я замер, поражённый открывшимся видом. Его стоило запечатлеть на бумаге, чтобы другие не прошли мимо такой красоты."

#. ja: 「アム」は「偉大な」、「マリク」は「ナバスアレン男性王の称号」を意味する。かつてはナバスアレンの政治と軍事の中枢であったが、「光の氾濫」を押し止める基点となった際に、半ば光の波に呑み込まれ崩壊してしまった
#. de: In der Sprache des Königreichs Nabaath Areng bedeutet „Amh“ so viel wie „groß, gewaltig“ und „Malik“ war der offizielle Titel des Königs. Dieser Palast war einst Sitz der politischen und militärischen Machthaber des ehemaligen Königreichs, wurde aber durch die Lichtflut fast vollständig zerstört.
#. fr: Dans la langue du royaume de Nabaath Areng, “Amh” signifie “illustre” et “Malik” est l'équivalent du titre de “roi”. Ce palais était autrefois le siège du pouvoir politique et militaire de l'ancien royaume, mais il a été à moitié détruit par la déferlante du déluge de Lumière.
#. column 13: The Pristine Palace of Amh Malik
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162916:0:15"
msgid "In the common tongue, “amh malik” translates into “majestic king,” and it was within this royal residence that was housed the core of Nabaath Areng's political and military might. When the Flood came, however, it was halted moments too late─half the palace toppled before a titanic wave of Light like a sand castle caught by the tide."
msgstr "На общем языке «амх-малик» означает «великий король». В этой королевской резиденции находился центр политической и военной власти Набас-Арэнга. Когда пришёл Потоп, его остановили слишком поздно: гигантская волна Света обрушилась на дворец, словно прилив на песочный замок, и разрушила половину здания."

#. ja: ビラン大鉱山
#. de: Biran-Mine
#. fr: Grandes mines de Biran
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: The shafts carved into the side of Mount Biran were the center of a large-scale mining operation which employed the relentless strength of an army of Talos. As is the case with Garik, Kelk, and many other places in the region, “Biran” was a name taken from a Ronso of historical note.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162917:0:13"
msgid "Mount Biran Mines"
msgstr "Шахты горы Биран"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nアム・アレーンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Amh Araeng gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations en Amh Araeng que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Mount Biran Mines
#. column 15: The shafts carved into the side of Mount Biran were the center of a large-scale mining operation which employed the relentless strength of an army of Talos. As is the case with Garik, Kelk, and many other places in the region, “Biran” was a name taken from a Ronso of historical note.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162917:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Странствуя по Амх-Араэну, я замер, поражённый открывшимся видом. Его стоило запечатлеть на бумаге, чтобы другие не прошли мимо такой красоты."

#. ja: ビラン山に拓かれた鉱山で、以前はタロースを使った大規模採掘の中心地として栄えていた。ちなみに「ビラン」とはロンゾ族の偉人の名であり、周辺にはガリク村やケルク遺跡など、同様に故人の名を戴いた地名が散見される
#. de: Dieses Netzwerk von Tunneln und Stollen, das in den Berg Biran gegraben wurde, war eine wichtige Erzförderstätte, in der Taloi verwendet wurden. Biran folgt der Ronso-Tradition, einen Ort nach einem berühmten Vertreter ihres Volkes zu benennen, genau wie bei Garik und Kelk.
#. fr: Ce réseau de galeries creusé au cœur du Mont Biran était un important site d'extraction minière où l'on utilisait notamment des talos. Biran suit la tradition ronso qui veut qu'on donne le nom d'un illustre personnage à un lieu, tout comme c'est le cas pour Garik et Kelk.
#. column 13: Mount Biran Mines
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162917:0:15"
msgid "The shafts carved into the side of Mount Biran were the center of a large-scale mining operation which employed the relentless strength of an army of Talos. As is the case with Garik, Kelk, and many other places in the region, “Biran” was a name taken from a Ronso of historical note."
msgstr "Шахты, прорубленные в склоне горы Биран, были центром масштабной добычи, где трудились целые армии талосов. Как и названия Гарик, Келк и многих других мест в округе, «Биран» — имя прославленного ронсо."

#. ja: トゥワイン
#. de: Pfotenschlag
#. fr: Queues-liées
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: In days past, Nabaath Areng contracted a Talos engineer to establish its mining railway, and these cabins were built to provide lodgings for the laborers who would lay the trolley tracks. The settlement was later maintained as a miners' village, but its dwindling population has mirrored the steady decline of the mining industry.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162918:0:13"
msgid "Twine"
msgstr "Твин"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nアム・アレーンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Amh Araeng gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations en Amh Araeng que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Twine
#. column 15: In days past, Nabaath Areng contracted a Talos engineer to establish its mining railway, and these cabins were built to provide lodgings for the laborers who would lay the trolley tracks. The settlement was later maintained as a miners' village, but its dwindling population has mirrored the steady decline of the mining industry.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162918:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Странствуя по Амх-Араэну, я замер, поражённый открывшимся видом. Его стоило запечатлеть на бумаге, чтобы другие не прошли мимо такой красоты."

#. ja: ナバスアレンが、ミステル族のタロース技師を招いて鉱山鉄道を開設した際に、線路敷設に関わる作業員たちの宿泊所として成立。その後も、鉱山労働者の村として存続してきたが、鉱業の衰退とともに人口は減る一方のようだ
#. de: Damals, als das Königreich Nabaath Areng Mystel-Ingenieure einlud, die auf Talos-Technologie spezialisiert sind, wurde dieses Dorf gegründet, um die vielen Arbeiter unterzubringen, die die Eisenbahnverbindungen zwischen den Minen bauten. Später lebten dort die Bergleute, aber seit dem Niedergang der Bergbauindustrie ist die Bevölkerung immer weiter zurückgegangen.
#. fr: Ce village a été fondé afin d'héberger les travailleurs venus mettre en place la voie ferrée reliant les mines, lorsque le royaume de Nabaath Areng a invité des ingénieurs mystels spécialisés dans la technologie des talos. Plus tard, ce sont les mineurs qui y ont habité, mais depuis le déclin de l'industrie minière, la population est en constante diminution.
#. column 13: Twine
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162918:0:15"
msgid "In days past, Nabaath Areng contracted a Talos engineer to establish its mining railway, and these cabins were built to provide lodgings for the laborers who would lay the trolley tracks. The settlement was later maintained as a miners' village, but its dwindling population has mirrored the steady decline of the mining industry."
msgstr "Когда Набас-Арэнг нанял инженера-талоса для строительства железной дороги, эти бараки стали жильём для рабочих, прокладывавших рельсы. Позже здесь поселились шахтёры, но по мере упадка горного дела деревня пустела."

#. ja: ケルク遺跡
#. de: Kelk
#. fr: Ruines de Kelk
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: The ruins of a Ronso settlement. Residents abandoned Kelk for the cities long before the Flood arrived, and thus it is known amongst scavengers as a prime location for finding trinkets and relics untouched by conflict.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162919:0:13"
msgid "Kelk"
msgstr "Келк"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nアム・アレーンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Amh Araeng gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations en Amh Araeng que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Kelk
#. column 15: The ruins of a Ronso settlement. Residents abandoned Kelk for the cities long before the Flood arrived, and thus it is known amongst scavengers as a prime location for finding trinkets and relics untouched by conflict.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162919:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Странствуя по Амх-Араэну, я замер, поражённый открывшимся видом. Его стоило запечатлеть на бумаге, чтобы другие не прошли мимо такой красоты."

#. ja: ロンゾ族の集落跡地。「光の氾濫」以前に、すでに人口が都市部に移ったことで廃墟となっていたようだが、それだけに大きな戦いとは無縁で、スカベンジャーにとっては掘り出し物が見つかる穴場として知られている
#. de: Diese ehemalige Ronso-Siedlung war bereits vor der Lichtflut verlassen, weil ihre Bevölkerung in die Städte abgewandert war, aber heutzutage ist sie eine Pilgerstätte für Schatz<shy>sucher aller Art, weil dort viele wertvolle Objekte gefunden wurden.
#. fr: Cette ancienne colonie ronso était déjà abandonnée avant même le déluge de Lumière, car sa population avait migré vers les villes. De nos jours, c'est un lieu de prédilection pour les chasseurs de trésors en tout genre, en raison des nombreux objets de valeur qui y sont enfouis.
#. column 13: Kelk
#. column 14: In my wanderings across Amh Araeng, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162919:0:15"
msgid "The ruins of a Ronso settlement. Residents abandoned Kelk for the cities long before the Flood arrived, and thus it is known amongst scavengers as a prime location for finding trinkets and relics untouched by conflict."
msgstr "Руины поселения ронсо. Жители покинули Келк и перебрались в города задолго до Потопа. Поэтому здесь не было больших сражений, и теперь место славится среди искателей редкостей нетронутыми безделушками и реликвиями."

#. ja: リダ・ラーン
#. de: Lydha Lran
#. fr: Lydha Lran
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: Finding it abandoned by its former inhabitants following the events of the Flood, the pixies have claimed this Voeburtite village as their own. The fae have continued the villagers' practice of keeping sheep, making use of the weed-choked pens to raise and milk their wooly livestock.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162920:0:13"
msgid "Lydha Lran"
msgstr "Лидха-Лран"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nイル・メグのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Meine Reise durch Il Mheg führte mich an einen Aussichtspunkt, an dem sich ein atemberaubender Ausblick bot. Ich habe keine Zweifel, dass diese einzigartige Landschaft die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage zu Liedern und Weisen inspirieren wird.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations en Il Mheg que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Lydha Lran
#. column 15: Finding it abandoned by its former inhabitants following the events of the Flood, the pixies have claimed this Voeburtite village as their own. The fae have continued the villagers' practice of keeping sheep, making use of the weed-choked pens to raise and milk their wooly livestock.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162920:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Ил-Мегу я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: 元々はフッブート王国に属す山村だったが、「光の氾濫」後に住人が去ったため、ピクシー族が勝手に棲み込むようになった。かつての主産業は牧畜であり、今も厩舎跡では、羊乳を求めるピクシー族がシープを育てている
#. de: Eingerahmt in ein Meer aus Blumen, schmiegt sich Lydha Lran und seine malerischen Losamente in die bunte Hügellandschaft. Einst verheerte die Lichtflut den kleinen Weiler und hinterließ nichts als Trümmer. Doch dann kamen die Pixies und verwandelten die verwaisten Ruinen in ein blühendes Kleinod. Heute leben sie unbeschwert mit ihren Schafen, weitgehend unbehelligt von der Außenwelt.
#. fr: Ce village qui était autrefois sous la coupe du royaume de Voeburt a été repeuplé par les Pixies, après que ses habitants d'origine l'ont abandonné suite au déluge de Lumière. Parce qu'on y pratiquait autrefois l'élevage, on trouve encore de nos jours les vestiges d'étables, où les Pixies friandes de lait ont installé leurs moutons.
#. column 13: Lydha Lran
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162920:0:15"
msgid "Finding it abandoned by its former inhabitants following the events of the Flood, the pixies have claimed this Voeburtite village as their own. The fae have continued the villagers' practice of keeping sheep, making use of the weed-choked pens to raise and milk their wooly livestock."
msgstr "После Потопа прежние жители покинули эту деревню Воебурта, и пикси присвоили её себе. Феи продолжили разводить овец, как и местные жители прежде: в заросших загонах они растят овец и добывают их молоко."

#. ja: 篤学者の荘園
#. de: Lehnsgut des Gelehrten
#. fr: Villégiature du Lettré
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: Lately the borrowed residence of a foreign scholar, this manor once belonged to a Voeburtite lord known for the eclectic nature of his hobbies. In a miraculous turn of events, the noble's extensive collection of books and academic apparatus have largely been left undisturbed by curious pixie hands.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162921:0:13"
msgid "The Bookman's Shelves"
msgstr "Усадьба учёного"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nイル・メグのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Meine Reise durch Il Mheg führte mich an einen Aussichtspunkt, an dem sich ein atemberaubender Ausblick bot. Ich habe keine Zweifel, dass diese einzigartige Landschaft die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage zu Liedern und Weisen inspirieren wird.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations en Il Mheg que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: The Bookman's Shelves
#. column 15: Lately the borrowed residence of a foreign scholar, this manor once belonged to a Voeburtite lord known for the eclectic nature of his hobbies. In a miraculous turn of events, the noble's extensive collection of books and academic apparatus have largely been left undisturbed by curious pixie hands.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162921:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Ил-Мегу я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: さる異邦の賢人が、借りぐらししていた館。本来は、多趣味で知られるフッブート王国の地方領主の邸宅であり、その持ち物である蔵書や機材が、奇跡的に妖精たちの手で荒らされず、そのまま保管されていたのだという
#. de: An den Gestaden eines Sees ragt ein opulentes Landhaus in die Höhe. Es heißt, das Lehnsgut des Gelehrten sei einst der Sitz eines vielseitig interessierten Adeligen des Königreichs Voeburt gewesen, und verfüge daher über eine überraschend umfangreiche Privatbibliothek, die auf wundersame Weise die Lichtflut unbeschadet überstanden und von den Feen unberührt geblieben sei.
#. fr: Cette bâtisse, où a temporairement vécu un érudit originaire d'une contrée étrangère, était la résidence du gouverneur du royaume de Voeburt, connu pour ses nombreux centres d'intérêt. Les ouvrages et appareils qui y sont conservés n'ont étrangement pas été abîmés par le peuple féerique.
#. column 13: The Bookman's Shelves
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162921:0:15"
msgid "Lately the borrowed residence of a foreign scholar, this manor once belonged to a Voeburtite lord known for the eclectic nature of his hobbies. In a miraculous turn of events, the noble's extensive collection of books and academic apparatus have largely been left undisturbed by curious pixie hands."
msgstr "Этот особняк недавно служил временным домом учёному из чужих краёв. Прежде он принадлежал вуэбуртскому лорду, славившемуся разнообразием увлечений. Поразительно, но любопытные феи почти не тронули обширную библиотеку и научные приборы вельможи."

#. ja: プラ・エンニ茸窟
#. de: Pla Enni
#. fr: Pla Enni
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: Known for their harmonious relationship with the now-faded Kingdom of Voeburt, the Nu Mou people reside in this cavern under the leadership of their elder, Wyd Aenc. As well as being the name of the village, “pla enni” is a variety of mushroom the Nu Mou grow to incredible size─large enough for them to hollow out and use as comfortable dwellings.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162922:0:13"
msgid "Pla Enni"
msgstr "Пла-Энни"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nイル・メグのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Meine Reise durch Il Mheg führte mich an einen Aussichtspunkt, an dem sich ein atemberaubender Ausblick bot. Ich habe keine Zweifel, dass diese einzigartige Landschaft die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage zu Liedern und Weisen inspirieren wird.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations en Il Mheg que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Pla Enni
#. column 15: Known for their harmonious relationship with the now-faded Kingdom of Voeburt, the Nu Mou people reside in this cavern under the leadership of their elder, Wyd Aenc. As well as being the name of the village, “pla enni” is a variety of mushroom the Nu Mou grow to incredible size─large enough for them to hollow out and use as comfortable dwellings.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162922:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Ил-Мегу я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: ウィド＝インク以下、かつてフッブート王国と共存していたン・モゥ族たちが暮らす洞窟。「プラ・エンニ」とは、彼らが育てている大きなキノコのことで、その内部をくり抜くことで住居としても利用されている
#. de: Pla Enni ist die Heimstatt der geschäftstüchtigen Nu Mou, die schon zu Zeiten des Königreichs Voeburt die imposante Wohngrotte in den Bergen bewohnten. Seinen Besuchern bietet sich eine farbenfrohe Kulisse: die Gewölbe werden von riesigen, bunt schillernden Pilzen, die die Nu Mou dort geschickt kultivieren, in allen Farben des Regenbogens beleuchtet.
#. fr: C'est dans cette grotte que vivent Wyd Aenc et les autres Nu Mou, qui cohabitaient autrefois avec le royaume de Voeburt. Le nom de leur colonie est à l'origine celui des énormes champignons qu'ils font pousser, puis creusent pour y aménager leurs habitations.
#. column 13: Pla Enni
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162922:0:15"
msgid "Known for their harmonious relationship with the now-faded Kingdom of Voeburt, the Nu Mou people reside in this cavern under the leadership of their elder, Wyd Aenc. As well as being the name of the village, “pla enni” is a variety of mushroom the Nu Mou grow to incredible size─large enough for them to hollow out and use as comfortable dwellings."
msgstr "В этой пещере живёт народ ну-мо под началом старейшины Вид-Энка. Когда-то они поддерживали добрые отношения с королевством Вуэбурт. «Пла-энни» — не только название поселения, но и вид грибов, которые ну-мо выращивают до невероятных размеров, а затем выдалбливают изнутри и устраивают там уютные жилища."

#. ja: 魚たちの街
#. de: Stadt der Fische
#. fr: Bois Profond
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: In the time of Voeburt, when Lyhe Ghiah was yet known as Gruenes Licht, these ruins were a thriving castle town. Now they languish at the bottom of Longmirror Lake, submerged in the waters drawn forth by the Fuath as the faeries laid claim to Il Mheg.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162923:0:13"
msgid "Deepwood Swim"
msgstr "Глубинный плёс"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nイル・メグのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Meine Reise durch Il Mheg führte mich an einen Aussichtspunkt, an dem sich ein atemberaubender Ausblick bot. Ich habe keine Zweifel, dass diese einzigartige Landschaft die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage zu Liedern und Weisen inspirieren wird.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations en Il Mheg que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Deepwood Swim
#. column 15: In the time of Voeburt, when Lyhe Ghiah was yet known as Gruenes Licht, these ruins were a thriving castle town. Now they languish at the bottom of Longmirror Lake, submerged in the waters drawn forth by the Fuath as the faeries laid claim to Il Mheg.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162923:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Ил-Мегу я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: フッブート王国の王城、グリュネスリヒト城の城下町。イル・メグが妖精郷となった際に、フーア族によって水が引き込まれた結果、今では巨大な「姿見の湖」の水底に沈んでおり、文字通り「魚たちの街」と化している
#. de: Unter der Was<shy>ser<shy>o<shy>ber<shy>flä<shy>che des schillernden Sees sind die Ruinen einer vergangenen Zivilisation zu erahnen. Wo einst Bürger durch die Straßen flanierten, huschen nun Fischschwärme durch die Überreste der Hauptstadt des Königreichs Voeburt. Dessen Herzstück<nbsp>- Schloss Grünes Licht<nbsp>- ragt in wolkige Höhen und lässt die reiche Kultur erahnen, die von der Lichtflut zerstört wurde.
#. fr: Cette ville s'est construite autour du Gruenes Licht, un château re<shy>pré<shy>sen<shy>tant le siège du pouvoir de l'ancien royaume de Voeburt. Elle a été inondée par les Fuath lorsque le peuple féerique s'est installé en Il Mheg et gît désormais au fond du lac Psyché, ce qui lui vaut son nom actuel.
#. column 13: Deepwood Swim
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162923:0:15"
msgid "In the time of Voeburt, when Lyhe Ghiah was yet known as Gruenes Licht, these ruins were a thriving castle town. Now they languish at the bottom of Longmirror Lake, submerged in the waters drawn forth by the Fuath as the faeries laid claim to Il Mheg."
msgstr "Во времена Воэбурта, когда Лихе Гиа ещё назывался Грюнес Лихт, у подножия замка кипела жизнь. Теперь руины покоятся на дне озера Длинное зеркало, затопленные водами, которые фуаты призвали, завладев Ил-Мегом."

#. ja: リェー・ギア城
#. de: Schloss Lyhe Ghiah
#. fr: Lyhe Ghiah
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: Once the royal seat of Voeburt, Lyhe Ghiah later became a prison for Titania when the faerie king succumbed to the aether of a slain Lightwarden. The castle's name has its origin in both the faerie and Voeburtite tongues, the words thought to translate as the “wings of dreams.”
msgctxt "Adventure:2162924:0:13"
msgid "Lyhe Ghiah"
msgstr "Лихе Гиа"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nイル・メグのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Meine Reise durch Il Mheg führte mich an einen Aussichtspunkt, an dem sich ein atemberaubender Ausblick bot. Ich habe keine Zweifel, dass diese einzigartige Landschaft die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage zu Liedern und Weisen inspirieren wird.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations en Il Mheg que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Lyhe Ghiah
#. column 15: Once the royal seat of Voeburt, Lyhe Ghiah later became a prison for Titania when the faerie king succumbed to the aether of a slain Lightwarden. The castle's name has its origin in both the faerie and Voeburtite tongues, the words thought to translate as the “wings of dreams.”
msgctxt "Adventure:2162924:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Ил-Мегу я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: かつてのフッブート王国の王城。大罪喰いと化した妖精王ティターニアが幽閉されてきた場所でもある。なお、その名は妖精語とフッブート語の合成語で、「夢の羽の城」といった意味合いを持っているようだ
#. de: Schloss Grünes Licht ragt grandios in wolkige Höhen und lässt die reiche Kultur erahnen, die von der Lichtflut unwiederbringlich zerstört wurde. Heute durchstreift der Licht<shy>bringer Titania, die tragische Anführerin der Feenvölker, seine majestätischen Hallen. Die Pixies tauften das Schloss „Lyhe Ghiah“: Schloss der geflügelten Träume.
#. fr: Ce château était autrefois le centre du pouvoir du royaume de Voeburt et sert désormais de prison à Titania, le monarque du peuple féerique devenu purgateur. Son nom serait composé de mots venant de la langue des fées et de celle de Voeburt et signifierait quelque chose comme “château des ailes du rêve”.
#. column 13: Lyhe Ghiah
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162924:0:15"
msgid "Once the royal seat of Voeburt, Lyhe Ghiah later became a prison for Titania when the faerie king succumbed to the aether of a slain Lightwarden. The castle's name has its origin in both the faerie and Voeburtite tongues, the words thought to translate as the “wings of dreams.”"
msgstr "Когда-то в замке Лихе Гиа жили правители Воэбурта. Позже он стал темницей для Титании, короля фейри, которого поглотил эфир павшего Стража Света. Название замка происходит из языков фейри и воэбуртцев и, по-видимому, означает «крылья снов»."

#. ja: 聖ファスリクの額
#. de: Tempel des Heiligen Fathric
#. fr: Temple de Saint-Fathric
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: This secluded mountain shelf was favored by Saint Fathric of the Church of the First Light as a place to perform rites of penance. Amongst the faeries of Il Mheg, only the Nu Mou would remember or understand the significance of the location's history.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162925:0:13"
msgid "Saint Fathric's Temple"
msgstr "Храм святого Фатрика"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nイル・メグのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Meine Reise durch Il Mheg führte mich an einen Aussichtspunkt, an dem sich ein atemberaubender Ausblick bot. Ich habe keine Zweifel, dass diese einzigartige Landschaft die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage zu Liedern und Weisen inspirieren wird.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations en Il Mheg que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Saint Fathric's Temple
#. column 15: This secluded mountain shelf was favored by Saint Fathric of the Church of the First Light as a place to perform rites of penance. Amongst the faeries of Il Mheg, only the Nu Mou would remember or understand the significance of the location's history.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162925:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Во время странствий по Ил-Мегу я остановился полюбоваться открывшимся видом. Не удержался и занёс его на бумагу, чтобы другие тоже не прошли мимо."

#. ja: この地で苦行を行ったことで知られる光耀教会の聖人、聖ファスリクの名が残る山間の土地。しかし、その由来を語る者も、意味を理解する者も、妖精郷と化したイル・メグではン・モゥ族くらいのものであろう
#. de: An einer Steilklippe, die einen fantastischen Blick auf ein zerklüftetes Tal bietet, liegen die Ruinen der Wallfahrtskirche von Dammroen. In den Mauern des verfallenen Sakralbaus übten sich einst die Geweihten der Kirche des Strahlenden Lichts in Askese. Heute ist jedoch nichts von seiner ursprünglichen Pracht erhalten geblieben, außer dem Namen.
#. fr: Ce terrain situé dans la montagne porte le nom de Saint-Fathric, un membre de l'église de l'Aurore qui y aurait pratiqué l'ascétisme. Toutefois, des habitants de cette région devenue l'Il Mheg, seuls les Nu Mou savent encore l'origine de ce nom et comprennent même sa si<shy>gni<shy>fi<shy>ca<shy>tion.
#. column 13: Saint Fathric's Temple
#. column 14: In my wanderings through Il Mheg, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162925:0:15"
msgid "This secluded mountain shelf was favored by Saint Fathric of the Church of the First Light as a place to perform rites of penance. Amongst the faeries of Il Mheg, only the Nu Mou would remember or understand the significance of the location's history."
msgstr "Святой Фатрик из Церкви Первого света избрал это укромное горное плато местом для покаянных обрядов. Среди фейри Ил-Мега лишь Ну Мо помнят историю этого места и понимают её значение."

#. ja: ゴーンの砦
#. de: Gohn-Feste
#. fr: Forteresse de Gohn
#. column 14: In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: Built by the Night's Blessed, little now remains of this wooden fortification. By all accounts, a fire broke out during a sin eater attack, and even before the violence had ended, the compound had collapsed into a charred ruin. Survivors of the slaughter had no choice but to relocate to the nearby Slitherbough.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162926:0:13"
msgid "Fort Gohn"
msgstr "Форт Гон"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラケティカ大森林のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Großen Waldes Rak'tika gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Rak'tika que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Fort Gohn
#. column 15: Built by the Night's Blessed, little now remains of this wooden fortification. By all accounts, a fire broke out during a sin eater attack, and even before the violence had ended, the compound had collapsed into a charred ruin. Survivors of the slaughter had no choice but to relocate to the nearby Slitherbough.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162926:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Странствуя по Великому лесу Рактика, я вдруг замерла, заворожённая открывшимся видом. Нельзя дать такой красоте затеряться — я должна запечатлеть её на бумаге."

#. ja: ラケティカ大森林に流入した「夜の民」が築いた砦の跡地。罪喰いの群れに襲撃され大規模な火災が発生した結果、無残にも焼け落ちてしまった。なお、生き残りの住民たちは、スリザーバウに身を寄せているようだ
#. de: Diese Feste diente den Untertanen der Nacht, die im Wald Zuflucht gesucht hatten, als Stützpunkt, bis eine Herde Sünden<shy>ver<shy>tilger über sie herfiel und sie niederbrannte. Die Überlebenden zogen sich nach Schlangenzweig zurück.
#. fr: Ce sont les ruines du fort construit jadis par le peuple de la Nuit à Rak'tika, qui fut presque totalement détruit après l'incendie causé par l'attaque de purgateurs. Depuis, les survivants de cette bataille se sont installés à Serpentige.
#. column 13: Fort Gohn
#. column 14: In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162926:0:15"
msgid "Built by the Night's Blessed, little now remains of this wooden fortification. By all accounts, a fire broke out during a sin eater attack, and even before the violence had ended, the compound had collapsed into a charred ruin. Survivors of the slaughter had no choice but to relocate to the nearby Slitherbough."
msgstr "Народ Ночи построил здесь деревянный форт, от которого теперь почти ничего не осталось. По всей видимости, во время нападения пожирателей грехов вспыхнул пожар, и ещё до окончания битвы укрепление обратилось в обугленные руины. Пережившие резню были вынуждены перебраться в соседний Змеиный Приют."

#. ja: 水蛇の宝卵
#. de: Kleinod der Beschützerin
#. fr: L'Œuf du Serpent marin
#. column 14: In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: Cradled within the branches of a giant tree, this immense crystal boulder is suspended above the waters of Lake Tusi Mek'ta. The “Fruit of the Protector,” as it is known, has been the subject of worship since the time of the Ronkan Empire, and even now folk tell the legend of the great entity believed to be cocooned within.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162927:0:13"
msgid "Fruit of the Protector"
msgstr "Плод Защитницы"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラケティカ大森林のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Großen Waldes Rak'tika gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Rak'tika que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Fruit of the Protector
#. column 15: Cradled within the branches of a giant tree, this immense crystal boulder is suspended above the waters of Lake Tusi Mek'ta. The “Fruit of the Protector,” as it is known, has been the subject of worship since the time of the Ronkan Empire, and even now folk tell the legend of the great entity believed to be cocooned within.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162927:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Странствуя по Великому лесу Рактика, я вдруг замерла, заворожённая открывшимся видом. Нельзя дать такой красоте затеряться — я должна запечатлеть её на бумаге."

#. ja: トゥシ・メキタ湖の水上で大樹に支えられ浮かぶ巨大なクリスタル塊。ロンカ帝国以前の古き時代から、この地の人々に祀られていたらしく、「水蛇」と呼ばれる大いなる存在が封じられていたとの伝承も今に伝わる
#. de: Ein Kristall, der über der Oberfläche des Schlangensees Tusi Mek'ta schwebt und schon zu Zeiten, als das Ronka-Reich noch nicht bestand, von den Eingesessenen verehrt wurde. Sie glaubten, dass in dem Kristall eine Wasserschlange eingeschlossen sei.
#. fr: Cet énorme cristal, enserré par un arbre gigantesque, surplombe les eaux du lac Tusi Mek'ta. Il est mentionné dans les légendes datant d'avant même les débuts de l'empire ronka, et est depuis toujours considéré comme sacré par les habitants de la région.
#. column 13: Fruit of the Protector
#. column 14: In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162927:0:15"
msgid "Cradled within the branches of a giant tree, this immense crystal boulder is suspended above the waters of Lake Tusi Mek'ta. The “Fruit of the Protector,” as it is known, has been the subject of worship since the time of the Ronkan Empire, and even now folk tell the legend of the great entity believed to be cocooned within."
msgstr "Огромный кристалл покоится на ветвях исполинского дерева над озером Туси-Мекта. Его называют «Плодом Защитницы» и почитают ещё со времён империи Ронка. До сих пор ходят легенды, что внутри заключено могущественное существо."

#. ja: ダワトリ溺没神殿
#. de: Versunkenes Heiligtum von Dwatl
#. fr: Sanctuaire englouti de Dwatl
#. column 14: In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: One of the sacred temples built by the Ronkans, these stone halls were safeguarded by a sect of priests even after the fall of the empire. The rising waters of the lake, however, could not be denied, and rumors persist of a secret treasure which was swallowed along with the temple.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162928:0:13"
msgid "The Covered Halls of Dwatl"
msgstr "Затопленные чертоги Дватла"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラケティカ大森林のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Großen Waldes Rak'tika gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Rak'tika que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: The Covered Halls of Dwatl
#. column 15: One of the sacred temples built by the Ronkans, these stone halls were safeguarded by a sect of priests even after the fall of the empire. The rising waters of the lake, however, could not be denied, and rumors persist of a secret treasure which was swallowed along with the temple.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162928:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Странствуя по Великому лесу Рактика, я вдруг замерла, заворожённая открывшимся видом. Нельзя дать такой красоте затеряться — я должна запечатлеть её на бумаге."

#. ja: ロンカ帝国が築いた石造神殿のひとつ。同帝国が崩壊した後も、さる神官一族によって護られていたようだが、いつしか湖に呑まれ水没してしまった。噂では、ロンカ皇帝の秘宝が眠るとも言われているが真相は謎である
#. de: Ein steinerner Tempel des Ronka-Kaiserreiches. Nachdem das Kaiserreich untergegangen war, wachte eine Priesterfamilie über das Heiligtum, doch mit der Zeit versank es im See. Gerüchten zufolge soll sich ein großer Schatz in seinem Inneren befinden.
#. fr: L'un des temples construits par l'empire ronka. Même après l'ef<shy>fon<shy>dre<shy>ment de ce dernier, les prêtres qui y vivaient continuèrent à le protéger, ce qui ne l'empêcha malheureusement pas de se faire engloutir par les eaux du lac. On dit que le trésor de l'empire ronka y repose toujours, mais personne n'a jamais pu le prouver.
#. column 13: The Covered Halls of Dwatl
#. column 14: In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162928:0:15"
msgid "One of the sacred temples built by the Ronkans, these stone halls were safeguarded by a sect of priests even after the fall of the empire. The rising waters of the lake, however, could not be denied, and rumors persist of a secret treasure which was swallowed along with the temple."
msgstr "Один из священных каменных храмов, возведённых ронканцами. Даже после падения империи его оберегала община жрецов, но воды озера всё же поглотили святыню. Говорят, вместе с храмом на дно ушёл тайный клад. Правда ли это — никто не знает."

#. ja: ロツァトル大階段
#. de: Treppe des Lozatl
#. fr: Conquête de Lozatl
#. column 14: In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: According to Ronkan legend, the great steps of this waterfall were carved by the giant Lozatl. Historians speculate that this mythical figure was, in fact, an early form of Talos, and likely the selfsame construct responsible for building Ronka's resplendent places of worship.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162929:0:13"
msgid "Lozatl's Conquest"
msgstr "Завоевание Лоцатля"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラケティカ大森林のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Großen Waldes Rak'tika gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Rak'tika que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Lozatl's Conquest
#. column 15: According to Ronkan legend, the great steps of this waterfall were carved by the giant Lozatl. Historians speculate that this mythical figure was, in fact, an early form of Talos, and likely the selfsame construct responsible for building Ronka's resplendent places of worship.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162929:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Странствуя по Великому лесу Рактика, я вдруг замерла, заворожённая открывшимся видом. Нельзя дать такой красоте затеряться — я должна запечатлеть её на бумаге."

#. ja: ロンカ神話に登場する巨人「ロツァトル」が作ったと伝えられている階段状の滝。ある史学者の説によれば、ロツァトルは初期のタロースであり、ロンカ文明の壮麗な石造神殿も、その手によるものではないかと考察されている
#. de: Es heißt, diese Kaskade aus unzähligen Treppenstufen hätte Lozatl, ein Riese aus der Ronka-Mythologie, geschaffen. Einige Historiker sind der Meinung, dass Lozatl einer der ersten Taloi der Geschichte ist, und dass er selbst die prächtigen steinernen Tempel der Ronka-Zivilisation gebaut hat.
#. fr: Cette cascade en escalier aurait été créée par Lozatl, un géant apparaissant dans la mythologie ronka. Certains historiens considèrent que Lozatl serait l'un des premiers talos de l'histoire, et qu'il aurait construit lui-même les magnifiques temples issus de la civilisation ronka.
#. column 13: Lozatl's Conquest
#. column 14: In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162929:0:15"
msgid "According to Ronkan legend, the great steps of this waterfall were carved by the giant Lozatl. Historians speculate that this mythical figure was, in fact, an early form of Talos, and likely the selfsame construct responsible for building Ronka's resplendent places of worship."
msgstr "По преданию ронка, ступени этого водопада высек великан Лозатль. Историки предполагают, что мифический великан был одним из первых талосов и, вероятно, именно он построил великолепные святилища Ронки."

#. ja: ファノヴの里
#. de: Fanow
#. fr: Fanow
#. column 14: In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: Unfailingly loyal to the last-known commands of the Ronkan emperor, the Viis of this village have protected the ruins of Rak'tika for countless generations. With many of its sister settlements destroyed by the Flood of Light, however, Fanow faces an uncertain fate in its isolation.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162930:0:13"
msgid "Fanow"
msgstr "Фанов"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラケティカ大森林のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Großen Waldes Rak'tika gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Rak'tika que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: Fanow
#. column 15: Unfailingly loyal to the last-known commands of the Ronkan emperor, the Viis of this village have protected the ruins of Rak'tika for countless generations. With many of its sister settlements destroyed by the Flood of Light, however, Fanow faces an uncertain fate in its isolation.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162930:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Странствуя по Великому лесу Рактика, я вдруг замерла, заворожённая открывшимся видом. Нельзя дать такой красоте затеряться — я должна запечатлеть её на бумаге."

#. ja: ロンカ皇帝の命により、数千年に渡ってラケティカ大森林の遺跡群を護ってきたヴィースたちの里。しかし、大半の里が「光の氾濫」により消滅したため、この里単独での存続は難しく、先行きが危ぶまれてもいる
#. de: Seit Tausenden von Jahren wachen die Viis auf Befehl des Kaisers von Ronka über die Ruinen von Rak'tika. Da jedoch die meisten ihrer Dörfer durch die Lichtflut ausgelöscht wurden, ist ihr Fortbestand nun bedroht.
#. fr: Sur ordre de l'empereur ronka, les Viis de ce village ont protégé les ruines de Rak'tika pendant des milliers d'années. Cependant, une grande partie du village ayant été exterminée par le déluge de Lumière, il leur est devenu difficile de survivre sans aide extérieure.
#. column 13: Fanow
#. column 14: In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162930:0:15"
msgid "Unfailingly loyal to the last-known commands of the Ronkan emperor, the Viis of this village have protected the ruins of Rak'tika for countless generations. With many of its sister settlements destroyed by the Flood of Light, however, Fanow faces an uncertain fate in its isolation."
msgstr "Виесы из этой деревни уже бесчисленные поколения хранят руины Рактики, следуя последним известным приказам императора Ронки. Но многие соседние поселения уничтожил Потоп Света, и теперь изолированному Фанову грозит неопределённое будущее."

#. ja: 四つの明星
#. de: Morgensterne
#. fr: Étoiles du Matin
#. column 14: In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
#. column 15: These pyramids were built to venerate the four chief deities of the Ronkan religion: Ox'Gatorl, keeper of flame; Ox'Charl, keeper of the winds; Yx'Lokwa, bringer of rain; and Yx'Anpa, bringer of the harvest. For the inhabitants of Fanow, guardians of Ronka's heritage, there are few sites more sacred.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162931:0:13"
msgid "The Morning Stars"
msgstr "Утренние звёзды"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラケティカ大森林のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Großen Waldes Rak'tika gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage inspirieren zu Liedern und Weisen.
#. fr: C'est au cours de pérégrinations à Rak'tika que j'ai découvert cet endroit offrant une vue splendide sur un fantastique paysage. Sa beauté était telle que j'ai ressenti la nécessité de le partager.
#. column 13: The Morning Stars
#. column 15: These pyramids were built to venerate the four chief deities of the Ronkan religion: Ox'Gatorl, keeper of flame; Ox'Charl, keeper of the winds; Yx'Lokwa, bringer of rain; and Yx'Anpa, bringer of the harvest. For the inhabitants of Fanow, guardians of Ronka's heritage, there are few sites more sacred.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162931:0:14"
msgid "In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by."
msgstr "Странствуя по Великому лесу Рактика, я вдруг замерла, заворожённая открывшимся видом. Нельзя дать такой красоте затеряться — я должна запечатлеть её на бумаге."

#. ja: ロンカの大星座を司る4柱の神々、すなわち火の神ガトル、水の女神ロックワ、風の神チャール、土の女神アンパを祀る4基のピラミッドが連なる遺跡群。ロンカの護り手を自認するファノヴの民にとっては、聖地に等しい
#. de: In diesen Heiligtümern liegen die Gräber der vier Götter der Ronka-Mythologie, nämlich des Feuergottes Ox'Gatorl, der Wassergöttin Yx'Lokwa, des Windgottes Ox'Charl und der Erdgöttin Yx'Anpa. Es ist ein heiliger Ort für die Bewohnerinnen von Fanow, die stolz darauf sind, die Ruinen zu hüten.
#. fr: Dans ces ruines sont enfouies les sépultures des quatre déités de la mythologie ronka, à savoir le dieu du feu Ox'Gatorl, la déesse de l'eau Yx'Lokwa, le dieu du vent Ox'Charl et la déesse de la terre Yx'Anpa. C'est un lieu sacré pour les habitants du village de Fanow qui s'enorgueillissent d'en être les protecteurs.
#. column 13: The Morning Stars
#. column 14: In my wanderings through the Rak'tika Greatwood, I found myself pausing in wide-eyed wonder as I looked out upon the view before me. I knew that I must capture this sight in ink, lest others simply pass it by.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162931:0:15"
msgid "These pyramids were built to venerate the four chief deities of the Ronkan religion: Ox'Gatorl, keeper of flame; Ox'Charl, keeper of the winds; Yx'Lokwa, bringer of rain; and Yx'Anpa, bringer of the harvest. For the inhabitants of Fanow, guardians of Ronka's heritage, there are few sites more sacred."
msgstr "Эти пирамиды воздвигли в честь четырёх главных божеств Ронки: Окс'Гаторла, хранителя огня; Окс'Чарла, хранителя ветров; Икс'Локвы, дарительницы дождя; и Икс'Анпы, дарительницы урожая. Для жителей Фанова, хранителей наследия Ронки, нет места священнее."

#. ja: オンドの潮溜まり
#. de: Ondo-Becken
#. fr: Baïne
#. column 14: I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware...
#. column 15: Hidden at the bottom of the Tempest, this Ondo settlement was established by those few foragers who escaped the Flood's destruction of their homeland. “Cups” refers to the hollows on the shore that remain filled with seawater when the tide recedes—miraculous shelters not unlike the Ondo's refuge.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162932:0:13"
msgid "The Ondo Cups"
msgstr "Чаши ондо"

#. ja: ――前人未踏の地へと赴け。\nノルヴラントのいずこか、まだ見ぬ絶景を記せ。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Es gibt Winkel in Norvrandt, die nie ein Reisender betrat. Ohne Zweifel bieten sie dem, der sie findet und betrachtet, einen erstaunlichen Anblick.
#. fr: Il reste en Norvrandt des endroits qu'aucun humain n'a encore visités, et celui-ci en est un. Nul doute qu'il offrira une vue splendide à celui qui saura trouver le meilleur point pour l'observer.
#. column 13: The Ondo Cups
#. column 15: Hidden at the bottom of the Tempest, this Ondo settlement was established by those few foragers who escaped the Flood's destruction of their homeland. “Cups” refers to the hollows on the shore that remain filled with seawater when the tide recedes—miraculous shelters not unlike the Ondo's refuge.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162932:0:14"
msgid "I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware..."
msgstr "Я увидела укромный уголок Норврандта, о котором мало кто знает и куда и вовсе немногие добирались. В этом тайном краю скрывается вид, о котором должны узнать все..."

#. ja: 黒風海の底に築かれたオンド族の集落。「潮溜まり」は、干潮時に海岸に残された海水の水たまりのことで、「光の氾濫」時に偶然、陸上にいたことで命を永らえた者たちが、仮設の避難先として設立したことに由来する
#. de: Auf dem Boden des Meeres der Schwarzen Winde haben die Ondo ihre Becken errichtet. Sie erinnern damit an ihre in der Lichtflut untergegangene Heimat, die mit Brandungswasser gefüllten Steinbecken an einer längst vergessenen Küste.
#. fr: Ce hameau ondo se trouve au fond de la Mer des Vents noirs. Son nom provient des mares d'eau qui se forment le long de la côte à marée basse. Elles ont servi de refuge temporaire à ceux qui ont eu la vie sauve, car ils étaient par chance sur la terre ferme au moment du déluge de Lumière.
#. column 13: The Ondo Cups
#. column 14: I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162932:0:15"
msgid "Hidden at the bottom of the Tempest, this Ondo settlement was established by those few foragers who escaped the Flood's destruction of their homeland. “Cups” refers to the hollows on the shore that remain filled with seawater when the tide recedes—miraculous shelters not unlike the Ondo's refuge."
msgstr "Поселение ондо, затерянное на дне Бури, основали немногие собиратели, пережившие Потоп, уничтоживший их родину. «Чашами» называют впадины у берега, где после отлива остаётся морская вода. Эти природные убежища стали спасением для ондо."

#. ja: 奇人のアトリエ
#. de: Die Werkstatt
#. fr: Atelier de l'Original
#. column 14: I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware...
#. column 15: This facility was built by a Crystarium native─a genius artisan seeking to escape from the distractions of the outside world. Although he simply calls the place his “Workbench,” the mundane naming is at odds with the fantastical concept of a forge constructed malms beneath the ocean.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162933:0:13"
msgid "The Workbench"
msgstr "Мастерская"

#. ja: ――前人未踏の地へと赴け。\nノルヴラントのいずこか、まだ見ぬ絶景を記せ。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Es gibt Winkel in Norvrandt, die nie ein Reisender betrat. Ohne Zweifel bieten sie dem, der sie findet und betrachtet, einen erstaunlichen Anblick.
#. fr: Il reste en Norvrandt des endroits qu'aucun humain n'a encore visités, et celui-ci en est un. Nul doute qu'il offrira une vue splendide à celui qui saura trouver le meilleur point pour l'observer.
#. column 13: The Workbench
#. column 15: This facility was built by a Crystarium native─a genius artisan seeking to escape from the distractions of the outside world. Although he simply calls the place his “Workbench,” the mundane naming is at odds with the fantastical concept of a forge constructed malms beneath the ocean.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162933:0:14"
msgid "I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware..."
msgstr "Я увидела укромный уголок Норврандта, о котором мало кто знает и куда и вовсе немногие добирались. В этом тайном краю скрывается вид, о котором должны узнать все..."

#. ja: クリスタリウム出身の某天才職人が、人社会から逃れるために隠れ棲んでいるアトリエ。彼自身は、この場所を単純に「アトリエ」と呼ぶが、海の底に工房を設けるという発想自体が常人ではないことを示している
#. de: Die Arbeitsstätte eines genialen Handwerkers aus Crystarium, der alles zurückließ, um hinter die technischen Geheimnisse der Alten zu kommen. Ein Sonderling, dem das einsame Leben auf dem Meeresboden zugesetzt zu haben scheint.
#. fr: Ce lieu a été bâti par un artisan cristarien de génie lorsqu'il a décidé de vivre à l'écart de la société des humains. Bien qu'il l'appelle simplement son “atelier”, seul un esprit des plus originaux aurait pu avoir l'idée de le construire au fond de la mer.
#. column 13: The Workbench
#. column 14: I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162933:0:15"
msgid "This facility was built by a Crystarium native─a genius artisan seeking to escape from the distractions of the outside world. Although he simply calls the place his “Workbench,” the mundane naming is at odds with the fantastical concept of a forge constructed malms beneath the ocean."
msgstr "Эту мастерскую построил гениальный ремесленник из Кристариума, желавший скрыться от суеты внешнего мира. Сам он просто зовёт её «Мастерской», хотя устроить кузницу на много миль под водой мог додуматься лишь человек с весьма необычным складом ума."

#. ja: 陸人の墓標
#. de: Seelenruh der Landler
#. fr: Crypte du Sans-branchies
#. column 14: I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware...
#. column 15: When the Ondo beheld the coral within this cavern, its crimson branches put them in mind of a land-dweller's veins─thus began the legend that it was a resting place for finless ones who had perished at sea. It was not until recently, however, that folk from the surface learned the reason behind the rather ominous-sounding name.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162934:0:13"
msgid "Where the Dry Return"
msgstr "Там, где возвращаются сухими"

#. ja: ――前人未踏の地へと赴け。\nノルヴラントのいずこか、まだ見ぬ絶景を記せ。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Es gibt Winkel in Norvrandt, die nie ein Reisender betrat. Ohne Zweifel bieten sie dem, der sie findet und betrachtet, einen erstaunlichen Anblick.
#. fr: Il reste en Norvrandt des endroits qu'aucun humain n'a encore visités, et celui-ci en est un. Nul doute qu'il offrira une vue splendide à celui qui saura trouver le meilleur point pour l'observer.
#. column 13: Where the Dry Return
#. column 15: When the Ondo beheld the coral within this cavern, its crimson branches put them in mind of a land-dweller's veins─thus began the legend that it was a resting place for finless ones who had perished at sea. It was not until recently, however, that folk from the surface learned the reason behind the rather ominous-sounding name.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162934:0:14"
msgid "I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware..."
msgstr "Я увидела укромный уголок Норврандта, о котором мало кто знает и куда и вовсе немногие добирались. В этом тайном краю скрывается вид, о котором должны узнать все..."

#. ja: 珊瑚が群生する洞窟。その赤い珊瑚が地上人の血管のように見えるため、オンド族の間では陸人（おかびと）らの魂が眠る場所と伝えられてきた。しかし、当の陸人は、その事実を近年まで知らなかったのである
#. de: Die roten Korallenäste dieser Höhle erinnern die Ondo an die Blutgefäße der Flossenlosen. Irgendetwas lässt sie glauben, dass die Seelen der Land<shy>be<shy>wohner sich in diese Höhle zurückziehen, um Ruhe zu finden.
#. fr: Cette cavité formée na<shy>tu<shy>rel<shy>le<shy>ment par des coraux, qui ressemblent à s'y méprendre à des veines d'humain, est considérée par les Ondos comme le lieu où dorment paisiblement les âmes de ceux qu'ils appellent les “sans-branchies”. Ce fait est toutefois resté inconnu des humains jusqu'à il y a peu.
#. column 13: Where the Dry Return
#. column 14: I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162934:0:15"
msgid "When the Ondo beheld the coral within this cavern, its crimson branches put them in mind of a land-dweller's veins─thus began the legend that it was a resting place for finless ones who had perished at sea. It was not until recently, however, that folk from the surface learned the reason behind the rather ominous-sounding name."
msgstr "В этой пещере растут кораллы. Их алые ветви напомнили ондо вены наземных жителей — так родилась легенда, будто здесь покоятся души тех, кто погиб в море. Лишь недавно обитатели суши узнали, откуда взялось это зловещее название."

#. ja: プルプラ洞
#. de: Purpurhöhle
#. fr: Grotte purpurine
#. column 14: I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware...
#. column 15: The Ondo use the shells they gather from this cave to make dye, the purple hue prized as a symbol of nobility. It is said that Eulmore's obsession with the color purple can be traced back to these underwater origins.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162935:0:13"
msgid "Purpure"
msgstr "Пурпурная пещера"

#. ja: ――前人未踏の地へと赴け。\nノルヴラントのいずこか、まだ見ぬ絶景を記せ。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Es gibt Winkel in Norvrandt, die nie ein Reisender betrat. Ohne Zweifel bieten sie dem, der sie findet und betrachtet, einen erstaunlichen Anblick.
#. fr: Il reste en Norvrandt des endroits qu'aucun humain n'a encore visités, et celui-ci en est un. Nul doute qu'il offrira une vue splendide à celui qui saura trouver le meilleur point pour l'observer.
#. column 13: Purpure
#. column 15: The Ondo use the shells they gather from this cave to make dye, the purple hue prized as a symbol of nobility. It is said that Eulmore's obsession with the color purple can be traced back to these underwater origins.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162935:0:14"
msgid "I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware..."
msgstr "Я увидела укромный уголок Норврандта, о котором мало кто знает и куда и вовсе немногие добирались. В этом тайном краю скрывается вид, о котором должны узнать все..."

#. ja: プルプラ貝の群生地。この巻き貝の貝殻からは染料を作ることができ、それを使って染められた紫色の布地は、高貴な者の象徴として珍重されてきた。ユールモアで紫色が好まれるのも、こうした歴史に由来する
#. de: In dieser Höhle gedeihen Muscheln, die einen Farbstoff abgeben, der sich bei den Reichen und Adeligen von Eulmore größter Beliebtheit erfreut. Die daraus gefertigten purpurnen Kleider erzielen Höchstpreise und sorgen für neidische Blicke.
#. fr: Cette caverne sous-marine tient son nom de la colonie de pourpres qui y vit. La coquille en spirale de ces gastéropodes permet d'obtenir un pigment qui sert à teindre les tissus et qui est considéré comme un symbole de noblesse, notamment dans des villes comme Eulmore.
#. column 13: Purpure
#. column 14: I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162935:0:15"
msgid "The Ondo use the shells they gather from this cave to make dye, the purple hue prized as a symbol of nobility. It is said that Eulmore's obsession with the color purple can be traced back to these underwater origins."
msgstr "Ондо собирают в этой пещере раковины и делают из них краску. Пурпурный цвет издавна считается символом благородства. Говорят, любовь Юлмора к пурпуру пошла именно отсюда, с морского дна."

#. ja: アーモロート
#. de: Amaurot
#. fr: Amaurote
#. column 14: I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware...
#. column 15: If Ondo testimony is to be believed, this vast city simply appeared overnight. Unlike the ancient remnants which endure silently upon the sea floor, its illuminated towers are of a decidedly different nature─a meticulously new and vibrant metropolis, compelling in its mystery.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162936:0:13"
msgid "Amaurot"
msgstr "Амаврот"

#. ja: ――前人未踏の地へと赴け。\nノルヴラントのいずこか、まだ見ぬ絶景を記せ。\nその場で見渡すべし。
#. de: Es gibt Winkel in Norvrandt, die nie ein Reisender betrat. Ohne Zweifel bieten sie dem, der sie findet und betrachtet, einen erstaunlichen Anblick.
#. fr: Il reste en Norvrandt des endroits qu'aucun humain n'a encore visités, et celui-ci en est un. Nul doute qu'il offrira une vue splendide à celui qui saura trouver le meilleur point pour l'observer.
#. column 13: Amaurot
#. column 15: If Ondo testimony is to be believed, this vast city simply appeared overnight. Unlike the ancient remnants which endure silently upon the sea floor, its illuminated towers are of a decidedly different nature─a meticulously new and vibrant metropolis, compelling in its mystery.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162936:0:14"
msgid "I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware..."
msgstr "Я увидела укромный уголок Норврандта, о котором мало кто знает и куда и вовсе немногие добирались. В этом тайном краю скрывается вид, о котором должны узнать все..."

#. ja: オンド族の証言によれば、その海底都市は一夜にして生じたという。海の底で長き時を経て、朽ちてきたその他の遺跡とは明らかに異なり、街並みは真新しく、整備が行き届いて見えるなど謎が多い場所である
#. de: Laut den Ondo erleuchtete die Stadt am Meeresgrund eines Nachts ohne Vorwarnung. Anders als die Ruinen in der Nähe ihres Dorfes waren die Türme neu und erhoben sich hoch über ihre Köpfe, was die Ondo mit so viel Ehrfurcht  erfüllte, dass sie den Zugang zu dem Erleuchteten Land verboten.
#. fr: D'après les Ondos, cette ville sous-marine serait apparue en une nuit. Con<shy>trai<shy>re<shy>ment aux ruines que l'on trouve sous les eaux et qui ont fini par s'écrouler sous l'effet du temps, Amaurote resplendit mys<shy>té<shy>rieu<shy>se<shy>ment par son aspect neuf et ses ins<shy>tal<shy>la<shy>tions en parfait état.
#. column 13: Amaurot
#. column 14: I have looked out upon a corner of Norvrandt that few will know, and even fewer will have visited. Yet within this secret realm hides a vista of which all must be made aware...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162936:0:15"
msgid "If Ondo testimony is to be believed, this vast city simply appeared overnight. Unlike the ancient remnants which endure silently upon the sea floor, its illuminated towers are of a decidedly different nature─a meticulously new and vibrant metropolis, compelling in its mystery."
msgstr "По словам ондо, этот огромный город возник за одну ночь. В отличие от древних руин, безмолвно лежащих на морском дне, его освещённые башни выглядят совсем иначе: город словно только что отстроили, и он полон жизни. Его тайна завораживает."

#. ja: ルヴェユール邸
#. de: Anwesen der Leveilleurs
#. fr: Résidence des Leveilleur
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: This elegant mansion has stood for three centuries, and is a treasured example of Sharlayan's architectural heritage. For generations, it has served as the home of House Leveilleur─a noble family from which has arisen many distinguished Forum members.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162937:0:13"
msgid "The Leveilleur Estate"
msgstr "Поместье Левейёров"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nオールド・シャーレアンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Alt-Sharlayans gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Und die Herrlichkeit, die ich erblickte, übertraf alles, was mir je über diese Stadt zu Ohren gekommen war.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Vieille Sharlayan, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: The Leveilleur Estate
#. column 15: This elegant mansion has stood for three centuries, and is a treasured example of Sharlayan's architectural heritage. For generations, it has served as the home of House Leveilleur─a noble family from which has arisen many distinguished Forum members.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162937:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Старый Шарлаян, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая, я потянулась за пером и пергаментом..."

#. ja: ルヴェユール家の邸宅。現当主であるフルシュノ氏をはじめ、同家は数多く哲学者議会の議員を輩出してきた名門として知られている。築300年を誇るその美しい邸宅は、シャーレアン建築の遺産との呼び声も高い
#. de: Die Architektur dieses 300 Jahre alten Prachtbaus ist ein glanzvolles Beispiel traditioneller, sharlayanischer Handwerkskunst. Seit vielen Generationen befindet sich das Anwesen in Besitz der Adelsfamilie Leveilleur, aus welcher zahlreiche namhafte Ratsmitglieder hervorgegangen sind.
#. fr: Cette bâtisse, érigée il y a trois cents ans, témoigne du savoir-faire architectural sharlayanais. Elle appartient aux Leveilleur, une famille de renom, dont nombre de membres se sont succédé au sein du Conseil de Sharlayan. Le dernier en date étant Fourchenault, le chef de famille actuel.
#. column 13: The Leveilleur Estate
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162937:0:15"
msgid "This elegant mansion has stood for three centuries, and is a treasured example of Sharlayan's architectural heritage. For generations, it has served as the home of House Leveilleur─a noble family from which has arisen many distinguished Forum members."
msgstr "Этот изящный особняк стоит уже три столетия и считается драгоценным памятником архитектуры Шарлаяна. Поколениями он служит домом семьи Левейёр — знатного рода, давшего множество выдающихся членов Форума."

#. ja: 知神の港
#. de: Thaliaks Pforte
#. fr: Port de l'Érudit
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Although known for its distinctively curving piers, the most prominent feature of the city's port is, without a doubt, the towering statue of Thaliak. Sharlayan's patron deity faces out towards the water, His eternal gaze watching over every vessel which arrives and departs by sea.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162938:0:13"
msgid "Scholar's Harbor"
msgstr "Порт Мудрости"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nオールド・シャーレアンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Alt-Sharlayans gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Und die Herrlichkeit, die ich erblickte, übertraf alles, was mir je über diese Stadt zu Ohren gekommen war.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Vieille Sharlayan, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Scholar's Harbor
#. column 15: Although known for its distinctively curving piers, the most prominent feature of the city's port is, without a doubt, the towering statue of Thaliak. Sharlayan's patron deity faces out towards the water, His eternal gaze watching over every vessel which arrives and departs by sea.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162938:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Старый Шарлаян, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая, я потянулась за пером и пергаментом..."

#. ja: オールド・シャーレアンの港湾地区。同都市の守護神でもある知神「サリャク」に由来する名で呼ばれるとおり、その石像がそびえ立ち、往来する船を見守っている。弧を描く埠頭も、大きな特徴のひとつ
#. de: Die perfekt geschwungenen Schiffspiere von Alt-Sharlayans Pforte zur Welt sind ein wahrer Blickfang, doch die Anmut der über allem thronenden Statue inmitten des Hafens vermögen sie nicht zu übertreffen. Sie ist ein Abbild von Sharlayans Schutzgott Thaliak und wacht, den Blick gen Wasser gerichtet, über Ankunft und Abschied aller Reisenden.
#. fr: Les bateaux qui entrent dans le port de Sharlayan sont accueillis par la statue de Thaliak, le dieu tutélaire de la Cité du savoir. Ils accostent ensuite des quais tracés en arc de cercle à l'élégance incomparable.
#. column 13: Scholar's Harbor
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162938:0:15"
msgid "Although known for its distinctively curving piers, the most prominent feature of the city's port is, without a doubt, the towering statue of Thaliak. Sharlayan's patron deity faces out towards the water, His eternal gaze watching over every vessel which arrives and departs by sea."
msgstr "Порт города славится изогнутыми причалами, но главное его украшение — возвышающаяся над ним статуя Талияка. Покровитель Шарлаяна обращён к морю, и его вечный взор провожает и встречает каждое судно."

#. ja: 哲学者議会議場
#. de: Sitzungssaal des Rates
#. fr: Les Rostres
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: In order to accommodate the ninety-nine members of the Forum, the seating in their assembly hall is arranged in the shape of a spiral. Viewed from above, one is reminded of the symbol emblazoned upon the Sharlayan flag─the nautilus shell that keeps the water of knowledge.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162939:0:13"
msgid "The Forum"
msgstr "Форум"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nオールド・シャーレアンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Alt-Sharlayans gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Und die Herrlichkeit, die ich erblickte, übertraf alles, was mir je über diese Stadt zu Ohren gekommen war.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Vieille Sharlayan, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: The Forum
#. column 15: In order to accommodate the ninety-nine members of the Forum, the seating in their assembly hall is arranged in the shape of a spiral. Viewed from above, one is reminded of the symbol emblazoned upon the Sharlayan flag─the nautilus shell that keeps the water of knowledge.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162939:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Старый Шарлаян, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая, я потянулась за пером и пергаментом..."

#. ja: 哲学者議会の議場。定数99名の議員たちが一堂に会することができるように、螺旋を描くように議席が並べられている。その様子を俯瞰すると、国旗にも用いられている知識の水を溜め込む巻き貝の模様に見えるという
#. de: Damit alle 99 Mitglieder des Rates der Philosophen im Saal Platz finden, sind die Sitze darin spiralförmig angeordnet. Von oben betrachtet symbolisiert diese Anordnung die sharlayanische Flagge, auf welcher eine Spiralmuschel gefüllt mit dem Wasser der Weisheit dargestellt ist.
#. fr: Le Conseil de Sharlayan se réunit dans cette salle qui compte quatre-vingt-dix-neuf sièges, un pour chaque membre. Vue d'en haut, cette disposition forme le motif de l'emblème national, un coquillage spiralé censé incarner la source de toute con<shy>nais<shy>san<shy>ce.
#. column 13: The Forum
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162939:0:15"
msgid "In order to accommodate the ninety-nine members of the Forum, the seating in their assembly hall is arranged in the shape of a spiral. Viewed from above, one is reminded of the symbol emblazoned upon the Sharlayan flag─the nautilus shell that keeps the water of knowledge. "
msgstr "Чтобы вместить девяносто девять членов Форума, места в зале заседаний расположили по спирали. Если взглянуть сверху, они напоминают символ на флаге Шарлаяна — раковину наутилуса, хранящую воды знания."

#. ja: ヌーメノン大書院
#. de: Noumenon
#. fr: Noumène
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: The pride of the Studium and parent institution to the Great Gubal Library, this massive collection of scrolls and tomes is the largest of its kind. Knowledge from every corner of the world is collected here, and efforts to compile the <i>Bibliotheca Historica</i>─the ultimate repository of wisdom─is an endeavor without end.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162940:0:13"
msgid "Noumenon"
msgstr "Ноумен"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nオールド・シャーレアンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Alt-Sharlayans gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Und die Herrlichkeit, die ich erblickte, übertraf alles, was mir je über diese Stadt zu Ohren gekommen war.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Vieille Sharlayan, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Noumenon
#. column 15: The pride of the Studium and parent institution to the Great Gubal Library, this massive collection of scrolls and tomes is the largest of its kind. Knowledge from every corner of the world is collected here, and efforts to compile the <i>Bibliotheca Historica</i>─the ultimate repository of wisdom─is an endeavor without end.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162940:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Старый Шарлаян, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая, я потянулась за пером и пергаментом..."

#. ja: シャーレアン魔法大学が誇る世界最大規模の大図書館。グブラ幻想図書館の本館にあたり、世界各地から集めた多種多様な書物を収蔵している。すべての知識の集積を目指し、「世界図鑑」の編纂を進めているという
#. de: Mit der größten Sammlung an Schriften und Büchern in der bekannten Welt ist das Noumenon als Hauptzweig der großen Gubal-Bibliothek der ganze Stolz der Magieakademie von Sharlayan. Unter den hier gesammelten Werken befindet sich auch die wohl wichtigste und doch längst nicht vollendete Anthologie des Wissens selbst, die Encyclopaedia Universalis.
#. fr: C'est dans ce bâtiment de leur académie de magie que les Sharlayanais entreposent tout le savoir écrit qu'ils récupèrent de par le monde – une collection dont la diversité rivalise celle de la Grande bibliothèque de Gubal. La dévotion des glaneurs a fait du Noumène la plus grande bibliothèque connue, mais leur travail de compilation se poursuit encore à ce jour.
#. column 13: Noumenon
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162940:0:15"
msgid "The pride of the Studium and parent institution to the Great Gubal Library, this massive collection of scrolls and tomes is the largest of its kind. Knowledge from every corner of the world is collected here, and efforts to compile the <i>Bibliotheca Historica</i>─the ultimate repository of wisdom─is an endeavor without end."
msgstr "Гордость Студиума и главный корпус Большой библиотеки Губала — Нуменон хранит крупнейшее в мире собрание свитков и книг. Сюда стекаются знания со всех концов света, а составление <i>Исторической библиотеки</i> — величайшего хранилища мудрости — не прекратится никогда."

#. ja: 哲学者の広場
#. de: Das Forum
#. fr: Conseil de Sharlayan
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: This building houses the assembly hall where the Forum debates Sharlayan national policy. Once a simple outdoor plaza, the Rostra would ring with heated discussion through rain, wind, and worse.  Following a death by lightning strike, however, plans were drawn up for the imposing stone structure which now crowns Archons' Design.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162941:0:13"
msgid "The Rostra"
msgstr "Ростра"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nオールド・シャーレアンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Alt-Sharlayans gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Und die Herrlichkeit, die ich erblickte, übertraf alles, was mir je über diese Stadt zu Ohren gekommen war.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Vieille Sharlayan, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
