#. column 15: This building houses the assembly hall where the Forum debates Sharlayan national policy. Once a simple outdoor plaza, the Rostra would ring with heated discussion through rain, wind, and worse.  Following a death by lightning strike, however, plans were drawn up for the imposing stone structure which now crowns Archons' Design.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162941:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Старый Шарлаян, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая, я потянулась за пером и пергаментом..."

#. ja: シャーレアンの政策を論じる哲学者議会が開かれる議事堂。元来は円形の広場であり、雨の日も風の日も屋外で議論が行われていたが、ある時、落雷により死者が出たため、石造の巨大議事堂が造られることになった
#. de: Bevor das Kuppelgebäude entstand, das heute den Sitzungssaal des Rates beherbergt, war das Forum ein schlichter, ringförmiger Ver<shy>samm<shy>lungs<shy>platz unter freiem Himmel. Erst ein Blitzeinschlag, der während einer Tagung inmitten eines Sturmes Todesopfer forderte, konnte den Rat davon überzeugen, ein Gebäude am höchsten Punkt des Gartens der Exegeten zu errichten.
#. fr: Le Conseil de Sharlayan, la plus haute autorité politique du pays, se réunissait autrefois dans un amphithéâtre à ciel ouvert, et ce, qu'il pleuve ou qu'il vente. Lorsqu'un de ses membres mourut foudroyé pendant un orage, le Conseil décida alors, dans sa grande sagesse, de faire construire un édifice en pierre et pourvu d'un toit pour se protéger des intempéries.
#. column 13: The Rostra
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162941:0:15"
msgid "This building houses the assembly hall where the Forum debates Sharlayan national policy. Once a simple outdoor plaza, the Rostra would ring with heated discussion through rain, wind, and worse.  Following a death by lightning strike, however, plans were drawn up for the imposing stone structure which now crowns Archons' Design."
msgstr "Здесь заседает Форум, обсуждая государственную политику Шарлаяна. Когда-то на этом месте была простая открытая площадь, где споры не стихали ни в дождь, ни в ветер. Но после того как один из участников погиб от удара молнии, решили возвести внушительное каменное здание, венчающее ныне Сад Архонтов."

#. ja: 漂流者の丘
#. de: Hügel der Gestrandeten
#. fr: Colline des Naufragés
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Occupying the eastern side of Old Sharlayan, the residential district takes its name from the tale of the city's original settlers. History tells that it is upon this hill, alongside a colony of auks, where the refugees of the great flood chose to build their new homes.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162942:0:13"
msgid "Journey's End"
msgstr "Конец пути"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nオールド・シャーレアンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Alt-Sharlayans gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Und die Herrlichkeit, die ich erblickte, übertraf alles, was mir je über diese Stadt zu Ohren gekommen war.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Vieille Sharlayan, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Journey's End
#. column 15: Occupying the eastern side of Old Sharlayan, the residential district takes its name from the tale of the city's original settlers. History tells that it is upon this hill, alongside a colony of auks, where the refugees of the great flood chose to build their new homes.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162942:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Старый Шарлаян, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая, я потянулась за пером и пергаментом..."

#. ja: オールド・シャーレアンの東側に広がる居住区。その奇妙な名は、シャーレアンの開祖ニュンクレフによって大洪水から救われた者たちが、パフィンの群生地であったこの丘に、居留地を築いたことに由来しているという
#. de: Das Wohngebiet Alt-Sharlayans befindet sich im östlichen Teil der Stadt. Geschichtlichen Erzählungen zufolge rührt sein eigentümlicher Name daher, dass die ersten Siedler der Gegend diesen Hügel nach der Flucht vor der großen Flut zu ihrer neuen Heimat machten, wobei sie sich von einer direkt angrenzenden Papageientaucher-Kolonie offenbar nicht stören ließen.
#. fr: Qui sont les “naufragés” qui ont donné leur nom à cette colline<nbsp>? Il ne s'agit pas des habitants du quartier résidentiel d'aujourd'hui, mais des hommes et des femmes que Nyunkrepf a autrefois secourus des inondations. Après s'être échoués au milieu d'une colonie d'alques, ce sont eux qui ont construit ici les premières maisons de Sharlayan.
#. column 13: Journey's End
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162942:0:15"
msgid "Occupying the eastern side of Old Sharlayan, the residential district takes its name from the tale of the city's original settlers. History tells that it is upon this hill, alongside a colony of auks, where the refugees of the great flood chose to build their new homes."
msgstr "Жилой район в восточной части Старого Шарлаяна. Его необычное название связано с преданием о первых поселенцах города. Говорят, спасшиеся от великого потопа беженцы построили здесь дома на холме, где гнездились тупики."

#. ja: 公開講堂
#. de: Auditorium
#. fr: Aula
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: This public lecture hall in Phenomenon is open to Studium pupils and Sharlayan citizens alike. When prominent professors are scheduled to take the lectern, crowds of aspiring academics and established scholars often fill the room to capacity.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162943:0:13"
msgid "Learners' Meet"
msgstr "Место встречи учащихся"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nオールド・シャーレアンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Alt-Sharlayans gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Und die Herrlichkeit, die ich erblickte, übertraf alles, was mir je über diese Stadt zu Ohren gekommen war.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Vieille Sharlayan, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Learners' Meet
#. column 15: This public lecture hall in Phenomenon is open to Studium pupils and Sharlayan citizens alike. When prominent professors are scheduled to take the lectern, crowds of aspiring academics and established scholars often fill the room to capacity.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162943:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Старый Шарлаян, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая, я потянулась за пером и пергаментом..."

#. ja: シャーレアン魔法大学のフェノメノン大講堂内にある教室。魔法大学の学生はもちろんのこと、広く市民に開放された「公開講義」が催される場所であり、人気講師が教壇に立つと、多くの聴講者で埋め尽くされることになる
#. de: Sowohl Mitgliedern der Magieakademie von Sharlayan als auch der Öffentlichkeit ist die Nutzung dieses geräumigen Hörsaals gestattet. Für gewöhnlich finden hier offene Vorlesungen für Studenten statt, doch wenn berühmte Professoren ihre Vorträge ankündigen, ringen Wissbegierige und angehende Forscher geradezu um einen Platz in den Sitzreihen.
#. fr: Cette salle de classe du Phénomène a la particularité d'être aussi utilisée lors des cours magistraux ouverts aux auditeurs libres. Suivant la cote du professeur sur l'estrade, il faut parfois se contenter de rester debout et d'observer depuis le couloir tant il y a foule.
#. column 13: Learners' Meet
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Old Sharlayan had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162943:0:15"
msgid "This public lecture hall in Phenomenon is open to Studium pupils and Sharlayan citizens alike. When prominent professors are scheduled to take the lectern, crowds of aspiring academics and established scholars often fill the room to capacity."
msgstr "Эта открытая лекционная аудитория в Феномене доступна и ученикам Студиума, и жителям Шарлаяна. Когда здесь выступают известные профессора, зал до отказа заполняют начинающие и маститые учёные."

#. ja: ルヴェーダ製糸局
#. de: Ruveydahs Zwirn
#. fr: Soierie de Ruveydah
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: This state-sponsored workshop is famed for producing silk thread of exquisite quality. Its sericulture and weaving techniques were once jealously guarded secrets, but security measures have become lax since Ul'dah and other nations began manufacturing their own silk fabrics.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162944:0:13"
msgid "Ruveydah Fibers"
msgstr "Прядильня Рувейды"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラザハンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Radz-at-Hans gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Betört von der schieren Vielfalt an Farben ergriff ich meine Feder und versuchte, die Schönheit in Worte zu fassen.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Radz-at-Han, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Ruveydah Fibers
#. column 15: This state-sponsored workshop is famed for producing silk thread of exquisite quality. Its sericulture and weaving techniques were once jealously guarded secrets, but security measures have become lax since Ul'dah and other nations began manufacturing their own silk fabrics.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162944:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Радз-ат-Хан, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая ярким многоцветьем, я взялась за перо, чтобы облечь эту красоту в слова."

#. ja: 上質な絹糸を紡ぐことで名高いラザハンの国営工房。その養蚕法と製糸技術は長らく門外不出とされてきたが、ウルダハなどの諸外国でも絹の生産が始まったことで、現在ではさほど厳重に警備されてはいない
#. de: Diese staatlich unterstützte Spinnerei ist die erste Anlaufstelle für jeden, der Seidengarne von feinster Qualität benötigt. Lange Zeit waren ihre Methoden zur Fadenherstellung ein streng gehütetes Geheimnis, doch seit auch andere Länder wie Ul'dah mit der Seidenproduktion begonnen haben, nimmt man es mit den Sicher<shy>heits<shy>maß<shy>nahmen nicht mehr allzu genau.
#. fr: L'industrie textile hannoise rayonne dans le monde entier – à tel point que ses secrets de fabrication ont pendant longtemps été jalousement gardés. Cette méfiance s'est quelque peu dissipée depuis que d'autres Cités comme Ul'dah ont rattrapé leur retard dans les techniques de tissage de la soie.
#. column 13: Ruveydah Fibers
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162944:0:15"
msgid "This state-sponsored workshop is famed for producing silk thread of exquisite quality. Its sericulture and weaving techniques were once jealously guarded secrets, but security measures have become lax since Ul'dah and other nations began manufacturing their own silk fabrics."
msgstr "Эта государственная мастерская славится шёлковой нитью высочайшего качества. Технологии разведения шелкопрядов и прядения долго хранили в тайне, но когда шёлк стали производить в Ульде и других странах, охрану ослабили."

#. ja: バルシャーン・バザール
#. de: Balshahn-Basar
#. fr: Bazar de Balshahn
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: If commerce is the lifeblood of Radz<hyphen>at<hyphen>Han, then these roofed market stalls would be its heart. Balshahn himself was a legendary merchant who made a vast fortune through trade with other nations. It was his final wish that his estate be spent on the construction of a great bazaar, ever flowing with coin and wares.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162945:0:13"
msgid "Balshahn Bazaar"
msgstr "Базар Балшахана"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラザハンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Radz-at-Hans gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Betört von der schieren Vielfalt an Farben ergriff ich meine Feder und versuchte, die Schönheit in Worte zu fassen.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Radz-at-Han, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Balshahn Bazaar
#. column 15: If commerce is the lifeblood of Radz<hyphen>at<hyphen>Han, then these roofed market stalls would be its heart. Balshahn himself was a legendary merchant who made a vast fortune through trade with other nations. It was his final wish that his estate be spent on the construction of a great bazaar, ever flowing with coin and wares.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162945:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Радз-ат-Хан, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая ярким многоцветьем, я взялась за перо, чтобы облечь эту красоту в слова."

#. ja: 交易都市としてのラザハンの中枢とも言うべき、屋根付き市場。他国との通商で莫大な財産を築いた伝説的商人、バルシャーンが遺言によって遺産を寄付することで整備されたもので、今日も金と商品が飛び交っている
#. de: Auf dem Basar, dem Herzstück Radz-at-Hans, pulsiert zwischen prächtig verzierten Marktständen das Leben. Seine Erbauung ist dem Namensgeber selbst zu verdanken, denn der legendäre Kaufmann Balshahn vermachte der Stadt vor seinem Dahinscheiden sein im Handel mit anderen Nationen erwirtschaftetes Vermögen, um den Basar zu finanzieren.
#. fr: Ce marché couvert est pour ainsi dire le cœur battant du commerce hannois. Il fut construit grâce au don posthume de Balshahn, un marchand international aussi riche que légendaire. Aujourd'hui encore, bien après sa mort, son nom reste synonyme d'opulence.
#. column 13: Balshahn Bazaar
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. macro: <hyphen> — a hyphen that does not break the line (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162945:0:15"
msgid "If commerce is the lifeblood of Radz<hyphen>at<hyphen>Han, then these roofed market stalls would be its heart. Balshahn himself was a legendary merchant who made a vast fortune through trade with other nations. It was his final wish that his estate be spent on the construction of a great bazaar, ever flowing with coin and wares. "
msgstr "Если торговля — жизненная сила Радз-ат-Хана, то крытые рыночные ряды — его сердце. Легендарный купец Балшахан сколотил огромное состояние на торговле с другими странами. В последней воле он завещал потратить своё наследство на большой базар, где и поныне не иссякают товары и звон монет."

#. ja: ニーローパラ畜産局
#. de: Nilopalas Vielfalt
#. fr: Ferme de Nilopala
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Hamsa were originally reared for the sole purpose of harvesting their venom, until a breeder by the name of Nilopala devised a technique to remove the creatures' toxin glands. The birds suddenly became a viable source of tender, succulent meat, and, before long, Hamsa dishes were considered a staple of Hannish cuisine.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162946:0:13"
msgid "Nilopala Nourishments"
msgstr "Сады Нилопалы"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラザハンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Radz-at-Hans gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Betört von der schieren Vielfalt an Farben ergriff ich meine Feder und versuchte, die Schönheit in Worte zu fassen.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Radz-at-Han, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Nilopala Nourishments
#. column 15: Hamsa were originally reared for the sole purpose of harvesting their venom, until a breeder by the name of Nilopala devised a technique to remove the creatures' toxin glands. The birds suddenly became a viable source of tender, succulent meat, and, before long, Hamsa dishes were considered a staple of Hannish cuisine.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162946:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Радз-ат-Хан, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая ярким многоцветьем, я взялась за перо, чтобы облечь эту красоту в слова."

#. ja: ラザハンの畜産研究所。元々は錬金素材とする毒液を目的に飼育されていたハンサだが、ニーローパラという牧獣士が、毒腺を除去する技法を開発。食肉としての利用も促進され、ハンサ料理はラザハンの名物となっている
#. de: Lange wurden Hamsas nur für die Entnahme ihrer Giftdrüse gezüchtet, da diese eine wichtige Zutat in der Alchemie darstellt. Es war der Züchter Nilopala, der eine Methode zur Förderung des Giftes aus der Drüse entwickelte, wodurch die Hamsas ohne frühzeitige Schlachtung weitergezüchtet werden konnten. So wurde ihr Fleisch zu einem wertvollen Bestandteil der lokalen Küche.
#. fr: L'élevage de hamsa ne date pas d'hier. En effet, les Hannois les accouplent depuis longtemps afin d'extraire leur puissant poison à des fins alchimiques. Nilopala fut la première éleveuse à développer un moyen de le rendre inopérant, érigeant par là même un nouveau pilier de la gastronomie nationale.
#. column 13: Nilopala Nourishments
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162946:0:15"
msgid "Hamsa were originally reared for the sole purpose of harvesting their venom, until a breeder by the name of Nilopala devised a technique to remove the creatures' toxin glands. The birds suddenly became a viable source of tender, succulent meat, and, before long, Hamsa dishes were considered a staple of Hannish cuisine. "
msgstr "Прежде ханс разводили лишь ради яда. Всё изменилось, когда скотовод по имени Нилопала придумал удалять у птиц ядовитые железы. Ханс стало возможно разводить на мясо, нежное и сочное, и вскоре блюда из них вошли в число главных кушаний ханской кухни."

#. ja: メリードズメイハネ
#. de: Mehrydes Meyhane
#. fr: Meyhane de Mehryde
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Owned and run by the eponymous Mehryde, this meyhane offers light meals and beverages, with the main draw being its myriad varieties of liquor distilled by local alchemists. Foreign visitors are often entranced by the stage performers, whose movements incorporate elements of traditional Thavnairian dance.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162947:0:13"
msgid "Mehryde's Meyhane"
msgstr "Мейхана Мехриды"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラザハンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Radz-at-Hans gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Betört von der schieren Vielfalt an Farben ergriff ich meine Feder und versuchte, die Schönheit in Worte zu fassen.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Radz-at-Han, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Mehryde's Meyhane
#. column 15: Owned and run by the eponymous Mehryde, this meyhane offers light meals and beverages, with the main draw being its myriad varieties of liquor distilled by local alchemists. Foreign visitors are often entranced by the stage performers, whose movements incorporate elements of traditional Thavnairian dance.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162947:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Радз-ат-Хан, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая ярким многоцветьем, я взялась за перо, чтобы облечь эту красоту в слова."

#. ja: メリードが経営するメイハネ、つまり軽食や酒類を提供する店である。地元の錬金術師が醸造した多種多様な蒸留酒が売り。また、サベネア伝統の舞踏を取り入れた、踊り子たちのショーも異邦人に人気となっている
#. de: In diesem reich verzierten Lokal mit eindrucksvollem Ausblick kommen die Radz-at-Haner zusammen, um in entspannter Atmosphäre Speisen und Getränke zu genießen, die oft von der Besitzerin Mehryde selbst serviert werden. Reisende haben hier die Gelegenheit, sich von den traditionellen Tänzen Thavnairs auf der lokaleigenen Bühne verzaubern zu lassen.
#. fr: Un meyhane est un type d'estaminet thavnairois servant de la boisson ainsi que des repas légers. Celui de Mehryde propose des eaux-de-vie distillées par les alchimistes locaux et organise aussi des spectacles de danse tra<shy>di<shy>tion<shy>nel<shy>le qui ne manquent jamais d'émerveiller les visiteurs étrangers.
#. column 13: Mehryde's Meyhane
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162947:0:15"
msgid "Owned and run by the eponymous Mehryde, this meyhane offers light meals and beverages, with the main draw being its myriad varieties of liquor distilled by local alchemists. Foreign visitors are often entranced by the stage performers, whose movements incorporate elements of traditional Thavnairian dance."
msgstr "Мейхана Мехриды — заведение, где подают лёгкие закуски и напитки. Главная гордость — множество сортов крепкого алкоголя, который перегоняют местные алхимики. Иностранных гостей часто завораживают выступления танцовщиц, вплетающих в свои движения элементы традиционного сабенейского танца."

#. ja: メーガドゥータ宮
#. de: Meghaduta-Tempel
#. fr: Palais du Meghaduta
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: The palace of the satrap serves not only as a residence, but also as the center of Radz<hyphen>at<hyphen>Han's government. Meaning “cloud messenger” in the old Arkasodara tongue, Meghaduta was built at the summit of a rocky megalith, its great doors admitting an endless stream of servants, petitioners, and official visitors.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162948:0:13"
msgid "Meghaduta"
msgstr "Мегхадута"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラザハンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Radz-at-Hans gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Betört von der schieren Vielfalt an Farben ergriff ich meine Feder und versuchte, die Schönheit in Worte zu fassen.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Radz-at-Han, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Meghaduta
#. column 15: The palace of the satrap serves not only as a residence, but also as the center of Radz<hyphen>at<hyphen>Han's government. Meaning “cloud messenger” in the old Arkasodara tongue, Meghaduta was built at the summit of a rocky megalith, its great doors admitting an endless stream of servants, petitioners, and official visitors.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162948:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Радз-ат-Хан, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая ярким многоцветьем, я взялась за перо, чтобы облечь эту красоту в слова."

#. ja: ラザハン太守が住まう私邸にして、政治の中心でもある宮殿。アルカソーダラ族の古語で「雲の使者」を意味する名で呼ばれるように、巨石の頂きに造られており、太守の使者や陳情に訪れる者が絶え間なく出入りする
#. de: Meghaduta bedeutet „Bote der Wolken“ in der alten Sprache der Arkasodara. Als Residenz des Magistrats und Machtzentrum der Regierung Radz-at-Hans wird der Tempel seinem Namen nur allzu gerecht. Tagtäglich hasten zahllose offizielle Besucher, Bedienstete und Bittsteller die lange Treppe vor seinen reich verzierten Toren auf und ab.
#. fr: Ce palais est la demeure du satrape et le centre du pouvoir à Radz-at-Han. Il se dresse au bout d'une excroissance rocheuse, qui d'en bas, semble caresser le ciel. Meghaduta signifie d'ailleurs “messager des nuages” dans un ancien dialecte Arkasodara, un sens qui se rapporte aux re<shy>pré<shy>sen<shy>tants et autres envoyés qui vont et viennent sans cesse là-bas.
#. column 13: Meghaduta
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. macro: <hyphen> — a hyphen that does not break the line (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162948:0:15"
msgid "The palace of the satrap serves not only as a residence, but also as the center of Radz<hyphen>at<hyphen>Han's government. Meaning “cloud messenger” in the old Arkasodara tongue, Meghaduta was built at the summit of a rocky megalith, its great doors admitting an endless stream of servants, petitioners, and official visitors."
msgstr "Дворец сатрапа служит не только его резиденцией, но и средоточием власти Радз-ат-Хана. Мегхадута на древнем языке аркасодара означает «вестник облаков». Дворец построен на вершине скального исполина, и его двери не закрываются: сюда нескончаемо идут слуги, просители и официальные посетители."

#. ja: アルザダール廟
#. de: Alzadaals Ruh
#. fr: Repos d'Alzadaal
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Within this mausoleum is interred the mortal remains of Alzadaal, leader of the Auri tribe which sailed to Thavnair from the mainland. By joining the might of his people with the Arkasodara, Alzadaal tipped the scales against the Gajasura, bringing an end to the internecine war of the Matanga tribes.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162949:0:13"
msgid "Alzadaal's Peace"
msgstr "Покой Алзадааля"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラザハンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Radz-at-Hans gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Betört von der schieren Vielfalt an Farben ergriff ich meine Feder und versuchte, die Schönheit in Worte zu fassen.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Radz-at-Han, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Alzadaal's Peace
#. column 15: Within this mausoleum is interred the mortal remains of Alzadaal, leader of the Auri tribe which sailed to Thavnair from the mainland. By joining the might of his people with the Arkasodara, Alzadaal tipped the scales against the Gajasura, bringing an end to the internecine war of the Matanga tribes.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162949:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Радз-ат-Хан, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая ярким многоцветьем, я взялась за перо, чтобы облечь эту красоту в слова."

#. ja: 大陸側からサベネア島に移住してきたアウラ族の族長、アルザダールを祀った霊廟。彼はアルカソーダラ族とガジャースラ族に分かれていたマタンガ族の争いを、前者に力を貸すことで平定し、調和をもたらしたと伝えられている
#. de: In diesem Mausoleum ruht Alzadaal, ein großer Khan der Au Ra, welcher einst vom Festland aus nach Thavnair einwanderte. Indem er sich mit den Arkasodara verbündete und im Kampf an ihrer Seite stand, leistete er einen entscheidenden Beitrag zur Beendigung des Konflikts zwischen den Arkasodara und den Gajasura.
#. fr: Comme son nom l'indique, ce mausolée a été érigé à la mémoire d'Alzadaal, le chef de la première tribu aoranne à venir du continent. On raconte qu'à son arrivée, il restaura l'harmonie entre les Gajasuras et les Arkasodaras en prêtant main-forte à ces derniers.
#. column 13: Alzadaal's Peace
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162949:0:15"
msgid "Within this mausoleum is interred the mortal remains of Alzadaal, leader of the Auri tribe which sailed to Thavnair from the mainland. By joining the might of his people with the Arkasodara, Alzadaal tipped the scales against the Gajasura, bringing an end to the internecine war of the Matanga tribes."
msgstr "В этом мавзолее покоятся останки Алзадааля, предводителя племени ау-ра, прибывшего морем на Тавнаир с материка. Объединив силы своего народа и аркасодара, Алзадааль помог переломить ход войны против гаджасур и положить конец междоусобице племён матанга."

#. ja: ルヴェーダ製糸局空中庭園
#. de: Dachgarten von Ruveydahs Zwirn
#. fr: Jardin suspendu de la soierie de Ruveydah
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Hidden from view atop the workshops of Ruveydah Fibers is a squat golden statue of a gaja, surrounded by a garden of mulberry bushes. Sitting upon the statue is said to bring good fortune, the proof of which is tested as one wanders about the unfenced rooftop.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162950:0:13"
msgid "Ruveydah Fibers Rooftop Garden"
msgstr "Сад на крыше прядильни Рувейды"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラザハンのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Radz-at-Hans gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Betört von der schieren Vielfalt an Farben ergriff ich meine Feder und versuchte, die Schönheit in Worte zu fassen.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Radz-at-Han, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Ruveydah Fibers Rooftop Garden
#. column 15: Hidden from view atop the workshops of Ruveydah Fibers is a squat golden statue of a gaja, surrounded by a garden of mulberry bushes. Sitting upon the statue is said to bring good fortune, the proof of which is tested as one wanders about the unfenced rooftop.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162950:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Радз-ат-Хан, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая ярким многоцветьем, я взялась за перо, чтобы облечь эту красоту в слова."

#. ja: ラザハンが誇る国営製糸局。その屋上庭園には、数多の桑に囲まれた黄金のガジャ像があり、座ると運気が上昇すると伝えられる。効能の真偽は不明だが、少なくともここに至るまでに墜死しなかった点は幸運と言えるだろう
#. de: Fernab aller Blicke, auf dem Dach von Ruveydahs Zwirn, verbirgt sich ein geheimer Garten voller Maulbeersträucher. Es soll Glück bringen, sich auf die goldene Gaja-Statue des Gartens zu setzen. Ob das stimmt, lässt sich sogleich feststellen, falls es einem gelingt, beim Spaziergang über das ungesicherte Dach nicht den Halt zu verlieren.
#. fr: Si Radz-at-Han est la capitale de la soie, alors la soierie de Ruveydah en est le cœur. Au milieu des mûriers blancs qui décorent son jardin suspendu, on trouve un gaja en or censé attirer la bonne fortune lorsque l'on s'assoit à ses côtés. Même si son efficacité reste à démontrer, on constatera tout de même que personne n'a jamais chuté du toit du bâtiment malgré des clôtures par endroit dan<shy>ge<shy>reu<shy>se<shy>ment basses.
#. column 13: Ruveydah Fibers Rooftop Garden
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Radz-at-Han had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162950:0:15"
msgid "Hidden from view atop the workshops of Ruveydah Fibers is a squat golden statue of a gaja, surrounded by a garden of mulberry bushes. Sitting upon the statue is said to bring good fortune, the proof of which is tested as one wanders about the unfenced rooftop."
msgstr "Над мастерскими прядильни Рувейды, скрытая от посторонних глаз, раскинулась крыша-сад. Среди тутовых деревьев стоит приземистая золотая статуя гажи. Говорят, если посидеть на ней, удача не заставит себя ждать. Проверить это можно, прогулявшись по крыше без ограждений."

#. ja: アルティフィスパス
#. de: Pfad der Kunst<shy>fer<shy>tig<shy>keit
#. fr: Passage de l'Ingéniosité
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: This massive lift is one of several which connects the surface of Old Sharlayan to the subterranean research and storage complex of Labyrinthos. At the end of its descent, the mechanism opens up onto the hub of upper Acrinthos, from where passengers or cargo continue onwards towards other facilities.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162951:0:13"
msgid "The Path of Artifice"
msgstr "Путь мастерства"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラヴィリンソスのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Labyrinthos gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage zu Liedern und Weisen inspirieren.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans le Labyrinthos, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: The Path of Artifice
#. column 15: This massive lift is one of several which connects the surface of Old Sharlayan to the subterranean research and storage complex of Labyrinthos. At the end of its descent, the mechanism opens up onto the hub of upper Acrinthos, from where passengers or cargo continue onwards towards other facilities.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162951:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Лабиринтос, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая, я потянулась за пером и пергаментом..."

#. ja: 地上のオールド・シャーレアンと、地下に広がるラヴィリンソスとを繋ぐ巨大昇降機のひとつ。この装置で降ろされてきた人や物資は、玄関口たるアッパー・アクリンソスに至り、そこから各施設へと向かうことになる
#. de: Der Pfad der Kunst<shy>fer<shy>tig<shy>keit verbindet die Oberfläche Alt-Sharlayans mit dem unterirdischen Labyrinthos. Personen, die mit dem riesigen Aufzug in die Tiefe fahren, gelangen zunächst ins Ober-Acrinthos, um von dort aus zu den unter<shy>schied<shy>lichen Bereichen und Einrichtungen des Labyrinthos weiterzuziehen.
#. fr: Ce passage abrite l'un des gi<shy>gan<shy>tesques ascenseurs permettant au personnel du Labyrinthos d'y descendre avec ses cargaisons. Il débouche sur l'Acrinthos supérieur, qui communique avec tous les bâtiments du complexe.
#. column 13: The Path of Artifice
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162951:0:15"
msgid "This massive lift is one of several which connects the surface of Old Sharlayan to the subterranean research and storage complex of Labyrinthos. At the end of its descent, the mechanism opens up onto the hub of upper Acrinthos, from where passengers or cargo continue onwards towards other facilities."
msgstr "Этот огромный подъёмник — один из нескольких, связывающих поверхность Старого Шарлаяна с подземным научно-исследовательским комплексом Лабиринтос. Внизу он выходит к Верхнему Акринтосу — главному узлу, откуда пассажиры и грузы направляются в другие части комплекса."

#. ja: タウマゼイン
#. de: Thaumazein
#. fr: Thaumazein
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Thaumazein, or “wonder,” is the emotion one feels at the onset of the quest for knowledge. Such a quest was begun here, in an effort to pierce the mysteries of the aetherial sea, yet what researchers encountered was the will of Hydaelyn Herself. The site became a shipyard, where they would construct an ark destined to reach the very moon.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162952:0:13"
msgid "Thaumazein"
msgstr "Таумазейн"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラヴィリンソスのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Labyrinthos gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage zu Liedern und Weisen inspirieren.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans le Labyrinthos, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Thaumazein
#. column 15: Thaumazein, or “wonder,” is the emotion one feels at the onset of the quest for knowledge. Such a quest was begun here, in an effort to pierce the mysteries of the aetherial sea, yet what researchers encountered was the will of Hydaelyn Herself. The site became a shipyard, where they would construct an ark destined to reach the very moon.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162952:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Лабиринтос, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая, я потянулась за пером и пергаментом..."

#. ja: タウマゼインとは「驚嘆」を示す古語であり、知的探求の始まりにある驚きを示す。星の秘密を知るために星海探索の拠点として作られたが、そこでハイデリンの意思と接触。やがて月に至る方舟の造船所となったのだった
#. de: Thaumazein bedeutet „Staunen“ in der alten Sprache Sharlayans und ist Ausdruck der inneren Haltung, die jeder philosophischen Betrachtung zugrunde liegt. Im übertragenen Sinn diente das Thaumazein als Ausgangspunkt der Erforschung der Geheimnisse des Sternengrunds. Dabei gerieten die Forscher in Kontakt mit Hydaelyn. Zuletzt wurde hier die Arche für die Reise zum Mond gebaut.
#. fr: Du “thaumazein”, ou l'émerveillement comme le disent les Sharlayanais d'aujourd'hui, découle la soif de savoir. Des savants devaient partir de cette base pour explorer la mer des étoiles, mais leur mission changea lorsqu'ils entrèrent en contact avec Hydaelyn, la conscience de la planète. Ils s'attelèrent alors à la con<shy>struc<shy>tion d'un vaisseau capable de voyager à travers l'espace et de rallier la lune.
#. column 13: Thaumazein
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162952:0:15"
msgid "Thaumazein, or “wonder,” is the emotion one feels at the onset of the quest for knowledge. Such a quest was begun here, in an effort to pierce the mysteries of the aetherial sea, yet what researchers encountered was the will of Hydaelyn Herself. The site became a shipyard, where they would construct an ark destined to reach the very moon."
msgstr "Таумазейн — древнее слово, означающее «изумление»: так называют чувство, с которого начинается поиск знаний. Именно здесь учёные попытались раскрыть тайны эфирного моря, но вместо ответов встретили волю самой Хайделин. Позднее здесь построили корабль, которому предстояло достичь Луны."

#. ja: メリオール実験農場
#. de: Meryalls Agrarbotanik
#. fr: Laboratoire agronomique de Meryall
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: In this experimental crop farm, researchers explore agricultural methodology and study the growth of seeds collected from various regions across the world. It is named after Meryall─one of the seven Archons instrumental in Sharlayan's foundation─whose botanical knowledge helped enrich the island's barren soils and resolve food shortages.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162953:0:13"
msgid "Meryall Agronomics"
msgstr "Агрономическая станция Мерьялл"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラヴィリンソスのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Labyrinthos gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage zu Liedern und Weisen inspirieren.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans le Labyrinthos, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Meryall Agronomics
#. column 15: In this experimental crop farm, researchers explore agricultural methodology and study the growth of seeds collected from various regions across the world. It is named after Meryall─one of the seven Archons instrumental in Sharlayan's foundation─whose botanical knowledge helped enrich the island's barren soils and resolve food shortages.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162953:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Лабиринтос, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая, я потянулась за пером и пергаментом..."

#. ja: 世界各地から収集された植物標本や農法を研究する実験農場。メリオールは、シャーレアンの建国に貢献した「七賢人」のひとりの名である。彼女は園芸師の知識で、痩せた島を開墾し、食料問題を解決へと導いた
#. de: In Meryalls Agrarbotanik werden botanische Proben aus aller Welt archiviert und neue landwirtschaftliche Methoden erforscht. Meryall war eine der sieben Exegeten, die an der Gründung Sharlayans beteiligt war. Mit ihrem profunden botanischen Wissen half sie dabei, die karge Insel fruchtbar zu machen und die Bewohner mit Lebensmitteln zu versorgen.
#. fr: Ce laboratoire étudie les plantes du monde entier ainsi que les moyens de les cultiver. À l'origine de sa création, on trouve Meryall, l'une des sept Fondateurs de Sharlayan. À l'époque, cette grande botaniste cherchait à aménager l'île afin de résoudre les carences alimentaires de son peuple. Ses efforts ont permis à la Cité du savoir de rayonner à l'échelle mondiale.
#. column 13: Meryall Agronomics
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162953:0:15"
msgid "In this experimental crop farm, researchers explore agricultural methodology and study the growth of seeds collected from various regions across the world. It is named after Meryall─one of the seven Archons instrumental in Sharlayan's foundation─whose botanical knowledge helped enrich the island's barren soils and resolve food shortages."
msgstr "На этой экспериментальной ферме учёные исследуют методы земледелия и выращивают растения из семян, собранных в разных уголках мира. Станция названа в честь Мерьялл, одной из семи архонтов, заложивших основы Шарлаяна. Её знания о растениях помогли возделать бесплодную почву острова и решить проблему нехватки пищи."

#. ja: 洞穴生物繁殖区
#. de: Grotte der Troglophilen
#. fr: Repaire des Cavernicoles
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: This cavern serves as a breeding ground for certain subterranean species deemed vital to ongoing research efforts─including a study into creating fertilizer from the subjects' phosphorous-rich excrement. Troglofauna reproduction is, however, an inexact science, routinely resulting in excessive numbers of cave-dwelling offspring spilling out into nearby habitats.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162954:0:13"
msgid "Troglophile's Deep"
msgstr "Глубины троглофилов"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラヴィリンソスのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Labyrinthos gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage zu Liedern und Weisen inspirieren.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans le Labyrinthos, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Troglophile's Deep
#. column 15: This cavern serves as a breeding ground for certain subterranean species deemed vital to ongoing research efforts─including a study into creating fertilizer from the subjects' phosphorous-rich excrement. Troglofauna reproduction is, however, an inexact science, routinely resulting in excessive numbers of cave-dwelling offspring spilling out into nearby habitats.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162954:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всем, что мог предложить Лабиринтос, и взгляд мой остановился на одном месте. Заворожённая, я потянулась за пером и пергаментом..."

#. ja: 研究対象とされる洞穴生物を繁殖するために用いられている場所。しばしば、増えすぎた生物が溢れ出すことで知られている。なお、洞穴生物の糞には豊富なリンが含まれるため、肥料としての利用も研究されているらしい
#. de: Diese Höhle dient als Brutstätte für bestimmte Arten, die für die Forschungsbemühungen als wichtig erachtet werden<nbsp>- einschließlich einer Studie zur Herstellung von Dünger aus den phosphorreichen Exkrementen der Höhlenbewohner. Die Reproduktion der Troglofauna ist jedoch Fluktuationen unterworfen, wodurch es auch immer wieder zu bedrohlichen Plagen kommt.
#. fr: Les Sharlayanais utilisent ce réseau de grottes pour leurs recherches sur les cavernicoles et leurs déjections riches en phosphore servant au développement d'engrais. Mais la population peut rapidement croître et déborder sur les autres environnements du Labyrinthos<nbsp>; un excès de vitalité dont se passeraient bien les chercheurs devant nettoyer derrière.
#. column 13: Troglophile's Deep
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162954:0:15"
msgid "This cavern serves as a breeding ground for certain subterranean species deemed vital to ongoing research efforts─including a study into creating fertilizer from the subjects' phosphorous-rich excrement. Troglofauna reproduction is, however, an inexact science, routinely resulting in excessive numbers of cave-dwelling offspring spilling out into nearby habitats."
msgstr "Эта пещера служит местом размножения некоторых подземных видов, важных для текущих исследований. Здесь, например, изучают возможность создания удобрений из богатых фосфором экскрементов этих существ. Однако размножение пещерной фауны предсказать непросто: её потомство регулярно расползается по соседним местам обитания."

#. ja: リトルシャーレアン
#. de: Klein-Sharlayan
#. fr: Petite Sharlayan
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Located in the Central Circuit, this self-contained settlement provides housing for Forum-authorized researchers. Due to the highly confidential nature of their projects and a strictly enforced information protocol, the men and women here are rarely permitted egress to the city proper.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162955:0:13"
msgid "Sharlayan Hamlet"
msgstr "Посёлок Шарлаяна"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nラヴィリンソスのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung des Labyrinthos gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird die Barden bis ans Ende aller Tage zu Liedern und Weisen inspirieren.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans le Labyrinthos, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Sharlayan Hamlet
#. column 15: Located in the Central Circuit, this self-contained settlement provides housing for Forum-authorized researchers. Due to the highly confidential nature of their projects and a strictly enforced information protocol, the men and women here are rarely permitted egress to the city proper.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162955:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами Лабиринтоса, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: セントラルサーキットで働く人々が暮らす宿泊所。彼らは、哲学者議会直轄の極秘計画に従事している都合上、情報管理のために地上への出入りを制限されており、事実上、この簡易集落だけで暮らしていた
#. de: In dieser Wohnstätte lebten vom Rat der Philosophen einberufene Forscher, die für die Arbeit im Zentralzirkel zuständig waren. Aufgrund der strengen Vorschriften zur Geheimhaltung ihrer Projekte war es ihnen nur selten erlaubt, das in sich geschlossene Klein-Sharlayan zu verlassen.
#. fr: Certaines missions confiées par le Conseil de Sharlayan sont si secrètes que les allées et venues sont ex<shy>trê<shy>me<shy>ment ré<shy>gle<shy>men<shy>tées dans le Circuit central. Dans les faits, ceux qui y travaillent ne sortent jamais et élisent domicile dans ce petit quartier d'habitation.
#. column 13: Sharlayan Hamlet
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Labyrinthos had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162955:0:15"
msgid "Located in the Central Circuit, this self-contained settlement provides housing for Forum-authorized researchers. Due to the highly confidential nature of their projects and a strictly enforced information protocol, the men and women here are rarely permitted egress to the city proper."
msgstr "В Центральном контуре расположено обособленное поселение для исследователей, получивших разрешение Форума. Их проекты строго засекречены, а правила разглашения сведений соблюдаются неукоснительно, поэтому обитателям посёлка редко разрешают выбираться в город."

#. ja: イェドリマン
#. de: Yedlihmad
#. fr: Yedlihmad
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Meaning “new harbor” in a language brought to the island's shores by mainland settlers, Yedlihmad is Thavnair's main port town. Owing to the shallow waters surrounding the island, however, larger trading vessels are forced to anchor at Alnair, and ferry over to the harbor in smaller boats before making their way to Radz<hyphen>at<hyphen>Han.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162956:0:13"
msgid "Yedlihmad"
msgstr "Едлихмад"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nサベネア島のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Thavnairs gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Betört von der schieren Vielfalt an Farben ergriff ich meine Feder und versuchte, die Schönheit in Worte zu fassen.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais à Thavnair, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Yedlihmad
#. column 15: Meaning “new harbor” in a language brought to the island's shores by mainland settlers, Yedlihmad is Thavnair's main port town. Owing to the shallow waters surrounding the island, however, larger trading vessels are forced to anchor at Alnair, and ferry over to the harbor in smaller boats before making their way to Radz<hyphen>at<hyphen>Han.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162956:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами Тавнаира, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 大陸系の住人たちの古語で「新しい港」を意味する名で呼ばれる港街。サベネア島の周囲は水深が浅いため、大型の外洋交易船は、対岸のアルネア島に停泊。小舟でここに渡ってきて、ラザハンを目指すことになる
#. de: Yedlihmad, „der neue Hafen“ in der Sprache der Siedler vom Festland, ist die wichtigste Hafenstadt Thavnairs. Die seichten Gewässer rund um die Insel machen es großen Handels<shy>schiffen unmöglich, direkt vor Ort zu ankern. Händler planen daher stets einen Zwischenstopp auf dem gegenüberliegenden Alnair ein und setzen von dort aus mit Segelbooten nach Yedlihmad und Radz-at-Han über.
#. fr: Les côtes de Yedlihmad, ou Port-Nouveau, dans l'ancien dialecte des continentaux, baignent dans des eaux peu profondes. Cet aléa géographique force les grands navires marchands à jeter l'ancre au large, près de l'île d'Alnair. Là-bas, leur cargaison est chargée sur des batelets capables de faire le reste du trajet grâce à leur ligne de flottaison plus modeste.
#. column 13: Yedlihmad
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. macro: <hyphen> — a hyphen that does not break the line (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "Adventure:2162956:0:15"
msgid "Meaning “new harbor” in a language brought to the island's shores by mainland settlers, Yedlihmad is Thavnair's main port town. Owing to the shallow waters surrounding the island, however, larger trading vessels are forced to anchor at Alnair, and ferry over to the harbor in smaller boats before making their way to Radz<hyphen>at<hyphen>Han."
msgstr "На языке переселенцев с материка Едлихмад означает «новая гавань». Это главный портовый город Тавнаира. Из-за мелководья вокруг острова крупным торговым судам приходится вставать на якорь у Алнаира, а до гавани и дальше до Радз-ат-Хана добираться на лодках."

#. ja: カジャーヤ演舞場
#. de: Kadjayas Bühne
#. fr: Pas de Kadjaya
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Known as the mother of the Kriegstanz, Kadjaya is honored in both name and form at this open-air stage for dancers. Those who carry on her legacy perform here beneath her stone-carved likeness, strutting and twirling for the glory of their gods and ancestors.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162957:0:13"
msgid "Kadjaya's Footsteps"
msgstr "Следы Каджая"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nサベネア島のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Thavnairs gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Betört von der schieren Vielfalt an Farben ergriff ich meine Feder und versuchte, die Schönheit in Worte zu fassen.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais à Thavnair, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Kadjaya's Footsteps
#. column 15: Known as the mother of the Kriegstanz, Kadjaya is honored in both name and form at this open-air stage for dancers. Those who carry on her legacy perform here beneath her stone-carved likeness, strutting and twirling for the glory of their gods and ancestors.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162957:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами Тавнаира, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 武の舞踏「クリークタンツ」の創始者とされる踊り子、カジャーヤの名を冠した演舞場であり、その姿を象った石像が掲げられている。彼女の技術を継承する踊り子たちが、今も神々や先祖たちに捧げるために舞い踊る
#. de: Unter dem wachsamen Blick ihres steinernen Ebenbilds huldigen Tänzer und Tänzerinnen auf dieser Bühne Kadjaya, der Mutter des Kriegstanzes. Jede hier stattfindende Darbietung zu Ehren der Vorfahren und Götter erweckt den Eindruck eines rituellen Kräfteringens zwischen Stärke und Anmut.
#. fr: Cette piste circulaire est dédiée à Kadjaya, l'inventrice de la Kriegstanz, la danse de guerre. Des statues à son effigie accueillent d'ailleurs les danseurs et danseuses qui font perdurer son art, bien sûr, mais aussi celles et ceux qui souhaiteraient offrir un pantomime aux Dieux ou à leurs ancêtres.
#. column 13: Kadjaya's Footsteps
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162957:0:15"
msgid "Known as the mother of the Kriegstanz, Kadjaya is honored in both name and form at this open-air stage for dancers. Those who carry on her legacy perform here beneath her stone-carved likeness, strutting and twirling for the glory of their gods and ancestors."
msgstr "Эту открытую сцену для танцоров назвали в честь Каджая, которую считают прародительницей боевого танца крик-танц. Её каменное изваяние возвышается над сценой, а продолжающие её дело танцоры выступают здесь во славу богов и предков."

#. ja: ギガントガル採石場
#. de: Gallenerz-Feld
#. fr: Mines de fiel-de-géant
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Quarried here by the wagonload, the purple-streaked stone known as “giantsgall” is one of Thavnair's most coveted exports. Incredibly dense and possessed of high aetherial conductivity, it is prized not only as a building material, but also as a component in the crafting of unyielding arms and armor, and the brewing of alchemical concoctions.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162958:0:13"
msgid "Giantsgall Grounds"
msgstr "Каменоломня «Желчь великана»"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nサベネア島のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Thavnairs gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Betört von der schieren Vielfalt an Farben ergriff ich meine Feder und versuchte, die Schönheit in Worte zu fassen.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais à Thavnair, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Giantsgall Grounds
#. column 15: Quarried here by the wagonload, the purple-streaked stone known as “giantsgall” is one of Thavnair's most coveted exports. Incredibly dense and possessed of high aetherial conductivity, it is prized not only as a building material, but also as a component in the crafting of unyielding arms and armor, and the brewing of alchemical concoctions.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162958:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами Тавнаира, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: サベネア島の特産品のひとつである「巨人石」を産する採石場。独特の紫色を帯びたこの石材は、硬く、エーテル伝導率も高いため、建材はもちろん武器防具の素材や、錬金薬の材料としても有用である
#. de: Was hier aus dem Steinbruch geschlagen wird, ist Thavnairs wertvollstes Handelsgut. Während der enorme Härtegrad des Gallenerzes es zu einem begehrten Baumaterial macht, sorgt seine violette Maserung für eine hohe Ätherleitfähigkeit, die sich perfekt zur Herstellung von Waffen und Rüstungen eignet. Sogar in der Alchemie findet Gallenerz als Zutat Verwendung.
#. fr: Le fiel-de-géant, cette pierre magique à l'éclat violet si particulier, est extrait à Thavnair. Sa dureté et sa richesse en éther font d'elle un matériau de prédilection pour la manufacture d'armes, d'outils et même de divers composants alchimiques.
#. column 13: Giantsgall Grounds
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162958:0:15"
msgid "Quarried here by the wagonload, the purple-streaked stone known as “giantsgall” is one of Thavnair's most coveted exports. Incredibly dense and possessed of high aetherial conductivity, it is prized not only as a building material, but also as a component in the crafting of unyielding arms and armor, and the brewing of alchemical concoctions."
msgstr "Здесь добывают телегами полосатый фиолетовый камень, известный как «желчь великана». Это один из самых ценных товаров Тавнаира. Камень необычайно плотный и хорошо проводит эфир, поэтому из него строят здания, делают крепкое оружие и доспехи, а также готовят алхимические снадобья."

#. ja: 衆園の森
#. de: Schleier der Sangha
#. fr: Jungle des Sangha
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Dense jungle vegetation grows wild and unchecked across a wide band of Thavnair's inland region. Amongst the trees, however, can be found a sprinkling of shrines and temples dedicated to the pantheon of locally worshipped gods─holy sites where once resided the ranks of the faithful.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162959:0:13"
msgid "The Shroud of the Samgha"
msgstr "Покров Самгхи"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nサベネア島のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Thavnairs gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Betört von der schieren Vielfalt an Farben ergriff ich meine Feder und versuchte, die Schönheit in Worte zu fassen.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais à Thavnair, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: The Shroud of the Samgha
#. column 15: Dense jungle vegetation grows wild and unchecked across a wide band of Thavnair's inland region. Amongst the trees, however, can be found a sprinkling of shrines and temples dedicated to the pantheon of locally worshipped gods─holy sites where once resided the ranks of the faithful.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162959:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами Тавнаира, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: サベネア島の内陸部に広がる密林地帯。その大半が打ち捨てられてしまってはいるが、現地住民が信仰する数多の神々を祀る寺院や神殿が点在しており、かつては多くの僧侶たちが暮らしていたため、衆園の森と呼ばれる
#. de: Auf den ersten Blick erscheint dieser Ort wie ein gewöhnlicher Dschungel, in dem die Natur sich selbst überlassen wurde. Wandert man jedoch tiefer ins Dickicht, stößt man alsbald auf die alten Ruinen von Schreinen und Tempeln, an denen Gläubige einst ihre Götter verehrten. Selbst jetzt vermitteln die zerfallenen Gemäuer noch einen Eindruck ihrer damaligen Herrlichkeit.
#. fr: Cette forêt dense s'étend dans toute la partie intérieure de l'île. Ou plutôt s'étendait, car une bonne moitié a été rasée au fil des siècles, mais les divers lieux sacrés qui la parsemaient et où officiaient les fameux Sangha sont restés.
#. column 13: The Shroud of the Samgha
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162959:0:15"
msgid "Dense jungle vegetation grows wild and unchecked across a wide band of Thavnair's inland region. Amongst the trees, however, can be found a sprinkling of shrines and temples dedicated to the pantheon of locally worshipped gods─holy sites where once resided the ranks of the faithful."
msgstr "По всему внутреннему Тавнаиру тянутся густые джунгли. Среди зарослей то и дело встречаются святилища и храмы местных богов. Когда-то здесь жили многочисленные верующие, а теперь эти священные места почти заброшены."

#. ja: マーヤーの幻泉
#. de: Mayaquell
#. fr: Source de la Maya
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: This temple was once the abode of an order of Arkasodara ascetics who sought divine enlightenment through the spiritual power that is maya. Abandoned for a stronghold deeper in the jungle, the structure now sits derelict and half-submerged in rainwater.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162960:0:13"
msgid "The Font of Maya"
msgstr "Источник Майи"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nサベネア島のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Thavnairs gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Betört von der schieren Vielfalt an Farben ergriff ich meine Feder und versuchte, die Schönheit in Worte zu fassen.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais à Thavnair, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: The Font of Maya
#. column 15: This temple was once the abode of an order of Arkasodara ascetics who sought divine enlightenment through the spiritual power that is maya. Abandoned for a stronghold deeper in the jungle, the structure now sits derelict and half-submerged in rainwater.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162960:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами Тавнаира, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: その昔、アルカソーダラ族の魔術僧たちが集団生活を送りながら、マーヤー、すなわち神通力を得ようと修行に励んでいた寺院跡。より森深い場所に拠点を移した今では、半ばまで水没した形で打ち捨てられている
#. de: Seinerzeit beherbergte dieser große Tempel eine Gilde Arkasodara-Magier, die nach der Erleuchtung einer göttlichen Kraft namens Maya strebten. Nachdem man ihn gegen eine tiefer im Dschungel gelegene Festung eintauschte, geriet der Tempel in Vergessenheit. Heute ist der Zugang ins Innere durch Schutt und Regenwasser versperrt.
#. fr: Une communauté de prêtres mages arkasodaras vivait autrefois dans ce temple, où elle s'évertuait à maîtriser une force nommée la Maya. Elle a depuis laissé l'endroit à l'abandon pour se réfugier plus pro<shy>fon<shy>dé<shy>ment dans la jungle.
#. column 13: The Font of Maya
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162960:0:15"
msgid "This temple was once the abode of an order of Arkasodara ascetics who sought divine enlightenment through the spiritual power that is maya. Abandoned for a stronghold deeper in the jungle, the structure now sits derelict and half-submerged in rainwater."
msgstr "Когда-то в этом храме жили отшельники-арксодара, стремившиеся обрести божественное просветление с помощью духовной силы майи. Позже они перебрались в крепость глубже в джунглях, а храм забросили. Теперь он наполовину затоплен дождевой водой."

#. ja: デミールの遺烈郷
#. de: Daemirs Werk
#. fr: Le Grand Œuvre
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Even in Thavnair, the birthplace of alchemy, the practitioners of House Daemir are renowned for the craft of their concoctions. It was they who founded the settlement of the Great Work, and to this day, many talented alchemists choose to reside here and carry on the family's peerless endeavors.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162961:0:13"
msgid "The Great Work"
msgstr "Великое творение"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nサベネア島のいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Thavnairs gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Ort. Betört von der schieren Vielfalt an Farben ergriff ich meine Feder und versuchte, die Schönheit in Worte zu fassen.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais à Thavnair, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: The Great Work
#. column 15: Even in Thavnair, the birthplace of alchemy, the practitioners of House Daemir are renowned for the craft of their concoctions. It was they who founded the settlement of the Great Work, and to this day, many talented alchemists choose to reside here and carry on the family's peerless endeavors.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162961:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами Тавнаира, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 錬金術発祥の地であるサベネア島において、もっとも有名な錬金術師一族である「デミール家」が築き上げた集落。彼らの大いなる業を称えて「遺烈の郷」と呼ばれる同地では、いまも最高水準の人材が研究を続けている
#. de: Von allen Alchemisten-Familien Thavnairs, welches bekanntlich die Wiege der Alchemie selbst ist, war das Haus der Daemirs das erfolgreichste. Hier an diesem Fleck errichteten sie ihr Alchemiewerk, welches bald zum Dreh- und Angelpunkt vieler talentierter Alchemisten wurde, die das Vermächtnis der Daemirs bis zum heutigen Tag fortführen.
#. fr: Si l'on considère Thavnair comme le berceau de l'alchimie, ce hameau construit par les célèbres Daemir pourrait en être le cœur. Aujourd'hui, les meilleurs alchimistes s'y réunissent pour travailler ensemble avec zèle et poursuivre le “Grand Œuvre” de leurs maîtres à penser.
#. column 13: The Great Work
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Thavnair had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162961:0:15"
msgid "Even in Thavnair, the birthplace of alchemy, the practitioners of House Daemir are renowned for the craft of their concoctions. It was they who founded the settlement of the Great Work, and to this day, many talented alchemists choose to reside here and carry on the family's peerless endeavors."
msgstr "Даже на Тавнаире, родине алхимии, прославились зелья мастеров дома Даемир. Именно они основали поселение Великое творение, и по сей день здесь живёт немало талантливых алхимиков, продолжающих непревзойдённое дело семьи."

#. ja: テルティウム駅
#. de: Tertium
#. fr: Gare de Tertium
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Tertium is the third station along the rail network which serves the imperial capital of Garlemald. Equipped as a dispatch yard with generators and other facilities, it was taken over and fortified by the remnants of the Ist Legion following the city's fall into ruination.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162962:0:13"
msgid "Tertium"
msgstr "Терциум"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nガレマルドのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Garlemalds gelangte ich an einen eindrucksvollen Ort. Kalte Winde peitschten über die Landschaft, während ich meine Eindrücke versuchte niederzuschreiben.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais en Garlemald, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Tertium
#. column 15: Tertium is the third station along the rail network which serves the imperial capital of Garlemald. Equipped as a dispatch yard with generators and other facilities, it was taken over and fortified by the remnants of the Ist Legion following the city's fall into ruination.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162962:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами Гарлемальда, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: ガレマール帝国の首都地域を繋いでいた魔導列車網の「テルティウム（第III）」駅。操車庫が併設されており、発電機その他の施設が揃っていることから、首都崩壊後は第I軍団の残余が中心となって拠点化していた
#. de: Tertium ist ein Rangierbahnhof an dritter Stelle des Zugnetzes der Reichshauptstadt, was seine Benennung erklärt. Nach dem Fall der Stadt machten die Überlebenden der I. Legion ihn zu ihrer provisorischen Basis, da er sowohl über einen Generator zur Versorgung der Magitek-Anlagen als auch andere strategisch wichtige Einrichtungen verfügt.
#. fr: Cette gare de triage occupe la troisième position sur le réseau ferroviaire de la capitale impériale, d'où son nom. Elle dispose entre autres d'un générateur capable d'alimenter les ins<shy>tal<shy>la<shy>tions magitek<nbsp>; un atout stratégique qui explique pourquoi les survivants de la 1re légion en ont fait leur base de fortune.
#. column 13: Tertium
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162962:0:15"
msgid "Tertium is the third station along the rail network which serves the imperial capital of Garlemald. Equipped as a dispatch yard with generators and other facilities, it was taken over and fortified by the remnants of the Ist Legion following the city's fall into ruination."
msgstr "Терциум — третья станция железнодорожной сети, обслуживавшей столицу империи Гарлемальд. Здесь есть сортировочная площадка, генераторы и другие необходимые сооружения. После падения столицы остатки Первого легиона заняли станцию и превратили её в укреплённую базу."

#. ja: ユートゥルナG水上リグ
#. de: Juturna-Plattform G
#. fr: Plateforme Juturna G
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: This mining platform is designed to pump vast quantities of ceruleum-rich water from the icy depths of Cerulea Ingens. Six more rigs were built within the region for the same purpose, but the eruption of civil war brought all operations to a standstill.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162963:0:13"
msgid "Juturna Platform G"
msgstr "Платформа Ютурна G"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nガレマルドのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Garlemalds gelangte ich an einen eindrucksvollen Ort. Kalte Winde peitschten über die Landschaft, während ich meine Eindrücke versuchte niederzuschreiben.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais en Garlemald, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Juturna Platform G
#. column 15: This mining platform is designed to pump vast quantities of ceruleum-rich water from the icy depths of Cerulea Ingens. Six more rigs were built within the region for the same purpose, but the eruption of civil war brought all operations to a standstill.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162963:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами Гарлемальда, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 大セルレア湖の底から、青燐水が混ざった水を汲み上げるための採掘プラットフォーム。ガレマルド周辺には、このような水上リグが他にも計6基存在していた。しかし、そのいずれも内戦を機に操業を停止していたようだ
#. de: Von ehemals sieben Bohrinseln, die von A bis G benannt waren, blieb nach Ende des Bürgerkriegs lediglich Plattform G in Betrieb. Sie wurde gebaut, um den am Grund des Sees Cerulea Ingens im Wasser enthaltenen Erdseim zu fördern.
#. fr: Cette plateforme a été construite afin d'extraire le céruleum contenu dans l'eau qui repose au fond du Cerulea Ingens. Il en existait autrefois six autres, allant de A à F, mais la guerre civile n'a laissé que celle-ci en état de marche.
#. column 13: Juturna Platform G
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162963:0:15"
msgid "This mining platform is designed to pump vast quantities of ceruleum-rich water from the icy depths of Cerulea Ingens. Six more rigs were built within the region for the same purpose, but the eruption of civil war brought all operations to a standstill."
msgstr "Эта добывающая платформа предназначена для откачки воды, богатой синим топливом, из ледяных глубин озера Церулеа-Ингэнс. В окрестностях построили ещё шесть таких платформ, но с началом гражданской войны все работы остановились."

#. ja: 脱線した列車
#. de: Der entgleiste Zug
#. fr: Train fuyard
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: A Mark XLIX passenger train was forced off the tracks by tempered soldiers as it attempted to flee the capital, its twisted bulk left to rust in the ice and snow. Only nobles, high-ranking officers, or citizens with special dispensation were permitted to ride this exclusive service.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162964:0:13"
msgid "The Runaway Train"
msgstr "Сошедший с рельсов поезд"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nガレマルドのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Garlemalds gelangte ich an einen eindrucksvollen Ort. Kalte Winde peitschten über die Landschaft, während ich meine Eindrücke versuchte niederzuschreiben.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais en Garlemald, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: The Runaway Train
#. column 15: A Mark XLIX passenger train was forced off the tracks by tempered soldiers as it attempted to flee the capital, its twisted bulk left to rust in the ice and snow. Only nobles, high-ranking officers, or citizens with special dispensation were permitted to ride this exclusive service.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162964:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами Гарлемальда, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 脱線して放棄された魔導列車。このXLIX式客車は貴族用であり、貴族か高位軍人、もしくはその推薦がある市民しか乗車することができなかった。首都からの脱出を試みたものの、テンパード化した兵に襲われ脱線したようだ
#. de: Dieser Zug entgleiste, als er bei einem Fluchtversuch aus der Hauptstadt von besessenen Soldaten attackiert wurde. Den luxuriösen Waggons des Modells XLIX nach zu urteilen, befanden sich unter den Passagieren hauptsächlich Adlige, hochrangige Soldaten und ausgewählte Zivilisten, die vermutlich alle bei dem Zugunglück ums Leben kamen.
#. fr: Ce train a été laissé à l'abandon après son déraillement. À en juger par les luxueuses rames modèle XLIX attachées à la locomotive, il trans<shy>por<shy>tait uniquement des nobles, des militaires hauts-gradés et des civils triés sur le volet. Tout ce beau monde semble avoir péri lors d'une attaque de subjugués alors qu'il tentait de fuir la capitale.
#. column 13: The Runaway Train
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162964:0:15"
msgid "A Mark XLIX passenger train was forced off the tracks by tempered soldiers as it attempted to flee the capital, its twisted bulk left to rust in the ice and snow. Only nobles, high-ranking officers, or citizens with special dispensation were permitted to ride this exclusive service."
msgstr "Пассажирский поезд модели XLIX сошёл с рельсов, когда порабощённые солдаты напали на него во время попытки бегства из столицы. Теперь его искорёженные останки ржавеют среди снега и льда. Ездить на этом привилегированном поезде могли только дворяне, высокопоставленные офицеры и гражданские, получившие особое разрешение."

#. ja: ガレマール元老院
#. de: Senaculum Imperialis
#. fr: Senaculum Imperialis
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Once the center of government for the Republic of Garlemald, this stately building would later house the Emperor's advisory council. Within its walls, countless campaigns were planned and executed─decisions that would result in untold bloodshed, and bring ever greater prosperity to the Empire.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162965:0:13"
msgid "Senaculum Imperialis"
msgstr "Сенакулум Империалис"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nガレマルドのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Garlemalds gelangte ich an einen eindrucksvollen Ort. Kalte Winde peitschten über die Landschaft, während ich meine Eindrücke versuchte niederzuschreiben.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais en Garlemald, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Senaculum Imperialis
#. column 15: Once the center of government for the Republic of Garlemald, this stately building would later house the Emperor's advisory council. Within its walls, countless campaigns were planned and executed─decisions that would result in untold bloodshed, and bring ever greater prosperity to the Empire.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162965:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами Гарлемальда, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: ガレマール共和国時代における統治機関にして、ガレマール帝国時代における皇帝の助言機関。この重厚な建築物の中で幾度となく遠征が議決され、そして、多くの血が流れ、富がガレマルドに集まることになった
#. de: Bereits zur Zeit der Garleischen Republik fungierte das Senaculum Imperialis als Zentrum der Entscheidungsgewalt, woran sich auch nach der Reichsgründung bei seiner Umwandlung in ein Beratungsorgan des Kaisers nichts änderte. Viele der Entscheidungen, die hinter diesen Mauern getroffen wurden, besiegelten das blutige Schicksal anderer Nationen.
#. fr: Du temps de la république, Senaculum Imperialis représentait le siège du pouvoir décisionnel. Il fut converti en conseil gouvernemental lors de la fondation de l'Empire, et c'est derrière ses murs que le destin de multiples pays étrangers fut scellé, chaque vote versant un peu plus de sang pour la gloire et la fortune de Garlemald.
#. column 13: Senaculum Imperialis
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162965:0:15"
msgid "Once the center of government for the Republic of Garlemald, this stately building would later house the Emperor's advisory council. Within its walls, countless campaigns were planned and executed─decisions that would result in untold bloodshed, and bring ever greater prosperity to the Empire."
msgstr "Когда-то в этом величественном здании заседало правительство Гарлемальдской республики, а позже — совет при императоре. Здесь планировали и проводили бесчисленные военные кампании: решения, стоившие множества жизней и приносившие империи всё больше богатства."

#. ja: ウルバニッシマ区
#. de: Regio Urbanissima
#. fr: Regio Urbanissima
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Here did beat the heart of the Empire─a district pulsing with political, financial, and military authority. Yet these institutions, which once sought dominion over the world, now lie in ruins. Any structure not outright destroyed in the war of succession has been torn apart, its materials cannibalized for the construction of the Tower of Babil.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162966:0:13"
msgid "Regio Urbanissima"
msgstr "Регион Урбаниссима"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nガレマルドのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Garlemalds gelangte ich an einen eindrucksvollen Ort. Kalte Winde peitschten über die Landschaft, während ich meine Eindrücke versuchte niederzuschreiben.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais en Garlemald, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'exploratrice que de le partager.
#. column 13: Regio Urbanissima
#. column 15: Here did beat the heart of the Empire─a district pulsing with political, financial, and military authority. Yet these institutions, which once sought dominion over the world, now lie in ruins. Any structure not outright destroyed in the war of succession has been torn apart, its materials cannibalized for the construction of the Tower of Babil.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162966:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами Гарлемальда, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 世界に覇を唱えていたガレマール帝国。その首都地域の中心地とも言える区画であり、政治と軍事、そして経済の心臓部であった。しかし、皇位を巡る内戦と、バブイルの塔建築に伴う資材収奪の対象となり、崩壊してしまった
#. de: Ein Stadtbezirk, der das grenzenlose Streben nach Macht des Garleischen Reiches verkörperte. Er war das politische, militärische und wirtschaftliche Herz der Hauptstadt, bevor der Bürgerkrieg ihn in einen schwelenden Trümmerhaufen verwandelte. Die zerstörten Gebäude lieferten anschließend das Baumaterial für den Turm von Babil.
#. fr: Regio Urbanissima était un quartier à l'échelle de l'ambition de la conquête impériale. Il constituait le centre politique, militaire et commercial de la capitale, mais la guerre civile en a fait un amas de ruines fumantes qui a fourni les matériaux de con<shy>struc<shy>tion de la tour de Babil.
#. column 13: Regio Urbanissima
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162966:0:15"
msgid "Here did beat the heart of the Empire─a district pulsing with political, financial, and military authority. Yet these institutions, which once sought dominion over the world, now lie in ruins. Any structure not outright destroyed in the war of succession has been torn apart, its materials cannibalized for the construction of the Tower of Babil."
msgstr "Здесь билось сердце империи — средоточие политической, финансовой и военной власти. Когда-то эти учреждения стремились покорить весь мир, а теперь лежат в руинах. Всё, что уцелело в войне за престол, разобрали на материалы для строительства Вавилонской башни."

#. ja: フォルム・ソリウス
#. de: Forum Solius
#. fr: Forum Solius
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: It was in this square that Emperor Solus inspected his troops before embarking upon his second campaign into the Far East. The imperial legions were ultimately successful in their subjugation of the Kingdom of Dalmasca, and officials celebrated the grand victory by transforming the parade ground into a commemorative public park.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162967:0:13"
msgid "Forum Solius"
msgstr "Форум Солиус"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nガレマルドのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Garlemalds gelangte ich an einen eindrucksvollen Ort. Kalte Winde peitschten über die Landschaft, während ich meine Eindrücke versuchte niederzuschreiben.
