#. column 15: It was in this square that Emperor Solus inspected his troops before embarking upon his second campaign into the Far East. The imperial legions were ultimately successful in their subjugation of the Kingdom of Dalmasca, and officials celebrated the grand victory by transforming the parade ground into a commemorative public park.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162967:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами Гарлемальда, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 第二回東方遠征に際して、ソル帝による出陣前の閲兵式が行われた広場。ダルマスカ制圧が成し遂げられ、遠征が成功裏に終わったことを記念して、その偉業を称えるために市民広場として整備された
#. de: Vor Beginn des zweiten Eroberungsfeldzugs im Osten hielt Kaiser Solus hier eine große Militärparade ab. Nach dem darauffolgenden Sieg über Dalmasca wurde der Platz in eine öffentliche Gedenkstätte umgewandelt.
#. fr: Solus organisa ici une parade militaire avant le début de sa deuxième campagne de conquête en Orient. Lorsque Garlemald déclara sa victoire sur Dalmasca, la place fut réaménagée en parc commémoratif ouvert à tous.
#. column 13: Forum Solius
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that Garlemald had to offer, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162967:0:15"
msgid "It was in this square that Emperor Solus inspected his troops before embarking upon his second campaign into the Far East. The imperial legions were ultimately successful in their subjugation of the Kingdom of Dalmasca, and officials celebrated the grand victory by transforming the parade ground into a commemorative public park."
msgstr "На этой площади император Солус проводил смотр войск перед вторым походом на Дальний Восток. Имперские легионы покорили королевство Далмаска, и в честь великой победы плац превратили в мемориальный парк."

#. ja: 異土の庭
#. de: Schwarzmulchkuppen
#. fr: Jardin chthonien
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: The researchers of this small facility are unlike their colleagues in that they seek to manifest new creations without the aid of creation magicks. Their natural breeding program pairs creatures with differing characteristics, relying purely on chance to conceive heretofore unimagined possibilities.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162968:0:13"
msgid "The Chthonic Horns"
msgstr "Хтонические рога"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Elpis folgte ein atemberaubender Anblick auf den nächsten. Was ich sah, erfüllte mich mit dem Bestreben, allen Geheimnissen dieses wundersamen Ortes auf die Spur kommen zu wollen.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: The Chthonic Horns
#. column 15: The researchers of this small facility are unlike their colleagues in that they seek to manifest new creations without the aid of creation magicks. Their natural breeding program pairs creatures with differing characteristics, relying purely on chance to conceive heretofore unimagined possibilities.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162968:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 「創造魔法を用いることなき創造」を目指す、風変わりな者たちが研究を行っている小屋。様々な特徴を持つ創造生物を、自然交配で掛け合わせることで、偶然の揺らぎによる想像しなかった結果を求めているようだ
#. de: Eine Gruppe ambitionierter Wissenschaftler nutzte diesen kleinen Garten am Rande von Elpis, um sich der Forschung ohne Anwendung von Schöpfungsmagie zu widmen. Im Gegensatz zu ihren Kollegen zogen sie es vor, verschiedene Lebewesen auf natürliche Weise miteinander zu kreuzen und sich von den daraus entstehenden Zufallsergebnissen überraschen zu lassen.
#. fr: Con<shy>trai<shy>re<shy>ment à leurs confrères, les savants de ce jardin botanique n'avaient pas recours à la magie créatrice pour leurs expériences. Eux préféraient laisser le gros du travail à la nature en ne procédant qu'à de simples croisements, car seulement ainsi pouvaient-ils espérer des résultats inattendus.
#. column 13: The Chthonic Horns
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162968:0:15"
msgid "The researchers of this small facility are unlike their colleagues in that they seek to manifest new creations without the aid of creation magicks. Their natural breeding program pairs creatures with differing characteristics, relying purely on chance to conceive heretofore unimagined possibilities."
msgstr "В этой небольшой лаборатории работают необычные исследователи: они хотят создавать новые виды без магии созидания. Они скрещивают существ с разными свойствами и полагаются на случай, надеясь получить нечто, чего прежде никто не мог вообразить."

#. ja: メタバシス六洋院
#. de: Metabaseos Thalassai
#. fr: La Métabase
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: An annex to Ktisis Hyperboreia, this facility is mainly concerned with the observation and evaluation of sea life. Although its construction appears too narrow to support such an ambitious project, the building's interior harbors six separate marine habitats, each painstakingly recreated via arcane means.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162969:0:13"
msgid "Metabaseos Thalassai"
msgstr "Метабасеос Талассай"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Elpis folgte ein atemberaubender Anblick auf den nächsten. Was ich sah, erfüllte mich mit dem Bestreben, allen Geheimnissen dieses wundersamen Ortes auf die Spur kommen zu wollen.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: Metabaseos Thalassai
#. column 15: An annex to Ktisis Hyperboreia, this facility is mainly concerned with the observation and evaluation of sea life. Although its construction appears too narrow to support such an ambitious project, the building's interior harbors six separate marine habitats, each painstakingly recreated via arcane means.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162969:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: ヒュペルボレア造物院の別館にあたる施設で、主に海洋生物の観察、評価を担う。細長い外観からは想像できないが、その内部には魔法的に再現された6種類の海洋環境が再現されているという
#. de: Ein Ablegergebäude der Hyperboreia, dessen Inneres wesentlich größer ist, als es von außen den Anschein hat. Zur Erforschung und Beobachtung von Meereskreaturen wurden darin stolze sechs ozeanische Biotope errichtet, in denen neue Schöpfungen verschiedenen Umweltbedingungen ausgesetzt werden konnten.
#. fr: C'est dans ce bâtiment à l'écart de l'Hyperborée qu'étaient observées et évaluées les créations marines. Plus vaste à l'intérieur que vu de l'extérieur, il regroupe pas moins de six environnements océaniques permettant de mettre à l'épreuve des espèces diverses et variées.
#. column 13: Metabaseos Thalassai
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162969:0:15"
msgid "An annex to Ktisis Hyperboreia, this facility is mainly concerned with the observation and evaluation of sea life. Although its construction appears too narrow to support such an ambitious project, the building's interior harbors six separate marine habitats, each painstakingly recreated via arcane means."
msgstr "Это отделение Ктисис Гипербореи главным образом занимается наблюдением за морской жизнью и её оценкой. Снаружи здание кажется слишком узким для столь масштабной работы, но внутри скрыты шесть разных морских сред, тщательно воссозданных с помощью магии."

#. ja: レーテー海
#. de: Lethe
#. fr: Le Léthé
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Following a process of exhaustive testing, a creation deemed unsuitable for release into the world is brought to this lake, where its life energies are magically unbound and allowed to dissipate. It is at once the most beautiful as well as the most sorrowful locale in Elpis.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162970:0:13"
msgid "Lethe"
msgstr "Лета"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Elpis folgte ein atemberaubender Anblick auf den nächsten. Was ich sah, erfüllte mich mit dem Bestreben, allen Geheimnissen dieses wundersamen Ortes auf die Spur kommen zu wollen.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: Lethe
#. column 15: Following a process of exhaustive testing, a creation deemed unsuitable for release into the world is brought to this lake, where its life energies are magically unbound and allowed to dissipate. It is at once the most beautiful as well as the most sorrowful locale in Elpis.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162970:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 十分な検討の末に、世に放たないことが決まった創造生物は、この泉にて魔法的に命を「解かれ」た末に流され、冥界へと送られる。エルピスにおける、もっとも美しく、そしてもっとも哀しい場所と言えるかもしれない
#. de: Der schönste und dennoch wohl bedrückendste Ort in Elpis. Hierher wurden Schöpfungen gebracht, die man als ungeeignet für das Leben in den Ökosystemen der Welt betrachtete. Dieselbe Magie, mit der sie erschaffen wurden, zog ihre Essenz durch die Quelle wieder hinab in die Unterwelt.
#. fr: Le Léthé est le lieu le plus magnifique d'Elpis, mais pro<shy>ba<shy>ble<shy>ment aussi le plus mé<shy>lan<shy>co<shy>li<shy>que. C'est ici que les espèces jugées impropres à rejoindre l'écosystème de la surface sont amenées. Leur essence y est défaite par la même magie qui les a créées, puis elle retourne aux Enfers.
#. column 13: Lethe
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162970:0:15"
msgid "Following a process of exhaustive testing, a creation deemed unsuitable for release into the world is brought to this lake, where its life energies are magically unbound and allowed to dissipate. It is at once the most beautiful as well as the most sorrowful locale in Elpis."
msgstr "После всесторонних испытаний творение, признанное непригодным для выпуска в мир, приносят к этому озеру. Здесь его жизненные силы магически освобождают и дают им рассеяться. Пожалуй, это самое прекрасное и в то же время самое печальное место Эльписа."

#. ja: ヒュペルボレア造物院
#. de: Ktisis Hyperboreia
#. fr: L'Hyperborée
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: The most extensive facility in Elpis, Ktisis Hyperboreia is a sprawling complex of magically simulated environs. Concepts awaiting evaluation are brought here for the last stages of observation, and, upon meeting the appropriate criteria, are finally released into the world at large.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162971:0:13"
msgid "Ktisis Hyperboreia"
msgstr "Ктисис Гиперборея"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Elpis folgte ein atemberaubender Anblick auf den nächsten. Was ich sah, erfüllte mich mit dem Bestreben, allen Geheimnissen dieses wundersamen Ortes auf die Spur kommen zu wollen.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: Ktisis Hyperboreia
#. column 15: The most extensive facility in Elpis, Ktisis Hyperboreia is a sprawling complex of magically simulated environs. Concepts awaiting evaluation are brought here for the last stages of observation, and, upon meeting the appropriate criteria, are finally released into the world at large.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162971:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: エルピス最大にして、中枢とも呼べる施設。内部には多種多様な自然環境が魔法的に再現されており、審査を待つ創造生物が放たれ、観察の対象として飼育されている。ここで認められて初めて、世界に解き放たれるのだ
#. de: Die Hyperboreia war die wichtigste Einrichtung in Elpis, denn hier wurde über das Schicksal aller geschaffenen Arten gerichtet. Zu diesem Zweck beherbergte das riesige Gebäude viele verschiedene Biome, in denen man die Schöpfungen auf ihre Nützlichkeit hin prüfte.
#. fr: L'Hyperborée constitue le centre névralgique d'Elpis, puisque c'est en son sein que les espèces créées sont mises à l'épreuve pour juger de leur utilité. À cette fin, l'immense bâtiment abrite de nombreux biomes divers et variés, à l'exception des environnements océaniques qui sont regroupés dans la Métabase.
#. column 13: Ktisis Hyperboreia
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162971:0:15"
msgid "The most extensive facility in Elpis, Ktisis Hyperboreia is a sprawling complex of magically simulated environs. Concepts awaiting evaluation are brought here for the last stages of observation, and, upon meeting the appropriate criteria, are finally released into the world at large. "
msgstr "Ктисис Гиперборея — крупнейший комплекс Эльписа, где магией воссозданы самые разные природные условия. Сюда доставляют творения, ожидающие оценки, чтобы провести заключительные наблюдения. Лишь выдержав проверку, они попадают в большой мир."

#. ja: アナグノリシス天測園
#. de: Anagnorisis
#. fr: L'Anagnorisis
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: Named for an ancient word meaning “recognition” or “discovery,” this settlement houses those whose job it is to assess the creations admitted to Ktisis Hyperboreia. These observers study every aspect of their charges, and determine if a concept will add to─or detract from─the environ for which it was designed.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162972:0:13"
msgid "Anagnorisis"
msgstr "Анагнорисис"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Elpis folgte ein atemberaubender Anblick auf den nächsten. Was ich sah, erfüllte mich mit dem Bestreben, allen Geheimnissen dieses wundersamen Ortes auf die Spur kommen zu wollen.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: Anagnorisis
#. column 15: Named for an ancient word meaning “recognition” or “discovery,” this settlement houses those whose job it is to assess the creations admitted to Ktisis Hyperboreia. These observers study every aspect of their charges, and determine if a concept will add to─or detract from─the environ for which it was designed.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162972:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 古代言語において「認知」、あるいは「発見」を意味するこの集落では、ヒュペルボレア造物院などで監察官として働く者たちが暮らしている。彼らは、創造生物を世界にとって有益か否かという視点で見極めることを務めとする
#. de: Die Beobachter der Hyperboreia waren in dieser kleinen Siedlung untergebracht. Anagnorisis bedeutet „Erkenntnis“ oder „Entdeckung“ in der alten Sprache und ist eine treffende Umschreibung ihrer Aufgabe. Sie waren dafür zuständig zu entscheiden, ob eine neue Schöpfung in die freie Wildbahn entlassen werden konnte, oder aber in der Lethe ihr Ende fand.
#. fr: Les Anciens devaient évaluer la compatibilité de chaque espèce créée avec l'écosystème d'Ætherys avant d'espérer les y introduire. Les employés de l'Hyperborée qui s'attelaient à cette tâche étaient hébergés à l'Anagnorisis – un espace résidentiel dont le nom signifie “recon<shy>nais<shy>san<shy>ce”, notamment d'une erreur déjà commise lors du processus de création.
#. column 13: Anagnorisis
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162972:0:15"
msgid "Named for an ancient word meaning “recognition” or “discovery,” this settlement houses those whose job it is to assess the creations admitted to Ktisis Hyperboreia. These observers study every aspect of their charges, and determine if a concept will add to─or detract from─the environ for which it was designed."
msgstr "На древнем языке название этого поселения означает «познание» или «открытие». Здесь живут наблюдатели, оценивающие творения, допущенные в Ктисис Гиперборею. Они изучают подопечных со всех сторон и решают, пойдёт ли творение на пользу среде, для которой его создали, или навредит ей."

#. ja: シドニア・ノールズ
#. de: Kydonias Antlitz
#. fr: Butte de Cydonia
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: This lifelike face of enormous scale appears to peek out from the surface of Mare Lamentorum. Obviously no natural formation, it is nevertheless unknown who carved this piece, or indeed, whose features it is meant to resemble. One thing is certain: the model would not find the depiction particularly flattering.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162973:0:13"
msgid "Kydonia Knolls"
msgstr "Холмы Кидонии"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Mare Lamentorum gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird mit keiner Zunge meines Heimatgestirns je in gebührende Worte zu fassen sein.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: Kydonia Knolls
#. column 15: This lifelike face of enormous scale appears to peek out from the surface of Mare Lamentorum. Obviously no natural formation, it is nevertheless unknown who carved this piece, or indeed, whose features it is meant to resemble. One thing is certain: the model would not find the depiction particularly flattering.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162973:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 嘆きの海に突如として現れた人面岩。どうみても人工的に作られているのだが、いったい誰をモチーフにして彫られたものなのかは、ようとして知れない。まぁ、誰を模したものであろうと、本人は決して望んでいなかったはずだ
#. de: Wer für die Züge dieses gigantischen Felsens Modell stand, dessen Antlitz stumm gen Sternenmeer starrt, wird wohl mitsamt dem Schöpfer des Gebildes für alle Zeit ein Mysterium bleiben. Vielleicht ist das auch besser so<nbsp>- sonderlich schmeichelhaft ist jene Darstellung nämlich nicht.
#. fr: Cette butte apparue sou<shy>dai<shy>ne<shy>ment à la surface de Mare Lamentorum ressemble étrangement à un visage. Personne ne doute de sa nature ar<shy>ti<shy>fi<shy>cielle, mais on ignore encore qui lui a servi de modèle. Une chose est sûre, l'intéressé s'en serait bien passé.
#. column 13: Kydonia Knolls
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162973:0:15"
msgid "This lifelike face of enormous scale appears to peek out from the surface of Mare Lamentorum. Obviously no natural formation, it is nevertheless unknown who carved this piece, or indeed, whose features it is meant to resemble. One thing is certain: the model would not find the depiction particularly flattering."
msgstr "Над поверхностью Моря Стенаний словно выглядывает гигантское каменное лицо. Оно явно создано искусственно, но кто его высек и чьи черты изобразил — неизвестно. Одно можно сказать наверняка: модели такое сходство вряд ли пришлось бы по душе."

#. ja: キャロットリウム
#. de: Carrotorium
#. fr: Carrotorium
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: This district was specifically designed to sustain the continued existence of mankind, and, more importantly, as a wonderful place to cultivate the miraculous orange vegetables known as carrots. Because let's face it: any trial or trouble becomes easier to bear when one holds a carrot in one's paw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162974:0:13"
msgid "The Carrotorium"
msgstr "Карротиум"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Mare Lamentorum gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird mit keiner Zunge meines Heimatgestirns je in gebührende Worte zu fassen sein.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: The Carrotorium
#. column 15: This district was specifically designed to sustain the continued existence of mankind, and, more importantly, as a wonderful place to cultivate the miraculous orange vegetables known as carrots. Because let's face it: any trial or trouble becomes easier to bear when one holds a carrot in one's paw.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162974:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 人類の生存に適した人工環境が構築されている区画のひとつであり、また世界最高の食物であるニンジンの栽培が行われているイカした場所。世の中、苦労も多いが、まぁ、ニンジンさえあればどうにかなるものだ
#. de: Wer ganz zu Recht glaubt, Möhren seien das höchste kulinarische Gut des Universums, der wird das Carrotorium nie wieder verlassen wollen. Umgeben von sich endlos vervielfachenden Kraft-, Knobel- und Glückskarotten sind sämtliche Sorgen des Daseins schnell nichtig und vergessen.
#. fr: Comme beaucoup d'ins<shy>tal<shy>la<shy>tions sur la lune, le Carrotorium a été construit afin de rendre l'arche habitable par les humains. On y cultive aussi la carotte, l'aliment le plus complet qui soit (selon les Loporrites). Comme on dit ici, tant qu'il y a des carottes, il y a de l'espoir.
#. column 13: The Carrotorium
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162974:0:15"
msgid "This district was specifically designed to sustain the continued existence of mankind, and, more importantly, as a wonderful place to cultivate the miraculous orange vegetables known as carrots. Because let's face it: any trial or trouble becomes easier to bear when one holds a carrot in one's paw."
msgstr "Этот район создали, чтобы люди могли жить на Луне. Но, что куда важнее, здесь выращивают чудесные оранжевые овощи — морковь! Сами посудите: любые тяготы легче перенести, если у тебя в лапе есть морковка."

#. ja: グレーテスト・エンズヴィル
#. de: Der schönste Wald
#. fr: La Garenne sempervirente
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: The architect of this district envisioned an ideal forest─a place where the new residents of the moon could sit or wander amidst arboreal splendor. The fact that it resembles a forest in only the most abstract sense of the word detracts somewhat from the intended effect. Well, it's the thought that counts...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162975:0:13"
msgid "Greatest Endsvale"
msgstr "Величайшая долина"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Mare Lamentorum gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird mit keiner Zunge meines Heimatgestirns je in gebührende Worte zu fassen sein.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: Greatest Endsvale
#. column 15: The architect of this district envisioned an ideal forest─a place where the new residents of the moon could sit or wander amidst arboreal splendor. The fact that it resembles a forest in only the most abstract sense of the word detracts somewhat from the intended effect. Well, it's the thought that counts...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162975:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 「最高の森」と銘打たれた人工森林区画。月に移住することになる人類たちにとって、心安らぐ場所を……というコンセプトで設計されたが、何から何まで本物の森とは違っていた。まぁ、時には失敗することもあるさ
#. de: Der Namensgeber dieses künstlich geschaffenen Stückchens Grün war zweifellos von seinem schöpferischen Talent überzeugt. Das Ergebnis ähnelt zwar weniger einem Wald als einem Laternengeschäft, ist aber dennoch hübsch anzusehen und wird seinem Zweck als Ort der Entspannung sicher gerecht werden.
#. fr: Un paysage aussi verdoyant qu'idyllique et un espace de détente calme pour les pauvres humains venus se réfugier sur la lune. Voilà ce que promet le nom de ce lieu. En y regardant de plus près, toutefois, on réalise bien vite que les apparences sont trompeuses dans cette forêt, à commencer par les arbres qui la composent. Mais comme on dit, c'est l'intention qui compte.
#. column 13: Greatest Endsvale
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162975:0:15"
msgid "The architect of this district envisioned an ideal forest─a place where the new residents of the moon could sit or wander amidst arboreal splendor. The fact that it resembles a forest in only the most abstract sense of the word detracts somewhat from the intended effect. Well, it's the thought that counts..."
msgstr "Архитектор этого района задумал идеальный лес — место, где новые обитатели Луны могли бы сидеть или гулять среди прекрасных деревьев. Жаль, что на лес он похож лишь в самом отвлечённом смысле слова. Ну, главное — старались..."

#. ja: ヘイムダル級観察艇の残骸
#. de: Heimdalls letzte Ruh
#. fr: Épave du Heimdall
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: The ancient Allagans launched this Heimdall-class vessel into the heavens to monitor Bahamut's prison, Dalamud. When that colossal satellite awakened around the time of the Seventh Umbral Calamity, the observation craft was shot down as it attempted to halt the activation process.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162976:0:13"
msgid "Heimdall's Last Sight"
msgstr "Последний взгляд Хеймдалля"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Mare Lamentorum gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird mit keiner Zunge meines Heimatgestirns je in gebührende Worte zu fassen sein.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: Heimdall's Last Sight
#. column 15: The ancient Allagans launched this Heimdall-class vessel into the heavens to monitor Bahamut's prison, Dalamud. When that colossal satellite awakened around the time of the Seventh Umbral Calamity, the observation craft was shot down as it attempted to halt the activation process.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162976:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 龍神バハムートの巨大封印装置であるところの衛星ダラガブを、監視する目的で月軌道上に配置されていた古代アラグ文明のヘイムダル級観察艇。第七霊災に前後して起動したダラガブを止めようと試み、撃墜されたようだ
#. de: Die Trümmer des allagischen Raumschiffs Heimdall zeugen von jenem Moment der Siebten Katastrophe, kurz bevor der in Dalamud versiegelte Bahamut Ætheris erreichte. Das Schiff diente seiner Überwachung und wurde vermutlich abgeschossen, um Bahamuts Beschwörung zu verhindern - wie man heute weiß, vergeblich.
#. fr: Ce satellite de classe Heimdall avait été envoyé en orbite autour de Dalamud par les Allagois afin de surveiller l'état du confinement de Bahamut. Ses programmes de contingence se mirent en branle lorsque le dragon se réveilla à l'aube du septième fléau, mais il fut rapidement pris pour cible et s'écrasa sur la surface de la lune.
#. column 13: Heimdall's Last Sight
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162976:0:15"
msgid "The ancient Allagans launched this Heimdall-class vessel into the heavens to monitor Bahamut's prison, Dalamud. When that colossal satellite awakened around the time of the Seventh Umbral Calamity, the observation craft was shot down as it attempted to halt the activation process."
msgstr "Древние аллагане запустили в космос корабль наблюдения класса «Хеймдалль», чтобы следить за Даламудом — тюрьмой Бахамута. Когда огромный спутник пробудился, незадолго до Седьмого Умбрального бедствия, корабль сбили, пока он пытался остановить запуск."

#. ja: 監視者の館
#. de: Palast des Wächters
#. fr: Palais du Veilleur
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: A structure of enduring design, this brooding tower stands resolute in its vigil of untold millennia. The aetherially conductive plate encircling its spires is reminiscent of a certain architectural style, one found only in the depths of the ocean on the First...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162977:0:13"
msgid "The Watcher's Palace"
msgstr "Дворец Наблюдателя"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung von Mare Lamentorum gelangte ich an einen spektakulären Aussichtspunkt. Und was ich erblickte, wird mit keiner Zunge meines Heimatgestirns je in gebührende Worte zu fassen sein.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: The Watcher's Palace
#. column 15: A structure of enduring design, this brooding tower stands resolute in its vigil of untold millennia. The aetherially conductive plate encircling its spires is reminiscent of a certain architectural style, one found only in the depths of the ocean on the First...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162977:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: 嘆きの海に、ひっそりと佇む監視者の館。螺旋状のエーテル伝導板が巻きつけられたその独特の建築様式は、第一世界のテンペストの底で見た街並みのものと酷似しているように思えるのだが……
#. de: Hoch über die stummen Weiten des Mondes hinaus winden sich die Zinnen dieses prunkvollen Palastes. Die spiralförmige Äthervorrichtung, die sich an das Bauwerk schmiegt, verleiht ihm eine einzigartige Eleganz, die entfernt an einen Ort in Tempest auf dem ersten Splitter erinnert ...
#. fr: Dans le calme de Mare Lamentorum se dresse un palais solitaire, celui du Veilleur. Le tracé hélicoïdal des conducteurs à éther qui l'enlacent rappelle la silhouette des vestiges qu'on peut apercevoir dans La Tempête. Cette ressemblance est-elle le fruit du hasard<nbsp>?
#. column 13: The Watcher's Palace
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162977:0:15"
msgid "A structure of enduring design, this brooding tower stands resolute in its vigil of untold millennia. The aetherially conductive plate encircling its spires is reminiscent of a certain architectural style, one found only in the depths of the ocean on the First..."
msgstr "Эта мрачная башня, сложенная на века, неподвижно несёт дозор уже многие тысячелетия. Обвитые вокруг шпилей пластины, проводящие эфир, напоминают особый архитектурный стиль, встречающийся лишь в морских глубинах Первого мира..."

#. ja: スティグマ・ワン
#. de: Stigma-1
#. fr: Stigma-1
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: The prime decision-making authority for an entire machine civilization, this mechanism has been faithfully reconstructed in Ostrakon Deka-hexi. Originally hailed as strategic matrix Alpha-1, catastrophic damage inflicted upon its systems resulted in its currently assigned designation.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162978:0:13"
msgid "Stigma-1"
msgstr "Стигма-1"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Ultima Thules gelangte ich an einen Ort, der mich daran zweifeln ließ, ob ich wachte oder träumte. Was ich erblickte, würde sich auf ewig tief in mein Gedächtnis brennen.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: Stigma-1
#. column 15: The prime decision-making authority for an entire machine civilization, this mechanism has been faithfully reconstructed in Ostrakon Deka-hexi. Originally hailed as strategic matrix Alpha-1, catastrophic damage inflicted upon its systems resulted in its currently assigned designation.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162978:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: オストラコン・デカークシに再現された機械文明における最高意思決定装置。往時は、戦争戦略マトリクス「アルファ・ワン」と呼ばれていたが、致命的な損傷を受けたことで「スティグマ・ワン」と改称したようだ
#. de: Die militärische Operationsmatrix einer Maschinenzivilisation, die von Meteion im Ostrakon Deka-hexi nachgebildet wurde. Sie ist die oberste Entscheidungsinstanz der Maschinen. Früher wurde sie Alpha-1 genannt, doch nachdem ein Angriff ihr beinahe fatale Systemschäden zufügte, startete sie sich unter dem Namen Stigma-1 neu.
#. fr: La matrice stratégique des opérations de combat a le rôle de décideur ultime au sein de la civilisation de machines reproduite par Météion dans l'Ostrakon Dékahexi. Autrefois désignée Alpha-1, elle se serait renommée Stigma-1 après que ses systèmes ont subi de lourds dégâts.
#. column 13: Stigma-1
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162978:0:15"
msgid "The prime decision-making authority for an entire machine civilization, this mechanism has been faithfully reconstructed in Ostrakon Deka-hexi. Originally hailed as strategic matrix Alpha-1, catastrophic damage inflicted upon its systems resulted in its currently assigned designation."
msgstr "Этот механизм, воссозданный в Остраконе Дека-хекси, был высшим органом принятия решений целой машинной цивилизации. Прежде он назывался стратегической матрицей «Альфа-1», но после катастрофических повреждений получил нынешнее имя."

#. ja: オストラコン・デカークシ
#. de: Ostrakon Deka-hexi
#. fr: Ostrakon Dékahexi
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: This sector is a recreation of the sixteenth civilization encountered by Meteion and her sisters. Although definitive answers remain elusive, it is speculated that the reconstruction echoes the Alphatron Star as it appeared in its last years, or perhaps even an Omicron outpost built upon an invaded world.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162979:0:13"
msgid "Ostrakon Deka-hexi"
msgstr "Остракон Дека-хекси"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Ultima Thules gelangte ich an einen Ort, der mich daran zweifeln ließ, ob ich wachte oder träumte. Was ich erblickte, würde sich auf ewig tief in mein Gedächtnis brennen.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: Ostrakon Deka-hexi
#. column 15: This sector is a recreation of the sixteenth civilization encountered by Meteion and her sisters. Although definitive answers remain elusive, it is speculated that the reconstruction echoes the Alphatron Star as it appeared in its last years, or perhaps even an Omicron outpost built upon an invaded world.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162979:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: メーティオンたちが、「16番目」に確認した文明を再現した区画。母星「アルファトロン星」の末期の姿、あるいは異星侵略に用いられた前哨基地を模しているのではないかと推測されるが、不明な点が多い
#. de: In diesem Sektor hat Meteion einen Teil der 16. Zivilisation reproduziert, auf die ihre Schwestern in den Weiten des Sternenmeeres stießen. Ungewiss bleibt, ob es sich hier um Überreste von Alphatron, der Heimatwelt der Omikron, oder aber eine ihrer hochentwickelten Außenposten handelt, die der Invasion anderer Planeten dienten.
#. fr: Météion a reproduit ici les restes de la seizième civilisation rencontrée par ses sœurs lors de leur voyage à travers l'espace. On peut y voir ce qui semble être les vestiges d'Alphatron, la planète mère des Omicrons, ou tout du moins une de leurs bases avancées. Toutefois, rien n'est moins sûr, car l'endroit reste nimbé de mystère.
#. column 13: Ostrakon Deka-hexi
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162979:0:15"
msgid "This sector is a recreation of the sixteenth civilization encountered by Meteion and her sisters. Although definitive answers remain elusive, it is speculated that the reconstruction echoes the Alphatron Star as it appeared in its last years, or perhaps even an Omicron outpost built upon an invaded world."
msgstr "Этот сектор воссоздаёт шестнадцатую цивилизацию, встреченную Метеион и её сёстрами. Точных ответов нет, но считается, что здесь показана Звезда Альфатрон в последние годы её существования или, возможно, аванпост омикронов на захваченной планете."

#. ja: オストラコン・トゥリア
#. de: Ostrakon Tria
#. fr: Ostrakon Tria
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: This sector is a recreation of the third civilization encountered by Meteion and her sisters. Known collectively as the “Ea,” the entities which reside here have cast off their corporeal shells and endure eternally in purely spiritual form. An awareness of the universe's inevitable end, however, has blighted their immortal gift with existential misery.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162980:0:13"
msgid "Ostrakon Tria"
msgstr "Остракон Триа"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Ultima Thules gelangte ich an einen Ort, der mich daran zweifeln ließ, ob ich wachte oder träumte. Was ich erblickte, würde sich auf ewig tief in mein Gedächtnis brennen.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: Ostrakon Tria
#. column 15: This sector is a recreation of the third civilization encountered by Meteion and her sisters. Known collectively as the “Ea,” the entities which reside here have cast off their corporeal shells and endure eternally in purely spiritual form. An awareness of the universe's inevitable end, however, has blighted their immortal gift with existential misery.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162980:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: メーティオンたちが、「3番目」に確認した文明を再現した区画。当地に住まう「イーア」と呼ばれる者たちは、肉体を脱して完全な精神体となることで永遠の命を得た。しかし、宇宙の揺るぎなき終焉を知り、絶望に落ちたという
#. de: Hier hat Meteion einen Teil der 3. Zivilisation reproduziert, auf die ihre Schwestern im Sternenmeer stießen. Die Ea erlangten ewiges Leben, indem sie ihre sterblichen Hüllen gegen körperlose Seelenformen eintauschten. Mit der Zeit häuften sie Wissen an, und mit dem Wissen kam die Erkenntnis über das Ende des Universums, welche sie fortan in die Ver<shy>zweif<shy>lung trieb.
#. fr: Météion a reproduit ici les restes de la troisième civilisation rencontrée par ses sœurs lors de leur voyage à travers l'espace. Les Éas, qui avaient atteint l'immortalité en délaissant leur enveloppe physique, découvrirent toutefois que cette prouesse ne leur serait d'aucun secours face à la mort thermique de l'univers. Le désespoir amorça alors leur déclin.
#. column 13: Ostrakon Tria
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162980:0:15"
msgid "This sector is a recreation of the third civilization encountered by Meteion and her sisters. Known collectively as the “Ea,” the entities which reside here have cast off their corporeal shells and endure eternally in purely spiritual form. An awareness of the universe's inevitable end, however, has blighted their immortal gift with existential misery."
msgstr "Этот сектор воссоздаёт третью цивилизацию, встреченную Метеион и её сёстрами. Обитатели этого места, которых называют «эа», сбросили телесную оболочку и обрели вечную жизнь в чисто духовной форме. Но знание о неизбежном конце Вселенной омрачило их бессмертие и обрекло на отчаяние."

#. ja: オストラコン・デカオクト
#. de: Ostrakon Deka-okto
#. fr: Ostrakon Dékaokto
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: This sector is a recreation of the eighteenth civilization encountered by Meteion and her sisters. Ruined and desolate, the world it represents was once the abode of a proud race of dragons who were driven to extinction in a titanic struggle against mechanical invaders from the Alphatron Star.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162981:0:13"
msgid "Ostrakon Deka-okto"
msgstr "Остракон Дека-окто"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Ultima Thules gelangte ich an einen Ort, der mich daran zweifeln ließ, ob ich wachte oder träumte. Was ich erblickte, würde sich auf ewig tief in mein Gedächtnis brennen.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: Ostrakon Deka-okto
#. column 15: This sector is a recreation of the eighteenth civilization encountered by Meteion and her sisters. Ruined and desolate, the world it represents was once the abode of a proud race of dragons who were driven to extinction in a titanic struggle against mechanical invaders from the Alphatron Star.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162981:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: メーティオンたちが、「18番目」に確認した文明を再現した区画。アルファトロン星を母星とする文明の機械兵器による侵略を受け、激しい戦いの末に滅亡してしまった。かつては誇り高きドラゴンたちが暮らしていたようだ
#. de: In diesem Sektor hat Meteion einen Teil der 18. Zivilisation reproduziert, auf die ihre Schwestern in den Weiten des Sternenmeeres stießen. Dies war der Planet eines stolzen Drachenvolkes, den die Invasion der Maschinen von Alphatron letztlich in Schutt und Asche legte. Mit ihrer Heimat vergingen die Drachen letztlich selbst.
#. fr: Météion a reproduit ici les restes de la dix-huitième civilisation rencontrée par ses sœurs lors de leur voyage à travers l'espace. Cette planète peuplée de fiers dragons a été ravagée par les machines ex<shy>trê<shy>me<shy>ment avancées venues de la planète Alphatron.
#. column 13: Ostrakon Deka-okto
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162981:0:15"
msgid "This sector is a recreation of the eighteenth civilization encountered by Meteion and her sisters. Ruined and desolate, the world it represents was once the abode of a proud race of dragons who were driven to extinction in a titanic struggle against mechanical invaders from the Alphatron Star."
msgstr "Этот сектор воссоздаёт восемнадцатую цивилизацию, встреченную Метеион и её сёстрами. Некогда здесь обитали гордые драконы, но мир опустел и пришёл в упадок после страшной войны с механическими захватчиками со Звезды Альфатрон."

#. ja: オストラコン・エーナ
#. de: Ostrakon Hena
#. fr: Ostrakon Éna
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
#. column 15: This sector is a recreation of the first civilization encountered by Meteion and her sisters. The structures are whole, but hauntingly empty─as if all life had come to an abrupt end.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162982:0:13"
msgid "Ostrakon Hena"
msgstr "Остракон Эна"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\n暁月の旅路の果てのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei der Erkundung Ultima Thules gelangte ich an einen Ort, der mich daran zweifeln ließ, ob ich wachte oder träumte. Was ich erblickte, würde sich auf ewig tief in mein Gedächtnis brennen.
#. fr: Certains paysages ne s'offrent qu'à ceux et celles qui ont arpenté le départ et l'arrivée, le début et la fin. Quiconque les verra s'en retrouvera à coup sûr transformé.
#. column 13: Ostrakon Hena
#. column 15: This sector is a recreation of the first civilization encountered by Meteion and her sisters. The structures are whole, but hauntingly empty─as if all life had come to an abrupt end.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162982:0:14"
msgid "As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment..."
msgstr "Я любовалась всеми чудесами, что встретились мне в конце пути Рассвета, и вдруг мой взгляд приковало одно место. Очарованная, я достала перо и пергамент..."

#. ja: メーティオンたちが、「1番目」に確認した文明を再現した区画。彼女を構成する1体が降り立ったとき、その街には生命体はただの1体も残っていなかった。ただこつ然と、生活感もそのままに消えていたのだという
#. de: In diesem Sektor hat Meteion einen Teil der 1. Zivilisation reproduziert, auf die ihre Schwestern in den Weiten des Sternenmeeres stießen. Was auch immer in dieser Stadt geschehen ist, es geschah unerwartet, denn die hinterlassene Infrastruktur erweckt den Eindruck eines urplötzlichen Verschwindens ihrer Bewohner.
#. fr: Météion a reproduit ici les restes de la première civilisation rencontrée par ses sœurs lors de leur voyage à travers l'espace. Tout être pensant semble avoir disparu du jour au lendemain, en ne laissant que des vestiges aussi intacts que lugubres.
#. column 13: Ostrakon Hena
#. column 14: As I soaked in all that lay at the end of Dawn's journey, I found my gaze drawn in one particular direction. Entranced, I reached for my quill and parchment...
msgctxt "Adventure:2162982:0:15"
msgid "This sector is a recreation of the first civilization encountered by Meteion and her sisters. The structures are whole, but hauntingly empty─as if all life had come to an abrupt end."
msgstr "Здесь воссоздана первая цивилизация, которую встретили Метеион и её сёстры. Здания целы, но в них жутко пусто — словно вся жизнь внезапно оборвалась."

#. ja: ベイサイド・ベヴィー
#. de: Küstenkolonie
#. fr: Baie commerçante
#. column 14: The sights of Tuliyollal were wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth required no embellishment.
#. column 15: Playing host to a never-ending stream of customers, the largest marketplace in Tuliyollal is replete with goods from every corner of Tural. Its proximity to the harbor ensures that cargo unloaded from the boats and barges can be transported directly to the shelves of local merchants.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162983:0:13"
msgid "Bayside Bevy"
msgstr "Прибрежный рынок"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nトライヨラのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei meiner Ankunft in Tuliyollal gelangte ich an einen Ort, an dem mir die Vielfalt des hiesigen Lebens schier den Atem raubte.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Tuliyollal, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'explorateur que de le partager.
#. column 13: Bayside Bevy
#. column 15: Playing host to a never-ending stream of customers, the largest marketplace in Tuliyollal is replete with goods from every corner of Tural. Its proximity to the harbor ensures that cargo unloaded from the boats and barges can be transported directly to the shelves of local merchants.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162983:0:14"
msgid "The sights of Tuliyollal were wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth required no embellishment."
msgstr "Тулийоллал открывался мне во всём великолепии. Я опишу его таким, каков он есть: правде не нужны украшения."

#. ja: トライヨラ随一の規模を持つ市場。「海辺の鳥の群れ」を意味する名のとおり、大陸各地から集められた品々が並び、多くの人で賑わう。港湾区画に面しているため、舟運を通じて運ばれてきた商品が、すぐさま並べられる
#. de: Der größte Markt Tuliyollals gleicht wahrhaftig einer Kolonie von Möwen, in der sich das Leben tummelt und sich die Reichtümer Turals häufen. Sie schimmern so golden wie die Sonne selbst, die sich auf den an der Küstenkolonie leckenden Wellen bricht.
#. fr: C'est le marché le plus important de Tuliyollal. Comme son nom l'indique, il est situé stratégiquement proche de la mer. Ceci permet aux manutentionnaires d'apporter les denrées venues des quatre coins du continent directement sur ses étals, qui ne désemplissent jamais.
#. column 13: Bayside Bevy
#. column 14: The sights of Tuliyollal were wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth required no embellishment.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162983:0:15"
msgid "Playing host to a never-ending stream of customers, the largest marketplace in Tuliyollal is replete with goods from every corner of Tural. Its proximity to the harbor ensures that cargo unloaded from the boats and barges can be transported directly to the shelves of local merchants."
msgstr "На крупнейшем рынке Тулийоллала всегда полно покупателей, а товары сюда привозят из всех уголков Турала. Рынок расположен у гавани, поэтому груз с лодок и барж можно сразу доставлять в лавки."

#. ja: 翼鏡の街
#. de: Glanzfeder-Viertel
#. fr: La Nuée bigarrée
#. column 14: The sights of Tuliyollal are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment.
#. column 15: Although seemingly uniform in appearance, a closer look at these domiciles reveals the eclectic adornments added by the residents, the decorations emblematic of each inhabitant's land of origin. If Tuliyollal were a giant bird, then these richly colorful homes would form its resplendent plumage.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162984:0:13"
msgid "The Resplendent Quarter"
msgstr "Сияющий квартал"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nトライヨラのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei meiner Erkundung Tuliyollals gelangte ich an einen Ort, an dem mir die Vielfalt des hiesigen Lebens schier den Atem raubte.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Tuliyollal, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'explorateur que de le partager.
#. column 13: The Resplendent Quarter
#. column 15: Although seemingly uniform in appearance, a closer look at these domiciles reveals the eclectic adornments added by the residents, the decorations emblematic of each inhabitant's land of origin. If Tuliyollal were a giant bird, then these richly colorful homes would form its resplendent plumage.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162984:0:14"
msgid "The sights of Tuliyollal are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment."
msgstr "Тулийоллал открывается мне во всём великолепии. Я опишу его таким, каков он есть: правде не нужны украшения."

#. ja: トライヨラの居住区画。立ち並ぶ家々は画一的だが、よく見ると大陸各地から移住してきた住人たちの手で、出身部族ごとに異なる装飾が施されている。その姿は、さながら王都トライヨラという巨鳥を彩る、極彩色の羽根のようだ
#. de: Auf den ersten Blick sieht Tuliyollals Wohngebiet aus wie eine Reihe gleicher Häuser, doch wagt man die genauere Betrachtung, erkennt man die unglaubliche Vielfalt der Bewohner - sie sind das bunte Gefieder der Hauptstadt selbst, das ihr ihren un<shy>ver<shy>gleich<shy>li<shy>chen Glanz verleiht.
#. fr: Le quartier résidentiel de Tuliyollal réserve lui aussi bien des surprises. L'apparence de chaque habitation a été modifiée par ses occupants pour arborer fièrement leur héritage culturel. Certains affirment que ces façades colorées feraient écho aux teintes vives du plumage de l'oiseau totem de la capitale.
#. column 13: The Resplendent Quarter
#. column 14: The sights of Tuliyollal are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162984:0:15"
msgid "Although seemingly uniform in appearance, a closer look at these domiciles reveals the eclectic adornments added by the residents, the decorations emblematic of each inhabitant's land of origin. If Tuliyollal were a giant bird, then these richly colorful homes would form its resplendent plumage."
msgstr "На первый взгляд, дома в жилом квартале Тулийоллала одинаковы. Но приглядитесь — и заметите яркие украшения, выбранные жильцами в память о родных краях. Будь Тулийоллал гигантской птицей, эти разноцветные дома стали бы её роскошным оперением."

#. ja: 満ちた玄関
#. de: Hochfluthafen
#. fr: Perron des Valeureux
#. column 14: The sights of Tuliyollal are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment.
#. column 15: Due to the abundance of reefs in Tuliyollal's coastal waters, marine visitors are forced to anchor their ships out at sea and board smaller vessels to make safe landfall. The harbor's name is no idle promise, as even boats with shallow drafts can be caught on rocks when the tide is low.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162985:0:13"
msgid "High Tide Harbor"
msgstr "Гавань Прилива"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nトライヨラのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei meiner Ankunft in Tuliyollal gelangte ich an einen Ort, an dem mir die Vielfalt des hiesigen Lebens schier den Atem raubte.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Tuliyollal, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'explorateur que de le partager.
#. column 13: High Tide Harbor
#. column 15: Due to the abundance of reefs in Tuliyollal's coastal waters, marine visitors are forced to anchor their ships out at sea and board smaller vessels to make safe landfall. The harbor's name is no idle promise, as even boats with shallow drafts can be caught on rocks when the tide is low.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162985:0:14"
msgid "The sights of Tuliyollal are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment."
msgstr "Тулийоллал открывается мне во всём великолепии. Я опишу его таким, каков он есть: правде не нужны украшения."

#. ja: トライヨラの港湾区画。近海には岩礁が多く存在するため、沖で大型船から小型船に乗り換えて上陸する必要がある。干潮時は岩が多く、小舟でも辿り着きにくいため、満潮時に開かれる港として「満ちた玄関」と呼ばれるようだ
#. de: Schwer beladene Boote fahren in stetem Strom zu den dickbauchigen Schiffen, die hinter den tückischen Riffen ankern - doch nur während der Flut, denn die Ebbe offenbart die scharfen, steinernen Meereszähne und versperrt selbst den kleinsten Kähnen den Weg.
#. fr: La côte turalienne étant infestée de récifs, les long-courriers préfèrent mouiller au large et rejoindre le port de Tuliyollal au moyen d'em<shy>bar<shy>ca<shy>tions plus légères. De par son nom, le “perron des Valeureux” honore les courageux marins qui ont bravé ces eaux traîtres pour rejoindre la capitale.
#. column 13: High Tide Harbor
#. column 14: The sights of Tuliyollal are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162985:0:15"
msgid "Due to the abundance of reefs in Tuliyollal's coastal waters, marine visitors are forced to anchor their ships out at sea and board smaller vessels to make safe landfall. The harbor's name is no idle promise, as even boats with shallow drafts can be caught on rocks when the tide is low."
msgstr "У берегов Тулийоллала множество рифов, поэтому пришлым кораблям приходится вставать на якорь в море и пересаживать пассажиров на лодки поменьше. Название гавани не случайно: во время отлива даже лодка с небольшой осадкой может сесть на мель."

#. ja: フォルアード・キャビンズ
#. de: Kielkajüten
#. fr: Cabines de Proue
#. column 14: The sights of Tuliyollal are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment.
#. column 15: Spanning the length of a pier, these pleasant cottages replaced the previous fleet of boats that once served visitors as rudimentary accommodations. It is said that a foreign explorer was responsible for naming the guesthouses when he likened their rooves to ship prows and their cozy interiors to a captain's cabin.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162986:0:13"
msgid "The For'ard Cabins"
msgstr "Каюты у причала"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nトライヨラのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei meiner Ankunft in Tuliyollal gelangte ich an einen Ort, an dem mir die Vielfalt des hiesigen Lebens schier den Atem raubte.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Tuliyollal, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'explorateur que de le partager.
#. column 13: The For'ard Cabins
#. column 15: Spanning the length of a pier, these pleasant cottages replaced the previous fleet of boats that once served visitors as rudimentary accommodations. It is said that a foreign explorer was responsible for naming the guesthouses when he likened their rooves to ship prows and their cozy interiors to a captain's cabin.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162986:0:14"
msgid "The sights of Tuliyollal are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment."
msgstr "Тулийоллал открывается мне во всём великолепии. Я опишу его таким, каков он есть: правде не нужны украшения."

#. ja: 沖に伸びた桟橋から一棟貸しの建物が連なる構造が特徴的な宿。かつては桟橋に停泊した小舟に寝泊まりする簡素な作りであったという。ある異国の冒険家が現在の建物を見て、屋根を船首に、客室を船室に喩えて屋号を命名したらしい
#. de: Der lange Steg führt an einer ganzen Reihe kleiner Häuser vorbei, die Reisenden ein flüchtiges Zuhause bieten. Früher schliefen Seeleute hier wohl in ihren ankernden Bötchen, und auch der Name der Kielkajüten entstammt einem fremdländischen Abenteurer, den die Dächer an den Bug eines Schiffes erinnerten.
#. fr: Ces cabines sur pilotis sont en réalité des chambres d'auberge, réparties sur le long de la côte. On dit que c'est un explorateur venu de terres lointaines qui a autrefois eu l'idée de ce concept, alors qu'il passait la nuit sur un canot amarré à ce ponton.
#. column 13: The For'ard Cabins
#. column 14: The sights of Tuliyollal are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162986:0:15"
msgid "Spanning the length of a pier, these pleasant cottages replaced the previous fleet of boats that once served visitors as rudimentary accommodations. It is said that a foreign explorer was responsible for naming the guesthouses when he likened their rooves to ship prows and their cozy interiors to a captain's cabin."
msgstr "Эти уютные домики тянутся вдоль причала и заменили стоявшие здесь прежде лодки, служившие простым пристанищем для гостей. Говорят, название гостиницам дал чужеземный путешественник: крыши напомнили ему носы кораблей, а уютные комнаты — каюты капитана."

#. ja: フヌイリーの塔
#. de: Hunu'iliy
#. fr: Phare de Hunu'iliy
#. column 14: The sights of Tuliyollal are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment.
#. column 15: Meaning “heartfire” in the Hanuhanu tongue, this lighthouse also once served as a watchtower for threats approaching from Xak Tural. These days, its only role is to warn coastal vessels away from the thundering waterfalls.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162987:0:13"
msgid "Hunu'iliy"
msgstr "Хунуилий"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nトライヨラのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei meiner Erkundung Tuliyollals gelangte ich an einen Ort, an dem mir die Vielfalt des hiesigen Lebens schier den Atem raubte.
#. fr: Alors que je vagabondais dans Tuliyollal, un paysage saisissant s'offrit à mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'explorateur que de le partager.
#. column 13: Hunu'iliy
#. column 15: Meaning “heartfire” in the Hanuhanu tongue, this lighthouse also once served as a watchtower for threats approaching from Xak Tural. These days, its only role is to warn coastal vessels away from the thundering waterfalls.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162987:0:14"
msgid "The sights of Tuliyollal are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment."
msgstr "Тулийоллал открывается мне во всём великолепии. Я опишу его таким, каков он есть: правде не нужны украшения."

#. ja: 葦舟を使うハヌハヌたちの言葉で、「心の炎」を意味する名を持つ灯台。かつてはサカ・トラル方面を警戒する監視塔の役割もあったが、現在は近海を行き来する船に大瀑布が近いことを警告する役目のみを担っている
#. de: In der Sprache der Hanuhanu bedeutet der Name dieses Leuchtturms „Herzensflamme“. Früher war er ein waches Auge auf Xak Tural, doch heute wacht er nur mehr über Schiffe, die den reißenden Riffen Turals zu nahe kommen.
#. fr: Le nom de ce phare signifie “flamme du cœur” dans la langue des Hanu Hanu. Il servait jadis de tour de guet, surveillant les allées et venues dans le Xak Tural. Aujourd'hui, ce phare permet aux marins de ne pas s'approcher trop près de la côte turalienne et de ses récifs.
#. column 13: Hunu'iliy
#. column 14: The sights of Tuliyollal are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162987:0:15"
msgid "Meaning “heartfire” in the Hanuhanu tongue, this lighthouse also once served as a watchtower for threats approaching from Xak Tural. These days, its only role is to warn coastal vessels away from the thundering waterfalls."
msgstr "На языке ханухану название этого маяка означает «пламя сердца». Когда-то он служил сторожевой башней, откуда высматривали угрозы со стороны Сак-Турала. Теперь маяк лишь предупреждает корабли у берега о близости грохочущих водопадов."

#. ja: ワチュン・ペロ
#. de: Wachunpelo
#. fr: Wachunpelo
#. column 14: The sights of Urqopacha are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment.
#. column 15: Nestled in between the mountains, the dwellings of this village are noticeably scaled down to accommodate the smaller size of its inhabitants. It is here that the peddler clan of the Pelupelu manufacture their trading goods such as coffee and mezcal, as well as maintain a ranch for the breeding and training of alpacas.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162988:0:13"
msgid "Wachunpelo"
msgstr "Вачунпело"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nオルコ・パチャのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei meinen Streifzügen durch Urqopacha gelangte ich an einen Ort, der in mir sowohl großen Respekt für bewährte Traditionen als auch das leise Verlangen nach deren Neuerung erweckte.
#. fr: Alors que je visitais Urqopacha, un paysage magnifique apparut devant mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'explorateur que de le partager.
#. column 13: Wachunpelo
#. column 15: Nestled in between the mountains, the dwellings of this village are noticeably scaled down to accommodate the smaller size of its inhabitants. It is here that the peddler clan of the Pelupelu manufacture their trading goods such as coffee and mezcal, as well as maintain a ranch for the breeding and training of alpacas.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162988:0:14"
msgid "The sights of Urqopacha are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment."
msgstr "В Уркопаче открываются дивные виды. Я опишу это место как есть: правде не нужны украшения."

#. ja: 行商の民ペルペル族が故郷とする、山間の集落。一帯ではコーヒーやメスカル酒といった交易品が生産されているほか、アルパカを飼育する牧場も営まれている。小柄な住人に合わせ、家々もやや小さく作られているようだ
#. de: Dieses Bergdorf ist die Heimat der geschäftstüchtigen Pelupelu. Sie sind einerseits für ihren exquisiten Kaffee und Mezcal bekannt, andererseits für ihre Alpakazucht. Die Reihen kleiner Häuser, perfekt auf ihre Statur zugeschnitten, fügen sich zu einem heimeligen, possierlich wirkendem Bild.
#. fr: C'est dans ce hameau de montagne que se sont installés les Pelupelu, peuple de marchands ambulants. La région produit du café, de l'alcool appelé “mezcal” et d'autres produits dont ils font le commerce. Ils élèvent également des alpagas. Leurs petites maisons sont adaptées à la taille des habitants.
#. column 13: Wachunpelo
#. column 14: The sights of Urqopacha are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162988:0:15"
msgid "Nestled in between the mountains, the dwellings of this village are noticeably scaled down to accommodate the smaller size of its inhabitants. It is here that the peddler clan of the Pelupelu manufacture their trading goods such as coffee and mezcal, as well as maintain a ranch for the breeding and training of alpacas."
msgstr "Затерянная среди гор деревня, где живут пелупелу — народ торговцев. Здесь производят товары на продажу, например кофе и мескаль, а ещё разводят и обучают альпак. Дома здесь под стать невысоким жителям — заметно меньше обычных."

#. ja: ミープル・マテ茶園
#. de: Miplus Mategarten
#. fr: Matéière de Miplu
#. column 14: The sights of Urqopacha are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment.
#. column 15: Overseen by the eponymous Miplu, the cultivation of this mate tea garden has introduced lush greenery and fertile soil to Urqopacha's usual vistas of sparse vegetation. The operation has almost become a small village in its own right, with the number of field hands ever growing to match the garden's steady expansion.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162989:0:13"
msgid "Miplu's Mate Garden"
msgstr "Чайный сад Миплу"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nオルコ・パチャのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei meinen Streifzügen durch Urqopacha gelangte ich an einen Ort, der in mir sowohl großen Respekt für bewährte Traditionen als auch das leise Verlangen nach deren Neuerung erweckte.
#. fr: Alors que je visitais Urqopacha, un paysage magnifique apparut devant mes yeux. Je sus alors qu'il était de mon devoir d'explorateur que de le partager.
#. column 13: Miplu's Mate Garden
#. column 15: Overseen by the eponymous Miplu, the cultivation of this mate tea garden has introduced lush greenery and fertile soil to Urqopacha's usual vistas of sparse vegetation. The operation has almost become a small village in its own right, with the number of field hands ever growing to match the garden's steady expansion.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162989:0:14"
msgid "The sights of Urqopacha are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment."
msgstr "В Уркопаче открываются дивные виды. Я опишу это место как есть: правде не нужны украшения."

#. ja: ペルペル族のミープルが経営するマテ茶園。オルコ・パチャに茶の木の苗が持ち込まれる前は緑の薄い荒野だったが、茶畑の拡大とともに土壌改善も行われてきた。今では働き手も増え、小集落と呼べる規模になっている
#. de: Der Name dieser reizenden Plantage ist selbsterklärend. Mir wurde erzählt, dass das Land vor allem stachelig und karg war, ehe die Samen der Teesträucher nach Urqopacha kamen. Seither hat sich jedoch so viel getan, dass der Ort vor Leben und Handel geradezu zu summen scheint - und auch das Land ist seither fruchtbarer geworden.
#. fr: Cette plantation de thé maté est gérée par un Pelupelu du nom de Miplu. Avant que cette boisson ne soit importée à Urqopacha, la région n'était qu'une grande plaine déserte, mais les sols ont beaucoup gagné en fertilité au fur et à mesure que les plants se sont étendus. Ces dernières années, le nombre de travailleurs a beaucoup augmenté et la petite communauté a assez grandi pour qu'on puisse désormais la qualifier de “village”.
#. column 13: Miplu's Mate Garden
#. column 14: The sights of Urqopacha are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162989:0:15"
msgid "Overseen by the eponymous Miplu, the cultivation of this mate tea garden has introduced lush greenery and fertile soil to Urqopacha's usual vistas of sparse vegetation. The operation has almost become a small village in its own right, with the number of field hands ever growing to match the garden's steady expansion."
msgstr "Чайным садом мате заведует пелупелу по имени Миплу. Прежде эти места были почти безжизненной пустошью, но с появлением чайных саженцев здесь стало больше зелени, а почва сделалась плодороднее. Плантации разрастаются, работников становится всё больше, и теперь это место почти превратилось в небольшую деревню."

#. ja: 哀苦の影
#. de: Schatten der Trauer
#. fr: Ombres endeuillées
#. column 14: The sights of Urqopacha are wondrous to behold. I would capture this scene in honest words, for the truth requires no embellishment.
#. column 15: These ruins brood silently at the cliff's edge. Once a Yok Huy village, it was abandoned as the giants' population dwindled, the crumbling stone houses inhabited now only by the shadows of past sadness. Locals speak of a road which long ago stretched from the settlement down into Chabayuqeq, but little trace of such a path remains.
msgctxt "Adventure:2162990:0:13"
msgid "Shades of Grief"
msgstr "Тени скорби"

#. ja: ――この景色、後世に伝ふ。\nオルコ・パチャのいずこかにあり。\nその場で見渡す。
#. de: Bei meinen Streifzügen durch Urqopacha gelangte ich an einen Ort, der in mir sowohl großen Respekt für bewährte Traditionen als auch das leise Verlangen nach deren Neuerung erweckte.
